1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard was the son of Gilbert Talbot[1]. The writ for the Inquisition of his father Gilbert 'Talebot' was dated 08 Sep, 2 Edward I (1274) and concerned lands in Gloucestershire and Herefordshire. Richard his son, 
2 CONC aged 24 and more, was his next heir[2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Talbot died around 1306. Following a Writ of 3rd September, 34 Edward 1 [1306] his Inquisition concerned the manor of Eckeluswalle [Eccleswall], Herefordshire. Gilbert his son aged 29 on the feast of St Luke [18 October] l
2 CONC ast, was his next heir[6].
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 The Complete Peerage, or a history of the House of lords and all its members from the earliest times. Vol. XII, part 1: Skelmersdale to Towton. London: The St. Catherine Press. Talbot pp.606-632. ↑ 'Inquisitions Post Mor
2 CONC tem, Edward I, File 7', in Calendar of Inquisitions Post Mortem: Volume 2, Edward I, ed. J E E S Sharp (London, 1906), pp. 58-65. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/inquis-post-mortem/vol2/pp58-65 [accessed 29
2 CONC  August 2019]. Item 80.
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ J E E S Sharp and A E Stamp, 'Inquisitions Post Mortem, Edward I, File 122', in Calendar of Inquisitions Post Mortem: Volume 4, Edward I (London, 1913), pp. 238-249. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/inquis
2 CONC -post-mortem/vol4/pp238-249 [accessed 16 August 2019]. Item 377.
