1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://thepeerage.com/p21341.htm#i213401
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sarah de Beauchamp''' was the daughter of William de Beauchamp. She married Sir Richard Talbot, son of Gilbert Talbot and Gwenlyn Mechyll, after 7 January 1268/69. She died after July 1317.      From after 7 January 1268/69, he
2 CONC r married name became Talbot.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sarah de Beauchamp and Sir Richard Talbot
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert Talbot, 1st Lord Talbot+2,1 b. 18 Oct 1276, d. 13 Feb 1346
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct 
2 CONC or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XII/1. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, sister of William de Beauchamp, Earl of Warwick. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT He [Richard Talbot] is said to have married, after 7 January 1268/9, Sarah, sister of William (DE BEAUCHAMP), EARL OF WARWICK, daughter of William DE BEAUCHAMP, of Elmley, co. Worcester, by ISABEL, sister and heir of William (MAUD
2 CONC UIT), EARL OF WARWICK, daughter of William MAUDUIT, of Hanslope, Bucks. He died shortly before 3 September 1306. Sarah Talbot, probably his widow, was living, July 1317. [Complete Peerage XII/1:609-10, (transcribed by Dave Utzinge
2 CONC r)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elmley Castle
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah married Richard IV Talbot Of Eccleswall, Sir, son of Talbot and Unknown, after 7 Jan 1268-1269. (Richard IV Talbot Of Eccleswall, Sir was born about 1250 in Linton, , Herefordshire, England 1 2 6 and died before 3 Sep 1306 i
2 CONC n Eccleswall, Herefordshire, England .)
