2 CONT Criminal*	He was An order for his arrest was dated. The charges included attacking the King's subjects in Warwicckshire and attacking and burning Bridgnorth. His lands were taken into the King's (Edward II) hands. On 15 January 13
2 CONC 21/22.6,3 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Rebel) Battle-Boroughbridge	On 16 Mar 1322, Sir John Gifford, Sir Hugh de Audley, Sir Gilbert Talbot, Sir Bartholomew de Burghersh, Sir Bartholomew de Badlesmere and Sir Humphrey VIII de Bohun fought on the side of the Earl of La
2 CONC ncaster at the Battle of Boroughbridge in Yorkshire He was captured, but allowed to ransom his life and lands for £2000.7,3,8 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was released from prison on 11 July 1322.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was empowered to arrest malefactors in Gloucestershire. On 28 October 1322 at Gloucestershire, England.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was pardoned. On 1 November 1322.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He is to arrest disturbers of peace in Glou., Worc., and Here. He is made Custos of Gloucester Caslte, town, and barton under Hugh le Despenser, jun. On 1 November 1322.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc*	He is not to aggrieve Aymer, Earl of Pembroke for fishing in his ponds and taking his goods. On 27 December 1322.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was among the knights to attend the Great Council on 9 May 1324 at Westminster.6,3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Summoned	He was summoned to serve in Guienne on 7 January 1325.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc*	His fines were cancelled by King Edward III on 13 February 1326/27.6,3 
2 CONT
