2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was the king's chamberlain in March 1327/28.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He obtained grants for Eccleswall and Credenhill, Hereford, and Longhope in Gloucstershire. In April 1328.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was Justice of South Wales on 23 October 1330.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	Summoned to Parliament between 27 January 1332 and 20 April 1343.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He and Hugh le Despenser were appointed to be captains against the King's enemies. On 13 July 1337.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death*	He died on 24 February 1346 at Eccleswall, Herefordshire, England, at age 69.1,5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Title*	He held the title of 1st Lord Talbot.6 
2 CONT
