2 CONT
2 CONT TITLES- Prince of Powys Lord of, History of the Princes, The Lords Marcher and the Ancient Nobility of Powys Fadog Accession to Powys in 1132 Source-Fryde, Handbook of British Chronology(page 54)
2 CONT
2 CONT LIVING-1138-He put, Cynwrig, illegitimate son of Owain Gwynedd to death Source=  Lloyd,History of the Princes etc (vol 1, page 111)
2 CONT
2 CONT PROPERTY- Lord of Oswestry Source-Derbyshire Feudal History, Received from his father, Powys Fadog Source- Lloyd, History of the Princes etc.(vol1,page108) Lord of Powis Vadoc, and of Oswestry Source- J. Morris, Shropshire Genealo
2 CONC gies, (Vol 2, Page 911) He built the castles to Oswestry, Caerinion, Caraghota and Overton Madoc. Source- J. Morris, Shropshire Genealogies-Vol 2, page 911.
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH: He was prison in Winchester, where he died in 1159. Source- Lloyd, The History of the Princes etc,(vol 1-pages 119-120)
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTES: He was last to rule over the whole of Powys.  An elegy to Madog written by Gwalchmal ap Mellir is Found written in Welsh and (some translation into English) on pages 128-147, Vol 1 of Lloyds, History of the Princes etc
