2 CONT IV. DRUE DE MONTEACUTO
2 CONT
2 CONT upon the assessment of the aid for marrying the King's daughter, 12th Henry II. (ii67) certified his Knight's fees to be in number-nine, a half and a third part of the old feosment and one of the new 1 (64o acres made a Knight's f
2 CONC ee).
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Aliva, daughter. of Alan Basset, baron of Wiccomb in County of Buckingham. After his death she married second, Richard SOD of Gilbert Talbot, ancestor to the Earls of Shrewsbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT His eldest son, also named Drue, died during his father's lifetime, he married, however, and left two sons,-John and William de Montacute. The younger, William, had no male issue, and but two daughters, namely, Margaret, married t
2 CONC o William de Echingham; and Isabel, married to Thomas de Audham 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT The elder son, John 3, was seated at Marsh, in County Buckingham, a manor situated northwest from Alesbury and near the Oxford County line - he married Lucy *____ * and had a daughter Katherine, who married Warine Bassett.
