2 CONT
2 CONT Philip Basset (c. 1185 – 19 October 1271) was the Justiciar of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip was the son of Alan Basset of High Wycombe in Buckinghamshire and his wife, Aline Degai.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the manor of Wycombe; the town received market borough status in 1237.
2 CONT
2 CONT Basset served as the Justiciar of England between the two terms served by his son-in-law, Hugh le Despencer, 1st Baron le Despencer.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He served during the period that Henry III regained control of the government from the Barons.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_Basset
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip Basset (c. 1185 – 19 October 1271) was the Justiciar of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip was the son of Alan Basset of High Wycombe in Buckinghamshire and his wife, Alice, the daughter of Stephen Gray.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the manor of Wycombe; the town received market borough status in 1237.
2 CONT
2 CONT Basset served as the Justiciar of England between the two terms served by his son-in-law, Hugh le Despencer, 1st Baron le Despencer.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He served during the period that Henry III regained control of the government from the Barons.
2 CONT *_________________________
