1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''William de Beauchamp (d.1268)==
2 CONT '''William de Beauchamp (c1215–1268) was an English baron and hereditary sheriff.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was born and lived in Elmley Castle, Worcestershire the eldest son of Walter de Beauchamp and his wife Joan de Mortimer.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On the death of his father in 1236 he became hereditary Sheriff of Worcestershire which title he held until his own death.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He died in 1268. He had married Isabel, daughter of William Mauduit and sister of William Maudit, 8th Earl of Warwick. They had 8 children, of which his heir was William, who inherited the title of Earl of Warwick from his uncl
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_de_Beauchamp_(d.1268)
2 CONT *____________________________
2 CONT *'''William de Beauchamp1
2 CONT *'''M, #118565, d. 1269
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 Sep 2009
2 CONT *'''     William de Beauchamp was the son of Walter de Beauchamp and Joane de Mortimer.2 He married Isabel Mauduit, daughter of William Mauduit and Alice de Newburgh.3 He died in 1269.2
2 CONT *'''     He lived at Elmley, Worcestershire, England.4 He gained the title of Baron of Elmley [feudal barony].5
2 CONT *'''Child of William de Beauchamp
2 CONT ** 1.Sarah de Beauchamp+1 d. a Jul 1317
2 CONT *'''Children of William de Beauchamp and Isabel Mauduit
2 CONT ** 1.Sir Walter Beauchamp+4 d. 1303
2 CONT ** 2.John Beauchamp+6 d. a 1297
2 CONT ** 3.William de Beauchamp, 9th Earl of Warwick+1 b. 1237, d. 1298
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XII/1. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family."
2 CONT * 3.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume XII/1, page 610.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 44.
2 CONT * 5.[S22] Sir Bernard Burke, C.B. LL.D., A Genealogical History of the Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire, new edition (1883; reprint, Baltimore, Maryland: Genealogical Publishing Company, 1978
2 CONC ), page 399. Hereinafter cited as Burkes Extinct Peerage.
2 CONT * 6.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 45.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p11857.htm#i118565
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT *'''Sir William de Beauchamp, Earl of Warwick, 5th Baron Beauchamp, Sheriff of Worcester & Worcestershire1,2,3,4,5
2 CONT *'''M, #4062, b. 1215, d. circa 25 April 1269
2 CONT *Father      Walcheline de Beauchamp6 b. c 1180, d. 14 Apr 1236
2 CONT *Mother     Joane de Mortimer b. c 1190, d. 1268
2 CONT *'''     Sir William de Beauchamp, Earl of Warwick, 5th Baron Beauchamp, Sheriff of Worcester & Worcestershire was born in 1215 at of Elmley & Salwarpe, Worcestershire, England.4 He married Isabel Mauduit, daughter of Sir William 
2 CONC V Mauduit, Chamberlain of the Exchequer, Baron Hameslepe & Mauduit and Alice de Newburgh, circa 1236; They had 4 sons (William, Earl of Warwick; Sir Walter; Sir John; & James) & 6 daughters (Alice, wife of Bernard de Brus; Joan, w
2 CONC ife of Sir Martholomew de Sudeley; Isabel; Margaret (Margery), wife of Sir Hubert Hussey; Sibyl; & Sarah, wife of Richard Talbot).2,3,4 Sir William de Beauchamp, Earl of Warwick, 5th Baron Beauchamp, Sheriff of Worcester & Worcest
2 CONC ershire left a will on 7 January 1269; Requested burial at Friars Minor, Worcester.4,7 He died circa 25 April 1269.4,8
2 CONT *'''Family      Isabel Mauduit d. b 30 Jan 1268
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Joane Beauchamp+4,9 d. a 1298
2 CONT **Alicia de Beauchamp+10,4 d. b 1265
2 CONT **Sarah Beauchamp+4,5,7 d. a Jul 1317
2 CONT **Margaret (Margery) de Beauchamp+11,4 b. c 1235, d. a 1284
2 CONT **Isabel de Beauchamp+ b. c 1236, d. a 1323
2 CONT **Sir William de Beauchamp, 9th Earl Warwick, 6th Baron Beauchamp+2,4 b. c 1238, d. 5 Jun 1298 or 9 Jun 1298
2 CONT **Thomas de Beauchamp, Lord of Weston b. c 1240, d. a 1286
2 CONT **Sir Walter de Beauchamp, Constable of Gloucester Castle+12,3,4,13,8 b. b 1242, d. 16 Feb 1303
2 CONT **Sir James de Beauchamp b. c 1244, d. a 1277
2 CONT **John de Beauchamp+14 b. c 1250, d. a 1316
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S648] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. II, p. 44; Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 22.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 134-135.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 384-385.
