2 TITL William Beauchamp 1215-1268
1 NOTE his nobleman, William de Beauchamp, feudal Lord of Elmley,
2 CONT attended King Henry III, in the 37th year of his reign [1253],
2 CONT into Gascoigne, and in two years afterwards marched under the
2 CONT banner of Robert de Clare, Earl of Gloucester, against the
2 CONT Scots. In the 41st of the same reign, he had summons (with other
2 CONT illustrious persons) to meet the king at Chester on the feast
2 CONT day of St Peter de Vincula, well fitted with horse and arms to
2 CONT oppose the incursions of Llewellyn, Prince of Wales. Lord
2 CONT Beauchamp m. Isabel, dau. of William Mauduit, of Hanslape, co.
2 CONT Bucks, heritable chamberlain of the exchequer, and sister and
2 CONT heiress of William Mauduit, Earl of Warwick (who inherited that
2 CONT dignity from his cousin, Margery de Newburgh, Countess of
2 CONT Warwick, in the year 1263). His lordship made his will in 1268,
2 CONT the year in which he died. Besides the daus. mentioned above
2 CONT [there are no daughters named in this article], Lord Beauchamp
2 CONT left four sons, viz., William; John, of Holt, co. Worcester;
2 CONT Walter, of Powyke and Alcester; Thomas, d. s. p. [Sir Bernard
2 CONT Burke, Dormant and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd.,
2 CONT London, 1883, p. 30, Beauchamp, Earls of Warwick]
1 NOTE     WD 7 JAN 1268; FGRA
