1 NOTE William de Beauchamp, who inherited not only the feudal barony of Elmlyfrom his father, but had previously derived from his mother the Earldomof Warwick and the barony of Hameslape from the de Maudits. He marriedMaud, one of the d
2 CONC aughters and co-heirs of Richard FitzJohn, son of JohnFitzGeoffrey, Chief Justice of Ireland, and had Guy and five daughters:Isabel, Maud, Margaret, Anne and Amy. He died 1298 and was first Earl ofWarwick of the Beauchamp family, 
2 CONC having previous to his mother's deathused the style and title of Earl of Warwick.
