2 CONT WALTER de Beauchamp of Alcester (-after 7 Jan 1269).  "Willelmus de Bello Campo" granted "totum manerium meum de la Holte…cum advocatione ecclesie eiusdem" to "Johanni filio meo", with default to "Waltero fratri suo minori", by ch
2 CONC arter dated to [1258/69][972].  "Walterus filius Willelmi de Bello Campo" issued a quitclaim relating to "terra…in Schirrevelench" granted to him by his father by charter dated to [1259/69], witnessed by "Jacobo de Bello Campo…"[9
2 CONC 73].  The will of "William de Beauchamp", dated 7 Jan 1268, bequeathed property to "Walter my son...Joane my daughter...Isabel my daughter...Sibill my daughter...Sarah my daughter...William my eldest son...my daughter the countess
2 CONC  his wife...Isabel my wife..."[974].  same person as...?  WALTER de Beauchamp .  m ALICE de Tosny, daughter of RAOUL [VI] de Tosny & his wife Pernel de Lacy.  Pope Nicholas IV granted dispensation to “Walter de Bello Campo” and “A
2 CONC lice daughter of Ralph de Tonny to remain in the marriage they contracted in ignorance that they were related in the fourth degree of kindred”, and declared “their offspring legitimate”, dated 23 Sep 1289[975].
2 CONT
2 CONT =----------------------------------------=
2 CONT Note: The wife of Walter de Beauchamp of Elmley was '''Alice de Tosny (b. bef 1239), daughter of Raoul VI de Tosny & his wife Pernel de Lacy.'''  Charles Cawley [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3T-Z.htm#Alic
2 CONC eTosnyMWalterBeauchamp] notes that "Pope Nicholas IV granted dispensation to 'Walter de Bello Campo' and 'Alice daughter of Ralph de Tonny to remain in the marriage they contracted in ignorance that they were related in the fourth
2 CONC  degree of kindred”, and declared 'their offspring legitimate, dated 23 Sep 1289 [Bliss (1893), Vol. I, p. 503. 
2 CONT
2 CONT However, various sites have confused her with a possible niece Alice de Tosny possibly born c. 1254, possible daughter of her brother Roger VI and his wife Alice de Bohun, OR with her grandniece Alice de Tosny (aka de Toeni) b. 12
2 CONC 84, daughter of Ralph VII de Tosny, who married Sir Thomas Leybourne, Guy de Beauchamp Earl of Warwick, and William la Zouche de Mortimer.
2 CONT
