2 CONT *'''     Sir Walter de Beauchamp, Constable of Gloucester Castle Steward of Household of King Edward I. He was born before 1242 at of Beauchamp's Court, Alcester, Warwickshire, England; Of age in 1263.2,4,7 A settlement for the ma
2 CONC rriage Sir Walter de Beauchamp, Constable of Gloucester Castle and Alice de Tony was made in 1269; They had 7 sons (Sir Walter; John; Sir William; Humphrey, a cleric; Ralph; Giles; & Roger) and 4 daughters (Pernel; Eleanor; Margar
2 CONC et, wife of Sir Robert, 1st Lord Lisle of Rougemont; & Maud, Abbess of Godstow Abbey in Oxfordshire).2,12,4,13,5,6,7,8 Sir Walter de Beauchamp, Constable of Gloucester Castle and Alice de Tony obtained a marriage license in 1289; 
2 CONC Dispensation to remain in marriage, they being related in the 4th degree of kindred.2,3,7 Sir Walter de Beauchamp, Constable of Gloucester Castle died on 16 February 1303 at Chalfont, Buckinghamshire, England.2,4,7 He was buried o
2 CONC n 24 February 1303 at Grey Friars, Smithfield, Middlesex, England.4,7
