2 CONT Birth*	Sir Richard Talbot M.P. was born circa 1305.1,5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc*	Was taken in arms against the King with his father. On 13 March 1322 at Battle of Boroughbridge.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage*	He married Elizabeth Comyn, daughter of John Comyn and Joan de Valence, between 24 July 1326 and 23 March 1327.1,6,7,8 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	Had letters of protection, being ready to cross the sea with the King. On 14 April 1329.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	Summoned to parliament by writ directed Ricardo Talbot between 27 January 1332 and 20 September 1355.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	Joined Edward Balliol in his invasion of Scotland, contrary to the King's orders, and was present at the defeat of the Scots by the "disinherited lords" at Dupplin Moor . On 12 August 1332 at Dupplin Moor, Scone, Scotla
2 CONC nd.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	Sat as "dominus de Mar" in the Parliament held by Edward balliol and, as such, witnessed the treat of Newcastle, whereby Balliol surrendered Berwick, Roxburgh, etc, to Edward III, having previously received of Balliol a
2 CONC  conditional grant of Kildrummy Castle, Aberdeen, 17 Feb. On 10 February 1334 at Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	Was captured by the Scots and impresoned at Dumbarton; but after leaving hostages for his ransom of £2000, was brough south to the Marches under safe conduct from Edward III (2 Apr 1335). In September 1334 at Linlithgow
2 CONC , Scotland.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	Keeper of Berwick-upon-Tweed and Justiciar of the lands in Scotland occupied by the King of England. On 21 December 1337 at Berwick-upon-Tweed, Northumberland, England.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was appointed keeper of Southampton. On 23 February 1340 at Southampton, Hampshire, England.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He served at the siege of Tournay. In July 1340 at Tournay, France.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was a captain in the army of Sir William de Bohun which defeated Charles of Blois at Morlaix, when he took prisoner Geoffrey de Charny, one of the French leaders, and sent him to his castle at Goodrich, Hereford. On 
2 CONC 30 September 1342 at Morlaix, France.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He was Steward of the King's household. In May 1345.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	Although wounded earlier near the Seine, he was with the King at the battle of Crecy and at Calais. On 26 August 1346.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc	He had a license to found the priory of Austin Canons at Flanesford within the Lordship of Castle Goodrich. On 18 December 1346 at Flanesford Priory, Herefordshire, England.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death*	He died on 23 October 1356.1,6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial*	He was buried at Flanesford Priory, Herefordshire, England.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT Title*	He held the title of 2nd Lord Talbot.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family	Elizabeth Comyn b. 1 November 1299, d. 20 November 1372
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage*	He married Elizabeth Comyn, daughter of John Comyn and Joan de Valence, between 24 July 1326 and 23 March 1327.1,6,7,8 
