1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173392255932 (September 25, 2018; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter & coheir of Sir Payne de Tuberville. Her elder brothers Gilbert & Richard failed to leave any surviving issue, so the 4 sisters; Katherine, Margaret, Agnes & Sarah inherited the de Turberville lands. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is unlikely that Catherine died as early as 1325 as her surviving children were born in about 1339 [Lawrence] & 1332 [Gwenllian]. Her effigy is not dated, but her husband is known to have died 1351.
2 CONT
2 CONT  www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Katherine de Turberville de Berkerolles BIRTH	1300 Bridgend, Bridgend, Wales DEATH	unknown Barry, Vale of Glamorgan, Wales BURIAL	 Church of St Athan Barry, Vale of Glamorgan, Wales  MEMORIAL ID	100117284
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine was the eldest daughter of Payne de Turberville and Gwenllian, daughter of Richard Talbot and Sarah de Beauchamp. Katherine was a decendant of Payn "the Demon" de Tuberville one of the legendary Twelve Knights of Glamorg
2 CONC an supposed to have conquered Glamorgan under the leadership of Robert FitzHamon She married Sir Roger Berkerolles. They were the parents of at least four children: Gwenllian Berkerolles was born 1332. Sarah Berkerolles was born 1
2 CONC 336 in Bassaleg, Monmouthshire, Wales. Sir Lawrence Berkerolles Knight was born 1339 and died 18 Oct 1411. Gilbert Berkerolles was born 1342 in Bassaleg, Monmouthshire, Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents Pain de Turberville unknown–1318
