2 DATE 1216
2 ADDR
3 CITY Galway
3 CTRY Ireland
1 OCCU 1140 ALTB. BLAGDON SOMERSET?
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baron William Fitzmartin, son of Robert Fitzmartin and Alice de Nonant, was born in 1135 in Dartingham, Devonshire England. Also known as "William fitz Robert FitzMartin."
2 CONT
2 CONT "He held, as son of Robert son of Martin, 5 knight's fees, which had formerly been held by William son of Walter; but at the same time the Bishop of Bath returned Robert son of Martin as still tenant, implying William, Robert's he
2 CONC ir, was still a minor in 1166.3 He granted a messuage and land in the manor of Blagdon to the canons of St. Augustine's between 1170 and 1183 in Bristol, Gloucesteshire, England.2 He occurs in the Pipe Rolls from 1176 to the time 
2 CONC of King John." (My Lines )
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Angharad Griffydd (or Angaharad Verch Rhys - b. 1140/1150 in in Llandilo, Carmarthenshire, Wales) and had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     *
2 CONT
2 CONT       WILLIAM MARTIN b: 1160 in BLAGDON, SOMERSETSHIRE
2 CONT
2 CONT     *
2 CONT
2 CONT       Sir OLIVER MARTIN b: 1165 in Darlington House, England
2 CONT
2 CONT     *
2 CONT
2 CONT       DAVID MARTIN b: ABT 1163
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad was the daughter of Rhys ap Gruffydd, Prince of Wales and Gwenllian verch Madog o Powys.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron William also held the title of Lord. He died in 1216. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  Baron William FitzMartin (3), b-ca 1125 at Dartingham in Devon- shire, d-ca 1216.  He lived during the reign of both Henry II and Richard I and was a man of considerable importance.  He married Angharad Griffydd, d/o Rhys Ap Grif
2 CONC id (Griffydd) who was Prince of South Wales.  Three children.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Baron William Fitzmartin, son of Robert Fitzmartin and Alice de Nonant, was born in 1135 in Dartingham, Devonshire England. Also known as "William fitz Robert FitzMartin."
2 CONT
2 CONT "He held, as son of Robert son of Martin, 5 knight's fees, which had formerly been held by William son of Walter; but at the same time the Bishop of Bath returned Robert son of Martin as still tenant, implying William, Robert's he
2 CONC ir, was still a minor in 1166.3 He granted a messuage and land in the manor of Blagdon to the canons of St. Augustine's between 1170 and 1183 in Bristol, Gloucesteshire, England.2 He occurs in the Pipe Rolls from 1176 to the time 
2 CONC of King John." (My Lines )
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Angharad Griffydd (or Angaharad Verch Rhys - b. 1140/1150 in in Llandilo, Carmarthenshire, Wales) and had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM MARTIN b: 1160 in BLAGDON, SOMERSETSHIRE
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir OLIVER MARTIN b: 1165 in Darlington House, England
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT DAVID MARTIN b: ABT 1163
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad was the daughter of Rhys ap Gruffydd, Prince of Wales and Gwenllian verch Madog o Powys.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron William also held the title of Lord. He died in 1216. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron William FitzMartin (3), b-ca 1125 at Dartingham in Devon-
2 CONT
2 CONT shire, d-ca 1216. He lived during the reign of both Henry II and Richard I and was a man of considerable importance. He married Angharad Griffydd, d/o Rhys Ap Grifid (Griffydd) who was Prince of South Wales. Three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Children of Lord Rhys; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id187.html. (Steven Ferry, September 15, 2020.
