2 CONT Please see Peter Bartrum: Llywarch ap Bran 8; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173393115868 [NOTE: Bartrum charts Einion ap Llywarch as a son of Llywarch ap Bran, while Darrell Wolcott makes him a grandson of Owai
2 CONC n ap Idnerth found in Elystan Glodrydd 49; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173390904845. His reasoning is: "Several things led me to making this correction. First, there seemed to be an early tendency by some wri
2 CONC ters to add "ap Bran" to any Llywarch, much like those who wanted to add "ap Cynfyn" to any Bleddyn.  All the folks Bartrum charted as descending from this Einion ap Llywarch lived in the Brychieniog/Glamorgan area.  There was no 
2 CONC gwely in 1352 in Anglesey for any Einion ap Llywarch as there were for Llywarch ap Bran's sons Iorwerth, Cadwgan and Madog.  Griffith's Pedigrees of Anglesey, etc give no son named Einion to Llywarch ap Bran.  Williams' "Biologica
2 CONC l Dictionary of Eminent Welshmen" also gives him no such son.   I don't recall what factors led me to attach this Einion ap Llywarch to Owain ap Idnerth, but it is consistent with the timeline and the geography of the family."] (S
2 CONC teven Ferry, April 13, 2024.) [NOTE: Wolcott now connects Llywarch to Ednyfed ap Idnerth; S.F. 2/12/25]
