2 CONT At Medlands, he is listed as one of Madog'sthree illegitimate children by unknown mistresses: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WALES.htm#MararedMIorwerthDrwyndwyn
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Owain Brogyntyn, according to Welsh Biography Online, [accessed 3/11/2013] , author Professor Thomas Jones Pierce M.A. F.S.A. (1905-1964), Aberystwyth - Owain Brogyntyn (fl.1160-1188) was a Prince of Powys.  The natural son of Mad
2 CONC og ap Maredudd, the last king of Powys. He left three sons, Bleddyn, Iorwerth and Gruffydd by Margaret, daughter of Einion ap Seisyll of Mathafarn. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Courtesy of fantastically full family tree cf.:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hughes of Gwerclas 1/2/3/4:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_2.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_3.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_4.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT # 12711-Welsh Medieval database. Owain died after 1215.
2 CONT
2 CONT KINSHIP Illegitimate son- Source- Dwnn, Heraldic Visitations of Wales (vol 2, page 109)
2 CONT
2 CONT DISTINCTION: Esquire Source- Dunn's Heraldic etc (vol2 page 124)
2 CONT
2 CONT LIVING Flourished 1160-1188 1215- He together with his sons , Cadogen and Hywel, were witnesses to a deed from Owain de Brithdir, confirming the monks of Strata Florida (Ystrad Fflur), all their lands in Arwstyll. Source-History o
2 CONC f the Princes, the Lords Marches and the Ancient Nobility of Powys Fadog. (vol1, pages 125/6)
2 CONT
2 CONT RESIDENCE-He is said to have resided at Porkington, in Welsh Brogyntyn, Shropshire. Source-Dunn's Heraldic etc (Vol 2 , page 109, fn 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT RESIDENCE-He resided in Brogyntyn,near Oswestry. Source- Lloyd. History of the Princes etc.(Vol 1-page 125)
2 CONT
2 CONT PROPERTY-Lord of Dinmael and Edeirnion, Source- Lloyd, History of the Princes etc (vol 4 page 341.
2 CONT
2 CONT PROPERTY-He was given the commote of Dinmael by his father Maredudd. Source-Lloyd, History of the Princes etc. (vol 6-page 56)
2 CONT
2 CONT PROPERTY-He seems to have succeeded his half-brother Elise to Edeirnion in a deposition in 1202. Source-Lloyd, History of the Princes etc.(vol 6-page 56)
2 CONT
2 CONT PROPERTY- He gave to the monks of Basingwerk Abbey, the ville or township of Wenhewm, also of certain water in Penthlin ,called Thlinlegid,and all the pasture of the said land of Penthlin. This was witnessed by Reyner, who was Bis
2 CONC hop of St. Asaph (Llanelwy) from 1186 to 1224,and by Ithel Owain's chaplain. Source- Lloyd, The History of the Princes etc (Vol 6-page 134)
2 CONT
2 CONT CONFLICT-Lloyd, The History of the Princes etc.,(vol1-page126 andVol 6 -page 56) states that their was no issue from his marriage
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Owain Brogyntyn ap Madog (fl. 1186) was the youngest and illegitimate son of king Madog ap Maredudd, the last king of a united kingdom of Powys. He was the son of Madog by the daughter of the Maer du or "black mayor" of Rûg in Ede
2 CONC yrnion. He was the brother of Gruffydd Maelor the ancestor of Owain Glyndŵr. Presumably Owain Brogyntyn would have been raised by his mother at Rûg in Edeyrnion. He was acknowledged by his father and granted by him the lordship of
2 CONC  Edeyrnion and also Dinmael. It is quite possible that he inherited some of these lands through his maternal grandfather, the Maer Du, which were confirmed and perhaps extended by his father the king of Powys. At some point he als
2 CONC o came into possession of Castle Brogyntyn on the English borders at Selattyn close to Oswestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Owain first married Jonet verch Hywel (whose ancestor was Athelstan Glodrudd of the Fifth Royal Tribe) but with her had no children. He next married Marred ferch Einion ap Seisyllt who was to be the mother of his three sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT His youngest son, Iorwerth ab Owain Brogyntyn, married Efa verch Madoc the sole heir of Madoc, Lord of Mawddwy (the younger son of Gwenwynwyn, prince of Powys Wenwynwyn). The son of Iorwerth and Efa, Gruffudd ab Iorwerth, was conf
2 CONC irmed in his lands as Baron of Edeyrnion by Edward I under the terms of the Statute of Rhuddlan by which England organised the subjugation of Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Philip York writing in 1799 a cup and a dagger belonging to Owain Brogyntyn were preserved at Rûg in Edeyrnion. Later accounts in the National Gazetteer dated 1868 state that a cup and dagger in the possession of "Col
2 CONC onel Vaughan of Rhug" were once owned by another Owain of Powys, the much later Owain Glyndŵr. These objects, whoever the original owner, may now be lost.
2 CONT
2 CONT The direct patrilineal descendants of Iorwerth ab Owain Brogyntyn survived at least until the beginning of the 20th century and are known to genealogy as the Hughes of Gwerclas family.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT OWAIN BROGYNTYN ( fl. 1160-1188 ), prince of Powys . He was a natural son of Madog ap Maredudd (q.v.) , the last king of Powys . Brought up at Porkington , near Oswestry ( Madog held the lordship of Oswestry from 1149 to 1157 ), a
2 CONC  township known among the Welsh as Brogyntyn , he appears to have continued on very good terms with Henry II after his father's death in 1160 , for he is recorded as being a royal pensioner as late as 1169 . He was still alive in 
2 CONC 1188 holding lands in Edeirnion and Dinmael where his descendants are found in occupation until well after the Edwardian conquest . He left three sons, Bleddyn , Iorwerth , and Gruffydd , by Margaret , daughter of Einion ap Seisyl
2 CONC l of Mathafarn . Bibliography:
2 CONT
2 CONT A History of Wales ; Oxford Dictionary of National Biography Author:
2 CONT
2 CONT Professor Thomas Jones Pierce, M.A., F.S.A., (1905-1964), Aberystwyth
2 CONT
2 CONT Source; http://yba.llgc.org.uk/en/s-OWAI-BRO-1160.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Owain Brogyntjn became lord of Edeymion in 1202.
