1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT ''Updated 17 September 2023''
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Montagu-56 and then edited. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William de Montagu was born circa 1213. He was of Shepton Montague, Donyatt, Goathill, Thurlbear, & Chedzoy, Somersetshire, England. Keats-Rohan reports that he succeeded his grandfather as a minor in 1217.[1] Complete Peerage
2 CONC  reports he was still under-age in 1227.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Bertha circa 1233; They had 1 son (Sir Simon) & 1 daughter (Hawise, wife of Geoffrey de Neville).[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William de Montagu died circa 23 September 1270.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir William de Motacute had summons to attend the King into Gascony, against Alphonse 10th, King of Castile, who had usurped the province. The 41st of Henry III he was summoned to be with the King at Chester on the feast day of S
2 CONC t. Peter, well furnished with horse and arms, thence to march against Llewellin ap Griffith prince of Wales. 42d of Henry III he had a similar citation."[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Berthe and William de Montagu:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Hawise de Montagu b. c 1242, d. a 14 Feb 1273.  Married Geoffrey Neville.  
2 CONT # Sir Simon de Montagu, b. a 1249, d. 26 Sep 1316.  1st Lord Montagu, Custodian of Corfe & Beaumaris Castles, Captain & Governor of the Fleet.  Married 1)  Hawise de St. Armand 2) Isabel 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT < [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3L-O.htm#SimonMontagudied1316A MedLands] > “ ENGLISH LORDS L - O -  MONTAGU.” v4.6 Updated 03 December 2022
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       DREUX de Montagu (-before 1216) … m as her first husband, ALINE Basset, daughter of ALAN Basset of Wycombe & his second wife Aline de Gai.  … She married secondly ([1219/24]) Richard [V] Talbot.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Dreux & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)       '''WILLIAM de Montagu''' ([1213]-23 Sep 1270).  The Testa de Nevill includes a list of landholdings in Somerset, dated 1219, which includes "Willelmus filius Drogonis filii Willelmi de Monte Acuto est in custodia Alani B
2 CONC asset et terra sua de Turelberiz valet vi.l"[358].  … [360].  m '''BERTHE''', daughter of --.  
2 CONT
2 CONT William & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a.         SIMON de Montagu (after 1250-26 Sep 1316, bur Bruton Priory).  Confirmation of charters in favour of the canons of Christchurch Twynham, dated 27 Nov 1313, includes a charter under which "Simon de Monte Acuto, son and h
2 CONC eir of William de Monte Acuto" confirmed a conveyance made by "William de Monte Acuto" of the town of Pideleton, for the souls of "William his father, and Hawise wife of the said Simon" dated May 1287[361]. m firstly ([1270]) HAWI
2 CONC SE de Saint-Amand, m secondly (1287 or before) ISABEL, daughter of -(-after 1290). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-533734
2 CONT
2 CONT The Feet of Fines relating to the county of Dorset, --:” edited by Edward A. Fry and George S. Fry, published 1896.
2 CONT
2 CONT >The Dorset fine dated 1289-1290 [pages 249/50] defines that the Abbot of Bynedon held lands in the manor of Westlullesworth of Simon Montague at the same terms as the fine dated 1257-1258. Therefore confirms that Berca was the mo
2 CONC ther of Simon Montague.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
