1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMAS Basset [I] of Headington, Oxfordshire (-after [1180/82]).  The Red Book of the Exchequer refers to "Thomas Basset" in Oxfordshire in [1171/72][264].  m ALICE de Dunstanville, daughter of [ALAN de Dunstanville & his wife ---
2 CONC ] (-after 1186). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas [I] & his wife had [four] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GILBERT Basset [I] (-[1205/06]).  "Thomas Basset", with the consent of "Gilleberti primogeni filii mei", granted "Cumtonam…cuius medietas fuit maritagium matris mee, altera…medietatis…fuit maritagium uxoris mee matris e
2 CONC orum" to "Alano filio meo fratri suo" by charter dated to [1180/82?], witnessed by "…Walterus de Dunstanvill, Alanus de Dunstanvill, Fulco Basset…Thomas Basset juvenis…"[267].  ... m AIGELINE de Courtenay, daughter of RENAUD de Co
2 CONC urtenay & his second wife Hawise d’Avranches (-after 1219). 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         THOMAS Basset [II] of Headington, Oxfordshire (-1220).  "Thomas Bass" granted "manerium meum de Comptun cum terra de Berewic" to "Alano filio meo" by charter dated to [1180/82?], witnessed by "…Waltero de Dunstanvile, A
2 CONC lano de Dunstanvile, Fulcone Basset…Thoma Basset juvene…"[285].  Thomas was most likely his parents’ second son, as shown by the order of witness names in the charter dated to [1180/1205] under which [his brother] "Gillebertus Bas
2 CONC set" confirmed land at Cowley to "Waltero filio Tostani de Coveleia", witnessed by "Toma Basset, Alano Basset…"[286].  ... Thomas Basset” among the "consiliarios iniquissimos” of King John[288].  m PHILIPPA, daughter of WILLIAM Fi
2 CONC tzHugh Malbank & his wife ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         ALAN Basset (-1231).  "Thomas Bass" granted "manerium meum de Comptun cum terra de Berewic" to "Alano filio meo" by charter dated to [1180/82?], witnessed by "…Waltero de Dunstanvile, Alano de Dunstanvile, Fulcone Basse
2 CONC t…Thoma Basset juvene…"[299]. 
2 CONT -        see below www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice (Adelize) Dunstanville Basset BIRTH	1138 Castle Combe, Wiltshire Unitary Authority, Wiltshire, England DEATH	1210 (aged 71–72) Wallingford, South Oxfordshire District, Oxfordshire, England BURIAL	 Saint Peter's Churchyard Wa
2 CONC llingford, South Oxfordshire District, Oxfordshire, England  MEMORIAL ID	103035985
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Thomas Basset, who was the son of Gilbert Basset, Lord of Drayton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Gilbert Basset born 1154 in Oxfordshire, who married Aigeline de Courtenay, daughter of Renauld (Reginald) de Courtenay.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents Alan De Dunstanville 1080–1150
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Thomas Basset 1125–1182
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings Alan De Dunstanville 1104–1200
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter De Dunstanville
2 CONT
2 CONT d) '''ISABEL Basset''' .  The 1181/82 Pipe Roll records "Wido de Creon" accounting "pro habenda uxore que fuit Alberti Gresle" in Lincolnshire[422].  A genealogy of the founders of Freston Priory records that "monsieur Wythe de Cr
2 CONC oune" married "une Isabelle"[423]. 
2 CONT
