1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Previous information stated that William de Lanvaley married Maud Pecche; that information comes from web trees, with the source unclear.  According to the "The Magna Carta Sureties, 1215," from the Genealogical Pu
2 CONC blishing Co., Inc., he married one of the daughters (first name unknown) of Alan Bassett, who is named in the Magna Carta. (April 3, 2016, Anne Brannen, curator.)
2 CONT
2 CONT *********************
2 CONT
2 CONT ==William de Lanvallei==
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms of William de Lanvallei, Lord of Standway Castle
2 CONT William de Lanvallei III (died 1217) was an English landowner, governor of Colchester Castle, and a Magna Carta surety.[1] He was lord of Walkern.[2] William III accompanied King John of England on his expedition to Poitou in 1214
2 CONC  and was present at the truce. William III was related to several of the Magna Carta barons.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT William III's grandfather, William I (1125-1180), was an administrator for Henry II of England and came to England from Brittany. William I married Gunnora, the daughter of Hubert de Saint Clair (1120-1155).
2 CONT
2 CONT William II (c.1161-1204), son of William I, married Hawise, great-granddaughter of Hugh de Bocland (Buckland, Oxfordshire).[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT William III, son of William II, married Maud, daughter of Gilbert (Hamon) Peche.[1][4] Maud was niece of Robert Fitzwalter, a leader of the Magna Carta barons.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hawise, daughter of William III, was placed as ward with Hubert de Burgh . Hubert married Hawise to his son, John.[1][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT # http://www.sinclairgenealogy.info/lanvalei-family
2 CONT # http://www.oxforddnb.com
2 CONT # http://www.magnacartabarons.info/william-de-lanvalei
2 CONT # http://www.walkernhistorysociety.co.uk
2 CONT
