2 CONT B. BEAUCHAMP of ELMLEY, WORCESTERSHIRE
2 CONT
2 CONT William [II] (d. 1197) his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *2.         WALTER [III] de Beauchamp ([1195/97]-14 Apr 1236).  The Red Book of the Exchequer records "Walterus de Bello Campo" holding 207 knights’ fees "in Uptone, Stanes, Graftone, Ayntone, Chedeleswale, Kokesaye, Benetlega, Pa
2 CONC ncevot, Bouresdale, Costone, Dunclere" in Worcestershire in [1210/12][553].  He is named “Watekin” in the 10 Jul 1214 document cited below under his first wife.  The Annals of Worcester record the death “die Sancti Guthlaci” in 12
2 CONC 35 of “Walterus de Bello Campo”[554].  The Annals of Tewkesbury record the death “XVIII Kal Mai” in 1236 of “W de Bellocampo”[555].  
2 CONT **m firstly (after 10 Jul 1214) JOAN Mortimer, daughter of ROGER [III] de Mortimer & his [second] wife Isabel de Ferrers (-1225).  King John requested the bishop of Winchester to enquire into the marriage of “Watekini de Bello Cam
2 CONC po” and “Rogerus de Mortuo Mari...filie sue”, dated 10 Jul 1214[556].  The Annals of Worcester record that “Rogerus de Mortuo Mari…filiam suam” married “Waltero de Bello Campo”[557].  The Annals of Worcester record the death in 12
2 CONC 25 of “Johanna de Mortuo Mari uxor Willelmi de Bello Campo”[558]. Walter [III] & his first wife had one/ two children:
2 CONT *** a)         WILLIAM [IV] de Beauchamp (-[7 Jan/21 Apr] 1269, bur Worcester Franciscan Church). … m ISABEL Mauduit, daughter of WILLIAM [IV] Mauduit of Hanslope, Berkshire & his wife Alice of Warwick (-after 7 Jan 1269). 
2 CONT *** b)         JAMES de Beauchamp (-[late Sep/early Oct] 1296). The introduction to the Beauchamp Cartulary indicates that Walter [III]’s wife Joan was probably the mother of his son James[589]. 
2 CONT ** m secondly ANGHARAD, daughter of --- (-[1280/83]).  The introduction to the Beauchamp Cartulary records that "Angaret" was the mother of Walter [II]’s son Hugh, and suggests that she may also have been the mother of his sons Th
2 CONC omas, Walter and John[559].  Her parentage is not known, but her name indicates Welsh origin.  A lay subsidy roll for Worcester dated [1280] records "Domina Augereta de Bello Campo" in Bengeworth[560].   Walter [III] & his [first/
2 CONC second] wife had three children: 
2 CONT ***c)         THOMAS de Beauchamp (-before 1283). …
2 CONT *** d)         WALTER de Beauchamp (-before 1283) …
2 CONT *** e)         JOHN de Beauchamp (-before 1283).  …
2 CONT ** Walter [III] & his second wife had one child: 
2 CONT ***f)          HUGH de Beauchamp (-after 1283)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
