1 NOTE {geni:about_me} For marriage to Angharad verch Gruffudd, see Peter Bartrum, http://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5573/Bleddyn%20ap%20Cynfyn%204.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (December 26, 2016; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONC  _____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Vital Statistics'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Ralph le Boteler and Maud (Matilda) Pantulf, daughter and heiress of Wemme which is how the le Boteler became Barons of Wemme
2 CONT * William in the lifetime of his father married Ankaret, niece of James de Aidithley according to one of the more reliable peerage sources
2 CONT * Died in 1283 only a few years after inheriting his paternal property.
2 CONT * Left three (3) sons in order of birth: (1) John, (2) Gawine (3) William.   John and Gawine died very young and William (this William's son) inherited third after the decease of first John and then Gawine, and had a long tenure a
2 CONC s Baron of Oversley and Wemme and left at least 7 children 
2 CONT * The identity of this William's wife needs to be confirmed since the reliable source thinks it was his son who married Ankeret, daughter of Griffin.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources and Notes (some contradictory)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Name Variation	Sir William le Boteler of Wem was also styled William le Botiler.4  Marriage License*	He and Ankaret verch Griffith obtained a marriage license on 2 October 1261.1,3  Event-Misc	He was one of two knights serving for
2 CONC  Ralph le Boteler against Llywelyn on 1 July 1277.2,3  Event-Misc	He has done homage for Lopinton Manor on 10 January 1278.2  Event-Misc	Serves as a knight for his mother, Matilda de Pantulf in 1282.2  Summoned	He was summoned to 
2 CONC Parliament on 30 September 1283 at Shrewsbury.2  Death*	He died | holding, jointling with his wife Ingareta, Northbury Manor, Leic., by gift of his father and monther, 9 Ed. I, also lands at Dudinton and Lopinton, Salop, Ouersley 
2 CONC Manor and lands at Kingesbrome, Warw., and lands at Brensaghe, Wilts., and left wid. Angareta, to whom dower, and s. h. John, 17, the last being his Exor. Before 11 December 1283.2,3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family	Ankaret verch Griffith b. circa 1248, d. after 22 June 1308 Marriage License*	He and Ankaret verch Griffith obtained a marriage license on 2 October 1261.1,3  Children	 Anne le Boteler John le Boteler b. 17 Jul 1266, d. b 4
2 CONC  Sep 1287 Gawain le Boteler b. 2 Feb 1269/70, d. b 3 Mar 1289/90 Sir William le Boteler of Wem b. 11 Jun 1274, d. b 14 Sep 1334
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited	5 Feb 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations	 [S284] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, Blackmere 7. [S325] Rev. C. Moor, Knights of Edward I, v. 1, p. 121. [S301] Carl Boyer 3rd, Medieval English Ancestors of Robert Abell, p. 33. [S168] Frederick Lewis Weis
2 CONC , Ancestral Roots, 84A-30.
2 CONT
