1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Boteler, who in the 24th year of Edward I was in ward to Walter de Langton, lord treasurer of England, and Walter de Beauchamp, of Alcester, steward of the king's household.  This feudal lord obtaining reno
2 CONC wn in the Scottish wars of the period, was summoned to parliament as a Baron from 10 March 130_ to 10 October 1325.  His lordship married 1st Ankeret, daughter of Griffin, and had an only son, William, his successor.  He married E
2 CONC la, daughter and co-heiress of Roger de Herdeburgh, by whom he had two sons, Edmund and Edward, who both died issueless, and four daughters: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Ankeret, daughter of Griffin:
2 CONT ># William, eldest son and heir and successor
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Ela de Herdeburgh
2 CONT ># Edmund, died issueless
2 CONT ># Edward, died issueless
2 CONT ># Ankeret married to John le Strange, of Black mere
2 CONT ># Ida, married to Wm Tnusell
2 CONT ># Alice married to Nicholas STANDFORD
2 CONT ># Dionysa, married to Hugh de Cokesey
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1334 and was succeeded by his eldest son, William Boteler, 2nd Baron Boteler, of Wemme, but never summoned to parliament. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William 1st Baron did NOT marry a Beatrice
2 CONT
2 CONT He md 1 Ankaret daughter of Griffin and 2 Ela 
2 CONT
2 CONT ************
2 CONT
2 CONT William Bóteler, who, in the 24th Edward I., was In ward to Walter de Langton, lord treasurer of England, and Walter de Beauchamp, of Alcester, steward of the king's household. This feudal lord obtaining renown in the Scottish war
2 CONC s of the period, was summoned to parliament as a baron from 10 March, 1308, to 10 October, 1325.
2 CONT
2 CONT  His lordship m. 1st, Ankeret, dau. of Griffin. and had an only son, William, his successor. He m. 2ndly, Ela, dau. and co-heiress of Roger de Herdeburgh, by whom he had two sons, Edmund and Edward, who both died issueless, and fo
2 CONC ur daus., viz.,
2 CONT
2 CONT Ankeret m. to John Le Strange, of Blackmere.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ida, w. to Wm. Trussell
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice, m. to Nicholas Langford
2 CONT
2 CONT Dionyse, m. to Hugh de Cokesey.
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. in 1334, 
2 CONT
2 CONT This information is according to:
2 CONT
2 CONT "The history of Wem: and [other] ... townships [in Shropshire]" By Samuel Garbett pp 31-40
2 CONT
2 CONT "A genealogical history of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited, and extinct Peerages of the British Empire" by Sir Bernard Burke p. 63
2 CONT
2 CONT both found at Google books online complete and free
2 CONT
