1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nntpnews.net/f5043/c-p-addition-correction-guy-de-bryan-k-g-lord-bryan-his-1stwife-joan-de-carew-6528092/
2 CONT
2 CONT In summary, it appears that Sir Guy de Bryan was born say 1309, he being in arms in 1327 and stated to be of age in 1330. His first wife, Joan, was living 12 April 1348. It is Nicolas' supposition and my own that Joan was the daug
2 CONC hter of John de Carew, Knt., of Carew, Pembrokeshire, by his wife, Joan. As indicated above, Guy de Bryan's marriage was held by Lady Joan de Carew, and he occurs occurs together with Lady Carew in records in 1330, 1341, and 1342.
2 CONC  On the last date, Lady Joan de Carew released her life estate to her land holdings at Clifton, Dartmouth and Hardness, Devon to him. Sir Guy de Bryan was still in possession of this property as late as 1376-1377.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Guy de Bryan and his first wife, Joan de Carew, were the parents of at least two, possibly three daughters. There are living descendants through their daughter, Elizabeth de Bryan, who married Robert Fitz Payn (formerly de Gre
2 CONC y), Knt., of Stogursey, Bridghampton, Cheddon Fitzpaine, Rodway, etc., Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # ''The complete peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom : extant, extinct, or dormant''.  by Cokayne, George E. Vol 2, page 361-2. < [https://archive.org/details/completepeerageo02coka/page/36
2 CONC 0/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] >  “BRYAN or BRIENE.” (Joan Carew is not mentioned, a first wife for Guy de Bryan is inferred)
2 CONT # Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 201.< [https://archive.org/details/completepeerageo02coka/page/201/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] > BOHUN  (b) Their ist s., Edward, m. Philippe (da. of Sir Guy de B
2 CONC rian) and d. s.p. and v.p. Jan. 1 361/2, leaving John his next br. and h., aged 26 and more (Ch. Inq. p. m., Edw. Ill, file 166, no. 24), who also d. s.p. and v.p. Philippe was living 28 July 1368 {Close Roll, 42 Edw. Ill, m. 12).
2 CONT
2 CONT # Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 92-93. < [https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&lpg=PP1&vq=Brionne&pg=PA92#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT
