1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I can find noreliable source showing a Maud or Matilda de Longespee either married to Hugh or not (Terry Jackson Curator 5 Feb 2012) and none either showing her as a daughter of William "Clito" & Giovanna.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following from Medlands suggests that it is impossible that Matilda / Maud de Longespey was married to Hugh de Mortimer:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL2.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh de Mortimer m ([1150]) as her second husband, MATILDA de Rumilly, widow of PHILIP de Belmeis, daughter of WILLIAM FitzRanulf Meschin, of Skipton-in-Craven & his wife Cecily de Rumilly (-after 1189[239]).  The Complete Peerage
2 CONC  explains the the documents which confirm her parentage and second marriage[240]: including (1) pleadings in a suit concerning land at Kimbolton, Hampshire, and in a suit dated Jan 1282 in the Chester County Court, which both name
2 CONC  Roger de Mortimer as son and heir of "Maud la Meschine"[241]; (2) Roger Mortimer´s grant of rents in Bisley given to him by "his brothers Philip and Ranulph de Belmeis"[242]; (3) “Philippus de Belmeis” founding Lilleshall Abbey, 
2 CONC Shropshire by undated charter, witnessed by “Philippus filius Philippi de Belmis…domina Matilda filia Willielmi Meschin uxor prædicti Philippi de Belmis…”[243].  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Wigmore Abbey records that 
2 CONC she was “Matildem Longespey, filiam Willielmi Longespey, ducis Normanniæ”[244] but this is confused and cannot possibly be correct.  The undated charter, under which "Hugo de Mortuo mari" confirmed various donations to Saint-Victo
2 CONC r-en-Caux and other past donations including all donations of property in England "antequam duxissem uxorem"[245], indicates that Hugh married only once.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh & his wife had four children _____________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p53113.htm#i531128
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud de Marshal1  F, #531128 Last Edited=18 Apr 2012
2 CONT      Maud de Marshal married Hugh de Mortimer, 1st and last Lord Mortimer, son of Robert de Mortimer and Joyce la Zouche, before 1290.1
2 CONT      Circa 1305 she was tried for conspiracy to murder someone other than her husband.1 Children of Maud de Marshal and Hugh de Mortimer, 1st and last Lord Mortimer Joan de Mortimer1 b. 24 Nov 1291, d. b 12 Jan 1341/42 Margaret de
2 CONC  Mortimer+1 b. 14 Sep 1295, d. c Dec 1345 Citations [S37] BP2003 volume 3, page 4289. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37] ___________________________________________________________________
