1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Sir Gilbert Talbot, Justice of the Peace for Berkshire & Wiltshire1,2,3,4
2 CONT *''''''M, b. circa 1346, d. 6 February 1399
2 CONT *Father Sir John Talbot5,2,3 b. 29 Sep 1319, d. 20 Sep 1355 
2 CONT *Mother Juliane de Grey5,2,3 d. 29 Nov 1361 or 1 Dec 1361 
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Gilbert Talbot, Justice of the Peace for Berkshire & Wiltshire was born circa 1346 at of Wadley, Hanney, Letcombe Regis, & Wicklesham, Berkshire, England.2,3 He married Joan before 18 November 1383; No issue. Her 4
2 CONC th marriage.3 Sir Gilbert Talbot, Justice of the Peace for Berkshire & Wiltshire married Margaret Howard, daughter of Sir Robert Howard and Margaret Scales, between 13 February 1396 and 31 December 1396; They had 1 son, Richard. H
2 CONC is 3rd marriage.6,2,4 Sir Gilbert Talbot, Justice of the Peace for Berkshire & Wiltshire died on 6 February 1399 at of Richard's Castle, Herefordshire, England.1,6,2,3
2 CONT *''''''Family 1 Joan d. 27 Apr 1392 
2 CONT *''''''Family 2 Margaret Howard d. 25 Mar 1434 
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. III, p. 308.
2 CONT *2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 573.
2 CONT *3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 181-182.
2 CONT *4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 409.
2 CONT *5.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, SLC Archives.
2 CONT *6.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 495.
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1773.htm#i53304
2 CONT *_______
2 CONT *''''''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA436&lpg=PA436&dq=Constantine+De+Clifton+1372&source=bl&ots=2Excuq1G2I&sig=zFLwAqy79bZJ09bqMQTBteZj4p0&hl=en&ei=oBhxTvDKAaLiiALh4NXyBg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=10&ved
2 CONC =0CFIQ6AEwCTgU#v=onepage&q=Constantine%20De%20Clifton%201372&f=false/ Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham]
2 CONT *Pg. 436
2 CONT *   7. MARGARET (or MARGERY) DE SCALES, elder daughter. She married ROBERT HOWARD, Knt, of East Winch, Fersfield, Terrington, and Wiggenhall, etc., Norfolk, son and heir of John HOWARD, Knt., of East Winch and Wiggenhall, Norfolk,
2 CONC  Admiral of the Fleet north of the Thames, by Alice, daughter of Robert de Bois, Knt. He was born about 1342 (age 30 in 1372). They had one son, John, Knt., and one daughter, ''''''Margaret''''''. He was imprisoned in the Tower of
2 CONC  London in 1378-79, for detaining Margery de Nerford from her grandmother, Lady Alice Neville. SIR ROBERT HOWARD died testate at East Winch, Norfolk 18 July 1388. His widow, Margaret, married (2nd) Walter de Bermingham, Knt., of I
2 CONC reland (died before 10 Feb. 1401). She left a will dated 8 May 1416. She was buried with her 1st husband in the south side of the chancel at East Winch, Norfolk.  . . . . . 
2 CONT **Children of Margaret de Scales, by Robert Howard, Knt.:
2 CONT **''''''	ii. MARGARET HOWARD, married after Feb. 1389/90 CONSTANTINE DE CLIFTON, Esq. 2nd Lord Clifton, of Buckenham, Babingley, Hilborough, etc. Norfolk, Little Waltham, Essex, etc., son and heir of John de Clifton, Knt., 1st Lor
2 CONC d Clifton, by Elizabeth, daughter of Ralph de Cromwell, Knt., 1st Lord Cromwell. He was born about 1372 (aged 16 in 1388, aged 19 1/2 in 1391). They had one son, JOhn, Knt. [3rd Lord Clifton], and one daughter, Elizabeth. He was s
2 CONC ummoned to Parliament from 13 Nov. 1393 to 20 Nov. 1394. CONSTANTINE DE CLIFTON, Esq., 2nd Lord Clifton, died 19 Feb 1395/6. His widow, Margaret, married (2nd) (as his 3rd wife) GILBERT TALBOT, Knt., of Richard's Castle, Herefords
2 CONC hire and Wadley, Berkshire (died 6 Feb. 1398/9). They had one son, Richard. She died 25 March 1434, and was buried at Black Friars, Norwich. . . . . . 
2 CONT *____________
2 CONT *''''''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=p_yzpuWi4sgC&pg=PA495&lpg=PA495&dq=Constantine+De+Clifton+1372&source=bl&ots=RRtN2MZ486&sig=GSFmtjXCBkERKUJYQ02f4eZjEsk&hl=en&ei=Gx5xTquwFeXjiALVpKnsBg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ved=
2 CONC 0CDgQ6AEwAzge#v=onepage&q=Constantine%20De%20Clifton%201372&f=false/ Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham]
2 CONT *Pg. 495
2 CONT *   11. CONSTANTINE DE CLIFTON, Esq., 2nd Lord Clifton, of Buckenham, Babingley, Hilborough, etc., Norfolk, Little Waltham, Essex, etc., son and heir, born about 1372 (aged 16 in 1388, aged 19 1/2 in 1391). He married after Feb. 1
2 CONC 389/90 ''''''MARGARET HOWARD, daughter of Robert Howard, Knt., of East Winch, Fersfield, and Wiggenhall, Norfolk (descendant of King John), by Margaret (or Margery), daughter of Robert de Scales, 3rd Lord Scales [see CORNWALL 8 fo
2 CONC r her ancestry]''''''. They had one son, John, Knt. [3rd Lord Clifton], and one daughter, Elizabeth. He was summoned to Parliament from 13 Nov. 1393 to 20 Nov. 1394. CONSTANTINE DE CLIFTON, Esq., 2nd Lord Clifton, died 19 Feb. 139
2 CONC 5/6. ''''''His widow, Margaret, married (2nd) (as his 3rd wife) GILBERT TALBOT, Knt., of Richard's Castle, Herefordshire and Wadley, Berkshire (died 6 Feb 1398/9), They had one son, Richard. She died 25 March 1434, and was buried 
2 CONC at Black Friars, Norwich.'''''' . . . 
2 CONT *__________ Peerage.com & Tudor.com list different parents for Margaret Howard
