1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''Stirnet's "Talbot01" page does not mention this Katherine.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT also seen as '''Joan Talbot''' in The History of Parliament's article on her husband
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * Door Suffolk Institute of Archæology.  ''Proceedings of the Suffolk Institute of Archæology, Volume 2''.  [https://books.google.be/books?id=q-oGAAAAYAAJ&hl=nl&pg=PA414#v=onepage&q&f=false Page 414].
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT I. KATHERINE TALBOT, married (as his 1st wife) before 20 Jan. 1364 (date of fine) RALPH PARLES, Esq., of Shutlanger (in Stoke Bruerne), Watford, and Byfield, Northamptonshire,. They had one daughter, Margery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Katherine Talbot, by Ralph Parles, Esq.:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.	MARGERY PARLES, married (1st) JOHN HERVEY, Esq., of Thurleigh, Colworth, Felmersham, Risely, and Wotton, Bedfordshire, Knight of the
2 CONT
2 CONT * from [http://newsgroups.derkeiler.com/Archive/Soc/soc.genealogy.medieval/2008-05/msg00240.html Katherine Talbot, wife of Ralph Parles, and her daughter, Margery Parles, wife of John Hervey and William Argentine]  May 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas Richardson writes:
2 CONT
2 CONT > .... Thus, it would appear that Ralph Parles first wife was Katherine Talbot, not Joan Talbot, she being a daughter of John Talbot, Knt., of Richard's Castle, Herefordshire, by his wife, Juliane, daughter of Roger de Grey, Knt.,
2 CONC  1st Lord Grey of Ruthin. Katherine Talbot's mother's descent from Geoffrey Plantagenet can be found in my book, Plantagenet Ancestry (2004).
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT Proceedings of the Bury & West Suffolk Archæological Institute 2
2 CONT (1859): 293–425. Wigram, Chronicles of the Abbey of Elstow (1885) (Parles arms: Per pale indented or and azure). Repingdon, Reg. of Philip Repingdon 1 (Lincoln Rec. Soc. 57) (1963): 200. Roskell, House of Commons 1386–1421 4 (1992
2 CONC ): 17–19 (biog. of Ralph Parles). VCH Northampton 5 (2002): 388. PRO Documents, Feet of Fines, CP 25/1/178/82, number 538; CP 25/1/178/86, number 27; CP 25/1/179/91, number 52; CP 25/1/179/91, number 53; CP 25/1/179/92, number 4 (
2 CONC abstract of fines available online at http:// www.medievalgenealogy.org.uk/fines/search.php).
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ralph Parles, Esq., and his wife, Katherine Talbot, had one daughter, Margery Parles, who married (1st) John Hervey, Esq., of Thurleigh, Bedfordshire, and (2nd) William Argentine, Knt., of Halesworth, Suffolk and Great Wymondley,
2 CONC  Hertfordshire. Margery Parles had four known children by her Hervey marriage, but none by her Argentine marriage. There are many modern descendants of the Hervey marriage.  ...
