1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Sir Thomas Chaundos, 2nd Lord Chaundos1 
2 CONT *M, #215620, b. circa 1323, d. 6 October 1375
2 CONT *Last Edited=9 Jan 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Chaundos, 2nd Lord Chaundos was born circa 1323.1 He was the son of Sir Roger de Chaundos, 1st Lord Chaundos and Maud d'Acton.1 He married Lucy (?) before 1 July 1336.1 He died on 6 October 1375.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded as the 2nd Lord Chaundos [E., 1337] on 24 September 1353, de jure.1 He was Knight of the Shire for Herefordshire in 1355.1 He held the office of Sheriff of Herefordshire from 1359 to 1360.1 He was Knight of the Shire 
2 CONC for Herefordshire between 1360 and 1363.1 He held the office of Sheriff of Herefordshire from 1367 to 1368.1 He held the office of Sheriff of Herefordshire from 1370 to 1371.1 He was Knight of the Shire for Herefordshire in 1370/7
2 CONC 1.1 He held the office of Sheriff of Herefordshire from 1373 to 1374.1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Thomas Chaundos, 2nd Lord Chaundos and Lucy (?)
2 CONT
2 CONT #Elizabeth Chaundos+3. married Thomas Berkeley.
2 CONT #Sir John Chaundos, 3rd Lord Chaundos2 b. b 1349, d. 16 Dec 1428.  Married 1) Violette de la Bere 2) Philippe de Briene 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000075318221386& Inquisition Post Mortem] for Thomas Chaundos, knight, Writ, 12 October, 49 Edward III [1375]. <br>
2 CONT He died on 6 October [1375]. John his son, aged 26 years and more, was his heir. Mentions Lucy his wife, who was still living.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://thepeerage.com/p21562.htm#i215620 Cites
