2 CONT
2 CONT His ultimate heir was Thomas de la Bere who died a minor http://www.inquisitionspostmortem.ac.uk/view/inquisition/20-210/ LAWRENCE BERKKEROLLES and THOMAS DE LA BEER 210. ‡ . Commission to John Derehurst, Robert Andrewe, Nicholas 
2 CONC Sambourne the younger and Thomas Crekkelade [CPR 1413–16, p.263], as in writ devenerunt. 16 July 1414. [Wymbyssh]. Regarding lands which came into the king’s hand by the death of Laurence Berkerolles, chivaler, who held by knight 
2 CONC service of Richard, late lord le Despenser, a minor in the ward of Henry IV, and by the minority of Thomas de la Beere, now deceased, son of John, son of John de la Beere chivaler, son of Agnes, sister of Richard Turburvill, and o
2 CONC ne of the kin and heirs of the said Richard.
2 CONT
