1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This Kinard de la Bere profile does not belong here. John de la Bere & Agnes his wife did not leave male issue that "continued". A long series of IPM about the de Turberville lands makes it clear that their male li
2 CONC ne ran out with Thomas de la Bere on the 28th October 1414, still a minor. Appart from this, Agnes de Turberville would be too old to be his mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Kynard de la Bere that bests matches this profile was the son of Richard de la Bere & Sybil de Kinnardsley. He was born about 1345 & died at the battle of Pilleth 2 June 1402. His wife was Katherine Pecche.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Some Early English Pedigrees, Vernon M. Norr, Pennsylvania State University, 1968, p. 57
