1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Darrell Wolcott: Dafydd Goch ap Dafydd - His Real Ancestry; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id116.html. (Steven Ferry, August 22, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Thomas ap Rhodri, Father of Owain "Lawgoch"; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id153.html. (Steven Ferry, August 23, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Llywelyn died in 1287. It has been suggested that he was murdered, but all we know of the circumstances of his death is a brief entry in the accounts:
2 CONT
2 CONT In wax, oblations, and other necessities for the burial of Llywelyn, son of David, deceased, and his internment in the Dominican church of Bristol, £3 19s 4d.
