1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Weis says, with some contradiction between pages 152 and 153, that Reginald was the son of William and Maud de St Valerie.  Tompsett says, as we have recorded, that Reginald was the son of William, grandson of William and Maud
2 CONC , who died with Maud at the hands of King John 1210. Unknown GEDCOM info: MH:N160 Unknown GEDCOM info: B7CF9CD9-9436-47A7-8D1F-C7C650991EB9
1 NOTE Reginald supported Giles in his rebellions against King John. They were both active against the King in the barons' war. Neither was present at the signing of Magna Carta because they were still rebels who refused to compromise. K
2 CONC . John aquiesced to Reginald's claims to the de Braose estates in Wales in May 1216. He became Lord of Brecon, Abergavenny, Builth and other Marcher Lordships but was very much a vassal of Llewelyn Fawr, Prince of Gwynedd and now 
2 CONC his father-in-law. Henry III restored Reginald to favour and the Bramber estates (confiscated from William by K. John) in 1217. At this seeming betrayal, Rhys and Owain, Reginald's nephews who were princes of Deheubarth, were ince
2 CONC nsed and they took Builth (except the castle). Llewelyn Fawr also became angry and beseiged Brecon. Reginald eventually surrendered to Llewelyn and gave up Seinenydd (Swansea). By 1221 they were at war again with Llewelyn laying s
2 CONC eige to Builth. The seige was relieved by Henry III's forces. From this time on Llewelyn tended to support the claims of Reginald's nephew John concerning the de Braose lands.
2 CONT Reginald was a witness to the re-issue of Magna Carta by Henry III in 1225.
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT     1. The Plantagenet Ancestry, Eng. p. 78
2 CONT     2. Sussex Arch. Collections, Suss. 1, v. 5, p. 5, 152
2 CONT     3. The Complete Peerage, G.E.C., Eng. V, v. 1, p. 22
2 CONT     4. Burke's Extinct Peerage, 1883, Eng. p-1, p. 72
2 CONT     5. Arch. Cambr., Wales Pub. a, 4s, v. 14, p. 180, 181, 6s, v. 10, p. 343, 344
2 CONT     6. The Genealogist, os, v. 5, p. 66-70, 147, 161
2 CONT
2 CONT !RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT     There appears to be considerable conflict between the record sources above quoted relative to the parentage of the above Reginald; however, "The Complete Peerage", v. 1, p. 22, which is usually very accurate, indicates he is t
2 CONC he son ofWilliam de Braose by wife Matilda de St. Valery, which is also further amplifiedand explained in "The Genealogist", Eng. Pub. AF, os, v. 5, p. 147.
