1 NOTE Ralph de Mortimer, in 12th year of Henry III, had livery cf all his landsin Gloucester, Southampton, Berks, Salop and Hereford. He erected severalstrong castles, by which he was enabled to extend his possession againstthe Welsh; s
2 CONC o that Prince Llewelin, seeing that he could not successfullycope with him, gave him his daughter Gladuse Duy, widow of Reginald deBraose, in marriage.
1 NOTE SUCCEEDED HIS ELDER BROTHER; SUPPORTED HENRY III IN THE BARONS' REBELLION AND
