1 NOTE Sir Roger - - 6th Lord Wigmore Sheriff of Hereford; Lord of Kerry and Cydowain.     acquired by marriage Narberth Castle, Wales through his wife inherited Dunamase Castle, Co.Laois, died 1282, Dunamase went to Theobald de Verdun.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-887
1 NOTE     This individual has the following other parents in the Ancestral File:
2 CONT     Ralph De /MORTIMER/ (AFN:91QG-G0) and Llewelyn G /FERCH/ (AFN:GLCF-TX)
2 CONT     Ralph Of W /MORTIMER/ (AFN:HNJG-KD) and Gladys Of Wales // (AFN:HNJG-LK)
1 NOTE 6TH BARON MORTIMER OF WIGMORE; KNIGHTED BY THE KING 1253 AT WINCHESTER; SERVED
2 CONT ON THE MARCHES 1258-63, OPPOSING HIS COUSIN LLEWELLYN AP GRIFFITH; JOINED THE
2 CONT KING'S COUNCIL 4/1259; FOUGHT FOR THE KING AT LEWES 1264, BUT FLED THE FIELD;
2 CONT DEVISED AND CARRIED OUT THE PLAN WHICH ENABLED THE IMPRISONED PRINCE EDWARD TO
2 CONT ESCAPE FROM HEREFORD CASTLE; COMMANDED THE REARGUARD AT EVESHAM 8/1265, AND
2 CONT AFTER MONTFORT'S DEATH, MONFORT'S HEAD WAS SENT TO MORTIMER'S LADY AT WIGMORE
2 CONT AS A KEEPSAKE; RECEIVED HONOUR & LANDS OF OXFORD (FORFEITED BY ROBERT DE VERE),
2 CONT THOUGH TECHNICALLY NEVER HELD THE TITLE OF EARL OF OXFORD; BADLY DEFEATED AT
2 CONT BRECKNOCK BY THE WELSH (5/15/1266); TRUSTEE FOR PRINCE'S ESTATES WHEN EDWARD
2 CONT WAS ON CRUSADE; SHERIFF OF SEVERAL COUNTIES; ROYAL JUSTICE; KING'S PRINCIPAL
2 CONT MILITARY COMMANDER IN WALES; WIDELY REGARDED BY HIS PEERS AS "THE MOST
2 CONT TRUSTWORTHY NOBLEMAN IN THE KINGDOM"
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT     1. The Plantagenet Ancestry, Eng. 116, p. 72, 76, 78
2 CONT     2. The Complete Peerage, G.E.C., Eng. V, v. 9, p. 276-81
2 CONT     3. Arch. Cambr., Wales Pub. A, 3x, v. 3, p. 32, 4s, v. 3, p. 101
2 CONT     4. Dict. of Nat'; Biog., Eng. Pub. A, v. 39, p. 131-36
2 CONT     5. Antiquities of Shrops., Shrops 5, v. 4, p. 197, 216-24
2 CONT     6. Burke's Extinct Peerage 1883 Eng. Pub 383, 384, 385
