1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Gudröd Don Ragnvaldsson''', King of Mann and the Isles
2 CONT
2 CONT Gofraid mac Ragnaill (meaning "Gofraid, son of Ragnall"; Old Norse: Guðrøðr Rögnvaldsson) was a 13th century [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hebridean Hebridean] king, who descended from a long line of kings who ruled the Hebrides a
2 CONC nd the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isle_of_Man Isle of Man]. He is recorded within two 13th century chronicles with a byname meaning "the brown" (Gaelic: Gofraid Donn); although within a 13th century saga, and within Hebridean t
2 CONC radition dating from the 17th century, he is given the byname "the black" (Old Norse: Guðrøðr Svarti; Gaelic: Gofraid Dub). Gofraid Donn's father was [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raghnall_mac_Gofraidh Ragnall mac Gofraid], [http:
2 CONC //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_of_Mann_and_the_Isles King of Man and the Isles]; his mother was Ragnall's wife, who is described by a 13th century chronicle as the sister of a daughter of a nobleman from Kintyre. Gofraid Donn's male
2 CONC -line ancestry can be traced back with certainty to his great-great grandfather, [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gofraid_M%C3%A9r%C3%A1nach Gofraid Méránach], King of the Isles, King of Dublin (d. 1095). Gofraid Méránach is thought 
2 CONC to have taken control of the Kingdom of Man and the Isles in about the year 1079, and is recorded as the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Dublin King of Dublin] in 1091.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1187, on the death of Gofraid Donn's paternal grandfather, [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Godred_II_Olafsson Godred II Olafsson], King of Man and the Isles, Gofraid Donn's father, [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnvald-III-Gudr%C3
2 CONC %B6dsson/6000000001496413976 Ragnall], usurped the kingdom from the legitimate heir, his younger half-brother [http://www.geni.com/people/Olof-II-Gudr%C3%B6dsson/1341507 Olaf the Black Gudrödsson]. In consequence, a bitter family 
2 CONC feud broke out, in which Gofraid Donn played a part. According to a 13th century chronicle, when [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olaf_the_Black Olaf the Black]'s marriage to the sister of Ragnall's wife was nullified, Gofraid Donn w
2 CONC as tricked by his mother into attempting to kill his uncle Olaf the Black. Sometime later, he had his revenge, as Gofraid Donn was captured, and one of his followers blinded and castrated him. Olaf the Black later successfully too
2 CONC k the throne, and Ragnall was soon after assassinated. Olaf II was constantly under threat of Ragnall's powerful ally Alan, Lord of Galloway. In about 1230, Olaf the Black was forced to flee Man, and went to Norway to plead for as
2 CONC sistance from the king. He arrived just before the king sent a fleet into in the Hebrides to pacify the western coast of Scotland. Both Olaf the Black, and Gofraid Donn, travelled with the fleet, and upon the commander's death, Ol
2 CONC af the Black took control and retook the Isle of Man. Olaf the Black and Gofraid Donn then divided the kingdom between themselves, with Gofraid Donn controlling the Hebridean portion. Not long after the Norwegian fleet left the He
2 CONC brides, Gofraid Donn was killed on the Outer Hebridean island of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewis Lewis], in 1231.
2 CONT
