1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = AUFRICA Guðrøðardóttir=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Noblewoman in Ireland.
2 CONT * Affreca de Courcy or Affrica Guðrøðardóttir was a late 12th-/early 13th century noblewoman. She was the daughter of Godred Olafsson, King of the Isles, a member of the Crovan dynasty. In the late 12th century she married John de
2 CONC  Courcy. Affrica is noted for religious patronage in northern Ireland.
2 CONT * Affreca was the daughter of Godred Olafsson (Old Norse: Guðrøðr Óláfsson, a member of the Crovan dynasty. Godred ruled the Kingdom of the Isles.
2 CONT * Affreca founded in 1193 Grey Abbey, in the peninsula of Ards, where John had previously given lands to his family priory, St Andrew of Stogursey.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#GodredMandied1098 Project MedLands, SCOTTISH NOBILITY]
