1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hamon Le STRANGE
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: ABT 1293
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 1316
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: The Strange family of Hunstanton was a cadet branch of that of Strange of Knockin, seated in Shropshire. In the reign of Edward II, John, 2nd Lord Strange (d. 1311) had vested the Hunstanton estate in his younger brother, H
2 CONC amon, in return for the latter's promise never to lay claim to the principal family holdings. Hamon was succeeded by a son named after him, who, dying in 1361, left a son and heir underage.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Tudor website)
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunstanton_Hall
