1 NAME Elen /verch Thomas/
2 GIVN Elen
2 SURN verch Thomas
2 _MARNM verch Thomas
2 NICK Ellen
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1340
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1400
2 ADDR
3 STAE Wales
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Welsh Ancestry of the Tudor Dynasty; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id217.html. (Steven Ferry, April 8, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Ancestry of Owain Glyndwr; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id200.html. (Steven Ferry, September 13, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT See bottom right of: http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_2.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Courtesy of fantastically full family tree cf.:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hughes of Gwerclas 1/2/3/4:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_2.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_3.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_4.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Her ancestry is recorded in Welsh manuscripts written in the early 16th century, Peniarth MS 127 describes her as Elen, Lady Glyndyfrdwy ("arglwyddes glynn Dyvyrdwy"), the wife of Gruffudd Fychan. It records that her father was Th
2 CONC omas ap Llewelyn ap Owain. She had a sister of Margred, lady Uowddwy. Her ancestry is also recorded in Peniarth MS 129.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peniarth MS 127 records that Elen and Gruffudd had two sons and three daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Owain Glyndŵr
2 CONT Tudur
2 CONT Lowri, wife of Robert Puleston
2 CONT Isabel, wife of Adda ap Iorwerth Ddu ab Ednyfed Gam
2 CONT Morfudd, wife of David ab Ednyfed Gam
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elen appears to have been widowed before 1370/1 when she was recorded as Elen "lately" (jadis) the wife of "Gruff de Glindorde" on a list of loans made by Richard, Earl of Arundel. She owed 30 marks. The list records:
2 CONT
2 CONT Item livere a Elene jadys le femme de Gruff de Glindorde daprest par lettres le seigneur a repaier a feste de Pasque proscheyn pur queux le Receivour de Oswaldestre ad pris seurete - xxx mz
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ National Library of Wales. Llyfr Syr Thomas ap Ieuan ap Deicws, [c. 1510 - 1544]. Peniarth MS 127, p. 31, 38, 188, 212-3. NLW Catalogue; NLW Image. A transcript of the relevant pages is here.
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ National Library of Wales. Llyfr achau Gutun Owain, [1501x1540]. Peniarth MS 129, p. 60, 66. NLW catalogue; NLW image. A transcript of the relevant pages is here.
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ C. Given-Wilson. "Wealth and Credit, Public and Private: The Earls of Arundel 1306-1397." The English Historical Review, 1991, vol. 106, no. 418, p. 6-7, 23-5; citing Shrewsbury Borough Library, Craven MS 5923.
