2 CONT
2 CONT Rhun ab Owain Gwynedd
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhun_ab_Owain_Gwynedd
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhun ab Owain Gwynedd was the eldest child of Owain Gwynedd (the king of Gwynedd between 1137-1170). His mother was an Irish woman Pyfog (sometimes called Ffynnod Wyddeles) who was one of his father's many mistresses. Despite bein
2 CONC g illegitimate he was his father's favourite child and chosen successor. However, his premature death in 1146 is said to have cast his father into a deep depression which was only cured when he heard his forces had captured Mold C
2 CONC astle from the English.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Jones's translation of Peniarth MS 20 (55) gives an account of Owain's grief:  "And when the news of his death reached Owain, he fell into so great a sorrow that neither the splendor of sovereignty nor the entertainment of 
2 CONC bards nor the solace of courtiers nor the sight of costly objects could raise him from his...sorrow and grief."
