1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Caradog of Gwynedd With 3 Fathers; "Since Membyr Ddu does not appear among the sons of Cadwaladr listed in the 13th century manuscript Achau Brenhinoedd a Thywysogion Cymru, it is at
2 CONC  least possible that was not his birth name but a corrupt spelling of his nickname or perhaps his position at court. (The king's cup-bearer was called the 'menestr')  One good possibility is that his birth name was Richard, one of
2 CONC  the 4 sons Cadwaladr fathered by Alice deClaire[16].  This Richard's only daughter[18], Gwenllian, married Einion ap Gwalchmai[19], chief bard at the court of Llewelyn Fawr.  His closeness to the king's court suggests Richard was
2 CONC  himself a career court member and perhaps the king's cup-bearer." http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id114.html. (Steven Ferry, September 8, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Gwyn Ddistain - Seneschal for Llewelyn Fawr; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id120.html. (Steven Ferry, January 17, 2024.)
