2 CONT In 1277, the Lord of North Powys died leaving two young sons. (Roger) Mortimer was appointed by King Edward Longshanks to be their guardians. Four years later their bodies washed up in the River Dee, and Mortimer was accused of th
2 CONC eir murder. They were the last in a royal line, and Mortimer, guilty or not, was granted their lands. It is possible that Mortimer needed the lands to raise his nephew, Roger, as his guardian
