2 CONT # Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Acceded 1289. AKA William ap Gruffydd.
2 CONT
2 CONT     According to Bartrum an illegitimate son of Gruffudd ap Gwenwynwyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT     William ap Griffith, alias Wilcox, surnamed "de la Pole," Lord of Mowddwy, which was granted to him by his brother Owen, to be held of himself. This noble, who was living 17th Edward I [1289], and dead 9th Edward II (1315), m.
2 CONC  to Lady Eleanor, junior co-heir of the monarchs of South Cymru and Powys, 3rd dau. of Thomas ap Llewelyn, Lord of Yscoed, twenty-eight years of age and upwards, Sunday next after the Feast of St. Michael, 2 October, 2nd Edward II
2 CONC I (1328), and sister and co-heir of Owen ap Thomas, Lord of Half Yscoed, Monday next after the Feast of the Exaltation of the Holy Cross, 18th Edward III (20 September, 1334). By this lady he had Griffith ap William, son and heir,
2 CONC  appointed high sheriff of Merionethshire, 4th Edward III [1331], and John ap William, Lord of Mowddwy, under age at the death of his father. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, 
2 CONC Ltd., London, 1883, p. 115, Cherlton, Barons Cherlton, of Powys]
2 CONT
