0 @I6000000094199030989@ INDI
1 NAME Margaret /le Strange/
2 GIVN Margaret
2 SURN le Strange
2 _MARNM le Strange
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1245
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173393022889 (May 25, 2019; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT We had her as a daughter of John le Strange IV and Joan de Somery. Cawley says that couple had 1 child, John V (not the guitar player): https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3P-S.htm#Jo....
2 CONT
2 CONT The Peerage.com tends to agree: http://www.thepeerage.com/p56833.htm#i568321.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no sources saying that she was from that union, other than internet family genealogy sites.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartrum adds her as a note in his Marchudd 17 page: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173393022889. If she was the mother of Sir Gruffudd Llwyd she would date to c. 1245. If she was a later wife, she could date to 
2 CONC c. 1230. As she was added in, she does not appear in Bartrum's indexes, and the only source he provides is in the note, i.e. "see Siddons letter of May 1986." This is in ink. Below that in pencil he has a note that appears to say 
2 CONC that R.W. Llwyd suggests that the John le Strange in question is John III. He then adds that "As a widow Tregozznedd (as it seems to say) was settled on her till her death." John III was supposedly married to Lucy Tregoz. But Cawl
2 CONC ey and Peerage.com are silent on this issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT The John le Strange(s) are often conflated and dates are hard to lock down. At any rate, even if a child of John IV, I don't think she was a daughter of Joan de Somery. And Bartrum's little blurb that seems to say she inherited so
2 CONC me Tregoz land would argue for her to be a daughter of John III. I would argue that she be disconnected from Joan, at the least. (Steven Ferry, February 7, 2022.)
