2 CONT
2 CONT Edith married Gilbert DE BASSET of Wallingford, son of Ralph DE BASSET of Colston, Justice of England and Alice DE BUCI, after 1113 in Hook Norton, Oxfordshire, England 1524,2646. (Gilbert DE BASSET of Wallingford was born about 1
2 CONC 103 in Wallingford, Berkshire, England 803 and died in 1166 in Little Rissington, Gloucestershire, England 1135,26
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate spelling -- D 'Oilly
2 CONT =<nowiki>----------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/gen-medieval/2003-06/1054780248
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "Rosie Bevan" <rbevan@paradise.net.nz> 
2 CONT Subject: Who was Edith d'Oilly? 
2 CONT Date: Thu, 5 Jun 2003 14:30:48 +1200
2 CONT
2 CONT Since the last post on the d'Oillys, I've had several people ask me who Edith d'Oilly was. She was sister of Henry I d'Oilly, i.e. she was daughter of Robert II d'Oilly and Edith f. Forne. It has been said she married Gilbert Bass
2 CONC et, but there is doubt that she was mother of his son and heir, Thomas Basset, progenitor of the Bassets of Headington. Keats-Rohan in DD p.620 has Edith as wife of Wigan of Wallingford, alias Wigan nepos Brientii. Gilbert Basset 
2 CONC acquired d'Oilly property - Stratton, Oxon and Letcombe, Berks. and was holding 7 knights' fees of the honour of Wallingford in 1166. Whether he was holding this as Edith's maritagium and/or dower, or by a grant of the king after 
2 CONC the honour of Wallingford had escheated owing to the lack of heirs of Alditha de Wallingford, I don't know.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Basset was Philippa Basset's grandfather, and had Thomas been son of Edith, this would have meant she was related to her husband Henry de Newburgh in the second and third degree of consanguinity via his descent from Robert 
2 CONC II d'Oilly. The marriage would not have been allowed if that were the case.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is the pedigree of the d'Oilly family of Hook Norton based on a combination of Sanders 54, DD 620-622, William Bayley, The History of the House of Doyly (London, 1845), and the conclusions set out in my post.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Robert I d'Oilly of Oxford Castle d. c1093 + Aldith/Eadgyth, dau of Wigod, lord of Wallingford 2. Maud d'Oilly + Miles Crispin d.1107 3.Maud d.s.p.s. + Brian fitz Count d.s.p.s. 1154
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Nigel d'Oilly d.1112, lord of Hook Norton + Agnes 2. Robert II d'Oilly founded Oseney abbey d.c.1150 + Edith f. Forne d.1152 (mistress of Henry I, mother by him of Robert fitz Ede) 3. Henry I d'Oilly d.c.1163 + Maud de Bohun d a
2 CONC ft 1200, married secondly Walter fitz Robert d.1198 4. Henry II d'Oilly, b.c. 1161, in wardship of Humphrey de Bohun on father's death d.s.p.s.1232 + (1)Sybil 5. Maud d.Oilly d.s.p.1219 + Maurice de Gaunt alias de Berkeley d.s.p.1
2 CONC 230 + (2) Maud d.s.p. 1261 4.Robert d'Oilly 4.Margaret/Margery d'Oilly + Waleran, Earl of Warwick d.1203 5.Henry, Earl of Warwick d.1229 + Philippa Basset d.1265, married secondly Richard Siward 6. Thomas, Earl of Warwick b.1208-d
2 CONC .s.p.1242 + Ela Longespee d.s.p.1298 married 2nd Sir Philip Basset 6.Margery, Countess of Warwick d.s.p. 1253 + John Marshall de jure Earl of Warwick d.s.p.1242 + John du Plessis de jure Earl of Warwick d. 1263 4.Joan d'Oilly + Si
2 CONC mon fitz Walter, Lord of Daventry 5. Walter fitz Simon, Lord of Daventry, had issue 3.Gilbert d'Oilly 3.Edith d'Oilly +(1)Wigan de Wallingford alias Wigan nepos Brienntii ?+ (2)Gilbert Basset of Bicester, Oxon. d.1166 (father of T
2 CONC homas Basset of Headington d.1182) ?3.Alice d'Oilly (CP V :116 note (e)) + Ernulf de Mandeville 4.Ralph de Mandeville had issue 4.Geoffrey de Mandeville had issue 2. Fulk d'Oilly d.1126 3.Fulk d'Oilly 4.Fulk d'Oilly, the crusader 
2 CONC d.s.p.l. 2.Nigel d'Oilly
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Gilbert d'Oilly a quo D'Oyly of Estcote, Eston, Pushull, Eweden, Greenland, Chislehampton
2 CONT
2 CONT D'Oilly descendants may be found from the Daventry line. Other lines come from Gilbert, brother of Robert I and Nigel d'Oilly; possibly cadet Bassets; and Fulk d'Oilly's illegitimate issue which abounded in Yorkshire. There may be
2 CONC  also Mandeville descendants of Alice d'Oilly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cheers
2 CONT
2 CONT Rosie
