2 CONT Place: [Little] Rissington<br/>
2 CONT Hundred: Salmonsbury<br/>
2 CONT County: Gloucestershire<br/>
2 CONT Total population: 22 households (quite large)<br/>
2 CONT Total tax assessed: 10 geld units (very large).<br/>
2 CONT Taxable units: Taxable value 10 geld units. Taxed on 10.0.<br/>
2 CONT Value: Value to lord in 1066 £10. Value to lord in 1086 £8.<br/>
2 CONT Households: 12 villagers. 2 smallholders. 8 slaves.<br/>
2 CONT Ploughland: 4 lord's plough teams. 5 men's plough teams.<br/>
2 CONT Other resources: 2 mills, value 1.0.<br/>
2 CONT Lord in 1066: Siward.<br/>
2 CONT Lord in 1086: Robert d'Oilly.<br/>
2 CONT Tenant-in-chief in 1086: Robert d'Oilly.<br/>
2 CONT Phillimore reference: 48,1<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT This entry shows another connection between Gilbert Basset and his father-in-law, Robert d'Oilly.
2 CONT ----
