1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Medlands: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3D-K.htm#_Toc351372335 Untitled English Nobility D-K]:
2 CONT * Emma was born to "Alan [III] de Dunstanville"—the son of the Alan de Dunstanville to whom this profile is presently connected, who d. 1187 or 10 Oct 1200—"and his [second] wife", Muriel, by whom he had four children: 
2 CONT ** ...'''iii)''' EMMA de Dunstanville.  Wrottesley’s genealogical table, in his extract based on the [1242/43] claim cited above under Alan [III]’s wife Muriel, records “Emma” as oldest of three daughters of “Alan de Dunsterville”
2 CONC  [=Alan [III]], as mother of “Alan” and grandmother of “William de Englefeud, plaintiff”[246]. The Dunsterville/Englefield family relationship is indicated by the 28 Apr 1241 charter cited above.  
2 CONT ** '''m''' --- de Englefield, son of ---.
