1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''GUY de Craon'''
2 CONT
2 CONT s/o Maurice de Craon & Clarice
2 CONT
2 CONT ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANJOU,%20MAINE.htm#GuyCraonMIsabelBasset
2 CONT
2 CONT A genealogy of the founders of Freston Priory names "monsieur Wythe de Croune" as the son of “monsieur Maurice de Croune” and his wife "Clarice"[550].  The 1180/81 Pipe Roll records "Mauricius de Creon et Wido filius" accounting f
2 CONC or land at "Waltham quam habet versus Geruasium Painel" in Warwickshire/Leicestershire[551].  m as her second husband, ISABEL Basset, widow of ALBERT de Gresley, daughter of THOMAS Basset of Headington, Oxfordshire & his wife Alic
2 CONC e de Dunstanville.  A genealogy of the founders of Freston Priory records that "monsieur Wythe de Croune" married "une Isabelle"[552].  The 1181/82 Pipe Roll records "Wido de Creon" accounting "pro habenda uxore que fuit Alberti G
2 CONC resle" in Lincolnshire[553].  Guy & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)       PETRONILLA de Craon 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Accompanied Richard the Lionheart on crusade to the Holy Land. Died in the Levant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Source: A General and Heraldic Dictionary of of the peerages of England, Ireland and Scotland, extinct, dormant, and in abeyance. England. John Burke
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=aB0IAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA532&lpg=PA532&dq=Oliver+De+Vaux&source=bl&ots=disheR-YsZ&sig=rhozAOI6JE8E-XlbtbCzeufoRiE&hl=en&sa=X&ei=gXv8UfHkL5D68QSu4oDwAw&ved=0CEkQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=Oliver%20De%20Vaux&f=fals
2 CONC e
