2 CONT notes or source: LDS 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Little else is recorded of Baron William Draycote de Malbanc's  life. His wife Andilicia probably died early in the reign of Henry II. They had no male heirs and, on his death, his lands and the privileges of the Nantwich barony w
2 CONC ere divided between his three daughters.[1] Philippa, the eldest, inherited Nantwich Castle as part of her share of the town. She married Thomas, Lord Basset of Headington in Oxfordshire. The second daughter, Eleanor, did not marr
2 CONC y; her lands were granted to Henry de Audley.[1] Auda (also Adena), the youngest daughter, married Warin (also Warren) de Vernon; their daughter Auda (also Aldetha) brought Sandon in Staffordshire by marriage to Sir William Staffo
2 CONC rd, a member of the great baronial family of Stafford Castle.[1][2]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Basset” among the "consiliarios iniquissimos” of King John[288].  m PHILIPPA, daughter of WILLIAM FitzHugh Malbank & his wife ---.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONC  Thomas [II] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          PHILIPPA Basset (-before 29 Nov 1265, bur Bicester Priory)
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         JOANNA Basset (-after 1230).  
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)        ALICE Basset (-[1263]).  ...  m firstly [as his second wife,] WILLIAM Malet, son of GILBERT Malet & his wife Alice (-1215).  m secondly (before 1221, annulled) H--- de Chaceporc, son of ---.  m thirdly (1223 or before)
2 CONC  JOHN Bisset, son of MANASSER Biset & his wife Alice --- (-1241). 
2 CONT
