2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://clangrant.org.uk/library/Peter-Grant/03.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT (25) Alice Basset: c1200-c1263. Alice was the youngest daughter of Thomas Basset Lord of Colyton and Whitford, Devon. Alice inherited one third of the barony on Thomas’s death in 1220 and this increased the whole of the estate and
2 CONC  her heirs were her three daughters by John Bisset (24), Margery (33), Ela (35) and Isabel (38). Alice died sometime between 1248-9 to 1265.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice, wife of John Bisset (24), on her death the Advowson of Kidderminster which formed part of her dower went to litigation in England and in Rome (VCH- W. p, 175.) At her death the two co-heirs of John Bisset (24) surrendered a
2 CONC ll the rights in the Advowson to John Rivers (47). The two co-heirs regranted the church “with all its liberties and rights and customs.” to the priory of Maiden Bradley. In 1270 the prior obtained royal confirmation of these gran
2 CONC ts.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Basset, a Magna Charta Surety, 1215. His daughter Alice was heir of her two sisters for the Barony of Headington.
2 CONT
2 CONT The co-heirs of Alice by her 3rd husband, John Bisset:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Margery Bisset, wife of Sir Richard de Rivers
2 CONT # Ela Bisset, wife of Ralph de Neville, & of Sir John de Wotton
2 CONT # Isabel Bisset,  wife of Sir Hugh de Plescy
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#AliceBassetdied1263
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         THOMAS Basset [II] of Headington, Oxfordshire (-1220).  "Thomas Bass" granted "manerium meum de Comptun cum terra de Berewic" to "Alano filio meo" by charter dated to [1180/82?], witnessed by "…Waltero de Dunstanvile, A
2 CONC lano de Dunstanvile, Fulcone Basset…Thoma Basset juvene…"[435]. … m PHILIPPA, daughter of WILLIAM FitzHugh Malbank & his wife ---.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   [The f
2 CONC ollowing document suggests that Philippa predeceased her husband who married again, although it is uncertain to which Thomas Basset it relates: King John ordered the sheriff of Oxford to grant “terram de Dadinton...quam dedat Will
2 CONC o Malet in maritagium cum filia sua” to “Thom Basset”, dated 9 Nov 1215[440].  The fact that one of the daughters of Thomas Basset [II] married William Malet suggests that a double marriage may have been planned.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas [II] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)        ALICE Basset (-[1263]).  "Henry earl of Warwick…and Philippa his wife, and Reginald de Vautorte…and Joan his wife, and Alice sister of Philippa and Joan" performed homage for the lands formerly of "Thomas Basset, whose
2 CONC  heirs are Philippa, Joan and Alice", dated 19 May 1220[296].  Bracton records a claim, dated 1223, by "Walterus de Dunstanvilla" against "Johannem Byset et Aliciam Malet uxorem eius" concerning "terre…in Culintona", the defendant
2 CONC s claiming that "ipse Alicia" held the land "in proparte sororum unde Johanna uxor Reginaldi de Vautort et Philippa uxor Henrici comitis Warrewici"[297].  The Pipe Roll 1223 records “Johannes Biset et Alicia uxor eius” owing “de O
2 CONC blatis” in Devon[298].  
2 CONT
2 CONT *m firstly [as his second wife,] WILLIAM Malet, son of GILBERT Malet & his wife Alice (-1215). 
2 CONT *m secondly (before 1221, annulled) H--- de Chaceporc, son of ---.  
2 CONT *m thirdly (1223 or before) JOHN Bisset, son of MANASSER Biset & his wife Alice --- (-1241). 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/enguntlo.htm#WilliamMaletdied1215
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         GILBERT Malet (-1194).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   m ALICE Picot, daughter of RALPH Picot & his wife ---.  Salzman records her parentage and marriage[920].   Gilbert 
2 CONC & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT **i)          WILLIAM Malet (-before 20 Dec 1215).  iii)        ALICE Basset (-[1263]).  ...  m firstly [as his second wife,] WILLIAM Malet, son of GILBERT Malet & his wife Alice (-1215).  m secondly (before 1221, annulled) H--- d
2 CONC e Chaceporc, son of ---.  m thirdly (1223 or before) JOHN Bisset, son of MANASSER Biset & his wife Alice --- (-1241). 
2 CONT
2 CONT [m firstly ---.  The dates of the first marriages of William Malet’s daughters, together with the fact that his known wife Alice Basset had three children by her third husband, suggests that William’s two daughters may have been b
2 CONC orn from an otherwise unrecorded first marriage.] '' m [secondly] as her first husband, ALICE Basset, daughter of THOMAS Basset [II] of Headington & his wife Philippa Malbank (-[1263]).''  She married secondly (before 1221, annull
2 CONC ed) H--- de Chaceporc, and thirdly (1223 or before) John Bisset. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William & his [first] wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * (a)       MABEL Malet .  Her second marriage is confirmed by an order dated 18 Nov 1223 placing "in respite…the demand…from Hugh de Vivonne…for the debt that William Malet, father of the wife of Vivon, owed the king"[928].  m fi
2 CONC rstly NICHOLAS Avenell, son of --- (-[1221/22]).  m secondly (before 18 Nov 1223) HUGUES de Vivonne, son of --- (-1249). 
2 CONT * (b)       HAWISE Malet .  Henry III King of England made an order related to property "apud Exoniam" of "Hawisie que fuit uxor Hugonis Poinz", which she received from "Willelmi Malet patris vestri", dated 26 Aug 1220[929].  m fi
2 CONC rstly HUGH Poinz, son of --- (-before 26 Aug 1220).  m secondly ROBERT de Mucegros, son of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/enguntac.htm#JohnBisetdied1241B
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         JOHN Bisset (-before 24 Aug 1241).  His parentage is confirmed by the following document … m ([late 1220/1223]) as her third husband, ALICE Basset, widow firstly of WILLIAM Malet of Curry Malet, repudiated wife (secondl
2 CONC y) of H--- de Chaceporc, daughter of THOMAS Basset [II] of Headington & his wife Philippa Malbank (-[1263]).  …
2 CONT
2 CONT John & his [second] wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * i)          MARGARET Bisset (-Dec 1256 or before).  … m ([1237/39]) RICHARD de Rivers, son of RICHARD de Rivers & his third wife Maud de Beauchamp (-before 25 Apr 1243). 
2 CONT * ii)         ELA Bisset .  An order dated 9 Dec 1241 granted “Johi de Pless custodiam terras et El’ et Isabelle filiarurm et hedum Joh’s Byset una cum maritagio...”[1066].   …
2 CONT *iii)        ISABEL Bisset (-before 1279).  …  Her marriage is shown in The Complete Peerage, which does not cite the corresponding primary source[1070].  m as his first wife, HUGH du Plessis, son of JOHN du Plessis & his first wi
2 CONC fe Christiana de Sanford (-before 7 Jul 1292). 
2 CONT
