2 CONC r Cathedral).  He succeeded his brother Richard I in 1199 as JOHN King of England.  m secondly ([16/26] Jan 1214) as his second wife, '''GEOFFREY de Mandeville Earl of Essex''', son of GEOFFREY FitzPiers Earl of Essex & his first 
2 CONC wife Beatrice de Say (-London 23 Feb 1216, bur Trinity Prior within Aldgate).  He became Earl of Gloucester on his marriage, by right of his wife.  He was mortally wounded at a tournament in London[1947].  m thirdly ([Sep] 1217) a
2 CONC s his second wife, HUBERT de Burgh, son of --- & his wife Alice (-Banstead, Surrey 12 May 1243, bur Church of the Black Friars, Holborn).  Chamberlain of King John [1198]-1205.  He was granted the lands of Ctss Isabel 13 Aug 1217.
2 CONC   One of the chief advisers to King Henry III in the early years of his reign.  Created Earl of Kent 19 Feb 1227.  No issue. 
