2 CONT
2 CONT Maud was also called Alice of Gloucester.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud married Ranulph de Gernon, 5th Earl of Chester, son of Ranulph "le Meschin", 4th Earl of Chester and Lucy "the Countess" of Lincoln, circa 1141 in Gloucestershire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was suspected of poisoning her husband Ranulph, who was under excommunication, on 16 December 1153 (in England)--a deed she allegedly performed with the help of another of our ancestors, William Peverel the Younger, Lord of No
2 CONC ttingham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud founded Repton Priory in 1172 in Derbyshire.
2 CONT
