2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor remained a widow for over 30 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor remained a widow for over 30 years.  She came originally from Ryhall, Rutland, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor le Despencer was the daughter of Sir Hugh le Despenser, 1st Lord Despenser and Aliva Basset.
2 CONT She married Sir Hugh de Courtenay, son of John de Courtenay and Lady Isabel de Vere.
2 CONT She died on 30 September 1328.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====en.Wikipedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_de_Courtenay_(died_1292) Hugh de Courtenay (died 1292)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage and issue'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Courtenay married Eleanor le Despenser (d.1328),[6] daughter of Hugh le Despencer, 1st Baron le Despencer, Justiciar of England, of Loughborough, Leicestershire and Ryhall, Rutland by his wife Aline Basset, daughter of Sir Philip 
2 CONC Basset, Justiciar of England, of Wycombe, Buckinghamshire and Compton Bassett and Wootton Bassett, Wiltshire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife he had four[6] sons and five[6] daughters:[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hugh de Courtenay, 1st/9th Earl of Devon (1276–1340) of Tiverton Castle, eldest son and heir.
2 CONT 2. Sir Philip Courtenay (d.1314) of Moreton Hampstead in Devon, slain at Bannockburn on 24 June 1314, according to Vivian.[6] Died childless, when Moreton Hampstead was inherited by his elder brother the Earl of Devon.[8]
2 CONT 3. John Courtenay, died young.[6]
2 CONT 4. Robert Courtenay, died young.[6]
2 CONT 5. Isabel de Courtenay, wife of John de Saint John, 1st Baron St John (died 1329) of Basing.[6]
2 CONT 6. Aveline de Courtenay, wife of Sir John Giffard[6]
2 CONT 7. Egeline (or Eleanor) de Courtenay, wife of Robert le Scales.[6]
2 CONT 8. Margaret (or Margery) de Courtenay, wife of John de Moels.[9] Other sources give her husband as Nicholas de Moels, 2nd Baron Moels (d.1316), feudal baron of North Cadbury, Somerset. Without progeny.
2 CONT 9. Alice Courtenay, died young[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Eleanor Despenser (F) #921 Pop-up Pedigree
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship=20th great-grandmother of Raymond John Newcombe.
2 CONT
