1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===John de Burgh 
2 CONT * feudal Baron Lanvallei of Walkern [1, 2]
2 CONT *born: about 1235
2 CONT *died: 	Bef 3 Mar 1280
2 CONT *father: John de Burgh born about 1212 Banstead, Surrey, England died 1248
2 CONT *mother: Hawise de Lanvalay born about 1214 Lanvalay, Connauaght, Ireland died 1249
2 CONT *siblings: unknown
2 CONT *spouse: Cecilia de Baliol born about 1240 Bernard Castle, Gainford, Durham, England died 1289
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p113.htm#i3387
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Burgh, Baron Lanville & Walkern was born circa 1235 at Northamptonshire, Portslade, Sussex, Walkern, Hertfordshire; Age 40 in 1275.4,10 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Cecily de Baliol, daughter of Sir John de Baliol, Seigneur de Bailleul, Sheriff of Cumberland, Nottinghamshire, & Derbyshire, Lord Galloway, Barnard Castle and Dervorguille de Galloway, before 1255; 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 3 daughters (Devorguille, wife of Sir Robert, 1st Lord FitzWalter; Hawise, wife of Sir Robert de Grelley; & Margery, a nun at Chicksand or Sempringham).3,4,7,8,10 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Burgh, Baron Lanville & Walkern died circa 3 March 1280.4,10
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecily de Baliol b. c 1234, d. b 1273
2 CONT
2 CONT The 3 children of Cecily de Baliol and John de Burgh were:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Devorguille de Burgh born about 1257 Wakerley, Hertfordshire, England died 1284 buried Dunmow Priory, Essex, England; wife of Sir Robert, 1st Lord FitzWalter.
2 CONT *Hawise de Burgh born about 1260 Lanvalay, Connaught, Ireland died Wakerley, Hertfordshire, England; wife of Sir Robert de Grelley.
2 CONT *Margery / Margred de Burgh born about 1264 Portslade, Sussex, England died 1304; a nun, died unmarried.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000185243203889&size=large}}
2 CONT
