1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Hugh de Mortimer of Wigmore=
2 CONT son of Roger de Mortimer and Millicent de Ferrers married Annora de Braose
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL2.htm#HughMortimerdied1227
2 CONT
2 CONT '''HUGH Mortimer of Wigmore''' (-10 Nov 1227, bur Wigmore).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Wigmore Abbey names “Hugo” as son of “Rogero” and his first wife, adding that he supported King John and in a later passage that
2 CONC  he was killed in a tournament “IV Id Nov 1227”, dying without children, and was buried “in abbathia de Wyggemore”[283].  The Annals of Tewkesbury record the death in Nov 1227 of “Hugo de Mortuo-Mari”[284].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before 1210) '''ELEANOR [Annora], daughter of WILLIAM de Briouse''' & his wife Mathilde de Saint-Valéry Dame de la Haie (-after 26 Jan 1241).  King Henry III granted property "in Cherleton et in Chiriton, quam Willelmus de Breu
2 CONC sa pater predicte Annore ei dedit in maritagio" to "Annore que fuit uxor Hugonis de Mortuo Mari" dated 28 Sep 1232[285].
