1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Source: [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=u2NnAAAAMAAJ&focus=searchwithinvolume&q=Angaret Beauchamp Cartulary Charters, 1100-1268]
2 CONT
2 CONT The introduction to the Beauchamp Cartulary records that "Angaret" was the mother of Walter [II]´s son Hugh, and suggests that she may also have been the mother of his sons Thomas, Walter and John. Her parentage is not known, but 
2 CONC her name indicates Welsh origin. A lay subsidy roll for Worcester dated [1280] records "Domina Augereta de Bello Campo" in Bengeworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan, first wife of Walter, died in 1225, and he subsequently married Angaret, whose parentage is unknown. She held dower in Sheriff's Naunton, in Naunton Beauchamp, where the family were tenants of Westminster Abbey, and the advo
2 CONC wsons of Naunton Beauchamp and Comberton. Walter died on 11 April 1236, while Angaret still held land in Bengeworth in 1280 but died before the autumn of 1283.
