2 CONT Robert Mauduit Second Baron of Hanslape
2 CONT William Mauduit Third Baron of Hanslape+
2 CONT Isabella Basset
2 CONT Born: Bedfordshire, England
2 CONT Marriage: Robert Mauduit Second Baron of Hanslape 766,1378
2 CONT Died: 1225
2 CONT Noted events in her life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Background Information. 766
2 CONT Robert Mauduit married Isabella, daughter of Lord Thurston Basset, by whom he had two sons, William and Robert. His second son, Robert was given the lordship of Warminster and other lands in Wilshire and Somersetshire. Robert the 
2 CONC father, died in or before 1222.
2 CONT
2 CONT History and Antiquities of the Newport Pagnell Hundreds, pg. 109-110
2 CONT
2 CONT Background Information. 852
2 CONT Robert Malduit died about Jun 1222, or 6 Henry III. His widow was Isabella, daughter of Thurstan Basset.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biographi Juridica, p. 424
2 CONT
2 CONT Background Information. 1378
2 CONT Hawridge must have been included among the possessions of which Thurstan Basset died seised c. 1223 and passed to his daughter Isabel, widow of Robert Mauduit [Excerpta e Rot. Fin. (Rec. Com.), i, 98, 100]. Their son William Maudu
2 CONC it [Ibid. 87] held here in 1235 [Testa de Nevill (Rec. Com.), 258, 261], and was succeeded at his death about 1257 by his son Sir William Mauduit, afterwards Earl of Warwick [Chan. Inq. p.m. Hen. III, file 20, no. 2]. On his death
2 CONC  without issue about 1268 his estates passed to his nephew and heir William Beauchamp Earl of Warwick [Ibid. file 35, no. 13; Burke, Extinct Peerage, 30], who in 1284 occupied the position of mesne lord[Feud. Aids, i, 75].
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Parishes: Hawridge', in A History of the County of Buckingham: Volume 3, ed. William Page (London, 1925), pp. 367-369.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella married Robert Mauduit Second Baron of Hanslape, son of William Mauduit and Isabel St. Liz 681.,1378 (Robert Mauduit Second Baron of Hanslape was born in England and died in 1222 in England 160,1378.)
