1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilbert_de_Clare,_7th_Earl_of_Gloucester#Marriage_and_succession
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert and Alice separated in 1267; allegedly, Alice's affections lay with her cousin, Prince Edward. Previous to this, Gilbert and Alice had produced two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Isabella de Clare (10 March 1262-1333), after a marriage with Guy de Beauchamp, 10th Earl of Warwick having been contemplated, or possibly having taken place and then annulled, married Maurice de Berkeley, 2nd Baron Berkeley
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Joan de Clare (1264-after 1302), married (1) Duncan Macduff, 7th Earl of Fife; (2) Gervase Avenel
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella de Clare de Berkeley
2 CONT BIRTH 10 Mar 1262
2 CONT Worcestershire, England
2 CONT DEATH 4 Jun 1333 (aged 71)
2 CONT Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Tewkesbury Cemetery
2 CONT Tewkesbury, Tewkesbury Borough, Gloucestershire, England 
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 148769952 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella de Clare was the eldest daughter of Gilbert "the red" de Clare, 6th Earl of Gloucester, 7th Earl of Hertford, 9th Lord of Clare, 3rd Lord of Glamorgan (1243 - 1295) and Alice "of Angoulême" de Lusignan (1236 - 1290). She 
2 CONC married twice. Her first marriage was to Guy de Beauchamp, 10th Earl of Warwick (1272 - 1315) on 11 May 1279 at Warwick Castle, Warwickshire, England but was later annulled and found to be invalid. They had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her second marriage was to Maurice "the magnanimous" de Berkeley, 2nd Baron Berkeley, Warden of Gloucestershire (1271 - 1326) on 06 May 1314 at Berkeley Castle, Gloucestershire, England. Her marriage include the Lordship of Shipto
2 CONC n and the Lordship of Buford. Lord de Berkeley died ten years later in prison at Wallingford Castle and they had no known children. She died childless.
2 CONT
