1 NOTE {geni:about_me} THOMAS de Beauchamp, son of GUY de Beauchamp Earl of Warwick & his wife Alice de Tosny (14 Feb 1314-Calais 13 Nov 1369, bur Warwick, St Mary's).  The will of "Guy de Beauchamp Earl of Warwick", dated 28 Jul 1315, b
2 CONC equeathed property to "Alice my wife...Maud my daughter...Elizabeth my daughter...Thomas my son...John my son"[1448].  He succeeded his father in 1316 as Earl of Warwick.  King Edward II requested papal dispensation for the marria
2 CONC ge between “Guidonem de Bello Campo nuper comitem Warenæ defunctum...Thomam filium et hæredem prædicti comitis adhuc infra ætatem” and “Rogerum de Mortuo Mari dominum de Wygemor...unam de filiabus prædicti Roger”, related “in quar
2 CONC to et tertio gradu prohibito”, by charter dated 7 Feb 1319[1449].  He was elected Knight of the Garter in 1344, being one of the 25 original Knights of the order[1450].  The will of "Thomas Beauchamp Earl of Warwick", dated 6 Sep 
2 CONC 1369, chose burial “in the quire of the Collegiate Church of our Lady at Warwick”, bequeathed property to “my two sons Thomas and William...Isabel my daughter...to her marriage...Margaret my daughter a nun at Shouldham...Katherine
2 CONC  the daughter of my son Guy a nun at Shouldham...my daughter Alice...my daughter Clifford...John Beauchamp...Roger Beauchamp...Guy de Brienne...”[1451].  He died of the plague[1452]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Papal dispensation 19 Apr 1319) KATHERINE de Mortimer, daughter of ROGER [V] de Mortimer Lord Mortimer [later Earl of March] & his wife Joan de Geneville (-[4 Aug/6 Sep] 1369, bur Warwick, St Mary's).  A manuscript narrating th
2 CONC e foundation of Wigmore Abbey names “Edmundum primogenitum…Rogerum militem, Galfridum…Johannem…Katherinam…Johannam…Agnetam…Margaretam…Matildam… Blanchiam… et Beatricem” as children of “Roger comes et Johanna uxor eius”, adding tha
2 CONC t Katherine married “domino Thomæ de Bellocampo comiti Warwykie”[1453].  King Edward II requested papal dispensation for the marriage between “Guidonem de Bello Campo nuper comitem Warenæ defunctum...Thomam filium et hæredem prædi
2 CONC cti comitis adhuc infra ætatem” and “Rogerum de Mortuo Mari dominum de Wygemor...unam de filiabus prædicti Roger”, related “in quarto et tertio gradu prohibito”, by charter dated 7 Feb 1319[1454].  The will of "Katherine Countess 
2 CONC of Warwick", dated 4 Aug 1369, chose burial “where the Earl my husband shall appoint”, bequeathed property to “the Earl my husband...Thomas my son...William my other son...Maud de Clifford my daughter...Philippa de Stafford my dau
2 CONC ghter...my daughter Alice...Margaret Montfort my daughter...Isabel my daughter...Elizabeth the daughter of my son Guy...”[1455]. 
2 CONT
