2 CONT *'''Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900, Volume 04
2 CONT *Beauchamp, Thomas de     by John Horace Round
2 CONT *BEAUCHAMP, THOMAS de, Earl of Warwick (d. 1401), statesman, was '''son of Thomas de Beauchamp, earl of Warwick, who had distinguished himself at Crecy, Poitiers, and elsewhere, and was one of the founders of the order of the Gart
2 CONC er'''. He '''succeeded his father 13 Nov. 1369''', being then twenty-four years old. He accompanied John of Gaunt in the fruitless French campaign of 1373, and took part shortly after in the descent on Britanny (T. Wals. i. 318). 
2 CONC In the 'Good Parliament' of 1376, and in those of February and of October 1377, .... He was also one of those who challenged Arundel (ib. 310), and he is said, with other magnates (1 Jan. 1400), to have urged Henry to put Richard 
2 CONC to death (Chronique, 78). On 6 Jan. 1400 he set out with the king from London against the rebel lords (ib. 82), but after their capture disappeared fromm public life, and died 8 July 1401 (T. Wals. ii. 247, Trok. 337). He was succ
2 CONC eeded by his son, Richard de Beauchamp, 1382-1439 [q. v.].
2 CONT *[Chronique de la Traison (Eng. Hist. Soc.); Thomas of Walsingham and Trokelowe (Rolls series); a Latin MS. 6049, Bibl. du Roy. f. 30; Dugdale's Baronage, i. 236; The Rows Roll of the Earls of Warwick, 1845; Stuble's Constitutiona
2 CONC l History, chaps, xvi. xviii.]
