1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married Edmund Peverell 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lisle-87
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was born circa 1307, possibly at Campton, Bedfordshire, the daughter of Robert de Lisle, 1st Baron Lisle, and Margaret de Beauchamp
2 CONT
2 CONT She married her father's ward Edmund Peverel, her cousin, around 1325, with whom she had two children, John and Margaret (married Sir William de la Pole), before Edmund's early death in 1331.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1334 Edmund's widow, Elizabeth de Lisle, was cited by the Pope to appear as a witness with her parents, Robert and Margaret de Lisle, and her grandmother, Alice de Beauchamp, regarding the matter of the consanguinity which exi
2 CONC sted between their kinsman, John de Bohun, Earl of Hereford and Essex, and his wife, Margaret Basset. Elizabeth was living 28 Jan. 1348," (Richardson, 2007).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * Plantagenet Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, 2nd Edition, 2011, p.414. [https://books.google.com/books?id=kjme027UeagC&lpg=RA1-PA414&ots=qxEjMD2dgj&dq=Margaret%20Peverell%201331&pg=RA1-PA414#v=onepage&q&f=fal
2 CONC se GoogleBooks]
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&pg=RA2-PA31&lpg=RA2-PA31&dq=bishop+walter+de+langton+present+day+ancestors&source=bl&ots=kvpLGTNQc8&sig=15lrwBhrq57jT9ayMNvZxEYZcLA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiRuvuis8jSAhVowVQKHYFGB54Q6A
