2 GIVN Ralph III
2 SURN le Boteler
2 NSFX of Oversley
2 _MARNM le Boteler
2 NICK le Botilier
1 NAME Sir Ralph le Boteler of Wem
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1220
2 PLAC Oversley, Warwickshire, , England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 10 JAN 1278
2 ADDR
3 CITY Wem
3 STAE England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.gordonbanks.com/gordon/family/2nd_Site/geb-p/p290.htm#i14475
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph le Boteler of Wem1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, d. before 10 January 1278, #14475
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Maurice Boteler2
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms*	His arms were De goules a ung fesse escheque d'argent et de sable et croiselettes d'or (Glover). Gu. crusilly or. A fesse counter compony arg. and sa. (als. az.) (St. George.).3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage*	Sir Ralph le Boteler of Wem married Maud Pantulf, daughter of William Pantulf and Hawise FitzWarin, before 1243.1,4 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc*	They sued William de Atre for 7 acres of bsc in Wemme, as the right of Matilda, whereof Hugh de Pantun, Matilda's grandfather, was once seized. From Hugh the right descended to William, and from William to Elizabeth an
2 CONC d Matilda. On 3 November 1253 at Westminster, Middlesex, England.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Event-Misc*	Nearly 22 years ago, many knights and ladies were invited to his house at Wmme. A certain knight then present mentioned the circumstance at a proof of age in April 1273.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Feudal*	He held 1/3 Kt. Fee at Codington, Ches., late of Sir Rob. de Monte Alto on 16 September 1275.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Summoned*	He was summoned to serve against the Welsh he acknowledges 3 Kt. Fees, to be served by himself and 2 Kts. On 1 July 1277.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death*	He died | Manor, Little Castle, and 2 parks at Wmme, Hynestok hamlet, Manor and Little Castle of Tirley, as 3 Kt. Fees, all inheritance of his wife Maud before 10 January 1278.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family	Maud Pantulf d. before 6 May 1289
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage*	He married Maud Pantulf, daughter of William Pantulf and Hawise FitzWarin, before 1243.1,4 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William le Boteler of Wem d. b 11 Dec 1283
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph le Boteler d. b 5 Jun 1307
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited	14 May 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations	
2 CONT
2 CONT [S325] Rev. C. Moor, Knights of Edward I, v. 1, p. 121.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S342] Sir Bernard Burke, Extinct Peerages, p. 63.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S325] Rev. C. Moor, Knights of Edward I, v. 1, p. 118.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S301] Carl Boyer 3rd, Medieval English Ancestors of Robert Abell, p. 33.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S347] Carl Boyer 3rd, Medieval English Ancestors of Certain Americans, p. 36.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ralph le Botiler of Oversley was the son of Maurice le Botiler of Oversley.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph le Botiler of Oversley married Maud Pantulf Baroness of Wem, daughter of William Pantulf of Wem and Tyrley and Hawise fitz Warine, before 1243
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 2, 1242, we have Adam (it should be Ralph) le Butiller and Matilda (Pantulf) his wife suing Ralph de Hodnet for half a knight's fee in Cummeshal, as the escheat of Matilda. In Trinity Term 1243 and Easter Term 1244, th
2 CONC e Rolls supply other notices of this suit as one for two-thirds of half a knight's fee in Cunseshasel, in which Fulk fitz Warin, while Custos of Maud Pantulf's estates, had unjustly enfeoffed Ralph de Hodnet. Eyton.3 In October 12
2 CONC 69 It is presented etc. that Ralph le Botyler, senior, passing through the bailiwick of Gaule with his household (cum familia sua), on the Sunday after the Feast of St. Michael, 53 H. III., caused four couple of greyhounds (lessas
2 CONC  leporariorum) to run at a herd of doe. The Sheriff is commanded to produce him at Salop on the morrow of All Souls.4 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph le Botiler of Oversley died before 3 July 1281 being the date of the IPM.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ralph le Botiler of Oversley and Maud Pantulf Baroness of Wem
