1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Ralph le Botiler of Codynton, Pulverbatch and Norbury was the son of Ralph le Botiler of Oversley and Maud Pantulf, Baroness of Wem.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph le Botiler of Codynton, Pulverbatch and Norbury married Maud de Marmion, daughter of Philip de Marmion and Joan de Kilpec, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke will have it that there were no children of this marriage.4,5 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 7 January 1293 Jordan de Flotesbrok not appearing to prosecute his suit against Ralph le Botiler and Matilda his wife respecting tenements in Northbiri (Norbury) and Nethereoldeton (Oulton), it is dismissed, m. 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT The jury upon whom Jordan de Flosbrok and Ralph son of Ralph le Botyler had put themselves, convicted the said Ralph of having struck Jordan in the presence of the Justices, maliciously and to the contempt of the King and of the C
2 CONC ourt, when the said Jordan was withdrawing from the bar of this Court (a barrâ istius Curiae), after he had recovered his reasonable estovers against Ralph le Botyler the father of Ralph. Jordan is therefore to have half a mark fo
2 CONC r damages, and Ralph is to be committed to prison. m. 9.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph le Botiler of Codynton, Pulverbatch and Norbury died in 1307.4
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Ralph le Botiler of Codynton, Pulverbatch and Norbury and Maud de Marmion
2 CONT # Juliana Botiler+  (Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Juliana-Morton/6000000001783464004?through=6000000006419364330)
2 CONT # Sir Ralph le Botiler of Pulverbatch and Norbury+8 d. Mar 1342
2 CONT
