1 NAME William The Younger (Half Brother of Lord William) /le Boteler/
2 GIVN William The Younger (Half Brother of Lord William)
2 SURN le Boteler
2 _MARNM le Boteler
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Source= 
2 CONT Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families (Google eBook) by Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham.  Genealogical Publishing Company, 2004, p. 108.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gives parents - Ela de Herdeburgh and William le Boteler (or le Botiller), Knight, of Wem, Dodington and Hinstock, Shropshire and Oversley, Warwickshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was called "the younger" because he had an elder half-brother, William le Boteler who succeeded their father.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1334, his mother, Ela de Herdeburgh, granted her manor, Carshalton, Surrey, to her son William le Boteler "the younger".
