1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Philippe de Briene1 
2 CONT * F, #137463, d. after 28 July 1368
2 CONT * Last Edited=7 Feb 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Philippe de Briene''' was the daughter of Guy de Bryan, 1st Lord Bryan.2 She married, firstly, Edward de Bohun, son of John de Bohun, 1st Lord Bohun and Isabel de Tregoz.2 She married, secondly, Sir John Chaundos, 3rd Lord Chau
2 CONC ndos, son of Sir Thomas Chaundos, 2nd Lord Chaundos and Lucy (?).1 She died after 28 July 1368.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Chaundos.1 Her married name became de Bohun.2 She was also known as Philippe de Brian.2
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000075320072940& Inquisitions Post Mortem] for John Chaundos, knight, Writ. 20 December 1428. He died on 16 December [1428] without heir of his body. Giles Brugge, esquire, was kin a
2 CONC nd one of his next heirs as the son of Alice one of the daughters of Elizabeth sister of John Chaundos, and aged 30 and more. Margaret wife of Nicholas Mattesdon was kin and his other next heir as the other daughter of Elizabeth s
2 CONC ister of John Chaundos, and aged 40 and more. Mentions '''Philippa his wife who had died before him.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations
2 CONT # http://thepeerage.com/p13747.htm#i137463 Cites 
2 CONT ##[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinc
2 CONC t or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 149. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT ##  Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 201.< [https://archive.org/details/completepeerageo02coka/page/201/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] > BOHUN  (b) Their ist s., Edward, m. Philippe (da. of Sir Guy de
2 CONC  Brian) and d. s.p. and v.p. Jan. 1 361/2, leaving John his next br. and h., aged 26 and more (Ch. Inq. p. m., Edw. Ill, file 166, no. 24), who also d. s.p. and v.p. Philippe was living 28 July 1368 {Close Roll, 42 Edw. Ill, m. 12
2 CONC ).
