1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Elizabeth de Bryan=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Sir Guy de Brienne, KG, Lord Bryan and Joan de Carew 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Cokayne, George, Complete Peerage, vol 02 Bass-Canning, 1912, TN-271412_2=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.medievalgenealogy.org.uk/cp/bryan.shtml#p361 Some Corrections and Additions to the Complete Peerage: Volume 2: Bryan]
2 CONT
2 CONT The suggestion that Elizabeth, the wife of Robert FitzPayn, was a daughter of the elder Guy de Bryan (d. 1390), is confirmed by a reference in the wife of his son, the younger Guy de Bryan (d. 1386), to "mon tresch[er]e fr[er]e Ro
2 CONC bard le Fitzpayn" - showing that Robert was his brother-in-law [Collectanea Topographica et Genealogica, vol. 3, pp. 253, 254 (1836)]. The chronology suggests that she would have been Guy's daughter by a marriage earlier than that
2 CONC  to Elizabeth Montagu. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.thepeerage.com/p32798.htm#i327975 The PEERAGE]
2 CONT
2 CONT The PEERAGE DOES NOT HAVE INFORMATION ON GUY
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth de Briene is the daughter of Sir Guy de Briene.2 She married Robert FitzPayn, son of Sir Richard de Grey and Joan FitzPayn, between 16 August 1351 and 16 October 1354.1
2 CONT
2 CONT From between 16 August 1351 and 16 October 1354, her married name became FitzPayn.1
2 CONT
2 CONT =Child of Elizabeth de Briene and Robert FitzPayn=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Isabel Grey,''' +3 b. c 1364, d. 11 Apr 1394
2 CONT
2 CONT =Notes=
2 CONT
2 CONT In summary, it appears that Sir Guy de Bryan was born say 1309, he being in arms in 1327 and stated to be of age in 1330. His first wife, Joan, was living 12 April 1348. It is Nicolas' supposition and my own that Joan was the daug
2 CONC hter of John de Carew, Knt., of Carew, Pembrokeshire, by his wife, Joan. As indicated above, Guy de Bryan's marriage was held by Lady Joan de Carew, and he occurs together with Lady Carew in records in 1330, 1341, and 1342. On the
2 CONC  last date, Lady Joan de Carew released her life estate to her land holdings at Clifton, Dartmouth and Hardness, Devon to him. Sir Guy de Bryan was still in possession of this property as late as 1376-1377.  Sir Guy de Bryan and h
2 CONC is first wife, Joan de Carew, were the parents of at least two, possibly three daughters. There are living descendants through their daughter, Elizabeth de Bryan, who married Robert Fitz Payn (formerly de Grey), Knt., of Stogursey
2 CONC , Bridghampton, Cheddon Fitzpaine, Rodway, etc., Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT For interest's sake, the following is a list of the 17th Century New World immigrants that descend from Sir Guy de Bryan and his first wife, Joan de Carew, through their daughter, Elizabeth:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Robert De GREY (1° B. Fitzpayn)
2 CONT * Born: ABT 1321
2 CONT * Died: 21 May 1393
2 CONT * Father: Richard De GREY (2° B. Grey of Codnor)
2 CONT * Mother: Joan FITZPAYN
2 CONT * Married: Elizabeth BRYAN ABT 1352
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1666. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
