1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Talbot, Baroness Grey of Wilton''' (c. 1353 – January 1401/2) was a medieval English noblewoman. Her parentage was a point of genealogical debate for over a century, but modern forensic archival auditing has successfu
2 CONC lly identified her as a descendant of King Edward I, establishing her as a vital gateway ancestor for various royal and colonial lineages.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Parentage and Identity ===
2 CONT For decades, standardized references such as The Complete Peerage (TCP) listed Elizabeth’s parentage as "unknown" or "unproven." However, following the application of the '''Genealogical Proof Standard (GPS)''', modern scholarship
2 CONC —specifically by '''Douglas Richardson''' (2013) and '''Brad Verity''' in the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy (2016)—has definitively identified her as:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Father:''' Sir Gilbert Talbot, 3rd Lord Talbot (c. 1332–1387).
2 CONT * '''Mother:''' Petronilla Butler, daughter of James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormond, and Eleanor de Bohun.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through her mother, Elizabeth was a great-granddaughter of '''King Edward I''' and '''Eleanor of Castile'''. This identification corrected previous "identity smash-ups" that conflated her with other contemporary Elizabeth Talbots.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage and Issue ===
2 CONT Before 1370, Elizabeth married '''Henry de Grey, 5th Lord Grey of Wilton''' (c. 1340–1396). The marriage was reinforced by land settlements and the involvement of the Talbot family as feoffees for the Grey estates.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had issue, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Richard de Grey, 6th Lord Grey of Wilton''' (c. 1393–1442).
2 CONT * '''Margaret de Grey''', who married John Darcy, 5th Lord Darcy of Knayth.
2 CONT
2 CONT === The Evidence of Toseland ===
2 CONT The resolution of Elizabeth’s lineage is based on the forensic tracking of the '''Manor of Toseland''' in Huntingdonshire. Originally a '''de Bohun''' property, the manor passed through the '''Butler''' family and was subsequently
2 CONC  held by the '''Greys of Wilton'''. Archival audits demonstrate that the manor entered the Grey holdings as a maritagium (marriage portion) for Elizabeth, proving her descent from Petronilla Butler.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death and Inquisition Post Mortem ===
2 CONT Elizabeth survived her husband by approximately five years. A number of writs were issued in February and March 1401/1402 concerning the Inquisition Post Mortem of "Elizabeth the widow of Henry Grey of Wilton." The following were 
2 CONC recorded:
2 CONT
2 CONT * "She died on 9 Jan. 1402. Richard her son and heir is aged 12 years and more."
2 CONT * "She died on 10 Jan. Richard her son and heir is aged 10 years and more."
2 CONT
2 CONT The slight discrepancy in the recorded date of death (9 vs 10 January) and the age of her heir is common in contemporary colonial and medieval records and does not affect the confirmed filiation.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Digital Phantoms:''' Older scholarship often failed to link Elizabeth to her parents due to the lack of a direct filiation statement in her husband's Inquisition Post Mortem. There had been significant doubt as to her origins
2 CONC , but this is now considered resolved by the synthesis of property descent and onomastics.
2 CONT * '''Identity Firewall:''' Her identification relies on the synthesis of property descent (Toseland) and kinship circles, separating her from speculative 18th-century narratives that lacked primary source grounding.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Richardson, Douglas.''' Royal Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 5 vols., ed. Kimball G. Everingham. (Salt Lake City, UT: the author, 2013), vol. V, page 372, WILTON 11, Henry de Grey.
2 CONT * '''Verity, Brad.''' "Descendants to the Third Generation of Eleanor, Countess of Ormond." Foundations (Journal of the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy), vol. 8 (2016): 82-83.
2 CONT * '''Cokayne, G.E.''' The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant.
2 CONT * '''Public Record Office.''' Calendar of Inquisitions Post Mortem, Vol. XVIII, 1-6 Henry IV: 1399-1405. (London: 1987), nos. 493-498.
2 CONT * '''Richardson, Douglas.''' Royal Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 5 vols., ed. Kimball G. Everingham. (Salt Lake City, UT: the author, 2013), vol. V, page 372, WILTON 11, Henry de Grey.
