2 CONT Joyce LA ZOUCHE  	
2 CONT Born: Abt 1253, Norton, Daventry, Northamptonshire, England  Married (1): 1st husband  Married (2): Before 1268, Devonshire, England  Died: Before 13 Mar 1289-1290, Richard's Castle, Ludlow (Shrops), Herefordshire, England  Buried
2 CONC : 13 Mar 1289-1290, Worcester Cathedral, Worcestershire, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: Joyce la Zouche; m. Robert de Mortimer (d. 7 April 1287), of Richard's Castle, Herefs, and was buried 13 March 1289/90. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT He [Robert de Mortimer] married Joyce, daughter and heir of William DE LA ZOUCHE, who had Norton in Northants and other manors. He died 7 April 1287, and was buried next day in Worcester Cathedral, before the altar of Saints Simon
2 CONC  and Jude. Dower was assigned to his widow Joyce in November 1287. She was buried near him, 13 March 1289/90. [Complete Peerage IX:263-4, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information: Joyce married Nicholas DE WHELTON in 1st husband. (Nicholas DE WHELTON was born about 1240 in Welton, Lincoln, Lincolnshire, England and died before 1268.) www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Joyce la Zouche Mortimer  Birth 1250  Kings Nympton, North Devon District, Devon, England Death Mar 1290 (aged 39'9640)  Worcestershire, England Burial  Worcester Cathedral  Worcester, City of Worcester, Worcestershire, England   
2 CONC Memorial ID 105308942
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of William la Zouche and Maud de Mortimer, great grand daughter of Alan la Zouche and Alice de Belmeis.
2 CONT
