1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth de Hastings was a daughter of Sir John de Hastings, 1st Baron Hastings, by his 1st wife Isabel de Valence.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Sir Roger de Grey, a younger son of the 2nd Lord Grey of Wilton. Her husband had a goodly chunk of the family property settled on him, including Ruthin Castle, and became the 1st Lord Grey of Ruthin.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 2 sons
2 CONT
2 CONT #Sir John (dvp)
2 CONT #Sir Reynold, who succeeded and 4 daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT # Julian, wife of Sir John Talbot, of Richard's Castle
2 CONT # Mary, wife of Sir John de Burgh
2 CONT # Joan, wife of Sir William de Patshull
2 CONT # Maud, wife of William de la Roche
2 CONT # Many good sources show another daughter, Elizabeth, wife of Sir Philip Okeover, though this seems not to be uncontroversial.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Find-a-Grave Memoria; #126170912, located at:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/126170912/roger-de-grey
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger Grey, 1st Baron Grey de Ruthyn (c. 1298 – 6 March 1353) was summoned to parliament in 1324. He saw much service as a soldier.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of John Grey, 2nd Baron Grey de Wilton, by his second marriage, to Maud Bassett, a daughter of Ralph Bassett, 1st Baron Bassett. He married Elizabeth daughter of John Hastings, 1st Baron Hastings of Bergavenny, by w
2 CONC hom he had a son who succeeded as Reginald Grey, 2nd Baron Grey de Ruthyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Burkes Peerage and Baronetage (1939).
2 CONT * Leigh Rayment's Peerage Pages
2 CONT * http://thepeerage.com/p4051.htm#i40502
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Katherine Talbot, wife of Ralph Parles, and her daughter, Margery Parles, wife of John Hervey and William Argentine" - message posted May 2008 - Douglas Richardson writes:
2 CONT
2 CONT >.... Thus, it would appear that Ralph Parles first wife was Katherine Talbot, not Joan Talbot, she being a daughter of John Talbot, Knt., of Richard's Castle, Herefordshire, by his wife, Juliane, daughter of Roger de Grey, Knt., 
2 CONC 1st Lord Grey of Ruthin. Katherine Talbot's mother's descent from Geoffrey Plantagenet can be found in my book, Plantagenet Ancestry (2004).
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ralph Parles, Esq., and his wife, Katherine Talbot, had one daughter, Margery Parles, who married (1st) John Hervey, Esq., of Thurleigh, Bedfordshire, and (2nd) William Argentine, Knt., of Halesworth, Suffolk and Great Wymondley,
2 CONC  Hertfordshire. Margery Parles had four known children by her Hervey marriage, but none by her Argentine marriage. There are many modern descendants of the Hervey marriage. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Roger was 1st Baron Grey de Ruthyn.
2 CONT He was summoned to Parliament in 1324, and spent much of his life engaged in warfare.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/108457598/person/220155219625 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 1 2018, 1:36:41 UTC''
2 CONT * "Royal Ancestry" 2013 Douglas Richardson Vol. III. p. 124-125
2 CONT * "Royal Ancestry" 2013 Douglas Richardson Vol. III. p. 258
2 CONT * "Royal Ancestry" 2013 Douglas Richardson Vol. V. p. 369
2 CONT * Richardson, Douglas: Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd edn. (2011), 4 vols, Volume 2, page 271, GREY 5. Daughter Elizabeth not mentioned here.
2 CONT * HoP, discusses Elizabeth.
2 CONT * Marlyn Lewis.
