1 OCCU 2nd Baron Grey de Ruthyn, 2nd Baron Grey of Ruthyn, 2nd Baron of Ruthin, 2ND BARON GREY DE RUTHIN
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Reginald Grey (c.1322–c.4 August 1388), 2nd Baron Grey de Ruthyn was the son of Roger Grey, 1st Baron Grey de Ruthyn and Elizabeth de Hastings. He was summoned to Parliament from 1354 to 1388.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Alianore Le Strange, daughter of John Le Strange, 2nd Baron Strange of Blackmere and Ankaret Le Botiller. He succeeded his father and was succeeded by his son, Reginald. His youngest daughter, Ida de Grey, who married S
2 CONC ir John Cockayne, was an ancestress of Anne Boleyn and Mary Boleyn. He had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Reginald Grey, 3rd Baron Grey de Ruthyn (c.1362- 30 September 1440), married firstly, Margaret de Ros, by whom he had six children, and secondly, Joan de Astley, by whom he had another six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Eleanor Grey, married William Lucy.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.John Grey (born 1364)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Catherine Grey (born 1366)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.Ida de Grey (c.1368- 1 June 1426), married Sir John Cockayne, by whom she had six children. Her eldest daughter Elizabeth, wife of Sir Laurence Cheney, was the great-great-grandmother of Anne Boleyn.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] References
2 CONT
