1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''Place of birth seems wrong.  The cited source does not mention it.  Further research is warranted.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This Margery is the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Margery-Parles/6000000173668503366.  Merge not possible because that profile belongs to an isolated tree.  That profile should be deleted by its manager.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stirnet's "Argentine1" page does not mention this Margery.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''detached as mother from https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Hervey-I-of-Thurleigh/6000000007737560231 on April 7, 2026
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT From http://newsgroups.derkeiler.com/Archive/Soc/soc.genealogy.medieval/2008-05/msg00240.html (which is now invalid):
2 CONT
2 CONT >Douglas Richardson writes:
2 CONT >> .... Thus, it would appear that Ralph Parles first wife was Katherine Talbot, not Joan Talbot, she being a daughter of John Talbot, Knt., of Richard's Castle, Herefordshire, by his wife, Juliane, daughter of Roger de Grey, Knt.
2 CONC , 1st Lord Grey of Ruthin. Katherine Talbot's mother's descent from Geoffrey Plantagenet can be found in my book, Plantagenet Ancestry (2004).
2 CONT >>Ralph Parles, Esq., and his wife, Katherine Talbot, had one daughter, Margery Parles, who married (1st) John Hervey, Esq., of Thurleigh, Bedfordshire, and (2nd) William Argentine, Knt., of Halesworth, Suffolk and Great Wymondley
2 CONC , Hertfordshire. Margery Parles had four known children by her Hervey marriage, but none by her Argentine marriage. There are many modern descendants of the Hervey marriage.  ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From her Find A Grave memorial:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Margery was the daughter of Ralph Parles and Katherine Talbot.
2 CONT >She was previously the widow of John Hervey of Thurleigh. They were the parents of
2 CONT >Richard Hervey born 1397
2 CONT >Thomas Hervey born 1399
2 CONT >Joan Hervey born 1402
2 CONT >John Hervey born 1405
2 CONT >She married William Argentein late in life probably after 1410.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT attested in The History of Parliament's article on her father
2 CONT
2 CONT also seen as '''Marjory Parles
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Given name also has been reported to be '''Margaret'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of marriage to John Hervey also have been erroneously reported to be circa 1386 at Thurleigh, Bedfordshire, England <attestation unknown, conflicts with the cited Door Suffolk Institute of Archæology source>.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * The History of Parliament The House of Commons 1386-1421 (1993), Roskell, John Smith, (The History of Parliament [Series]. Stroud, Gloucestershire: Alan Sutton Pub. Ltd., c1992), FHL book 942 D3hp V 2., vol. 2 p. 50.
2 CONT * ''Magna Carta Ancestry: A study in Colonial and Medieval Families'', Richardson, Douglas, (Kimball G. Everingham, editor. 2nd edition, 2011), vol. 1 p. 28.
2 CONT * Medieval, royalty, nobility family group sheets (filmed 1996), Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. Family History Department. Medieval Family History Unit, (Manuscript. Salt Lake City, Utah : Filmed by the Genealogical 
2 CONC Society of Utah, 1996), FHL film 1553977-1553985..
