1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Page 1 Survey  for Sir William de Wysham
2 CONT * Page 1 Survey taken by NASH IN LATE 1700’s and was obtained from Herefordshire/Worcestershire county records office. These document are authentic as it was among Sir John de Wysham Woodmanton Manor papers, files:
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000050609032875?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000052930253158
2 CONT
2 CONT *    This Survey taken by NASH IN LATE 1700’s is evidences and is proof that Joan (Johanna) is the mother of William de Wysham Born abt 1365 and not (K)Catherine Hopton:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Collections Towards the History and Antiquities of the County of Herefordshire:
2 CONT * This is a Pedigree for the Wysham Family in this book:
2 CONT * https://books.google.com.au/books?id=q2c-AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA195&lpg=PA195&dq=who+was+the+Daughter+to+Anthony+Dastyn:&source=bl&ots=MdaZ2JC76m&sig=Tactqp-LtCpG1dcfTH25fgTS9BA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjd4v_02cLOAhUHFZQKHa4eCjoQ6AEIKTAC#v=
2 CONC onepage&q=who%20was%20the%20Daughter%20to%20Anthony%20Dastyn%3A&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Page 1 Survey Sir Richard de Wysham
2 CONT * Page 1 Survey taken by NASH IN LATE 1700’s and was obtained from Herefordshire/Worcestershire county records office. These document are authentic as it was among sir john de wysham woodmanton manor papers, files:
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000050608642865?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000052928337447&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT * Collections Towards the History and Antiquities of the County of Herefordshire:
2 CONT * This is a Pedigree for the Wysham Family in this book:
2 CONT * https://books.google.com.au/books?id=q2c-AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA195&lpg=PA195&dq=who+was+the+Daughter+to+Anthony+Dastyn:&source=bl&ots=MdaZ2JC76m&sig=Tactqp-LtCpG1dcfTH25fgTS9BA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjd4v_02cLOAhUHFZQKHa4eCjoQ6AEIKTAC#v=
2 CONC onepage&q=who%20was%20the%20Daughter%20to%20Anthony%20Dastyn%3A&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT * The visitation of Herefordshire made by Robert Cooke,
2 CONT * This Book has a Pedigree for the de Wysham family:
2 CONT * https://archive.org/stream/visitationofhere00cookrich#page/80/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------* Other Holt Pedigree & Family Trees
2 CONT * The earliest known person the lineage traces back to was a man named Hamo I, Viscount of Alet, France who was born between 963-1023 AD.  The following is a pedigree from him:
2 CONT * Caradoc (or Caragod) de la Boussac (born in Boussac, Ille-et-Vilaine, Bretagne, France in 1035 AD)
2 CONT * Baderon Lord of Monmouth (born in Dol, Bretagne, France in 1060 AD)
2 CONT * William FitzBaderon, Baron of Monmouth (born in Monmouthshire, Wales around 1087 AD)
2 CONT * Fitzwilliam Baron of Monmouth Baderon (born in Monmouthshire, Wales in 1100 AD)
2 CONT * Gilbert FitzBaderon, Lord of Monmouth (born between 1105-1163 AD)
2 CONT * John FitzGilbert, Baron of Monmouth (born in Monmouthshire, around 1182 AD)
2 CONT * Richard, Lord of Wyesham (born in Monmouth Castle, Wales around 1223 AD)
2 CONT * Sir Ralph de Wysham (born in Wyesham Village, England in 1260 AD)
2 CONT * Sir John de Wysham (born in 1288 AD)
2 CONT * John de Wysham, Baron of Clifton (born in Woodmanton in 1320 AD) ''''Sir Richard de Wysham (born in 1350 AD)''''. His son, Richard Holt, also known as Wysham Holt was born in Holt, Worcestershire, England in 1370. He married Cri
2 CONC stine Coldrey and had a son with her named Richard. This son Richard was born around 1420. He married Joan Collingbourne (Darrell) and had two issue: Christian (Berkeley) and Elizabeth (Pownde).
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Reference •	https://coadb.com/surnames/holt-arms.html
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT * Other Holt Pedigree & Family Trees
2 CONT * The earliest known person the lineage traces back to was a man named Hamo I, Viscount of Alet, France who was born between 963-1023 AD.  The following is a pedigree from him:
2 CONT * Caradoc (or Caragod) de la Boussac (born in Boussac, Ille-et-Vilaine, Bretagne, France in 1035 AD)
2 CONT * Baderon Lord of Monmouth (born in Dol, Bretagne, France in 1060 AD)
2 CONT * William FitzBaderon, Baron of Monmouth (born in Monmouthshire, Wales around 1087 AD)
2 CONT * Fitzwilliam Baron of Monmouth Baderon (born in Monmouthshire, Wales in 1100 AD)
2 CONT * Gilbert FitzBaderon, Lord of Monmouth (born between 1105-1163 AD)
2 CONT * John FitzGilbert, Baron of Monmouth (born in Monmouthshire, around 1182 AD)
2 CONT * Richard, Lord of Wyesham (born in Monmouth Castle, Wales around 1223 AD)
2 CONT * Sir Ralph de Wysham (born in Wyesham Village, England in 1260 AD)
2 CONT * Sir John de Wysham (born in 1288 AD)
2 CONT * John de Wysham, Baron of Clifton (born in Woodmanton in 1320 AD) ''''Sir Richard de Wysham (born in 1350 AD)''''. His son, Richard Holt, also known as Wysham Holt was born in Holt, Worcestershire, England in 1370. He married Cri
2 CONC stine Coldrey and had a son with her named Richard. This son Richard was born around 1420. He married Joan Collingbourne (Darrell) and had two issue: Christian (Berkeley) and Elizabeth (Pownde).
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Reference •	https://coadb.com/surnames/holt-arms.html
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
