1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Agnes Crophulle is left money in the 1382 will of Sybille de la Bere, widow of Sir Richard de la Bere [who also died in 1382]
2 CONT
2 CONT *9 Richard II Proof of Age taken at Hereford, Saturday after St Matthew. Agnes, daughter of Thomas Crophull son of John Crophull. Writ to the escheator to take proof of age of the said Agnes, kinswoman and heir of the said John Cr
2 CONC ophull, whom Walter Deveros has taken to wife, warning Roger son of John Crophull son of John Crophull, in whose custody by the king’s commitment is one part of the lands of her inheritance, to be present and show just cause why t
2 CONC he said lands should not be restored to her 12 September 9 Richard II. The said Roger was warned and was present at the proof, but had nothing to say against it.  William Gerneston, William Pipe and William Smyth, aged 60 years an
2 CONC d more, say the said Agnes was born at the manor of Chabbenore and baptised in the church at Dilwyn on the second day after the feast of the Annunciation 45 Edward III [27 March 1371]. This they remember because on the same day th
2 CONC ey were in the company of Henry Bailly when he told of the birth of Joan his daughter, so they know that Agnes is 14 years of age and more. Walter Disshewal, Thomas Monyton and Henry Bailly, aged 50 years and more, agree and say t
2 CONC hat onthe day of the birth of the said Agnes, Walter Disshewall started on a pilgrimage to Santiago. Roger Crompe, William Carsewall and John Upton, aged 48 year and more, agree and say that on the same day Roger Crompe took to wi
2 CONC fe Joan, daughter of William Carsewall. William Chabbenore, Henry de la Coumbe and John Bradeley, aged 40 years and more, agree and say that on the same day William Chabbenore sold to John Bradeley a bugage tenement with curtilage
2 CONC  in Webbeley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Agnes Crophull1,2,3,4,5,6,7
2 CONT *'''F, #21887, b. circa 1372, d. 3 February 1436
2 CONT *Father      Sir Thomas de Crophull2,3,4,5,6,7 b. c 1350, d. 18 Nov 1381
2 CONT *Mother     Sibilla de la Bere2,3,4,5,6,7 b. 19 May 1338, d. b 18 Nov 1381
2 CONT *'''     Agnes Crophull was born circa 1372 at the Manor of Chaddenore, Herefordshire, England; Age 9 in 1381 & age 12 in 1383.5,6,7 She married Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Constable of Builth Castle''', son of 
2 CONC Sir William Devereux, Seneschal of Limousin and Anne Barre, '''before 1 November 1382 at of Braunston, Cotesbach, Hemington in Lockington, & Newbold Verdun, Leicestershire, England; They had 4 son''' (Sir Walter, John, Richard, & 
2 CONC Thomas) '''and 2 daughters''' (Elizabeth, wife of John Milborne, Esq; & Margaret).2,3,4,5,6,7 '''Agnes Crophull married Sir John Parr''', son of Sir William Parr and Elizabeth Roos, '''between 20 June 1401 and 1405; They had 1 son
2 CONC ''' (Sir Thomas).2,4,5,7 '''Agnes Crophull married John Merbury, Esq., Justice of South Wales, Sheriff & Escheater of Herefordshire, Steward of Brecon''', son of Sir Thomas Merbery, '''before March 1417; No issue.2,3,4,5,6,7 Agnes
2 CONC  Crophull died on 3 February 1436.2,3,4,5,6
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Constable of Builth Castle''' b. c 1359, d. 20 Jun 1401
