1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HEREFORDSHIRE AND THE ADJACENT MARCH OF WALES  Inquisition . Leominster  19 Feb. 1400. [Maunce]. Webley , 1/2 fee held by John de la Bere, esquire .
2 CONT
2 CONT Inquisition Post Mortem John de la Bere of Hereford and the adjacent Marches of Wales. 11 Henry IV [30 September 1409-29 September 1410. C 137/79/36 In Latin. Heir is Thomas de la Bere aged 7 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN DE LA BERE 743 Writ mandamus . ‡ 20 April 1410 [Wissyngsete]. <http://www.inquisitionspostmortem.ac.uk/view/inquisition/19-743> Regarding lands held of Thomas, late earl Marshal, son and heir of Thomas, late duke of Norfolk, 
2 CONC a minor in royal custody. HEREFORDSHIRE AND THE ADJACENT MARCH OF WALES . Inquisition  Hereford  2 May. [ap Harry]. Jurors: John Schellewik ; Hugh Watyes ; John Broyne ; Philip Fourches ; John Welynton ; William Forster ; Hugh Han
2 CONC ebury ; John Ward ; Richard Smyth of Leominster ; John Payn ; Hugh Benet ; and John Chaundos . He held a fortified manor called Webley  in the lordship of Gower  called ‘Gowereslond’ in Wales of Thomas late Earl Marshal , son and 
2 CONC heir of the duke of Norfolk , then under age in the king’s ward, by knight service of the castle and lordship of Swansea  ; annual values, the site nil because the house and buildings were destroyed by the rebels, the manor 30s. H
2 CONC e died on 24 Sept. 1403 . Thomas his son and heir is aged 9 years. John Seint Johan, knight , has held and taken the profits, title unknown. C 137/79/36 mm. 1-2
2 CONT
2 CONT The death of his kinsman, John de la Bere, in May 1409 [IPM date. Death actually 24 Sep 1403], brought him [John st John] temporary custody of all the latter’s possessions in Glamorgan; and when the next heir, Thomas, a royal ward
2 CONC , died without issue five years later the entire inheritance was duly partitioned, one half going to St. John’s cousin, John Basset, and the other to the MP himself. https://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/membe
2 CONC r/st-john-sir-john-1360-1424
2 CONT
