1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#WilliamLacyMdauLlywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.         WILLIAM de Lacy (-killed in battle Monach-cranncain 1233).  King John ordered the delivery of "William de Lascy to Walter de Lascy his brother…" after he gave assurances about his loyalty, dated 10 Feb 1215[861].  King 
2 CONC Henry III commanded "William de Lacy" to deliver "the castles of Rath and Carlingeford which he had taken" dated [Jan] 1217[862].  A report from William Marshall Earl of Pembroke to Henry III King of England, dated 5 Aug 1224, rec
2 CONC ords that he besieged "the castle of Trum…with William de Lascy its lord…conquered him and he with difficulty escaped, he had a brother killed there…[and] the castle was abandoned"[863].  The Annals of Ulster record in 1233 that "
2 CONC William de Lacy and Charles, son of Cathal Ua Conchobuir and many foreigners were killed by the Muinnter-Raighillaigh in Monach-cranncain”[864].  m GWENLLIAN of Wales, illegitimate daughter of LLYWELYN "Fawr/the Great" Prince of W
2 CONC ales & his mistress --- (-1281).  In his report to King Henry dated 5 Aug 1224 following the capture of castle Trum, William Marshall Earl of Pembroke records that "the wife of William de Lascy, the daughter of Llewllyn, Griffin´s
2 CONC  sister, the wife of Thomas Blund, William´s brother, and the mother of William, of Thomas, and of him that was killed" were in the castle[865]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT See papers by E. G. Lloyd on "Who was Gwenllian de Lacy?" in Arch. Cambrensis (July, 1919):
2 CONT
2 CONT "William 'Gorm'" married this daughter of Llewellyn the Great but left no issue by her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also see "A history of Medieval Ireland from 1086 to 1513" by Edmund Curtis, p. 135:
2 CONT
2 CONT "The annals of Ulster record in 1233 the death of William de Lacy. His welsh wife Gwenllian survived him and returned to Wales, but they left no issue".
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Llewelyn_the_Great
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Dafydd ap Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gruffydd ap Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Elen ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gwladus Ddu
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marared ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT ============ Gwenllian ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Angharad ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Susanna ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT According to represented data "William 'Gorm'" and Gwenllian, daughter of Llewellyn, had no mutual clildren. This is fact from independent sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT But at the same time we have other version, record in "The Legacy of the de Lacy, Lacey, Lacy Family 1066-1994", p. 56: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "He did miss his association with his half-brother William de Lacy. William
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== married the elder sister!!! of Llewellyn,
2 CONT
2 CONT the rebellious Prince of Wales, and William's activities absorbed in Leinster and Limerick...
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== William married Gwenllian or Gwendoline, or Winnefred as she variously called.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== Gwellian was sister!!! to Llewellyn, the paramount Prince of Wales,
2 CONT
2 CONT who kept wales in open rebellion to British rule for two generations".
2 CONT
2 CONT Last version is also based upon:
2 CONT ====De Lacy-Bellingari, Edward de Lacy-Harnett, The roll of the house of Lacy : pedigrees, military memoirs and synoptical history of the ancient and illustrious family of De Lacy from the earliest times, in all its branches, to t
2 CONC he present day.
