1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domhnall_I,_Earl_of_Mar accessed 31 May 2025
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Domhnall I, Earl of Mar''', also known by the name Domhnall mac Uilleim (Anglicized as "Donald, William's son"), was the seventh known mormaer of Mar in medieval Scotland, ruling from the death of his father, Uilleam of Mar, in
2 CONC  1276 until his own death sometime between 1297 and 1302. If Gille Críst is excluded, Domhnall I is considered the sixth mormaer or Earl of Mar.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1284, he joined with other Scottish noblemen who acknowledged Margaret of Norway as the heir to King Alexander III.[1] Domhnall was later a strong supporter of the Bruce cause during the crisis of the late 13th century. He was 
2 CONC at Norham in 1292, probably in the camp of Robert de Brus, then Earl of Carrick.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Domhnall married Helen after 1266 (sometimes called Ellen or Elen), the widow of Maol Choluim II, Earl of Fife. It has been claimed that she was a daughter of Llywelyn the Great of Wales, though genealogical inconsistencies make i
2 CONC t more likely that this was actually an unnamed first wife of the Earl of the Fife.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT By Helen, he had three sons and two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gartnait,_Earl_of_Mar Gartnait], his eldest son and successor, became the 8th Earl of Mar
2 CONT * Duncan of Mar
2 CONT * Alexander of Mar, imprisoned in the Tower of London on 12 December 1297 along with Edward Baliol, son of King John
2 CONT *[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabella_of_Mar Isabella of Mar], married Robert I of Scotland as his first wife, mother of Marjorie Bruce, who married Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland. Marjorie was the mother of Rober
2 CONC t II of Scotland, the first king of Scotland from the Royal House of Stuart.
2 CONT * Margaret of Mar (also called Marjory), married John of Strathbogie, 9th Earl of Atholl
2 CONT The last surviving record of Domhnall dates to 1297, and the earliest record of his son Gartnait as Earl dates to 1305; therefore, it is believed that Domhnall died sometime between these two dates. However, a document dating to 1
2 CONC 302[3] suggests that Domhnall had just died. The document contains terms of reconciliation between Edward I of England and Robert the Bruce, and stipulates that Robert should act as warden of Gartnait.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT SCOTLAND, MORMAERS, EARLS, LORDS
2 CONT v5.0 Updated 26 March 2025
2 CONT Chapter 5.                MAR
2 CONT A.         MORMAERS of MAR
2 CONT B.         EARLS of MAR
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#DonaldMardied1297B
2 CONT
2 CONT '''DONALD, son of WILLIAM Earl of Mar & his first wife Elizabeth Comyn of Buchan''' (-after 25 Jul 1297).  "Willelmus comes de Mar" confirmed the donations of "ecclesiam de Taruelond…de Migueth" made by "dñs Morgrundus avus noster
2 CONC …dña Agnes avia nostra quondam comitissa de Mar" to St Andrew’s priory by charter dated 23 Jan 1267 witnessed by "…Douenaldo Duncano filiis eiusdem comitis…"[506].  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "Doven
2 CONC aldus filius Willelmi comitis de Mar" was knighted "die Sancti Michaelis apud Sconam" in 1270[507].  He succeeded his father as Earl of Mar.  Donald Earl of Mar agreed the marriage of Margaret Pss of Scotland to Erik of Norway, da
2 CONC ted 25 Jul 1281[508].  He swore fealty to Edward I King of England as his overlord 13 Jun 1291, but was active in the Scottish revolt against England.  He was taken prisoner at the battle of Dunbar 27 Apr 1296, but did homage to t
2 CONC he English king after the submission of John Balliol in Jul 1296[509]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (after 1266) as her second husband, HELEN, widow of MALCOLM Macduff Earl of Fife, daughter of --- (-after 16 Feb 1295). The second marriage of the widow of Malcolm Earl of Fife is confirmed by the documents under which "Elenæ co
2 CONC mitissæ de Marre" accounted for payment of "xl s pro parte dotis suæ" in the accounts of lands formerly belonging to Duncan Earl of Fife 20 Nov 1293 and 16 Feb 1294[510].  However, it is not certain that this widow of Earl Malcolm
2 CONC  was the same person as his wife who was the daughter of Prince Llywelyn.  The birth of Earl Malcolm’s son Colban is estimated to [1244/46].  However, Earl Malcolm’s widow had four known children by her second husband.  This would
2 CONC  mean that she gave birth to children over an approximately thirty year span, which although not impossible would be unusual.  In addition, it seems unlikely that Earl Donald would have married, as his first marriage, a woman who 
2 CONC would have been more than 35 years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Donald & his wife had [five] children:
2 CONT * 1.         GRATNEY (-before Sep 1305).  '''He succeeded his father in 1297 as Earl of Mar.'''  m (1292 or after) as her first husband, CHRISTIAN Bruce, … She married secondly Christopher Seton, and thirdly (dispensation 20 Sep 1
2 CONC 326, Cambuskenneth 1326) Andrew Moray of Bothwell.   …  
2 CONT * 2.         DUNCAN (-after Aug 1296).  The Ragman Roll names "…Duncan fiz le Comte de Mar…" among those who swore allegiance to Edward I King of England at Berwick-upon-Tweed 28 Aug 1296[534].  
2 CONT * 3.         ISABEL of Mar (-before 1302).  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "Robertus…rex, quuando fuit comes de Carric" married "Isabellam sororem Garthenai comitis de Marr"[535].  m ([1295]) as his fir
2 CONC st wife, ROBERT Bruce Earl of Carrick, son of ROBERT de Brus, Earl of Carrick, Lord of Annandale & his first wife Margaret Ctss of Carrick (Writtle, near Chelmsford, Essex 11 Jul 1274-Cardross Castle, Dumbartonshire 7 Jun 1329, bu
2 CONC r Dunfermline Abbey, Fife).  He succeeded in 1306 as ROBERT I King of Scotland.  
2 CONT * 4.         MARGARET of Mar (-after [13 Dec 1309?]). … m JOHN of Strathbogie Earl of Atholl, son of DAVID of Strathbogie Earl of Atholl & his second wife Isabel of Chilham (-executed London 7 Nov 1306).  
2 CONT * 5.         [MARGARET of Mar .  She is named as wife of Malcolm Earl of Lennox by Fraser[539].  She may have been the daughter or the sister of Donald Earl of Mar.  m MALCOLM Earl of Lennox, son of MALCOLM Earl of Lennox & his wi
2 CONC fe --- (-killed in battle Halidon Hill 19 Jul 1333).]  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#WilliamMardied1281
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM (-<25 Jul 1281, maybe <Jan 1279) Earl of Mar. 
2 CONT s/o DUNCAN, (s/o MORGUND Earl of Mar & his [first wife Agnes ---]) (-[1242/7 Feb 1244]) Earl of Mar. & NN 
2 CONT x ELIZABETH Comyn, d/o WILLIAM Comyn Earl of Buchan &  Margaret Ctss of Buchan (-[1265/66]). 
2 CONT *'''DONALD''' (->25 Jul 1297) Earl of Mar x >1266 HELEN, wid/o MALCOLM Macduff Earl of Fife, d/o NN (->16 Feb 1295). 
2 CONT *'''DUNCAN''' (->Aug 1296) x  CHRISTINE, d/o NN
2 CONT xx (>1267) MURIEL of Strathearn, d/o MALISE Earl of Strathearn &  Marjory de Muschamp of Wooler ([1244]-[16 May/12 Nov] 1291).  
