2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Mar was the widow of John de Strathbogie, 9th Earl of Atholl. Kenneth 4th Earl of Sutherland was her second husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#IsabelMarMRobertIBrucedied1329
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         MARGARET of Mar (-after 1306).  A charter dated 3 Sep 1296 records petitions to King Edward I by women whose estates had been seized in Scotland, including an order of restoration of property to "la contesse de Atheles"
2 CONC [496].  "Gilbertus de Haia constabularius Scotie" confirmed donations to Cupar abbey, including the donation made by "Mariore comitisse Atholie, relicte quondam Johannis comitis Atholie et confirmatione David filii sui primogeniti
2 CONC  et heredis", by charter dated 5 Oct 1309[497].  m JOHN of Strathbogie Earl of Atholl, son of DAVID of Strathbogie Earl of Atholl & his second wife Isabel of Chilham (-executed London 7 Nov 1306). 
2 CONT
