2 CONT Joan de Braose, surnamed Tadody, had been privately nursed by a Welsh wom an at Gower. This John had grants of lands from King Henry III and was al so possessed of the Barony of Brembye, in Sussex, where he died in 123 1, by a fal
2 CONC l from his horse, his foot sticking in the stirrup. He marrie d, it is stated, Margaret, dau. of Llewellyn, Prince of Wales, by whom (w ho m. afterwards Walter de Clifford) he had a son, his successor, Willi am de Braose. [Sir Ber
2 CONC nard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited and Extin ct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, England, 1883, p. 72, Braos e, Baron Braose, of Gower]
2 CONT
2 CONT    Events:
