2 CONT  Sir William "1st Lord Brewes" de Braose 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1224 in Bramber, Sussex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John (Braose) de Brewes and Margaret (ferch Llywelyn) de Clifford
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Lucia (Clifford) de Saye [half], John (Braose) de Braose [half], Llywelyn (Braose) de Braose [half], Roger (Braose) de Braose [half], Hugh (Braose) de Braose [half], Richard (Braose) de Brewes Knt, Maud (Clifford) Giffa
2 CONC rd [half], Emma (Clifford) de Clifford [half] and Roger (Clifford) de Clifford [half]	
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Aline (Multon) Braose — married 1245 in Gower, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Agnes (Moels) de Brewes — married 1268 in Cadbury, Somersetshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Ros) de Braose — married 1271 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Margaret (Braose) de Braose, William (Braose) de Brewes Knt, Eleanor (Braose) de Braose, Giles (Braose) de Braose, Richard (Braose) de Brewes, Peter (Braose) de Braose and William (Braose) de Braose	
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 6 Jan 1291 in Findon, Sussex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT  Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT     William de Brewes, Knight, son and heir of John de Brewes, Knight was of full age 15 July 1245 (born about 1224).[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages
2 CONT
2 CONT     m.1 Aline de Multon 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Aline de Multon is William's first wife. Her parents are Thomas de Multon, of Burgh-on-Sands, Cumberland and Maud, dau. and heiress of Hubert de Vaux. They had one son:[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     William, 2nd Lord Brewes[1][2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     m.2 Agnes de Moels 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Agnes de Moels is William's second wife. Her parents are Nicholas de Moels and Hawise, daughter of James de Newmarch. They had one son:[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Sir Giles, Knt.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     m.3 (ante or during 1271) Mary de Roos 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mary de Roos is William's third wife. They married during or before 1271. Her parents are Sir Robert d Roos, Knt. and Isabel, dau. and heiress of William d'Aubeney.[1] They had three sons and 2 more daughters:[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Richard? (does NOT appear in Richardson Royal Ancestry) 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Sir Peter, knt.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     and allegedly William? (does NOT appear in Richardson Royal Ancestry) 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Margaret[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     dau. ____. (does NOT appear in Richardson Royal Ancestry) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT     "Sir William de Brewes, 1st Lord Brewes, died at Findon, Sussex 6 Jan 1290/1, and was buried at Sell, Sussex 15 January following."[1] (Findon is about six west of Bramber in Sussex.) 
2 CONT
