1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Page 281 of ''The Complete Peerage'' (2nd edition, vol.9) states:===
2 CONT "[RALPH DE MORTIMER, s. and h. ap., accompanied his father to the "Parl." of 1271. He succeeded his uncle, Hugh de Mortimer of Chelmarsh, as '''sheriff of Shropshire and Staffordshire, 23 Jan. 1272/3''', being appointed while his 
2 CONC father, as co-trustee of the absent King, was practically co-Regent. He ''d. v.p.'', '''and apparently unm'''., before 10 Aug. 1274.]"
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ”RALPH (-before 10 Aug 1274). A manuscript narrating the foundation of Wigmore Abbey names “Radulphum primogenitum militem” as son of “domina Matilda…[et] Rogero de Mortuomari”, adding that he predeceased his father. He succeeded 
2 CONC his uncle Hugh de Mortimer of Chelmarsh 23 Jan 1273 as sheriff of Shropshire and Staffordshire.“[1] [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL2.htm#RogerMortimerdied1247]
2 CONT ----
