1 NOTE He succeeded his father in the 18th year of the reign of Edward I. He spent the next year doing homage. He had livery of his lands. He was constantly employed in the Welsh wars. He was summoned to Pariliament as a Baron from 8 Jun
2 CONC  1294 to 2 Jun 1302. He was mortally wounded in 1303 at the Battle of Buelt against the Welsh.
1 NOTE He succeeded his father in the 18th year of the reign of Edward I. He spent the next year doing homage. He had livery of his lands. He was constantly employed in the Welsh wars. He was summoned to Pariliament as a Baron from 8 Jun
2 CONC  1294 to 2 Jun 1302. He was mortally wounded in 1303 at the Battle of Buelt against the Welsh.
