2 CONT iv)        [ALICE Corbet .  A manuscript relating to Ranton Priory, Staffordshire records that “Johanni de Harecourt” married secondly “Aliciam filiam domini Petri Corbet de Caus” after the death of his first wife[2030].  Both the
2 CONC  chronology and her name suggest that Alice may have been born from her father’s second marriage.  A writ dated 2 May "4 Edw III" and inquisitions 18 May “4 Edw III”, after the death of "John de Harecurt", do not name his widow[20
2 CONC 31], suggesting that she may have predeceased her husband.  m as his second wife, JOHN de Harcourt, son of RICHARD [II] de Harcourt & his first wife Margaret Beke (-before 2 May 1330).] 
