1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''[https://www.geni.com/people/Olaf-I-Morsel-King-of-Man-the-Isles/6000000001744995580 OLAV of Man], son of ([1080]-murdered 29 Jun 1153).  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum names “Lagmannum, Haraldum et Olavum” a
2 CONC s the three sons of [https://www.geni.com/people/Godred-Crovan-King-of-the-Isle-of-Man-and-of-Dublin/1341991?through=6000000001744995580  “Godredus Crovan”] [1288].  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum records that “Murecardum O’Bri
2 CONC en regem Hibernie” sent “Dompnaldum filium Tade” to island as regent for Olav after the death of Lagman, dating the event to 1111[1289].  King of Man.  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum records that the regent ruled for three year
2 CONC s with great tyranny until he was expelled to the Ireland by the people of Man[1290].  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum records that Olav was recalled from exile at the court of Henry I King of England in 1114 and ruled for forty
2 CONC  years[1291].  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum records that King Olav in 1134 gave land in the Isle of Man to Yvo Abbot of Furness on which to build the abbey of Rushen[1292].  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum records that “tre
2 CONC s filii Haraldi fratris Olavi” who had been brought up in Dublin demanded part of the kingdom of the Isles from their paternal uncle King Olav and that one of them “Reginald” murdered his uncle, dating the murder to 29 Jun 1153 in
2 CONC  a later passage[1293].''' 
