2 CONT
2 CONT * Olaf I Godredsson : Gudrødsønn
2 CONT *Olaf I Bitling the Red = Olaf I Morsel
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.dictionary.com/browse/morsel
2 CONT (Irish, informal) a term of endearment for a child (the little boy). Olaf I was the last born child of Godred IV Crovan (Orry). To be the youngest is not necessarily to be a dwarf!  
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, '''the free encyclopedia'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Olav I was King of Mann and the Isles from 1104 until 1153. His nickname was Morsel. He was born around 1080 and died 29 June 1153.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was King Godred Crovan. He succeeded, either together or after, his one or two brothers. Lagman who held the throne at between 1103-04 apparently was his (eldest) brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Reign'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Norway's Kings Magnus Barefoot and Sigurd Jorsalafare annexed the kingdom and caused disruption in successions. For forty years Olaf ruled them uncontested.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Kingdom of Mann and the Isles encompassed the Isle of Man and the Hebrides, extending from the Calf of Man to the Butt of Lewis. Olaf adopted the Latin style Rex Manniae et Insularum in his charters, a translation of the Gaeli
2 CONC c title ri Innse Gall (literally 'king of the foreigners' isles'), which had been in use since the late 10th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT The islands which were under his rule were called the Sullr-eyjar (Sudreys or the south isles, in contradistinction to the Norsr-eyjar, or the "north isles," i.e. the Orkneys and Shetlands, and they consisted of the Hebrides, and 
2 CONC of all the smaller western islands of Scotland, with Mann.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf I exercised considerable power, and according to the Chronicles of Mann, maintained such close alliance with the kings of Ireland and Scotland that no one ventured to disturb the Isles during his time (1104 - 1153).
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1130s the Church sent a small mission to establish the first bishopric on the Isle of Man, and appointed Wimund as the first bishop. He soon after gave up his role as fisher-of-men, and became the hunter-of-men, embarking w
2 CONC ith a band of followers on a career of murder and looting throughout Scotland and the surrounding islands.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the whole of the Scandinavian period the isles remained nominally under the suzerainty of the kings of Norway, but the Norwegians only occasionally asserted it with any vigour. Magnus Barfod about 1100 conquered the isles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage & Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf's first wife was Aufrica of Galloway, who bore herself and him a son and successor, Godred Olafsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife was Ingeborg Haakonsdottir, daughter of Haakon, Earl of the Orkneys. This marriage produced at least daughter Ragnhild, who married Somerled, King of Kintyre and the Isles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginald, Lagmann and Harald are mentioned as his other sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT After half a century of reign, Olaf I was killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Head of State of the Isle of Man
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Lagmann 	King of Mann and the Isles
2 CONT
2 CONT 1104 - 1153 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Succeeded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Godred II
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf was King of Man and Lord of the Isles. He was murdered by his nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf Gudrodson - Because of his small stature he was called "Olaf Dwarf". King of Man from 1113 to 1153. Olaf was raised in the English Court but returned to the Isle of Man in 1113. His first wife was the daughter of the Earl of 
2 CONC Galloway, and his second wife was Ingeborg, daughter of Hakon Paalsen, Earl of the Orkney Islands. A nephew of Olaf’s attacked him during a meeting and cut off his head.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alias/AKA Olav Bitling (Dverg) Kung av Suderöarna
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Familj med: Ingeborg Håkonsdotter (ca 1099-1126), dotter till jarlen Håkon Pålsson (1075-1126) på Orkneyöarna
2 CONT
2 CONT Dottern Ragnhild (Ayla) Olofsdotter blev gift med Sumerled Mac Gillabride, som var kung på Isle of Man och Hebriderna 1153-1164.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Källa: Regentlängd för Isle of Man)
2 CONT
2 CONT Vigsel: efter 1115 3)
2 CONT
2 CONT Familj med Afreca av GALLOWAY (1099 - 1130)
2 CONT
2 CONT Vigsel: omkring 1127 4)
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn: Gudröd II OLOFSSON (1127 - 1187)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Noteringar'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf kallas också för Olav 'the Dwarf (Dvärg)'.
2 CONT
2 CONT Galloway är ett landskap i sydvästra delen av Skottland och gränsar till Isle of Mans nordligaste del. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He took a wife named Affrica, daughter of Fergus of Galloway by whom he had issue Godred. He had also many concubines, by whom he had issue three sons, Reginald, Lagman and Harold, and many daughters, one of whom was married to Su
2 CONC merled, Lord of Argyll; and this was the cause of the ruin of the whole kingdom of the Isles, for he had issue by her four sons, Dugald, Reginald, Angus and Olave, of whom we shall speak more fully hereafter. (Källa: May Teistevol
2 CONC l)
2 CONT
2 CONT Kung Isle of Man och Hebriderna 1103-1153. (Källa: Regentlängd för Isle of Man)
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf was killed in 1154 at Ramsey. Now, Chronicle says that his son Godred had, just before that, gone to Norway to King Inge; made himself his man and, next autumn, on his return, put in at Orkney, 'and all the chiefs of the Isle
2 CONC s, hearing that he had come, were delighted'. He was in fact a connection. Godred from there came to Man, and turned out his cousins who had killed his father Olaf; blinded two of them, killed the third this maintaining a connecti
2 CONC on with Orkney at that date I think in harmony with my general view of Olaf´s connection with the family of the Saint. (Källa: Frances Coakley)
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf was brought up at the court of Henry I of England. (Källa: Frances Coakley)
2 CONT
2 CONT Källor
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Landsarkivets bibliotek, G.V.C. Young, Isle of Man, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Stewart Baldwin, England (webbplats)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Frances Coakley, England (epost)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Beräkning av Björn Espell, Frösön
2 CONT
2 CONT Senast uppdat. 010603
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT King of the Isle of Man
2 CONT
