2 CONT "'''Madog Llwyd''' the eldest son of '''Gruffydd''' of Maelor Saesneg, married three times; by his first wife '''Catherine''', daughter of '''Owain Barton''' of Chester, he had a son and heir '''David ab Madog''', of whom presentl
2 CONC y. He married, secondly, '''Lleuci''', daughter of '''Iorwerth Fychan ab Iorwerth ab Awr ab Ieuaf ab Niniaw ab Cynwrig ab Rhiwallon''' (''ermine, a lion rampant sable''), by whom he had issue one son, '''David ab Madog''' (see Bod
2 CONC ylltyn), and four daughters, 1, '''Cari''', ux. '''John Hoord''', Lord of Walverton, co. Salop (''azure, on a chief or, an owl sable''); 2, '''Annest''', ux. '''Sir... Roydon''' of Kent; 3, '''Dygoes''', ux. '''Howel ab Gruffydd a
2 CONC b Iorwerth Fychan''' of Groes Foel; and 4, '''Margaret''', ux. '''Thomas Roydon'''. Madog Llwyd married, thirdly, '''Gwerfyl''', daughter of '''Ednyfed ab Gruffydd ab Llywelyn ab Gruffydd''', by whom he had a son '''leuan ab Madog
2 CONC  of Rhuddallt'''"
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''': Jacob Youde William Lloyd, [http://books.google.com/books?id=xh0fAAAAMAAJ The history of the princes, the lords marcher, and the ancient nobility of Powys Fadog, and the ancient lords of Arwystli, Cedewen, and Meirio
2 CONC nydd, Volume 3]
