1 OCCU commander of the Welsh Marches between 1223 and 1246, Sheriff of Shropshire between 1227 and 1232, Custodian of Chester and Beeston Castle., Sheriff of Shropshire, Sheriff of Shropshire and staffordshire, Sheriff, Sherriff of Shro
2 CONC pshire
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry of Aldithley was born circa 1175.1 He was the son of Adam of Aldithley and Emma fitz Orm.1 He married Bertred Mainwaring, daughter of Ralf Mainwaring, in 1217.1 He died in 1246.1
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1214 he bought large estates from Eleanor Malbank.1 He held the office of Under Sheriff of Shropshire between 1217 and 1220.1 In 1223 he founded Hulton Abbey.1 He was commander of the Welsh Marches between 1223 and 1246.1 In 12
2 CONC 27 he acquired the manors of Edgmund and Newport, Shropshire.1 He held the office of Sheriff of Shropshire between 1227 and 1232.1 In 1230 he acquired the manor of Ford, Shropshire.1 He held the office of Custodian of Chester and 
2 CONC Beeston Castle on 22 June 1237.1 He built the castle of Heleigh, Staffordshire, and the Red Castle, Shropshire.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Henry of Aldithley and Bertred Mainwaring
2 CONT
2 CONT     * James of Aldithley+1 b. c 1220, d. c 11 Jun 1272
2 CONT     * Ralf of Aldithley1 b. c 1220, d. b 1240
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Ex
2 CONC tinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 337. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 	Audley of Staffordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam de Aldithley [a] b abt 1145, d 1203-1211. He md Emma abt 1166, daughter of Ralph Fitz Orm. She was b abt 1150.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Adam de Aldithley and Emma was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Aldithley [b], Sheriff of Shropshire and Staffordshire, b abt 1172, of Heleigh, Staffordshire, England, d sh bef Nov 1246. He md Bertrade de Mainwaring 1217, daughter of Sir Ralph de Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester, and 
2 CONC Amicia le Meschin. She was b abt 1198, d aft 1249.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Henry de Aldithley and Bertrade de Mainwaring were:
2 CONT
2 CONT James de Audley, Justiciar of Ireland, b abt 1220.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice de Aldithley b abt 1224, of Heleigh, Staffordshire, England, d aft Aug 1265. She md Sir Piers de Montfort abt 1238, son of Thurstan de Montfort and Daughter de Cantelou.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma de Aldithley b abt 1226, of Heleigh, Staffordshire, England. She md Sir Gruffydd ap Madog, Lord of Bromfield, abt 1244, son of Madog ap Gruffydd-Maelor and Gwladys verch Ithel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Aldithley or Audley had large possessions given him
2 CONT
2 CONT by Nicholas de Verdon whose Arms he also bore. He was Lord
2 CONT
2 CONT of Heleigh Castle, Com. Staff and justice of England died 1275
2 CONT
2 CONT (Reference A. Cart ii Henry III Ex ipsius Sigillo in Bib.Cotton.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Bertred, dau. Of Ralph de Meifnilwarin or Manwaring,
2 CONT
2 CONT of Chester. (Had issue)
2 CONT
2 CONT I) Ranulph de Aldithley first son. Ob. Vita Patris (died before
2 CONT
2 CONT father)
2 CONT
2 CONT II) James Aldithley, second son made Constable of Newcastle
2 CONT
2 CONT under Lyme 1251. Governor of the Castles of Salop and
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruges and Sheriff of Salop and Stafford 1261 &c Justice of
2 CONT
2 CONT Ireland 1263. Killed by a fall from his horse 1272. Vita Patris.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Reference B Rot Claus et Pat Temp Hen III). Married ??????
2 CONT
2 CONT dau of ?????????. (Had issue)
2 CONT
2 CONT i) James de Aldithley first son Ob S. P.(died without issue)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1273 (Reference C Rot. Fin I Edw I)
2 CONT
2 CONT ii) Henry de Aldithley second son Ob.S.P.(died without
2 CONT
2 CONT issue). 1276 (Reference D Esch 4 Edw I)
2 CONT
2 CONT iii) William de Aldithley third son slain in Wales unmar
2 CONT
2 CONT 1282 (Reference E Esch ii Edw I T Walsingham)
2 CONT
2 CONT iv) Nicholas de Aldithley, fourth son Sum to Parl. As
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron 26 Jan 25 Edw I 1297 died 1299. (Reference F
2 CONT
2 CONT Rot Claus 25 Edw I Esch 27 Edw I). Married
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine dau and coheir of John Gifford of
2 CONT
2 CONT Brimesfield, by Maud his Wife dau and heir of
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Baron Clifford, and Widow of Will
2 CONT
2 CONT Longespee.www.celtic-casimir.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry DE AUDLEY
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 1175, Haleigh Castle, Audley, Stafford, England 
2 CONT Married: 1217 
2 CONT Died: Before Nov 1246
2 CONT
2 CONT Another name for Henry was Henry of Aldithley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT Henry married Bertred (Bertrade) DE MAINWARING, daughter of Sir Ralph DE MAINWARING Seneschal and Amicia Le Meschines DE KEVELIOCK, in 1217. (Bertred (Bertrade) DE MAINWARING was born about 1197 in Mainwaring, Bersted, Essex, Engl
2 CONC and, died after 1249 and was buried in Hulton Abbey, Staffordshire, England.)
2 CONT
