1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Medlands: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands//ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#BertradeMainwaringMHenryAudley England, Earls Created 1067-1122]
2 CONT ** "ii) BERTRADE Mainwaring (-after 1249). “''Radulfus de Meidnilwar''” granted “''Smelewde...et Snellest...et dimid Pichemere''...” to “''Henrico de Alditelegh in liberum maritagium cum Bertrea filia mea''” by undated charter, wi
2 CONC tnessed by “''Ran com Cestr, Hug com Ultoniæ''...”[169]. Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by inquisitions after a writ dated 22 Apr "''4 Edw'' I", following the death of [her grandson] "Henry de Audidelegh..." which record
2 CONC  the manor of “Smalewode...given to Henry de Audithele grandfather of the said Henry” by “Thomas [error for Ralph?] de Meynwaryn as free marriage”[170]. '''m''' [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands//ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#HenryA
2 CONC udleydied1246 HENRY de Audley], son of ADAM de Audley & his wife Emma --- ([1175]-1246 before Nov)."
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Wikitree: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mainwaring-22  Bertrade (Mainwaring) de Audley (abt. 1196–aft. 1249)]
2 CONT
2 CONT –—————————
2 CONT Bertred Mainwaring was the daughter of Ralf Mainwaring.1 She married Henry of Aldithley, son of Adam of Aldithley and Emma fitz Orm, in 1217.1 She died after 1249.1 She was buried at Hulton Abbey.2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Bertred Mainwaring and Henry of Aldithley'''
2 CONT '''James''' of Aldithley+1 b. c 1220, d. c 11 Jun 1272
2 CONT '''Ralf''' of Aldithley1 b. c 1220, d. b 1240
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citations'''
2 CONT '''1.''' G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 337. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT '''2.''' Peter W. Hammond, editor, The Complete Peerage or a History of the House of Lords and All its Members From the Earliest Times, Volume XIV: Addenda & Corrigenda (Stroud, Gloucestershire, U.K.: Sutton Publishing, 1998), pag
2 CONC e 50. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage, Volume XIV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Abbey Hulton
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT '''1.''' Williams, Ann; G H Martin (2002). Domesday Book: A Complete Translation. London: Penguin. pp. pp. 681; 1303. ISBN 9780141439945.
2 CONT '''2.''' Domesday Book of 1086-7 as Heltone, in Pirehill Hundred, when it was held by Robert of Stafford.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Aldithley [b], Sheriff of Shropshire and Staffordshire, b abt 1172, of Heleigh, Staffordshire, England, d sh bef Nov 1246. He md Bertrade de Mainwaring 1217, daughter of Sir Ralph de Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester, and 
2 CONC Amicia le Meschin. She was b abt 1198, d aft 1249.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Henry de Aldithley and Bertrade de Mainwaring were:
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertrada Mainwaring Aldithley
2 CONT BIRTH	1197
2 CONT Bersted, Arun District, West Sussex, England
2 CONT DEATH	1249 (aged 51–52)
2 CONT Abbey Hulton, Stoke-on-Trent Unitary Authority, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Abbey of St Mary
2 CONT Abbey Hulton, Stoke-on-Trent Unitary Authority, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	67969203
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Rafe de Mainwaring (Meisnilwarin) and Amicia Hawise de Kevelioc. Granddaughter of Hugh de Keviloc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Henry de Aldithley, the son of Adam de Audley and Emma FitzOrm. They were married in 1217 and had two children:
2 CONT * Alice, wife of Peter de Montfort, Prolocutor
2 CONT * Emma, wife of Gruffydd ap Madog, Prince of Powys Fadog
2 CONT
2 CONT Other sources list a son, James born 1220.
2 CONT
