2 CONT He attacked Glyndwr after Glyndwr had killed his brother Hywel Sele, but survived, and was still alive in 1418; see https://books.google.com/books?id=aepTGZpT1FMC&pg=PA60-IA1&dq=gruffydd+derwas&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwji46X4mL3PAhVH
2 CONC 4WMKHT3MBzMQ6AEILTAD#v=onepage&q=gruffydd%20derwas&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT He is recorded in a Michalmas roll of Peniarth during the fourth year of the reign of King Henry V (1390) and was a Foreman of a Dolgelly Jury during the thirtieth year of the reign of King Henry VI (1451). ''citing'' "Powys-Land 
