2 CONC n of Cheshire Made in the Year 1566, by the Same Herald. With an Appendix, Containing the Visitation of a Part of Cheshire in the Year 1533, made by William Fellows, Lancaster Herald, for Thomas Benolte, Clarenceux King of Arms. A
2 CONC nd a Fragment of the Visitation of the City of Chester in the Year 1591, Made by Thomas Chaloner, Deputy to the Office of Arms, (London: Harleian Society, XVIII, 1882), 202, e-book Internet Archive (https://archive.org/details/vis
2 CONC itationofches00glov/page/202/mode/1up : accessed 2 June, 2022). Pedigree: Pro Savage.
