1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Batrtum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5559/puleston.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (March 2, 2017; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/4731/Hanmer%201.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (March 2, 2017; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Pulestons derived their name from the vill or manor of Pilston or Puleston, near Newport, Salop, where they were settled in the reign of Henry III, and continued to hold land at least until 1433.
2 CONT =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Puleston was a brother-in-law and supporter of Owain Glyndŵr, at the time of his rebellion against King Henry IV of England in the early 15th century and afterwards.   ....
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Puleston married Owain Glyndŵr's younger sister, Lowry. They had a son called ''''''John Puleston, whose will was proved in 1444. He married Angharad, a daughter of Griffith Hanmer, of the same family as Owain Glyndŵr's wif
2 CONC e, Margaret Hanmer. Angharad was a granddaughter of Gronw ap Tudor of Anglesey''''''. Another son, Roger Puleston (died 1469), who was a staunch ally of Jasper Tudor, Earl of Pembroke holding Denbigh Castle as Deputy Constable to 
2 CONC Jasper Tudor in 1460 and 1461.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT *http://www.robertsewell.ca/puleston.html
2 CONT * http://www.ffish.com/family_tree/Descendants_Roger_Puleston/D1.htm
2 CONT * http://www.puleston-jones.com/page21.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Puleston
2 CONT *_______________
