2 CONT Afandreg verch Gwair of Wales1
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 974
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Gwair ap Pill of Wales1,2 b. circa 949
2 CONT
2 CONT      Afandreg verch Gwair of Wales was born circa 974 at Aberffro, Malltraeth, Anglesey, Wales.1 She was the daughter of Gwair ap Pill of Wales.1,2 Afandreg verch Gwair of Wales married Brenin Gwynedd Iago ab Idwal o Gwynedd, son 
2 CONC of Brenin Gwynedd Idwal ap Meuric o Gwynedd and unknown (?), before 1014.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Brenin Gwynedd Iago ab Idwal o Gwynedd b. circa 974, d. 1039
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynan ab Iago, Prince of Gwynedd+ b. c 1014, d. 5 Aug 10631,3,4
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S245] LDS.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S483] Stewart Baldwin, Llywelyn ap Iorwerth's ancestors in "Baldwin-Llywelyn," listserve message Dec 1998, I consider this data doubtful..
2 CONT
2 CONT [S483] Stewart Baldwin, Llywelyn ap Iorwerth's ancestors in "Baldwin-Llywelyn," listserve message Dec 1998, "Afandreg ferch Wair ap Pyll ..." etc., a supposed descendant of the legendary Llywarch Hen through a string of unidentifi
2 CONC able names. I consider this data doubtful..
2 CONT
2 CONT [S489] Welsh genealogies, manuscript unknown repository, 6i.
