2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iago_ab_Idwal_ap_Meurig
2 CONT
2 CONT Iago ab Idwal ap Meurig From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Iago ab Idwal ap Meurig (died 1039) was a Prince of Gwynedd.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the death of Llywelyn ap Seisyll in 1023, the rule of Gwynedd returned to the ancient dynasty with the accession of Iago, who was a great-grandson of Idwal Foel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Very little is known about the reign of Iago. He was killed by his own men in 1039 and replaced by Llywelyn ap Seisyll's son, Gruffydd ap Llywelyn. Iago's grandson Gruffydd ap Cynan later won the throne of Gwynedd, and because his
2 CONC  father, Cynan ap Iago, was little known in Wales, Gruffydd was styled "grandson of Iago" rather than the usual "son of Cynan".
2 CONT
2 CONT References John Edward Lloyd (1911). A history of Wales: from the earliest times to the Edwardian conquest. Longmans, Green & Co. 
