1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Darrell Wolcott: Osbwrn Wyddel of Cors Gedol; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id203.html. (Steven Ferry, August 30, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: '''Gerald FitzMaurice Fitzgerald'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 1150 in Windsor, Berkshire, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 15 JAN 1202/03 in Offaly, Kildare, Ireland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  Gerald FitzMaurice FitzGerald, 1st Baron of Offaly (not a peerage of Parliament but a designation of the ancestors of the Earls of Kildare); c1150; took part in the conquest of Limerick c1197 and acquired Croom in that Co (
2 CONC hence the wording of the family motto); 
2 CONT
2 CONT married c1193 Eve (married 2nd Geoffrey FitzRobert (d 1211) and 3rd by Feb 1217/8 Geoffrey de Marisco/Mareis, Justiciar of Ireland, and died by Dec 1226), thought to have been daughter of Robert de Bermingham, by which marriage he
2 CONC  acquired the territorial Barony of Offaly (an entity wholly distinct from Ophelan aforementioned), though Offaly was in his wife's 3rd husband Geoffrey de Marisco's hands following her death (it was forfeited by Geoffrey in 1234,
2 CONC  however, and passed to Gerald's heir); Gerald died 1245. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: '''Maurice "The Invader" Fitzgerald Of Windsor''' b: ABT 1100 in Castle Carew, Pembrokeshire, Wales  Mother: '''Alice de Montgomery''' b: ABT 1115 in Munster, Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1''' Eve de Bermingham''' b: ABT 1172 in Offaly, Kildare, Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
