1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Maud de Bryan
2 CONT * AKA Maud de Brian
2 CONT *b. 25 December 1242, d. circa 1279 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud de Brian was born on 25 December 1242.1 She was the daughter of Guy de Brian and Eve de Tracy.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Nicholas Martin, son of Nicholas fitz Martin.1 on 1256 in Blagdon, Somerset, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Geoffrey de Canville, 1st Lord Canville, son of William de Canville and Lucy (?).1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died circa 1279.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Maud de Brian and Willam Martin: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *  		M	i	Sir William MARTIN Lord Martin was born 1257 and died Oct 1324.
2 CONT *  		M	ii	Warin MARTIN 1, 2, 3 was born 1260 in Blagdon, Somerset, England. He died after 1307.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Maud de Brian and Geoffrey de Canville, 1st Lord Canville 
2 CONT
2 CONT # William de Canville, 2nd Lord Canville+1 d. b 27 Jul 1338
2 CONT
2 CONT Richardson is very clear that https://www.geni.com/people/Amice-de-Camville/5598160038500116336?through=6000000000424760140 was the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Geoffrey-de-Camville-1st-Baron-Camville/600000000697117810
2 CONC 3?through=6000000000424760140 but not https://www.geni.com/people/Maud-de-Brian/6000000000424760140.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Heiress of her grandfather 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inquisition post Mortem'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.british-history.ac.uk/inquis-post-mortem/vol2/pp50-58
2 CONT
2 CONT C. Edw. I. File 6. (5.)
2 CONT 76.	[https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-de-Tracy-Lord-of-Barnstaple/6000000003858651174 Henry de Tracy].
2 CONT Writ, 21 Aug. 2 Edw. 1. [21 August 1274] 
2 CONT Devon.	Inq. and extent, Monday before the Nativity of the Blessed Virgin, 2 Edw. 1.
2 CONT Uppehesse. A hall, grange, chapel, lands &c. (extent given) held of the king in chief as member of the barony of Barnastap[le].
2 CONT Grenesnylche. A free tenant rendering 4s.; and 50a. arable held by the lord, of Sir Walter son of Payn of the fee of Wyr' by knight's service.
2 CONT Kelmeton. 33a. arable, 2a. meadow and 16s. rent from villeins, held of Walter de Merton of the fee of the countess of Devon by service of 1/5 knight's fee.
2 CONT ''[https://www.geni.com/people/Maud-de-Brian/6000000000424760140 Maud], daughter of his daughter, whom Geoffrey de Caunvile lately took to wife, aged 31 at Christmas in the said year, is his next heir.''  (Etc) 
