2 CONT ==Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000066987552835& Inquisition Post Mortem] for Griffith son and her of Owen de la Pole. Writ 25 June, 2 Edw. II [1309]. His death date is not recorded. He died before the 25 June 1309
2 CONC  (date of writ). Hawis his sister, aged 18 on the feast of St. James the Apostle last, is his next heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT June 17. 1310. Westminster.<br>
2 CONT To the treasurer and barons of the exchequer. Order to cause the king's yeoman Otto Ferre to have the 100 marks of the fine that Richard de Perers made with the king to obtain pardon for '''James de Perers''' for his trespass in '
2 CONC ''marrying without the king's licence Ela, late the wife of Griffin de la Pole''', a tenant in chief of the king, as the king had granted the said Otto what pertained to the king of the marriage of the said Ela, or any fine that s
2 CONC he might make with the king for her marriage, or any forfeiture thence arising if she should marry without licence from the king or the said Otto.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 'Close Rolls, Edward II: June 1310', in Calendar of Close Rolls, Edward II: Volume 1, 1307-1313, ed. H C Maxwell Lyte (London, 1892), pp. 217-218. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/cal-close-rolls/edw
2 CONC 2/vol1/pp217-218 [accessed 13 September 2017].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Gruffydd de la Pole 1, 2 was born 1288 in Powis, Montgomeryshire, Wales. He died Jun 1309 in Powis, Montgomeryshire, Wales. Son of Owain ap Gruffydd and Joan Corbet, daughter of Sir Robert Corbet, Sheriff of Shropshire and Ida.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gruffydd married Ela de Audley on 1307 in Powis, Montgomeryshire, Wales, daughter of Nicholas de Audley and Catherine Giffard.  She married James de Ferrers 2nd and Peter Corbet 3rd.
2 CONT
