2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia - Bulmer (family) :
2 CONT >>The Bulmer family were a noble family of Norman England , resident in Yorkshire . The family take their name from Bulmer, North Yorkshire . The name Bulmer comes from English "Bull mere", a lake frequented by a bull, and is an A
2 CONC nglicised form of Gaelic "Búir na mara" from the Celtic tribe Brigantes during their occupation of the area. Ansketil de Bulmer was the first documented member of the Bulmer family who lived in the area in the twelfth century with
2 CONC  the current spelling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bulmer of Bulmer and Brancepeth
2 CONT >>Ansketil was the High Sheriff of Yorkshire . The surname Bulmer is the subject of much discussion as it is believed that they were an aristocratic family of Anglo-Saxon origin who retained their status after the invasion of the 
2 CONC Normans. It is believed that the Bulmers were related to the Anglo-Saxon noble Liulf, who was the first member of the Lumley family. Liulf was murdered at Gateshead by the retainers of William Walcher , the first Norman Bishop of 
2 CONC Durham , in 1081.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>The Bulmers are thought to have continued as tenants of the Normans who inherited Liulf's land in Yorkshire. Sometime in the twelfth century Ansketil Bulmer is said to have married the daughter of the Lord of Brancepeth and thei
2 CONC r son Bertram Bulmer, who succeeded him as High Sheriff, inherited this property. Later the Bulmers intermarried with the powerful Norman family of Neville, who adopted the bull for their coat of arms and inherited Brancepeth Cast
2 CONC le . Raby Castle , the other great Neville property may also have belonged to the Bulmers as the oldest part of this castle, the Saxon Bulmer Tower, is inscribed with the initials BB for Bertram Bulmer.
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Anketil de Bulmer
