2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3P-S.htm#_Toc21501817 English Lords P–S]
2 CONT * '''NOTE:''' As of 2025, Medlands is not convinced of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-William-de-Saye-II/6000000003243522969?through=6000000006906655754 's parentage and does not postulate.
2 CONT ** 1. '''WILLIAM de Say''' (-[1155]). Empress Matilda made various grants of property by charter dated to [1141/42] including a grant of lands "''quæ fuerunt patris sui''" to "''Willelmus de Sai''"[473]. He fought with his brother
2 CONC -in-law at the siege of Burwell Castle in Aug 1144. A manuscript listing of the abbots of Ramsey names "''Walterus abbas''", noting that he suffered many trials "''in tempore Willelmi de Say et Galfredi de Mandeville, qui apud Bor
2 CONC ewelle interfecti fuerunt''"[474]. ''Domesday Descendants'' cites a charter of St Neots which shows that William de Say survived his brother-in-law Geoffrey de Mandeville "by a few years"[475]. 
2 CONT ** '''m''' as her second husband, '''BEATRIX de Mandeville''', divorced wife of HUGH [III] Talbot, daughter of WILLIAM de Mandeville & his wife Marguerite de Rie ([1105]–[Rickling, Essex] 19 Apr [1197 or before], bur Walden Abbey)
2 CONC . A manuscript listing property of Walden abbey states, quoting a charter of Stephen King of England dated 1147, that “''sororem suam…Beatricem''” (referring to "''Galfridus Essexiæ comes''") married "''Hugoni Talebot''" from whom
2 CONC  she was divorced and secondly "''Willielmo de Saye''"[476]. The ''Chronicon Rameseiensis'' records the donations made by "''Willelmum de Say…et mater sua Beatrix''", dated to [1150/60][477]. The ''History of the foundation of Wal
2 CONC den abbey'' records that “''Beatrix de Mandavilla domina de Say, soror Galfridi primi, fundatoris, et amita Willielmi''” succeeded her nephew[478]. The ''Rotuli de Dominabus'' of 1185 records “''Beatricia de Say…iiii.xx. annorum” 
2 CONC and “terra sua de Riklinge''”[479]. She was the heiress of her nephew William de Mandeville Earl of Essex, her son by her second husband, Geoffrey, being allowed to occupy her place in view of her age[480]. The History of the foun
2 CONC dation of Walden abbey records the death in 1200 of “''Beatrix de Say, soror fundatoris nostri et uxor Willielmi de Say''” and her burial in the abbey[481]. 
2 CONT ** '''William & his wife had two children:'''
2 CONT *** a) '''WILLIAM de Say''' of Kimbolton, Huntingdonshire and Saham, Norfolk (-before 1 Aug 1177)....&c.
2 CONT *** b) '''GEOFFREY''' [II] '''de Say''' ([1135 or before]–[1212/May 1214])....&c.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====BOOK
2 CONT * '''Burke, Sir Bernard. (1866) 1883.''' ''A Genealogical History of the Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire''. 2nd ed. London: Harrison. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.3901508843814
2 CONC 1&seq=518 Babel.HathiTrust.org], p. 476:—
2 CONT ** SAYE, OR SAY-BARONS SAYE.—By Writ of Summons, dated 22nd EDWARD I.
2 CONT ** LINEAGE
2 CONT ** The first member of the family of Say mentioned by Sir William Dugdale, is PICOT DE SAY who, in the time of the CONQUEROR. And living in 1083, was one of the principal persons in the co. Salop, under Roger de Montgomery, Earl o
2 CONC f Shrewsbury. The next is—
2 CONT ** INGELRAM DE SAY, one of the staunchest adherents of King STEPHEN in his contest with the Empress MAUD, and made prisoner with that monarch at the battle of Lincoln. After this gallant and faithful soldier, we come to—
2 CONT ** WILLIAM DE SAY, SON of WILLIAM DE SAY, and grandson of—
2 CONT ** WILLIAM DE SAY, who came into England with the CONQUEROR. He m. Beatrix, divorced wife of Hugh Talbot, and dau. of Geoffrey de Mandeville, Earl of Essex, sister of Geoffrey, and aunt, and eventually heiress of William de Mandev
2 CONC ille, Earls of Essex, by whom he had issue, 
2 CONT *** WILLIAM, who d. v. p., leaving two daus., viz., 
2 CONT **** Beatrix, who m. Geoffrey Fitz-Piers, and from whom descended the Fitz-Piers's, who subsequently s. to the Ear dom of Essex
2 CONT **** Maud, m. to William de Bocland.
2 CONT *** GEOFFREY.
2 CONT
