2 CONT ====William de Say====
2 CONT
2 CONT d. Aug 1144
2 CONT
2 CONT William de Say was the son of unknown de Say. He married Beatrice de Mandeville, daughter of William de Mandeville. He died in August 1144, allegedly killed in an attack on Burwell Castle, Cambridgeshires, along with his brother-i
2 CONC n-law 1st Earl of Essex, though he may well have died later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Between December 1141 and June 1142 he was granted his father's lands in a charter of the Empress Maud. In 1144 he joined his brother-in-law, Geoffrey de Mandeville, 1st Earl of Essex, in rebellion against King Stephen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William de Say and Beatrice de Mandeville
2 CONT
