2 CONT
2 CONT ====Marie de Meulan – "Marie de France" (nom de plume/pen name)???
2 CONT * One of five conjectures scholars have weighed is whether Marie de Meulan wrote several poetic works under the pen name "Marie de France." Without substantive sources coming to light after March 2026, conjecture will probably wil
2 CONC l never narrow in focus as to who "Marie de France" was.
2 CONT ** '''Excerpt: Wikipedia [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_de_France Marie de France]'''
2 CONT *** '''The actual name of the author now known as Marie de France is unknown; she has acquired this nom de plume from a line in one of her published works:''' "Marie ai num, si sui de France," which translates as "My name is Marie
2 CONC , and I am from France."[2] '''Some of the most commonly proposed suggestions for the identity of this 12th-century poet are''' '''[A]''' Marie of France, Countess of Champagne; '''[B]'''Marie, Abbess of Shaftesbury and half-siste
2 CONC r to Henry II, King of England; '''[C]'''Marie, Abbess of Reading; Marie I of Boulogne;[3] '''[D]'''Marie, Abbess of Barking;[4][5][''better source needed'']; '''[E]''' '''Marie de Meulan''', wife of Hugh Talbot and daughter of Wa
2 CONC leran de Meulan.[6][7][8] Based on evidence from her writings, it is clear that, despite being born in France, she spent much of her life living in England.[9]
