1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''The "untitled ENGLISH NOBILITY D - K" section of Charles Cawley's ''Medieval Lands'' prosopography and Stirnet's "Foliot1" page do not mention this Walter.  Evidence is needed to support him as a member of this family.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Foliot-42:
2 CONT
2 CONT >==Biography
2 CONT >'''Sir Walter Foliot''' of Nantwich, Cheshire, and Melbury Sampford married Alda Sampford, daughter of Laurence Sampford of Melbury Sampford and Osmond, and had 
2 CONT >#a daughter Joan.  Married 1) Nicholas Percy 2) second wife of John Maltravers 3) Alexander de Veneables
2 CONT >#Alice
2 CONT >#John
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.british-history.ac.uk/vch/hants/vol3/pp290-291:
2 CONT
2 CONT >MANORS
2 CONT >There is no record of holders of land in ''EXBURY'' previous to the thirteenth century, when there are various traces of the family of Foliot ([https://www.geni.com/surnames/faflet Faflet], [https://www.geni.com/surnames/fallet F
2 CONC allet], or [https://www.geni.com/surnames/follet Follet]). In 1244 Richard Foliot, a minor, was holding land in Exbury in chief of the crown, (fn. 2) and at the end of the century Walter Foliot held two carucates there by knight's
2 CONC  service. (fn. 3) On the death of Robert Foliot his lands were divided between his two daughters and coheirs: Maud, who was possessed of one messuage and one carucate in Exbury and Lepe, which she conveyed in 1304 to Andrew [https
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/surnames/grymstead de Grymstead] (fn. 4); and Mabel, who apparently married Robert [https://www.geni.com/surnames/gras le Gras]. (fn. 5)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * ''Collectanea Topographica Et Genealogica'', Volume 6. [https://books.google.com/books?id=PgyzSVb3OYYC&pg=PA339&lpg=PA339&dq=foliot+warren+cheney&source=bl&ots=DFUrbLwskr&sig=mWHCSq1SRJ4bTjh6MaroC_nzYlk&hl=en&sa=X&ei=74hmU-miF-7
2 CONC esASLqIDICA&ved=0CDsQ6AEwBg#v=onepage&q&f=false pp. 334-335]. 1840. Edited by Frederic Madden, Bulkeley Bandinel, John Gough Nichols. <[https://www.wikitree.com/photo/jpg/Mautravers-6 image]>
2 CONT * ''Proceedings of the Dorset Natural History and Antiquarian Field Club'', Volume 28.  [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Proceedings_of_the_Dorset_Natural_Histor/6JQ3AAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA236-IA1&printsec=frontcover pp. 
2 CONC 236-237, memorial brass of his father-in-law Laurence (Laurencius) Sampford].
2 CONT * https://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/member/browning-john-1369-1416
2 CONT
