1 OCCU Baroness Montagu
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elizabeth de Montfort, Baroness Montagu=
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#WilliamMontagudied1319 '''From Medlands:''']
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM de Montagu (-Gascony 18 Oct 1319).  Camden’s Britannia (written in 1607) records that “William de Montacute his kinsman [of John Waldebeof], descended from the kings of Man, did by arms” conquer the Isle of Man but mortgag
2 CONC ed the island to “Anthony Bec bishop of Durham and patriarch of Jerusalem”[1929].  Any relationship between the Montagu family and the kings of the Isle of Man has not yet been traced.  He succeeded his father in 1316 as Lord Mont
2 CONC agu.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1292]) as her first husband, '''ELIZABETH de Montfort''', daughter of PIERS de Montfort of Beaudesert, Warwickshire & his wife Matilda de la Mare (-Aug 1354, bur Oxford, Priory of St Frideswide).  She married secondly (8 Jun 1
2 CONC 322) Thomas de Furnivalle of Sheffield, Worksop.  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Monte Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acut
2 CONC o mariti eiusdem domine E, Iohannis Lincoln episcopi, Petri de Monte Forti patris, domine Matildis matris eiusdem domine, Iohannis de Monte Acuto, Willelmi de Monte Acuto nuper comitis Sar., Simonis Elien episcopi, Edwardi de Mont
2 CONC e Acuto, Alicie de Aubeneye, domine Marie Cogan, Elizabeth priorisse de Haliwell, domine Hawise Bauent, domine Matildis abbatisse de Berkyng, domine Isabelle sancte monialis de Berkyng, liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E., domini
2 CONC  Thome de Furneuall secundi mariti dicte domine, Petri Lymyseye militis et consanguinei eiusdem domine, Simonis de Islep”, charter dated 1 Mar 1380[1930].  William & his wife had ten children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         JOHN de Montagu (-Aug 1317, bur Lincoln Cathedral).  The Complete Peerage suggests that John was his father’s younger son[1931].  However, he is named first in the list of the couple’s children in the following source. 
2 CONC  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Monte Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acuto mariti eiusdem domine E...Iohannis de Monte Acu
2 CONC to, Willelmi de Monte Acuto nuper comitis Sar., Simonis Elien episcopi, Edwardi de Monte Acuto...liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E.”, charter dated 1 Mar 1380[1932].  m (1317) as her first husband, JOAN de Verdun, daughter and h
2 CONC eiress of THEOBALD [II] de Verdun Lord Verdun & his first wife Matilda de Mortimer (Wootton in Stanton Lacy, Shropshire 9 or 11 Aug 1303-Alton 2 Oct 1334, bur Croxden Abbey).  The Chronicle of Croxden records that “Johannam, enecy
2 CONC am [meaning unknown]”, daughter of Theobald [II], married firstly “filius domini Willielmi de Montague” and after his death “dominus Thomas de Furnivall die Sabati in festo sancti Mathei apostoli”[1933].  She married secondly (24 
2 CONC Feb 1318) Thomas de Furnivalle Lord Furnivalle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         WILLIAM de Montagu (Casington, Oxfordshire [1302/03]-30 Jan 1344, bur Bisham).  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Mon
2 CONC te Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acuto mariti eiusdem domine E...Iohannis de Monte Acuto, Willelmi de Monte Acuto nuper comitis Sar., Simonis Elien episcopi, Edwardi de Monte Acuto...liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E.”, char
2 CONC ter dated 1 Mar 1380[1934].  He succeeded his father in 1319 as Lord Montagu and was summoned to parliament as such 18 Feb 1331.  He was created Earl of Salisbury 16 Mar 1337. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         SIMON (-1345).  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Monte Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acuto mariti eiusdem domine
2 CONC  E...Iohannis de Monte Acuto, Willelmi de Monte Acuto nuper comitis Sar., Simonis Elien episcopi, Edwardi de Monte Acuto...liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E.”, charter dated 1 Mar 1380[1935].  King Edward II issued a charter dat
2 CONC ed 28 Nov 1318 in favour of “consanguineus noster Simon de Monte Acuto Oxoniæ Studio Litterarum insistens”[1936].  His family relationship with King Edward has not yet been traced.  Bishop of Ely. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         EDWARD de Montagu (-14 Jul 1361).  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Monte Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acuto ma
2 CONC riti eiusdem domine E...Iohannis de Monte Acuto, Willelmi de Monte Acuto nuper comitis Sar., Simonis Elien episcopi, Edwardi de Monte Acuto...liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E.”, charter dated 1 Mar 1380[1937].  He was summoned 
2 CONC to parliament 20 Nov 1348, whereby he is held to have become Lord Montagu.  m firstly (before 29 Aug 1338) ALICE of Norfolk, daughter and co-heiress of THOMAS "of Brotherton" Earl of Norfolk and Earl Marshal & his first wife Alice
2 CONC  Halys ([1324]-Bungay, Suffolk [14 Nov 1351/30 Jan 1352]).  m secondly JOAN, daughter of --- (-after 1379).  She died from wounds received in an assault by her husband[1938].  Lord Edward & his first wife had --- children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          EDWARD de Montagu (-before Feb 1359). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         AUDREY de Montagu (-before Feb 1359). 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)        ELIZABETH de Montagu ([1344]-1361).  m ([1351]) WALTER de Ufford, son of ROBERT de Ufford Earl of Suffolk & his wife Margaret de Norwich (-1360). 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv)       MATILDA de Montagu [1346]-). 
2 CONT
2 CONT v)        JOAN de Montagu (Bungay, Suffolk 2 Feb 1349-before 12 Jun 1376).  m (before 3 Feb 1363) as his first wife, WILLIAM de Ufford, son of ROBERT de Ufford Earl of Suffolk & his wife Margaret de Norwich ([1339]-15 Feb 1382, bu
2 CONC r Campsey Priory).  He succeeded his father in 1369 as Earl of Suffolk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Edward & his second wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT vi)       AUDREY de Montagu ([1359]-after Aug 1390).  m HUGH de Strelley, son of WILLIAM de Strelley of Hazelbadge, Derbyshire & his wife --- (-Aug 1390). 
2 CONT
2 CONT vii)      EDWARD de Montagu ([May/Jun] 1361-4 Oct 1361). 
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         ALICE (-before 1346).  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Monte Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acuto mariti eiusdem
2 CONC  domine E...Alicie de Aubeneye, domine Marie Cogan, Elizabeth priorisse de Haliwell, domine Hawise Bauent, domine Matildis abbatisse de Berkyng, domine Isabelle sancte monialis de Berkyng, liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E.”, ch
2 CONC arter dated 1 Mar 1380[1939].  m (1332) as his first wife, RALPH Daubeney, son of --- (1305-[after 1378]).   
2 CONT
2 CONT f)          MARY .  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Monte Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acuto mariti eiusdem domine E...Al
2 CONC icie de Aubeneye, domine Marie Cogan, Elizabeth priorisse de Haliwell, domine Hawise Bauent, domine Matildis abbatisse de Berkyng, domine Isabelle sancte monialis de Berkyng, liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E.”, charter dated 1 
2 CONC Mar 1380[1940].  m (before 1327) RICHARD de Cogan of Brampton, son of THOMAS de Cogan & his wife Pernell --- (9 Oct 1299-10 or 29 Apr 1368). 
2 CONT
2 CONT g)         ELIZABETH .  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Monte Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acuto mariti eiusdem domine E.
2 CONC ..Alicie de Aubeneye, domine Marie Cogan, Elizabeth priorisse de Haliwell, domine Hawise Bauent, domine Matildis abbatisse de Berkyng, domine Isabelle sancte monialis de Berkyng, liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E.”, charter date
2 CONC d 1 Mar 1380[1941].  Prioress of Halliwell. 
2 CONT
2 CONT h)         HAWISE .  John Bishop of Lincoln authorised the substitution of two regular canons at Oxford St Frideswide, for the souls of “domine Elizabeth de Monte Acuto ac domini Willelmi de Monte Acuto mariti eiusdem domine E...A
2 CONC licie de Aubeneye, domine Marie Cogan, Elizabeth priorisse de Haliwell, domine Hawise Bauent, domine Matildis abbatisse de Berkyng, domine Isabelle sancte monialis de Berkyng, liberorum dictorum dominorum W. & E.”, charter dated 1
2 CONC  Mar 1380[1942].  m --- Bavent, son of ---. 
