2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth_de_Montfort,_Baroness_Montagu '''From Wikipedia:''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Montfort'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Died	August 1354
2 CONT * Buried	Priory of St Frideswide, Oxford
2 CONT * Spouse(s)	William Montagu, 2nd Baron Montagu
2 CONT * Thomas Furnivall, Baron Furnivall
2 CONT * Issue
2 CONT * John Montagu
2 CONT * William Montagu
2 CONT * Simon Montagu
2 CONT * Edward Montagu
2 CONT * Alice Montagu
2 CONT * Katherine Montagu
2 CONT * Mary Montagu
2 CONT * Elizabeth Montagu
2 CONT * Hawise Montagu
2 CONT * Maud Montagu
2 CONT * Isabel Montagu
2 CONT * Father	Sir Peter Montfort
2 CONT * Mother	Maud de la Mare
2 CONT * Lady Elizabeth de Montfort (died August 1354) was an English noblewoman.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Life===
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Montfort was the daughter of Peter de Montfort, knight, of Beaudesert Castle, Warwickshire (d. before 4 March 1287) and Maud de la Mare.[1] She was born at Beaudesert Castle in Warwickshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her marriage to William Montagu was arranged by Eleanor of Castile, the first wife of King Edward I of England. Edward was eager to make peace with the aristocracy after the battle, and things were fairly well patched up within a 
2 CONC few years. His wife’s role in arranging the marriage was part of an elaborate system of arranged marriages designed to reinforce the power of the King and his aristocracy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Elizabeth and her husband came from wealthy families, and they donated some of their money to various causes. Elizabeth was a major benefactor of the Priory of St Frideswide, Oxford, now Christ Church Cathedral at Oxford Univ
2 CONC ersity. Her tomb now lies between the Latin Chapel, whose construction she funded, and the Dean’s Chapel, where she was originally buried under its magnificent painted ceiling (now faded by time).
2 CONT
2 CONT She also donated a large piece of land to St. Frideswide in exchange for a chantry. This meant that two chantry priests would say daily mass in black robes bearing the Montacute and Montfort coats of arms. This continued until the
2 CONC  Reformation. This piece of land, just south of the church is now called Christ Church Meadow. Later, the path through this was named Christ Church Walk and is now a very popular attraction in Oxford.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriages and issue===
2 CONT
2 CONT She married firstly, about 1292, William Montagu, 2nd Baron Montagu, by whom she had four sons and seven daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Montagu, eldest son and heir, who in 1317 married his father's ward, Joan de Verdun (d. 2 October 1334), daughter and heir of Theobald de Verdun by Maud Mortimer, daughter of Edmund Mortimer, 2nd Baron Mortimer, in the roya
2 CONC l chapel at Windsor Park, Berkshire, by whom he had no issue. He predeceased his father, and was buried at Lincoln Cathedral on 14 August 1317. His widow, Joan, married, on 24 February 1318, Sir Thomas Furnivall (d. October 1339),
2 CONC  by whom she had three sons and two daughters.
2 CONT * William Montagu, 1st Earl of Salisbury (1301–1344), who succeeded as 3rd Baron Montagu.
2 CONT * Simon Montagu (d.1345), who was successively Bishop of Worcester and Bishop of Ely
2 CONT * Edward Montagu (d. 14 July 1361), who married firstly, before 29 August 1338, Alice of Norfolk (d. before 30 January 1352), daughter and coheir of Thomas of Brotherton, and granddaughter of Edward I, by whom he had a son and fou
2 CONC r daughters. Alice of Norfolk is said to have died as the result of an assault by her husband and his retainers.He married secondly a wife named Joan, whose parentage is unknown, by whom he had a son and two daughters.
2 CONT * Alice Montagu, eldest daughter, who married, before 27 January 1333, as his first wife, Sir Ralph Daubeney (3 March 1305 – c.1378), by whom she was the mother of Sir Giles Daubeney (d. 24 June 1386).
2 CONT * Katherine Montagu, who married Sir William Carrington.
2 CONT * Mary Montagu, who married Sir Richard Cogan (d.1368) of Bampton, Devon.
2 CONT * Elizabeth Montagu, Prioress of Halliwell.
2 CONT * Hawise Montagu, who married Sir Roger Bavent (d. 23 April 1355), by whom she had a daughter, Joan, who married Sir John Dauntsey (d.1391).
2 CONT * Maud Montagu, Abbess of Barking from 1341-1352.
2 CONT * Isabel Montagu, Abbess of Barking from 1352-1358.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married secondly Thomas Furnivall, 1st Baron Furnivall (d. before 18 April 1332), who was pardoned and fined £200 on 8 June 1322 for marrying her without royal licence.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p201.htm#i2010 '''From The Peerage:'''] Lady Elizabeth Montfort was born in 1271 at Beaudesert, Warwickshire, England.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Sir William Montague, 2nd Lord Montagu, son of Simon Montagu, 1st Lord Monatgu and Aufricia Fergus.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died circa August 1354.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Elizabeth Montfort and Sir William Montague, 2nd Lord Montagu
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.Simon Montagu
2 CONT * 2.William Montagu, 1st Earl of Salisbury+ b. 1301, d. bt 30 Jan 1343 - 1344
2 CONT * 3.Sir Edward Mountagu, Lord Mountagu+ b. c 1304, d. 14 Jul 1361
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir Piers de Montfort [e] b abt 1215, of Beaudesert, Worcestershire, England, d 4 Aug 1265, Battle of Evesham, Worcestershire, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He md Alice de Aldithley abt 1238, daughter of Sir Henry de Aldithley and Bertrade de Mainwaring.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Peter de Montfort and Alice de Aldithley was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Piers de Montfort [e] b abt 1240, of Beaudesert, Worcestershire, England, d bef 4 Mar 1286/87.  He md Maud de la Mare abt 1266, daughter of Sir Henry de la Mare and Joan de Neville. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peter de Montfort and Maud de la Mare were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Montfort, Lord Montfort, b abt 1271.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth de Montfort b abt 1279, of Warwickshire, England.  She md Sir William de Montagu, Lord Montagu, Knight, abt 1295, son of Sir Simon de Montagu, Lord Montagu, Knight, and Hawise de St. Amand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Identified children of William de Montagu and Elizabeth de Montfort were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William de Montagu b abt 1302.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice de Montagu b abt 1315.  She md Sir Ralph Daubeney, Knight, bef 27 Jan 1332/33, son of Sir Helie/Elis Daubeney, Lord Daubeney, and Joan.
