2 CONT Sir Ralph DAUBENY of South Inbleby & Petherton
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 3 Mar 1304-1305, Guernsey, Channel Islands, England  
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (1): Before 27 Jan 1332-1333   
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (2): Before 8 Feb 1344-1345   
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: After Dec 1378, South Petherton, Somerset, England  Another name for Ralph was Ralph D' ALBINI.   
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: son and heir born 3 March 1304/5. On 2 July 1323 the King notified to the Duke of Brittany, the Bishop of Dol, and all others, that Ralph was heir of Elis. Having proved his age, the King took his homage, and he had
2 CONC  livery of his father's lands, 21 June 1326. Was knighted and had robes as a banneret, 16 January 1326/7. He was summoned for Milittry Service against the Scots, 27 March 1335, and to a Council, 25 February 1341/2, by writs direct
2 CONC ed Radulfo Daubeny or Daubeney. He was taken prisoner by the Scots, and was not released till after 6 October 1337. Was in the King's division at the battle of Crecy, being in the retinue of the Bishop of Durham, and was at the si
2 CONC ege of Calais in the retinue of the Earl of Huntingdon.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information: Ralph married Alice DE MONTAGU, daughter of William DE MONTAGU 2nd Lord Montecute and Elizabeth DE MONTFORT, before 27 Jan 1332-1333 . (Alice DE MONTAGU was born in 1311 in Shepton Montagu, Wincanton, Somerse
2 CONC t, England and died before 1345.)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marriage Information: Ralph also married Katherine DE THWENG, daughter of Marmaduke DE THWENG 1st Baron de Thweng of Kilton and Isabel DE ROS, before 8 Feb 1344-1345 . (Katherine DE THWENG was born about 1304 in Kilton Castle, Cl
2 CONC eveland, Yorkshire, England and died before 28 May 1374.)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/natoab?lang=en&iz=0&p=sir+ralph&n=daubeney
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph /d'Aubeney/
2 CONT
