2 CONT
2 CONT On 9 August 1333 Edward III renounced all English claims over the Isle of Man, and recognised it as an independent kingdom under its then King, William Montacute, 1st Earl of Salisbury.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William Montagu, 1st Earl of Salisbury was born in 1301 at Salisbury, Wiltshire, England.2 He was the son of Sir William Montague, 2nd Lord Montagu and Lady Elizabeth Montfort. He married Catherine Grandison, daughter of William G
2 CONC randison, 1st Lord Grandison, circa 1327. He died between 30 January 1343 and 1344, from injuries received in a joust. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      William Montagu, 1st Earl of Salisbury was also known as William de Montacute.2 He gained the title of 3rd Lord Montagu. He gained the title of 1st Earl of Salisbury in 1337. He was crowned King of Man in 1344.2 
