2 CONT http://gw.geneanet.org/nobily?lang=fr;pz=elisabeth+therese+marie+helene;nz=de+belgique;ocz=0;p=alberic;n=de+dammartin
2 CONT
2 CONT Alberic II of Dammartin From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Alberic II of Dammartin (Aubry de Dammartin) (died 1200 AD) was a French count. He married Marie, heiress to the county of Clermont. They had four children:[1] Renaud I
2 CONC , Count of Dammartin (c. 1165–1227), married 1) Marie de Châtillon and 2) Ide de Lorraine. Simon of Dammartin (1180 – 21 September 1239), married Marie, Countess of Ponthieu Julia of Dammartin, married Hugh de Gournay Agnes of Dam
2 CONC martin, married William de Fiennes [2] References[edit source | editbeta]
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Lindy Grant, Architecture and society in Normandy 1120-1270, Yale University Press, 2005 ^ John Woodward in Notes and queries Oxford Journals, Oxford University Press, 1871, pp 437-428
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''He is a Direct Descendant of Charlemagne.'''
2 CONT This is his lineage:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Charlemagne
2 CONT 2 Berta
2 CONT 3 Berthe I de Boulogne (de Ponthieu)
2 CONT 4 Herlouin de Ponthieu, I
2 CONT 5 Helgaud de Ponthieu, comte de Montreuil
2 CONT 6 Herluin II, count of Ponthieu
2 CONT 7 Unknown, of Hersinde de Ramerupt
2 CONT 8 Hildouin II de Ramerupt, I. comte de Montdidier
2 CONT 9 Manassès, comte de Dammartin
2 CONT 10 Hugues Ier de Dammartin, comte de Montdidier
2 CONT 11 Aelis de Dammartin
2 CONT 12 Aubri de Mello, chambrier de France, sieur de Dammartin
2 CONT 13 Aubry II, count of Dammartin
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hugues Capet, roi des Francs is Aubry II, count of Dammartin's fourth great grandfather.
2 CONT '''
2 CONT 1 Hugues Capet, roi des Francs
2 CONT 2 Robert II Capet, "the Pious" king of the Franks
2 CONT 3 Constance de France, heritiere de Dammartin
2 CONT 4 Hugues Ier de Dammartin, comte de Montdidier
2 CONT 5 Aelis de Dammartin
2 CONT 6 Aubri de Mello, chambrier de France, sieur de Dammartin
2 CONT 7 Aubry II, count of Dammartin
2 CONT ----
