1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The earliest family member from which all relationships are certain is Gilbert de Scarisbrick (d. 1359). ''This''  '''Gilbert de Scarisbrick''' (d. 1238), believed to be his gg-grandfather, was granted land in Scar
2 CONC isbrick from his brother, Simon de Grubhead.  From this land grant, Gilbert was given the toponym "de Scarisbrick.'  His heir was Walter de Scarisbrick, who died in 1260.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter de Scarisbrick's heir is believed to be Henry de Scarisbrick, who had two sons and a daughter.  His son Gilbert had a son, also named Gilbert, who married Joan de Kirby, daughter of Sir John de Kirby, in 1328. Gilbert, husb
2 CONC and of Joan, is the one who died in 1359.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Scarisbrick genealogy can be found at http://scarisbrickfamily.homestead.com/Tree1.html
