2 CONT https://finerollshenry3.org.uk/content/calendar/roll_059.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://finerollshenry3.org.uk/content/search/do_text_search
2 CONT
2 CONT 46/285 (11 April 1262)
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 April. Westminster. Concerning the relief of a baron. The king has taken the homage of Henry de Longchamp, son and heir of Petronilla de Vaux, for the manor of South Warnborough, which Petronilla, who has recently died, held fr
2 CONC om the king. Order to William de Weilond, the king’s escheator on this side of the Trent, that, having accepted security from Henry that he will answer at the Exchequer for his relief, as a baron, he is to cause him to have full s
2 CONC eisin of that manor without delay.
2 CONT
2 CONT 47/557 (27 May 1263)
2 CONT
2 CONT 27 May. Westminster. For Henry de Longchamp. To the treasurer and barons of the Exchequer. The king has granted to Henry de Longchamp that he may render £5 at the Exchequer of Michaelmas next to come for the £100 in which he is bo
2 CONC und to him for his relief, another £5 at the Exchequer of Easter next following, and £10 thus from year to year at the same terms until the aforesaid £100 have been paid to the king. Order to cause Henry to have the aforesaid term
2 CONC s and to cause this to be done and enrolled thus.
2 CONT
2 CONT 48/193 (18 September 1264)
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 Sept. Canterbury. For the executors of the earl of Winchester. The executors of R. de Quincy, formerly earl of Winchester, have found the king the below-written pledges, namely John de Eyvill’, Henry de Longchamp, Roger de Vaux
2 CONC  and William de Oilly, for rendering debts to the king if the same earl owed him any on the day he died, in as far as the goods and chattels of the same earl suffice to acquit the aforesaid debts.
2 CONT
