1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 23 Aubrey de Vere I gave distinguished service at the Battle of Hastings, and was awarded land near Northampton to build a manor house.''' In the early thirteenth century, Sir Walter de Vere dropped the “de Vere” f
2 CONC amily name, and assume the surname “Drayton”.''' The core of the house was built by Sir Simon de Drayton around 1300 and still survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT > Note this information comes from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drayton_House Wikipedia], which cites a book about houses and gardens in South Carolina: Magnolia Plantation and Gardens By Derek Fell. Giibs Smith. 2009. There cou
2 CONC ld not be a less reliable source for a medieval connection between the Draytons and de Veres. The more reliable [https://books.google.com/books?id=soI35rrNLMIC&printsec=frontcover&dq=Nikolaus+Pevsner.+Buildings+of+England:+Northam
2 CONC ptonshire&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwi3rp3gi9rNAhXFlB4KHaJ7AXsQ6AEIJTAA#v=onepage&q=drayton&f=false Buildings of England: Northamptonshire] by Nikolaus Pevsner says nothing about a connection. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~hwbradley/aqwg1859.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Walter de VERE Knight [Parents] 1, 2, 3, 4 was born 1172 in Drayton, Northamptonshire, England. He died 5 1210 in Drayton, Northamptonshire, England. Walter married Lucy BASSET on 1197 in Drayton, Northamptonshire, England.
2 CONT
