1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Malet_(Magna_Carta_baron) '''''Wikipedia'': William Malet (Magna Carta baron)''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Malet''' (born before 1175–1215), feudal baron of Curry Mallet in Somerset, was one of the guarantors of Magna Carta. In 1190, he accompanied King Richard the Lionheart on third crusade.[1] While still on crusade in 119
2 CONC 1, he took part in the Siege of Acre.[1] Upon returning to England, he served as Sheriff of Somerset and Dorset in 1209. The precise nature of his relationship to an earlier William Malet is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Malet was one of the rebel barons who were heavily indebted to King John.[1] It is believed that by 1214 he owed the king as much as £1333.[1] In 1214 he entered into an agreement to serve with the king along with 10 knigh
2 CONC ts and 20 other soldiers in exchange for the cancellation of his debts.[1] However, the agreement broke down for an unknown reason and by 1215 he joined the rebellion.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Malet seems to have died just a few months after Magna Carta was executed by King John.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''References'''
2 CONT >Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to American Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis, Lines 189-1, 234A-29
2 CONT >Hollister, C. Warren (1973). "Henry I and Robert Malet". Viator 4: 115–32. 
2 CONT >Hurt, Cyril. "William Malet and His Family". Anglo-Norman Studies XIX. 
2 CONT >Lewis, C. P. (1989). "The King and Eye: A Study in Anglo-Norman Politics". English Historical Review 104: 569–87. doi:10.1093/ehr/CIV.CCCCXII.569.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Malet-18
2 CONT
2 CONT The identity of his first wife is unknown (see below). Douglas Richardson lists four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #William, who, before 1196, witnessed a charter of his grandfather Gilbert Malet, and who died before his father, whose heirs were William's three sisters[1][2]: there may be a question-mark about this - see Research Notes below
2 CONT #Helewise, who married Hugh Poyntz and Robert de Muscegros[1][2][3]
2 CONT #Mabel, who married Nicholas Avenal and Hugh de Vivonne[1][2][3]
2 CONT #Bertha, who died unmarried before 11 April 1221[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT William's second wife was Alice Basset.[1][2][3] They had no children.[1][2] Alice was the daughter of Thomas Basset,[1][2] one of the Illustrious Men who were King John's counsellors listed in the preamble to the Magna Carta.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT William died very soon after his excommunication.[1][2][4] His heirs were his daughters Helewise, Mabel and Bertha.[3][4] William was probably buried in the parish church of Curry Mallet, Somerset.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife Alice subsequently married John Bisset. She died in about 1263.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Date
2 CONT
2 CONT The Oxford Dictionary of National Biography entry for William postulates a birth date of about 1175.[3] Douglas Richardson says he was of age in 1194.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of his Daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT Some sources give Alice Basset as mother of William's daughters. But Alice's heirs were not children by William Malet but children by her second marriage to John Biset. This strongly suggests that the daughters were children of Wi
2 CONC lliam by a previous marriage, to someone whose name is unknown.[1][2][8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son William
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas Richardson states that William had a son William who witnessed a charter of his grandfather Gilbert Malet in 1196, and who died before the William of this profile.[1][2] If the latter may have been born as late as 1173, th
2 CONC ere is a question as to whether a son would have been old enough to witness a charter in 1196.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other William Malets
2 CONT
2 CONT There were a number of other William Malets in this period, and they can be easily confused. Those with profiles on WikiTree at 24 February 2020 are:
2 CONT
2 CONT Malet-172 of Enmore, Somerset
2 CONT Malet-171, son of Malet-172
2 CONT
2 CONT In the records cited in Medieval Lands[8] it appears difficult to be certain which William Malet is being referred to.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''FMG [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/enguntlo.htm#WilliamMaletdied1215 Untitled English Nobility L - O]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *3.         WILLIAM Malet (-1169).  According to Domesday Descendants, William was the son of Robert [III] Malet (see above)[1056]. …  m firstly ---.  The name of William’s first wife is not known.  … William & his first wife had 
2 CONC [two] children: 
2 CONT **a)         GILBERT Malet (-1194).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   m ALICE Picot, daughter of RALPH Picot & his wife ---.  Salzman records her parentage and marriage[1066].   Gilber
2 CONC t & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT ***i)          '''WILLIAM Malet (-before 20 Dec 1215)''' m firstly ---.  The dates of the first marriages of William Malet’s daughters, together with the fact that his known wife Alice Basset had three children by her third husban
2 CONC d, suggests that William’s two daughters may have been born from an otherwise unrecorded first marriage.]  m [secondly] as her first husband, ALICE Basset, daughter of THOMAS Basset [II] of Headington & his wife Philippa Malbank (
2 CONC -[1263]).  She married secondly (before 1221, annulled) H--- de Chaceporc, and thirdly ([late 1220/1223]) John Bisset.  William & his [first] wife had two children: 
2 CONT ****(a)       MABEL Malet .  Her second marriage is confirmed by an order dated 18 Nov 1223 placing "in respite…the demand…from Hugh de Vivonne…for the debt that William Malet, father of the wife of Vivon, owed the king"[1074].  m
2 CONC  firstly NICHOLAS Avenell, son of --- (-[1221/22]).  m secondly (before 18 Nov 1223) HUGUES de Vivonne, son of --- (-1249). 
2 CONT ****(b)       HAWISE Malet .  Henry III King of England made an order related to property "apud Exoniam" of "Hawisie que fuit uxor Hugonis Poinz", which she received from "Willelmi Malet patris vestri", dated 26 Aug 1220[1075].  m
2 CONC  firstly HUGH Poinz, son of --- (-before 26 Aug 1220).  m secondly ROBERT de Mucegros, son of ---. 
2 CONT
