2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT FitzHamon (-Newbury Mar 1107). Lord of Glamorgan. Lord of Gloucester. The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey records that William II King of England granted the honor of Gloucester to ”Robertum filiu
2 CONC m Haymonis, dominum de Astramervilla in Normannia”[1467]. "…Rodberti Haimonis filii…" subscribed a charter dated 14 Sep 1101 under which Henry I King of England donated property to Bath St Peter[1468]. "…Robertus filius Hamonis et
2 CONC  Hamon frater eius…" witnessed the charter dated 13 Jan 1103 which records an agreement between “Philippus de Braosa” and the abbey of Fécamp[1469]. The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey records the death 
2 CONC “Marcii 1107” of ”Robertum filium Haymonis”[1470]. The Annals of Margan record that “Robertus filius Hamonis” died in 1107[1471]. The Gwentian Chronicle records that "Robert Fitzhamon died in his castle at Newbury, raving mad" in 
2 CONC 1110[1472]. m as her first husband, SIBYLLE de Montgommery, daughter of ROGER Sire de Montgommery, Vicomte d'Hiémois [later Earl of Shrewsbury] & his first wife Mabel d'Alençon. Guillaume de Jumièges names (in order) "Robert et Hu
2 CONC gues, Roger le Poitevin, Philippe et Arnoul, et les filles Emma, Mathilde, Mabille et Sibylle" as the five sons and four daughters of "Roger de Montgomeri" & his wife Mabile[1473]. She is named and her parentage given by Orderic V
2 CONC italis, who lists her fourth among her father's daughters by his first marriage and also names her first husband[1474]. The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey records that ”Robertum filium Haymonis, dominum
2 CONC  de Astramervilla in Normannia” married “Sibillam sororem Roberti de Belismo, comitis Salopiæ”[1475]. She married secondly Jean Sire de Raimes. The primary source which confirms her second marriage has not yet been identified. Rob
2 CONC ert & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i) MABEL [Matilda or Sibylle] (-[29 Sep] 1157). The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey names (in order) “Mabiliam, Hawysiam, Ceciliam, Amisiam” as the four daughters of ”Robertum filium Haymonis, dominum de
2 CONC  Astramervilla in Normannia”, recording that Mabile married Robert Fitzroy[1476]. Her marriage is recorded by Orderic Vitalis, who also names her parents[1477]. Robert of Torigny records that "filia Roberti Belismensis" was the mo
2 CONC ther of "Rogerius Wigornensis episcopus", son of "Robertus comes Gloecestrensis…filius primi Henrici regis Anglorum", clarifying that the bishop's grandfather was "Robertus filius Haimonis dominus de Torigneio"[1478]. The Annals o
2 CONC f Tewkesbury record that “Mabilia comitissa Gloucestriæ” died in 1157[1479].
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before [1112]) ROBERT Fitzroy, illegitimate son of HENRY I King of England & his mistress --- ([1090]-Bristol 31 Oct 1147, bur Priory of St James, Bristol). He was created Earl of Gloucester in [Jun/Sep] 1122.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii) HAWISE . The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey names (in order) “Mabiliam, Hawysiam, Ceciliam, Amisiam” as the four daughters of ”Robertum filium Haymonis, dominum de Astramervilla in Normannia”, addin
2 CONC g that Hawise became abbess of Winchester[1480].
2 CONT
2 CONT iii) CECILE . The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey names (in order) “Mabiliam, Hawysiam, Ceciliam, Amisiam” as the four daughters of ”Robertum filium Haymonis, dominum de Astramervilla in Normannia”, addi
2 CONC ng that Cecile became abbess of Shaftesbury[1481].
2 CONT
2 CONT iv) AMICE . The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey names (in order) “Mabiliam, Hawysiam, Ceciliam, Amisiam” as the four daughters of ”Robertum filium Haymonis, dominum de Astramervilla in Normannia”, adding
2 CONC  that Amice married “comiti Brytanniæ”[1482]. The identity of Amice´s husband has not yet been established.
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
