2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.mindfreedom.net/gen/t-s-p/p177.htm#i8461
2 CONT
2 CONT That Robert, a little known son of the Earl of Gloucester was even married, is revealed in a charter dated between June 1141 and 1161, probably before Oct 1147, in which Hawise, daughter of Earl Baldwin de Redvers, made a gift to 
2 CONC Quarr Abbey
2 CONT
2 CONT jointly with her husband, Robert, son of the Earl of Gloucester. CP, 5: 686 states Robert was a natural son of Earl Robert and that he was named c1160 in a charter and is addressed in a writ from King Henry II as Castellan of Glou
2 CONC cester. [Ronny Bodine, SGM, 18 Feb 1999]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: The marriage took place before the charter, which was June 1141 - Oct 1147 (probably). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT From Medlands:
2 CONT
