2 CONT • Web Reference.  The Genealogy of the Bostock and Bostwick Families gives three possible pedigress for ancestry of Warin de Bostwick. The first one is based on The Visitation of Cheshire, 1580, the second is based on the Harleyan
2 CONC  Manuscript of 1535 and the third on on Ormerod's History of Cheshire. I've started with Warin de Bostock because all three seem to agree on Warin. Also, I followed Ormerod's pedigree because I hae found him to be reliable, althou
2 CONC gh there seems to be no real proof that Sir Warin de Bostock's wife was actually Hawise of Chester, widow of Robert de Quincy. Anthony Bostock points out that the dates show that this is possible.
