2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh, Baron of Okehampton, distinguished himself in the Scottish wars during the reign of Edward I and was knighted by the King at Westminster as one of 300 persons of eminence.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the reign of Edward II, he was created a Knight-banneret.  He was summoned to Parliament many times during the reign of Edward III, under the name of Hugh Courtenay, Earl of Devon, being restored to that title in the right of h
2 CONC is great grandmother, Mary de Redvers [Colonial and Revolutionary Lineages of America, Vol. 1, p. 318].
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh distinguished himself in the Scottish wars during the reign of Edward I and was knighted by the King at Westminster as one of 300 persons of eminence.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the reign of Edward II, he was created a Knight-banneret.  He was summoned to Parliament many times durin the reign of Edward III, under the name of Hugh Courtenay, Earl of Devon, being restored to that title in the right of hi
2 CONC s great grandmother, Mary de Redvers [Colonial and Revolutionary Lineages of America, Vol. 1, p. 318].
2 CONT
