2 CONT  (-10 Oct 1335 or before).  The Fundationis et Fundatorum Historia of Ford Abbey names “Isabellam domini Johannis de St John uxorem, Avelinam domini Johannis Gifford militis uxorem, necnon Egelinam Roberti de Scales uxorem, et Mar
2 CONC garetam Johannis de Mulis…uxorem” as the four daughters of “Hugonem de Courtnay primum” & his wife[468].  m ROBERT de Scales, son of ROBERT de Scales Lord Scales & his wife Isabel --- ([1278/79]-20 Mar 1324).  He succeeded his fat
2 CONC her in 1305 as Lord Scales.www.wikipedia.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT Robert married Egelina[ (aka Egelma aka Evelina) daughter of Hugh de Courtenay and they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert de Scales, 3rd Baron Scales (?-1369) Eleanor (d. 1361), married John de Sudeley, 2nd Baron Sudeley (d. 1340) References
2 CONT  Philip Morant, The History and Antiquities of the County of Essex
2 CONT  Patent Rollswww.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Egelina De Courtenay Scales BIRTH	Jul 1282 Devon, England DEATH	10 Oct 1335 (aged 53) Norfolk, England BURIAL	Unknown  MEMORIAL ID	131601600 
2 CONT
2 CONT Egeline de Courtenay was born in July, 1282 in Okehampton Castle in Devonshire, Devon, England, UK. Egeline was the daughter of Hugh de Courtenay Baron of Okehampton (1248-1291) and Eleanor le de (Spencer) de Scales (1262-1328).
2 CONT
2 CONT Egelina married Sir Knight Robert De Scales, V (1279-1325) in Okehampton, Devon, England in 1309. He was the son of Robert de Scales IV (1249-1305) and Isabel (Burnell) de Scales (1252-1333).
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert V and Egeline de Scales were the parents of the following known children: Robert VI, Eleanor Isabelle and Parnel de Scales.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baroness Egeline de Courtenay de Scales died on 10 Oct 1335 in Middleton, Norfolk, England. Her burial is unknown at this time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Egeline de Courtenay is mentioned in this book in Volume: 41 on page #494: "Families directly des. from all the royal fams. in Europe (495 to 1932)". By Mrs. Eliz. M. Leach Rixford. Burlington, Vt. 1932. (175p.):25
2 CONT
