1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''MARGARET'''
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE as to following Medlands reference. Medlands now has Nicholas de Moels as the husband of Margaret de Courteney. Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol V, p. 370 has Maud de Grey as the wife of John de Moels, 1st Baron Moels.
2 CONC  (Steven Ferry, December 28, 2025.) :
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Medlands (see below) John de Mulis was the husband of Margaret de Courtenay NOT Nicholas.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#HughCourtenaydied1292
2 CONT
2 CONT *a) HUGH de Courtenay of Okehampton (-Colcombe 28 Feb 1292, bur Cowick near Exeter). The Fundationis et Fundatorum Historia of Forde Abbey names “Hugonem de Courtnay primum” as son of “dominum Johannem de Courtenay” and his wife “
2 CONC Isabellam filiam domini Johannis de Veere comitis Oxoniæ”[573]. Inquisitions after a writ dated 11 May "2 Edw I" following the death of "John de Corteney alias de Curtenay" name “Isabel sometime his wife...Hugh his son aged 24 is 
2 CONC his next heir”[574]. The Fundationis et Fundatorum Historia of Forde Abbey records the death ”apud Colecombe III Kal Mar 1291” of “Hugonem de Courtnay primum” and his burial “apud Cowick prope Exon.”[575]. m ELEANOR Le Despencer, 
2 CONC daughter of HUGH Le Despencer & his wife Aline Basset of Wycombe, Buckinghamshire (-30 Sep 1328, bur Cowick near Exeter). The Fundationis et Fundatorum Historia of Forde Abbey records that “Hugonem de Courtnay primum” married “Eli
2 CONC anoram filiam…domini Hugonis le Despencer primi, patris etiam domini Hugonis le Despencer…postea comitis Winton”[576]. The Fundationis et Fundatorum Historia of Forde Abbey records the death ”1328 II Kal Oct” of “Hugonem de Courtn
2 CONC ay primum…[vidua] domina Alianora” and her burial “prope maritum…apud Cowick”[577]. Hugh & his wife had [seven] children:
2 CONT **     i) .... etc.
2 CONT **'''     vii) MARGARET . The Fundationis et Fundatorum Historia of Ford Abbey names''' “Isabellam domini Johannis de St John uxorem, Avelinam domini Johannis Gifford militis uxorem, necnon Egelinam Roberti de Scales uxorem, et ''
2 CONC 'Margaretam Johannis de Mulis…uxorem” as the four daughters''' of “Hugonem de Courtnay primum” & his wife[469]. '''m JOHN de Mulis, son of ---. ___________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret Courtenay1,2,3,4,5
2 CONT *'''F, #46113, d. 18 March 1349
2 CONT *Father	Sir Hugh de Courtenay, Baron Oakhampton6,3,7,5 b. 25 Mar 1251, d. 28 Feb 1292
2 CONT *Mother	Eleanor le Despenser1,6,3,7,5 b. c 1260, d. 30 Sep 1328
2 CONT *'''     Margaret Courtenay married Nicholas de Moels, 2nd Lord Moels''', son of Sir John de Moels, 1st Lord Moels and Maud de Grey, '''before February 1313; No issue.1,2,3,4,5 Margaret Courtenay died on 18 March 1349.1,3,5
2 CONT *'''Family     Nicholas de Moels, 2nd Lord Moels''' b. 10 Aug 1289, d. c 29 Jan 1316
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. III, Tafel 629.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 538.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 148.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 323.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 94.
