2 CONT
2 CONT References  Richardson: p.493-494   Roberts p.403   Weis, Ancestral: 148A-32, 218-30, 31   Weis, Magna Charta: 132-7
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hunter, Joseph, (1819). "III: Sheffield under the Barons Furnival". Hallamshire. The History and Topography of the Parish of Sheffield in the County of York. London: Lackington, Hughes, Harding, Mayor & Jones.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Thomas 1st Baron de FURNIVAL , Sir was born ABT 1260 in Worksop, Nottinghamshire, England, and died BEF 18 APR 1332 in Sheffield Castle, Yorkshire, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jweber&id=I10123
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Thomas de FURNIVAL , Lord of Hallamshire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT # Joan le DESPENSER BEF JAN 1272/73 in 1st wife, daughter of Hugh 1st Baron le DESPENSER , Sir and Aline BASSET , Countess of Norfolk. She was born BEF 1266 in Ryhall, Rutland, England, and died 1322 in Worksop, Nottinghamshire, E
2 CONC ngland.  4 daughters, 1 son
2 CONT # Elizabeth de MONTFORT BEF 8 JUN 1322 in 2nd husband 2nd wife, daughter of Piers (Peter) de MONTFORT , of Beaudesert, Sir and Maud (Matilda) de la MARE , Heiress of Ashtead. She was born ABT 1280 in Beldesert Castle, Warwickshire
2 CONC , England, and died AUG 1354 in St Frideswide now Christ Church, Oxfordshire, England.  1 daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sir Thomas de Furnivall(e), 1st Lord (Baron) Furinvall(e), so created by writ of summons to Parliament 24 June 1295; fought at Battle of Falkirk against the Scots 1298; married 1st by Jan 1272/3 Joan, daughter of 1st Lord (Baron)
2 CONC  le Despenser of the putative 1264 creation, and had [Thomas, Catherine, Eleanor]. The 1st Lord (Baron) Furnivall(e) married 2nd by 8 June 1322 Elizabeth (died Aug 1354), widow of 2nd Lord (Baron) Montagu of the 1299 creation and 
2 CONC daughter of Sir Piers de Mo(u)ntfort, of Beaudesert, Warwicks, and died just prior to 18 April 1332, having had another son William, whether by his 1st or 2nd wife is unknown. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady_Elizabeth_Montacute
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth de Montfort married secondly Thomas Furnivall, 1st Baron Furnivall (d. before 18 April 1332), who was pardoned and fined L200 on 8 June 1322 for marrying her without royal licence.[27][28]
2 CONT
2 CONT * 27. Cokayne 1926 p 582.
2 CONT * 28. Cokayne 1936, pp 82, 85.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
