2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Marmion, 2nd Lord Marmion 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born circa 1292 (was 30 in 1322) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died on April 30, 1335
2 CONT
2 CONT     John was among the adherants of Thomas, Earl of Lancaster who were responsible for the beheading (without a trial) of King Edward II's friend Peter (Piers) Gaveston in 1312 for which he was pardoned in October 1313. He was sum
2 CONC moned to Parliament on December 3, 1326 and in May 1329 he had a protection for three years, going on a pilgrimage to the Holy Land.
2 CONT
2 CONT     John married Maud de Furnival, a daughter of Thomas de Furnival, Lord Furnival and his first wife Joan, daughter of Hugh le Despenser.  John and Maud had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Marmion who succeeded his father as 3rd Lord Marmion.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Marmion who married 1st John de Bernak, Knight and 2nd John de Folville, Knight.
2 CONT
2 CONT Avice Marmion
2 CONT
2 CONT References  Richardson: p.493-494   Roberts p.403   Weis, Ancestral: 148A-32, 218-30, 31   Weis, Magna Charta: 132-7
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Maud married John /Marmion/, son of John De /Marmion/ and Isabel /Unknown/, about 1309 in Tattershall, Lincolnshire, England. (John /Marmion/ was born in 1292 in Tattershall, Lincolnshire, England and died on 30 Apr 1335.)
