1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-de-Burgh/6000000003232558589 and not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-de-Burgh-feudal-Baron-Lanvallei-of-Walkern/6000000002173018346?through=6000
2 CONC 000003232558589
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Magred de Burgh''', daughter of John de Burgh (d c 1280) and Cecily de Baliol, was a nun at Chicksand or Sempringham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her name is also seen as Margaret, Marjorie, Margery.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Identity 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Guines-5
2 CONT
2 CONT >"(That) Margaret was emphatically not a daughter of John de Burgh of Lanvallay, grandson of the infamous justiciar John de Burgh. The younger John did leave 3 daughters, two of whose marriages are well attested (neither one to Ri
2 CONC chard de Burgh nor any member of that family); the third, '''who was named Margaret''', had become a nun before her father died, so the inheritance was divided only between her two elder sisters. The inheritance was never subseque
2 CONC ntly re- apportioned to provide for the third sister or any of her issue, and she evidently remained in her cloister to die unmarried and childless. " (Ref: http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/GEN-MEDIEVAL/1999-03/092042
2 CONC 1247 )
2 CONT
