2 CONC n his allegiance, his lands at Alcester wereseized by the crown, and given to William de Camvill. Returning, however,to his duty upon the accession of Henry III, those lands were restored tohim. He m. 1st, Alice, dau. of Roger Fit
2 CONC z-Roger, a great baron inNorthumberland, but by her had no issue; and 2ndly, the 3rd dau. andco-heir of William de Braose, Baron of Brecknock, and d. 1235, leaving ason, Herbert Fitz-Peter. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Fo
