2 CONT [S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William de Beauchamp - was born about 1105, lived in Elmley Castle, Worcestershire, England and died in 1169 . William married Maud de Braose in 1151 while living in Gower, Glamorganshire, Wales. Maud was born about 1109, lived in
2 CONC  Gower, Glamorganshire, Wales. She died after 1151 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud - - Some sources have shown Maud's father as William de Braose, born abt 1084. 
2 CONT
2 CONT However, other sources have found no hard evidence that William de Beauchamp married a Maud de Braose. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud De Braose (Wife)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:	 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Lord De Beauchamp
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud De Beauchamp
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma De Beauchamp
2 CONT
2 CONT See the following notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT William de Beauchamp (d.1170) of Salwarpe and Elmley allegedly married Bertha dau. of William de Braose (d.1211). The latter's great grandson, William de Braose (d.1230) of Abergavenny had a dau. & coheir Maud (d.1301) who married
2 CONC  Roger de Mortimer (d.1282) of Wigmore. Saunders gives no marriage of a Bertha de Braose (or of a Maud de B) to William de Beauchamp. Turton does give the marriage of Bertha and William based on information from the first edition 
2 CONC (1910) of Cokayne's *Complete Peerage*. As far as I can tell the second edition omits any reference to the early Beauchamps. B Burke's *Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire* (London, 1883) p.29 ha
2 CONC s William Beachamp marrying a Maud de Braose. Since (1) Burke is to be treated with extreme caution, (2)it seems that the editors of the second edition of *The Complete Peerage* deleted material on the early Beauchamps and (3) Sau
2 CONC nders notes marriages between the baronial families dealt with but omits this marriage, the upshot would seem to be that there is no hard evidence of a Braose marriage to William Beauchamp (d.1170). 
2 CONT
2 CONT I J Saunders *English Baronies: a study of their origin and descent 1086-1327* (London, 1963 1960), pp.7,21,75-76. 
2 CONT
2 CONT W H Turton *The Plantagenet Ancestry* (London, 1928), p.117.
2 CONT
2 CONT William - Next listing of a father is Walter with a birthdate oe 1120, before William's.
2 CONT
