2 CONT
2 CONT '''WILLIAM [III] Mauduit''' (-2 Oct 1194, bur Waverley Abbey).  Henry II King of England confirmed "baroniam totam quam pater suus de me tenuit, tan in Anglia quam in Normannia" to "Willelmo Malduit filio Willelmi Mald camerarii m
2 CONC ei" by charter dated to [Dec 1154/Aug.   Chamberlain.  "Comes Simon" confirmed to "Willelmo Malduit camerario domini regis et Isabelle uxori sue" the land "in Grendon…" which "comes Simon pater meus dedit Willelmo Malduit et Isabe
2 CONC lle uxori sue in libero maritagio" by charter dated to.   Military fee certifications in the Red Book of the Exchequer, in 1166, record the knight feeholders from "Willelmus Malduit camerarius" in Buckinghamshire.  The Red Book of
2 CONC  the Exchequer refers to "Willelmus Maudut, camerarius xxiii s iv d, et de novo xxxvi s viii d" in Buckinghamshire in.  The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage payments in [1190/91], records "Willelmus Mauduit camerarius" p
2 CONC aying "xvii s vi d, i militem et tres partes" in Buckinghamshire, Bedfordshire[1180].  The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage payments in, names "Willelmus Mauduit camerarius" among those granted delay in payment "per brev
2 CONC is" in Buckinghamshire, Bedfordshire.  The Annals of Waverley record the death “VI Non Oct” in 1194 of “Willelmus Maldut” and his burial “apud Waverleiam”.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ISABELLE de Senlis, daughter of SIMON de Senlis Earl of Huntingdon & his wife Isabelle de Beaumont.  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the charter dated to [1158/74] under which [her brother] "Comes Simon" confirmed to
2 CONC  "Willelmo Malduit camerario domini regis et Isabelle uxori sue" the land "in Grendon…" which "comes Simon pater meus dedit Willelmo Malduit et Isabelle uxori sue in libero maritagio".   William [III] & his wife had [two] children
2 CONC : 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ROBERT [II] Mauduit (-[1217/Jun 1222]).  "Robertus de Ousbravill filius Fulconis" granted "civitatem meam de Ousbravill", except land which "mea mater tenet in doario", to "Willelmo Mauduit camerario domini regis Anglie
2 CONC , cognato meo et Roberto filio suo" by charter dated to [Nov 1183/Nov 1184][1184]. 
2 CONT
