2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume de Jumièges records that "Roger comte de Warwick" and his wife had a son named Henri "plusieurs autres fils et deux filles"[1231].  However, Robert of Torigny names "Henricus filius suus" as son and successor of "Rogero 
2 CONC comite Warwicensi" & his wife[1232], clearly confusing him with William.  Assuming that the two sources are based on common information, it is likely that Henry did not exist.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Not to be confused with son of Henry de Beaumont and Marguerite du Perche
