2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard was the son of John de Handlo.[1] and Maud Burnell. [This is incorrect - he was the son of John de Haudlo and his first wife, Joan FitzNigel. Maud Burnell was John's second wife, and she was the widow of John Lovell with a
2 CONC t least two children by her first husband.] https://edwardthesecond.blogspot.com/2010/02/maud-fitzalan-and-maud-burnell.html (note: blog post includes primary documentation.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard married Isabella St. Amand[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard and Isabella had children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, who was married to Edmund atte Pole;[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, who was married to John de Appelby;[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard died before his father, John de Handlo, who died in 19 Edward III[1] which was 25 January 1345—24 January 1346.
2 CONT
2 CONT His widow Isabella then married Robert de Hildesle;[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 42 Edward III there was a Coram Rege suit respecting the inheritance in cos Bucks, Oxon, Kent and Glouc of Richard de Handlo, whose family sometimes styled themselves as Burnell.[1]
