1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000074900370872& Inquisitions Post Mortem] for Margaret de Roos or de Ros, Writ, 16 August, 23 Edward III [1349]. <br>
2 CONT She died on 22, 28 or 29 July [1349]. Philip le Despenser her son, who died on 22 August [1349], aged 22 years, was her heir. He entered upon no land of hers, because he died shortly after her death, nor took any profits from her 
2 CONC lands except from Market Staynton and Alkebarow, which he held, conjointly with Joan his wife, by the said Margaret’s gift. Philip [son of the said] Philip, [aged 7 years at the feast of St. Lucy next, is his] heir. Mentions John 
2 CONC de Ros, knight, deceased, sometime husband of the said Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes
2 CONT Ralph de Goushill [c] b abt 1274, Goxhill, Lincolnshire, England, d bef 30 Aug 1294. He md Hawise Fitz Warin abt 1292, daughter of Sir Fulk Fitz Warin and Margred verch Gruffydd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Ralph de Goushill and Hawise Fitz Warin was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Goushill [d] b 12 May 1294, of Whittington, Shropshire, England, d 29 Jul 1349. She md [1] Sir Philip le Despenser abt 1311, son of Sir Hugh le Despenser and Isabel de Beauchamp. She md [2] Sir John de Ros abt 1313-1314.
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
