2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas de Astley, 3rd Lord Astley''', 
2 CONT * summoned to parliament from 25 February, 1342, to 10 March, 1349. 
2 CONT * This nobleman founded a chantry in the parish church of Astley, in the 11th year of Edward III, and 
2 CONT * afterwards obtaining permission to change his chantry priests into a dean and secular canons , 
2 CONT ** he erected a fair and beautiful collegiate church in the form of a cross, with a tall spire, covered with lead, and dedicated it to the assumption of the blessed Virgin. 
2 CONT * His lordship m. Elizabeth, dau. of Guy de Beauchamp, Earl of Warwick, and left issue, 
2 CONT ** with daus. (of whom Alice m. Sir Richard Chapernoune of Modbury) 
2 CONT **  three sons, viz., '''William (Sir)''', his successor; 
2 CONT **  '''Thomas (Sir)''', M.P. for the co. of Warwick; 
2 CONT **  '''Giles''', ancestor of the Astleys of Wolvey. 
2 CONT * Thomas, 3rd Lord Astley, was s. at his decease by his eldest son, William de Astley, 4th Lord Astley. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 12, Astley, Baro
2 CONC ns Astley] ______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas of Astley''', 
2 CONT * nephew and h., being s. and h. of Sir Giles of A. (d. before 1316), 
2 CONT * br of the last Lord, by Alice, (living 1344-5), 2nd dau and coh. of Sir Thomas Wolvey. 
2 CONT * He had seizin 27 Mar 1326, having proved his age. 
2 CONT * He was summoned to Parliament from 25 Feb 1342/3 (17 Edward III), to Mar 1249/50 (23 Edward III). 
2 CONT * He''' founded a chantry''' in the parish church of Astley. 
2 CONT * He '''m. before''' 1336/7, when she was living, Elizabeth 
2 CONT ** dau of Guy (de Beauchamp), 2nd Earl of Warwick, by Alice '''dau of''' Ralph de Toni. 
2 CONT * He was living 3 May 1366. [Complete Peerage] '''Father:''' Guy Or Giles De Astley 
2 CONT * '''b:''' Abt 1279 in Astley, Warwickshire, England   '''Mother:''' Alice De Wolvey 
2 CONT * '''b:''' Abt 1283 in Wolvey, Nuneaton, Warwickshire, England
2 CONT * '''  Marriage 1''' Elizabeth De Beauchamp 
