1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William of Astley, 4th Lord Astley was born before 1344.1 He was the son of Thomas of Astley, 3rd Lord Astley and Elizabeth de Beauchamp.1 He married Joan Willoughby, daughter of John Willoughby, 2nd Lord Willoughb
2 CONC y de Eresby.1 He died after 1370, without male issue.1
2 CONT
2 CONT William of Astley, 4th Lord Astley succeeded to the title of 4th Lord Astley [E., 1295] circa 1370, although he was never called to Parliament.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of William of Astley, 4th Lord Astley and Joan Willoughby
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Joan of Astley, Baroness Astley+1
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinc
2 CONC t or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 283. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1818. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pe
2 CONC erage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
