2 CONT *<nowiki>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *''''''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA379&lpg=PA379&dq=Margaret+Astley+1354&source=bl&ots=2Ewczw6G5K&sig=iilXPneQJa9odaGKyufQH-JOz9M&hl=en&ei=SCHhTZ27N5HKiAKd4bW6Bg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=10&ved=0CFEQ6A
2 CONC EwCTge#v=onepage&q=Astley&f=false
2 CONT *   6. ELIZABETH DE BEAUCHAMP, married before 1336/7 (as his 2nd wife) THOMAS DE ASTLEY (or ASTELEY), Knt., of Astley, Bentley, and Weddington, Warwickshire, Broughton, Leicestershire, and Crick, Northamptonshire, son and heir of 
2 CONC Giles de Astley, Knt., by Alice, 2nd daughter and co-heiress of Thomas de Wolvey, Knt., of Wolvey, Warwickshire. He was born in or before 1305. They had three sons, ''''''William, Knt.'''''', Thomas, Knt., and Giles. He was marrie
2 CONC d previously to MARGARET ___, who was living 15 Jul 1334. They had no known issue. He was heir in 1325 to his uncle, Nicholas de Astley, 2nd Lord Astley. In 1338 he founded a chantry in Astley, Warwickshire, which, in 1343, he had
2 CONC  sanction to change into a collegiate church. He was summoned to Parliament from 25 Feb. 1342/3 to 10 Mar 1349/50. SIR THOMAS DE ASTLEY, 3rd Lord Astley, was living 3 May 1366.
2 CONT **   7. THOMAS DE ASTLEY, Knt., of Hillmorton, Warwickshire, and, in right of his wife, of Braunstone (in Glenfield and Little Stretton, Leicestershire, younger son. He married before 13 Dec. 1369 ELIZABETH DE HARCOURT, daughter a
2 CONC nd heiress of Richard de Harcourt, Knt., of Ellenhall, Staffordshire, by Joan, daughter of William de Shareshull, Knt., Chief Justice of the King's Bench, Chief Baron of the Exchequer [see HARCOURT 6.i. for her ancestry]. She was 
2 CONC born about 1347/9 (aged 22 in 1369 and 21 in 1370). They had two sons, Thomas, Esq., and John, and one daughter, Elizabeth, wife of John Clay, Knt. They were involved in a protracted series of lawsuits regarding the manor of Ellen
2 CONC hall, the reversion of which was awarded to them. His wife, Elizabeth, was living in 1383-84. SIR THOMAS DE ASTLEY died in 1399.
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *''''''Sir William Astley, 4th Baron Astley, Justice of the Peace for Warwickshire1,2,3,4,5
2 CONT *''''''M, b. before 1345, d. 1420
2 CONT *Father       Sir Thomas Astley, 3rd Lord Astley6 b. c 1305, d. a 21 Jul 1381
2 CONT *Mother      Elizabeth Beauchamp2,6 b. 1313
2 CONT *''''''     Sir William Astley, 4th Baron Astley, Justice of the Peace for Warwickshire was born before 1345 at of Astley, Bentley, & Weddington, Warwickshire, England.2 He married Joan (Katherine?) Willoughby, daughter of Sir Joh
2 CONC n Willoughby, 3rd Lord Willoughby de Eresby and Cecily de Ufford, before 1370; They had only the daughter, Joan.2,3,4 Sir William Astley, 4th Baron Astley, Justice of the Peace for Warwickshire died in 1420 at of Astley, Warwicksh
2 CONC ire, England.2,3
2 CONT *''''''Family       Joan (Katherine?) Willoughby d. bt 1404 - 1414
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Joan Astley+7,8,9,3,4,5 d. 3 Sep 1448 or 12 Nov 1448
