2 CONT *'''Katherine Mortimer1
2 CONT *'''F, #3487, d. 4 August 1369
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 Jan 2011
2 CONT *'''     Katherine Mortimer was the daughter of Roger de Mortimer, 1st Earl of March and Joan de Geneville, Baroness Geneville.1 She married Thomas de Beauchamp, 11th Earl of Warwick, son of Guy de Beauchamp, 10th Earl of Warwick 
2 CONC and Alice de Toni, in 1337.2 She died on 4 August 1369. She died circa 1371.2
2 CONT *'''      From 1337, her married name became Beauchamp.
2 CONT *'''Children of Katherine Mortimer and Thomas de Beauchamp, 11th Earl of Warwick
2 CONT ** 1.Philippa Beauchamp+
2 CONT ** 2.Joan Beauchamp3
2 CONT ** 3.Alice Beauchamp4 d. 26 Oct 1383
2 CONT ** 4.Maud de Beauchamp+5 d. Feb 1402/3
2 CONT ** 5.Sir William Beauchamp, 1st Lord Bergavenny+1 b. bt 1330 - 1340, d. 8 May 1411
2 CONT ** 6.Thomas de Beauchamp, 12th Earl of Warwick+ b. 1339, d. 8 Apr 1401
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 24. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S125] Richard Glanville-Brown, online <e-mail address>, Richard Glanville-Brown (RR 2, Milton, Ontario, Canada), downloaded 17 August 2005.
2 CONT * 3.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 3.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 49.
2 CONT * 5.[S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume III, page 292. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p349.htm#i3487
