3 CONT 1604	James I presented Warwick Castle to Sir Fulke Greville who was a poet and contemporary of Sir Philip Sidney. The castle had stood empty for 14 years and was in a dilapidated state. Sir Fulke Greville spent considerable money 
3 CONC on improvements and repairs
3 CONT 1618	The Earldom of Warwick was created for a third time for Robert Rich (d. 1619), 3rd Baron Rich and referred to as the 1st Earl of Warwick . However, unlike previous holders of the title, the Rich family did not control Warwick
3 CONC  Castle
3 CONT  	Warwick Castle remained in the hands of the Greville family who were eventually given the title in 1759
