2 CONT 1327 - 1377 Edward III (son of Edward II)
2 CONT 13th Nov 1312 Edward III was born at Windsor and known as Edward of Windsor
2 CONT The reign of Edward III saw the great Chivalric Age and Warwick Castle was the scene of many tournaments, feasts, banquets and processions
2 CONT 1338 -1342 Edward III pawned the Crown Jewels in order to pay his troops at the start of the Hundred Years War between England and France - the practice was forbidden after his reign
2 CONT 1346 Thomas de Beauchamp, 11th Earl of Warwick, commanded troops at the battle of Crecy
