2 CONC en his other son Ambrose
2 CONT 1551 John Dudley is given the title Duke of Northumberland which makes him the most powerful noble in England. The young King Edward is sickly and Dudley realises that if the King dies, and either of his sisters take the crown, th
2 CONC at Dudley will lose his power and probably his head 
2 CONT 1552 John Dudley plots with the Earl of Suffolk and arranges the marriage of his son, Guildford Dudley, to the Suffolk's daughter, Lady Jane Grey
2 CONT May 25, 1553 Guildford Dudley and Lady Jane Grey are forced into marriage
2 CONT 1553 Edward died of tuberculosis and he left the throne to 'the Lady Jane and her heirs male.' Lady Jane Grey was John Dudley's daughter- in-law
2 CONT Monday 10 July - 1553 Lady Jane Grey (Queen for just Nine Days)
2 CONT Monday 10th July 1553 Lady Jane Grey was proclaimed Queen of England
2 CONT 19th July 1553 Queen Jane was deposed as Queen
2 CONT 23rd August, 1553 John Dudley, Duke of Northumberland, was beheaded for treason
2 CONT 1553 - 1558 Mary (Henry's daughter by Queen Katherine of Aragon)
2 CONT 1553 - 1558 The eldest daughter of Henry VIII is referred to as 'Bloody Mary' for her persecution of Protestants and political rivals
2 CONT February 12, 1554 Lady Jane Grey and her husband Guildford were both executed
2 CONT 1553 John Dudley (b.c.1528 - d.1554) took the title 2nd Earl of Warwick but died shortly after due to ill health no doubt caused by his nine month imprisonment following his implication in the Lady Jane Grey situation
2 CONT 1554 Ambrose Dudley (d.1590), 3rd Earl of Warwick.
