2 CONT Warwick Castle - Ancient Timeline of Facts, Dates and Events
2 CONT
2 CONT 79AD
2 CONT
2 CONT Roman fort was established at the site of Warwick by Agricola - the Romans left England in 410AD
2 CONT Dark Ages - 425
2 CONT
2 CONT The Saxons had moved into the Avon valley when the Romans left
2 CONT Dark Ages - 584AD
2 CONT
2 CONT The Anglo-Saxon kingdom of Mercia is founded in England
2 CONT Dark Ages - 793
2 CONT
2 CONT The Vikings invade Britain
2 CONT Dark Ages - 874
2 CONT
2 CONT Large parts of Mercia to the east of Warwickshire were ceded to Danish (Viking) invaders
2 CONT Dark Ages - 886
2 CONT
2 CONT The north-eastern edge of Warwickshire, became the boundary 
2 CONT between the Danelaw (the kingdom of the Danes) to the east and 
2 CONT Mercia to the west.
2 CONT Dark Ages - 914
2 CONT
2 CONT To protect Mercia from the Vikings Edward the Elder, the son of Alfred the Great and his sister Aethelflaed the 'Lady of the Mercians', and daughter of King Alfred the Great, build a Burh at Warwick
2 CONT Dark Ages - 1001
2 CONT
2 CONT The first recorded use of the name Warwickshire  named after 
2 CONT Warwick meaning 'dwellings by the weir'. A weir was a fence or wattle built across a stream to catch or retain fish
2 CONT 1065
