1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_de_Beauchamp_II
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Guy de Beauchamp (born c. 1335 - died 28 April 1360), Knight, was an English nobleman and heir apparent to the title of Earl of Warwick, being the eldest son of the 11th Earl of Warwick. He served as a military commander in th
2 CONC e army of Edward III in France, where he was mortally injured in a freak hailstorm during the Siege of Chartres on 13 April. He died three weeks later on 28 April 1360.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT Born 1335, Guy was the son of Thomas de Beauchamp, 11th Earl of Warwick and Katherine Mortimer, Countess of Warwick.[1] He was knighted with his brother, Thomas, in July 1355, when the King was with the fleet in the Downs on the w
2 CONC ay to an invasion of France. For his good service, he was granted an annual pension of L100 on 27 November 1355.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT Guy de Beauchamp married Philippa de Ferrers before 1353:[1] daughter of Henry de Ferrers, 2nd Lord Ferrers of Groby, and Isabel de Verdun.[2] His widow Philippa died 5 August 1384, and was buried at Necton, Norfolk. He left a wil
2 CONC l dated 26 September 1359.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (born c. 1367 - died c. 1369)[1]
2 CONT Katherine, nun at Shouldham.[1]
2 CONT His daughters were, by entail, excluded from their grandfather's inheritance
2 CONT
