2 CONT ==========================================
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William de Beauchamp, 1st Baron Bergavenny, KG (circa 1343 – 8 May 1411) was an English peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT A younger son of the 11th Earl of Warwick, he was summoned to Parliament on 23 July 1392 as "Willilmo Beauchamp de Bergavenny", by which he is held to have become Baron Bergavenny.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage and heirs
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lady Joan FitzAlan, daughter of the 11th Earl of Arundel, and they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Richard de Beauchamp (before 1397-1422), later 2nd Baron Bergavenny and then 1st Earl of Worcester
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Joan de Beauchamp, married the 4th Earl of Ormonde
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight of the Garter
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord of Abergavenny
2 CONT
2 CONT 4th son, William de Beauchamp, Knight of the Garter, Lord of Abergavenny. (He was cousin of John, Lord Hastings, Lord of Abergavenny and Earl of Pembroke, whose grandmother was Agnes Mortimer, sister of William's mother, Catherine
2 CONC  de Mortimer.) He succeeded to the Castle and Honour of Abergavenny by virtue of the entail made by John, Earl of Perbroke, who was Seignior of Wieseford and Bergavenny. He served under the gallant Chandos and subsequently, in the
2 CONC  wars with France, with great distinction, and in 1375/6 was, by Edward III, nominated Knight of the Garter. Having succeeded to the lands of Abergavenny, he was summoned to Parliament from July 23, 1392, to December 18, 1409, as 
2 CONC a baron as Lord Bergavenny of Beauchamp of Bergavenny. All the writs being directed to "Willilmo Beauchamp de Bergavenny." In 1399 he was appointed Justiciary of South Wales and Governor of Pembroke. He married Joan, sister and ev
2 CONC entually (1415) co-heir of Thomas FitzAlan, Earl of Arundel, and daughter of Richard Fitz-Alan, Earl of Arundel, by Elizabeth, daughter of William de Bohun, Earl of Northampton. He died May 8, 1411. His widow, who was born 1375, h
2 CONC eld the Castle and Honour of Abergavenny in dower until her death on November 14, 1435.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Kin of Mellcene Thurman Smith, page 784)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Beauchamp, 1st Baron Bergavenny, K.G. (b.bef. 1369 - 8 May 1411) was an English Peer. The son of Sir Thomas de Beauchamp, 11th Earl of Warwick, he was created 1st Baron Bergavenny on 23rd July 1392.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Joan FitzAlan, daughter of Sir Richard FitzAlan, 11th Earl of Arundel
2 CONT
2 CONT (Wikipedia)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William Beauchamp, 1st Baron Bergavenny
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT William Beauchamp, 1st Baron Bergavenny, K.G. (b.circa 1343 - 8 May 1411) was an English Peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Thomas de Beauchamp, 11th Earl of Warwick, he was created 1st Baron Bergavenny on 23 July 1392. This was the second creation of the title.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriage and heirs
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Joan FitzAlan, daughter of Sir Richard FitzAlan, 11th Earl of Arundel, and they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Beauchamp, 1st Earl of Worcester, 2nd Baron Bergavenny (b.bef. 1397-1421/22)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan de Beauchamp, married James Butler, 4th Earl of Ormonde
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]References
2 CONT
2 CONT Carpenter, Christine (2004). "Beauchamp, William (V), first Baron Bergavenny (c.1343–1411)". Oxford Dictionary of National Biography. Oxford University Press. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Beauchamp, 1st Lord Bergavenny was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) in 1375/76.1 He held the office of Captain of Calais in 1383.1 He succeeded to the title of  Lord Abergavenny [Feudal] on 30 December 
2 CONC 1389.1 He was created  1st Lord Bergavenny [England by writ] on 23 July 1392, possibly also described as Lord Beauchamp de Bergavenny.1 He held the office of Governor of Pembroke in 1399.1 He held the office of Justiciar of South 
2 CONC Wales in 1399.1 On 5 June 1411 an inquest was held.2
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_de_Beauchamp,_1st_Baron_Bergavenny
2 CONT
2 CONT About the original Norman motte and bailey castle:  http://www.elmleycastle.com/index.php/history-of-the-castle/
2 CONT
