1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married John de Beauchamp, Knt., of Powick, Worcestershire. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John married first about 17 April 1351 Joan de Cherleton, daughter of Sir John de Cherleton, 2nd Lord Cherleton of Powis, by Maud, daughter of Sir Roger de Mortimer, 1st Earl of March.[1] They had two sons and two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # William, Knt., died shortly before 29 September 1420, married Katherine Usflete and had issue[1]
2 CONT # Walter, Knt., died 30 December 1429 or 1 January 1429/30, married Elizabeth Roches and had two sons[1]
2 CONT # Alice, wife of Sir Thomas le Boteler of Sudeley, Gloucestershire and Sir John Dallingridge of Bodiam, Sussex[1]
2 CONT # Sibyl[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second before 22 September 1374 Elizabeth, possibly daughter of Nicholas Peyvre (or Pever), Knt., 3rd Lord Peyvre. They had no issue.[1] Richardson states that previous accounts of this branch of the Beauchamp family as
2 CONC sumed that Elizabeth was the mother of John de Beauchamp's children, likely because Elizabeth referred to William and Walter as her "sons" in her will. See more discussion on this in Royal Ancestry, vol. IV, page 414, footnote 20.
2 CONT
2 CONT == References 
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&lpg=RA2-PA106&ots=kuqLH_MRa7&dq=agnes%20beauchamp%201361%20compton&pg=PA425#v=onepage&q=mortimer%20geneville%20cherleton&f=true Magna Carta Ancestry:] A Study in Colonial and Mediev
2 CONC al Families, 2nd Edition, 2011 Douglas Richardson.  Page 426 "Cherleton"
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "John (Beauchamp) de Beauchamp (abt.1330-bef.1389)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Beauchamp-198 : accessed 28 May 2026).
