1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 20. Johane9 Clopton, of Toppesfield Manor, Hadleigh (William8, Walter7, William6, Walter5, William4, Walter3, William2, Guillaume1 Peche, Lord Of Cloptunna and Dalham)52 was born in Paston, County Norfolk, possibly
2 CONC , about 22 miles north of Norwich.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married (1) Walter Walcote, of County Norfolk.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married (2) Roger Beauchamp, 2nd Baron Beauchamp of Bletsho5354, son of Roger Beauchamp. He was born Abt. 1363 in Bletsoe, County Bedfordshire, about 24 miles west of Cambridge, County Cambridgeshire55, and died May 3, 140656.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married (3) John Cavendish, Knt.57.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Johane Clopton and Roger Beauchamp are:
2 CONT
2 CONT *+ 29 i. John10 Beauchamp, 3rd Baron Beauchamp of Bletsho.
2 CONT *+ 30 ii. Margaret Beauchamp.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT >Johane married into one of the most eminent and powerful families, the Beauchamps. A companion in arms of the victorious William the Conqueror, the family was represented by the Earls of Warwick and Albemarle, and, the Barons of 
2 CONC St. Amand, Barons of Bletsho, Hache, Kydderminster and Powyke. Counted among her direct descendants are most of the Kings and Queens of England who have held the throne since Henry, VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Descendants of Guillaume Peche, Lord of Cloptunna and Dalham
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
