2 CONT *'''Joan Clopton1
2 CONT *F, #118650
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Apr 2004
2 CONT *'''     Joan Clopton is the daughter of Sir Walter Clopton.1 She married, firstly, Sir Walter Walcot before 1366.1 She married, secondly, Roger Beauchamp, son of Roger Beauchamp, 1st Lord Beauchamp (of Bletsoe), after 1366.1
2 CONT *'''      From before 1366, her married name became Walcot.1 From after 1366, her married name became Beauchamp.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S2] Peter W. Hammond, editor, The Complete Peerage or a History of the House of Lords and All its Members From the Earliest Times, Volume XIV: Addenda & Corrigenda (Stroud, Gloucestershire, U.K.: Sutton Publishing, 1998), pag
2 CONC e 75. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage, Volume XIV.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p11865.htm#i118650
2 CONT *_________________________
2 CONT *'''Joan Clopton[1]
2 CONT *'''Family    Roger de Beauchamp,   b. Cal 1363, of , Bletsoe, Bedfordshire, England ,   d. 3 May 1406 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **          1. Sir John de Beauchamp, of , Bletsoe, Bedfordshire, England ,   d. 13 Apr 1412
2 CONT **          2. Catherine de Beauchamp
2 CONT *Sources 
2 CONT *1.[S2] Paget Heraldic Baronage, Paget, Gerald, (Manuscript, filmed by the Genealogical Society of Utah, 1957), chart no. 45 Beachamp of Bletsoe, FHL microfilm 170063 (Reliability: 3).
2 CONT *From:  https://histfam.familysearch.org//getperson.php?personID=I1757&tree=PagetHeraldicBaronag
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *Roger Beauchamp, 1st Baron Beauchamp of Bletsoe (c.1315 – 3 January 1380)[1][2] was an English soldier and peer who served both Edward III and his wife, Philippa of Hainault. He was an ancestor of Henry VII.
2 CONT *Roger Beauchamp, perhaps born about 1315, was the son and heir of Roger de Beauchamp, a younger son of Sir Walter de Beauchamp and Alice de Tony, daughter of Roger de Tony of Flamstead, Hertfordshire.[3] Clarification of the abov
2 CONC e relationship is required as it conflicts with the inset information box which shows this Roger as the son of Walter instead of another Roger as the son of Walter. Further, the dates shown for Alice de Tony (Toeni) are shown as b
2 CONC . 26 Apr 1284 - d. 1 Jan 1324 elsewhere with her as being the only daughter of Ralph VII de Toeni and being married to Guy de Beauchamp. .... etc.
2 CONT *Beauchamp married firstly, before 15 March 1337, Sibyl de Patteshull (d. before 1375), daughter and one of the four co-heirs of Sir John de Pateshull and Mabel de Grandison, daughter of William de Grandison, 1st Baron Grandison, 
2 CONC by whom he had two sons and a daughter:[2][1]
2 CONT **'''           Sir Roger de Beauchamp (d. before 15 May 1374), who married Joan de Clopton, widow of Sir Walter de Walcote, and daughter of Walter de Clopton, by whom he had a son''', Sir Roger de Beauchamp (d. 3 May 1406), '''an
2 CONC d a daughter''', Margaret Beauchamp, who married Robert Mautby, esquire. Sir Roger de Beauchamp (d. 3 May 1406) was the grandfather of Margaret Beauchamp of Bletso, grandmother of Henry VII.[2][5]
2 CONT **           Philip de Beauchamp .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_Beauchamp,_1st_Baron_Beauchamp_of_Bletso
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *BEAUCHAMP, Sir Roger (1362-1406), of Bletsoe, Beds. and Bloxham, Oxon.
2 CONT *b. Bletsoe, 14 Sept. 1362, s. of '''Sir Roger Beauchamp (d.v.p. 1373/4), prob. by his w. Joan, da. and h. of William Clopton, wid. of Sir Walter Walcot† of Gunton, Norf.'''; gds. and h. of Roger, Lord Beauchamp of Bletsoe (d.1380
2 CONC ), governor of Calais and chamberlain of Edward III’s household. m. Mary, at least 1s. suc. gdfa. 3 Jan. 1380; kntd. by 18 Feb. 1393.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/member/beauchamp-sir-roger-1362-1406
2 CONT *________________________
