2 CONC opton Hall, Wickhambrook, County Suffolk, possibly.  All Saints Church at Wickhambrook dates from about 1240, too late to be the burial place for William and Anne, although there was probably an earlier church.  A small Saxon figu
2 CONC re is on the south wall.  He married Anne Grey, of Buckingham Castle, County Norfolk5, daughter of John Grey, of Buckingham Castle, County Norfolk.  She died in Clopton Hall, Wickhambrook, County Suffolk, possibly.
