2 CONT www.celtic-casimir.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Margery DE VERDUN Heiress of Weobley 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 10 Aug 1310, Alton Castle, Cheadle, Staffordshire, England   
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (1): Before 20 Feb 1326-1327    Married (2): Before 10 Sep 1355, 3rd husband 1st wife    Married (3): Before 18 Oct 1339, 2nd husband   Died: Before 1377  Another name for Margery was Margeret DE VERDON.   
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: (iii) Margery, born and baptised 10 August 1310 at Alton, married, 1stly, before 20 February 1326/7, William (le Blount), Lord Blount, who died s.p. shortly before 3 October 1337. She married, 2ndly, before 18 Octob
2 CONC er 1339, Sir Mark Husee (son and heir apparent of Henry, 2nd Lord Husee), who died v.p. shortly before 10 February 1345/6. She married, 3rdly, before 10 September 1355, as his 1st wife, Sir John de Crophull, of Bonnington, Notts, 
2 CONC who died 3 July 1383. She died before him in or before 1377. Her representatives would appear to be those of Thomas Husee, her descendant by her 2nd marriage, living 1478 (g). [Complete Peerage XII/2:252, (transcribed by Dave Utzi
2 CONC nger)]  (g) As, however, her issue by her 2nd husband appears to have been disinherited and her lands descended to the issue of her 3rd marriage, it is possible that her representatives may be found among those of Robert Devereux,
2 CONC  Earl of Essex (who dsps 1646).   He [William le Blount] m. before 20 Feb 1326/7, Margery, 3rd daughter and coheir of Sir Theobald de Verdon, of Alton, co. Stafford [Lord Verdun], by his 1st wife, Maud, daughter of Sir Edmund de M
2 CONC ortimer, of Wigmore, co. Hereford. He and his wife had livery of her lands, 30 Oct 1328 and 26 Mar 1332. He dsp. shortly before 3 Oct 1337, when any Barony, that may be supposed to have been created by the writ of 1330, became ext
2 CONC inct. His widow, who was b. 10 Aug 1310, at Alton, aforesaid, and baptized there the same day, inherited Weobley Castle, co. Hereford, &c., of which she (again) had livery, 15 Dec 1337. She m. before 18 Oct 1339, Sir Mark Husse. T
2 CONC hey had livery of her lands, 1 Mar 1343/4. He d. before 21 Jul 1349. She m., 3rdly, before 10 Sep 1355, as 1st wife, Sir John Crophull, of Bennington, co. Notts. He d. 3 Jul 1383. [Complete Peerage II:196]   
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information: Margery married Sir William LE BLOUNT 1st Baron le Blount of Sodington, son of Sir Walter LE BLOUNT of Rock and Joanna DE SODINGTON, before 20 Feb 1326-1327 . (Sir William LE BLOUNT 1st Baron le Blount of Sod
2 CONC ington was born about 1295 in Sodington Hall, Mamble, Cleobury Mortimer, Worcestershire, England and died before 3 Oct 1337 in S.p.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information: Margery also married Sir John DE CROPHULL of Bonnington, son of Sir Ralph DE CROPHULL of Bonnington and Maud, before 10 Sep 1355 in 3rd husband 1st wife. (Sir John DE CROPHULL of Bonnington was born about 131
2 CONC 0 in Hemington, Leicestershire, England and died on 3 Jul 1383 in Sutton Bonington, Loughborough, Nottinghamshire, England.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information: Margery also married Sir Mark HUSEE of Moreton & Standen before 18 Oct 1339 in 2nd husband. (Sir Mark HUSEE of Moreton & Standen was born about 1315 in South Moreton, Wallingford, Berkshire, England and died 
2 CONC before 10 Feb 1345-1346 in Standen Manor, Hungerford, Berkshire, England (dvp).)
2 CONT
2 CONT
