1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT > '''John Beauchamp, 2nd Lord de Beauchamp, Baron of Kidderminster''' was born circa 1378. He was the son of John Beauchamp, 1st Lord de Beauchamp, Baron of Kidderminster and Joan le Fitzwith. He died in September 1420, without ma
2 CONC le issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT > He succeeded as the 2nd Lord de Beauchamp, Baron of Kidderminster [E., 1387] in 1398, after the reversal of his father's attainder. In 1399 he accompanied the King into Ireland. In 1400 his honours were forfeited, after the reaf
2 CONC firmation of the proceeding against King Richard II. He held the office of Escheator of Worcestershire in 1406/7.
2 CONT
2 CONT > On his death, the Lordship of Beauchamp became extinct (after being in attainder for 20 years).
2 CONT
2 CONT > Child of John Beauchamp, 2nd Lord de Beauchamp, Baron of Kidderminster
2 CONT
2 CONT ># Margaret Beauchamp+ b. c 1400
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p11860.htm#i118596 The Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Reference:
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Beauchamp-1151
