2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Ralph Boteler1
2 CONT
2 CONT Note*	 He was one of the justices of assize for Warwickshire and a commissioner for assessing and collecting the 14th part of all men's moveable goods. 13 and 15 Henry III.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family	
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph le Boteler of Wem d. b 10 Jan 1278
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited	8 Feb 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations	
2 CONT
2 CONT [S342] Sir Bernard Burke, Extinct Peerages, p. 63.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=REG&db=jweber&id=I05470
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice le BOTELER , of Oversley (Ralph le BOTELER , of Oversley5, Robert le BOTELER , of Oversley4, Ralph le BOTELER , of Oversley3, Robert le BOTELER , of Oversley & Ingleby2, Ralph le BOTELER , of Oversley1) was born ABT 1185 i
2 CONC n Oversley, Alcester, Warwickshire, England.
2 CONT  	  Children of Maurice le BOTELER , of Oversley are:
2 CONT *+	2	  i.	Ralph le BOTELER , Lord of Oversley was born ABT 1220 in Oversley, Alcester, Warwickshire, England, and died 3 JUL 1281.
2 CONT *+	3	  ii.	Joan le BOTELER was born ABT 1221 in Oversley, Alcester, Warwickshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice Boteler, one of the justices of assize for the co. of Warwick in the 13th and 16th Henry III [1229 and 1232], and a commissioner for assessing and collecting the fourteenth part of all men's movable goods, according to the
2 CONC  form and order then appointed. This feudal lord filled the office of justice of assize for the same shire a second and third time, and was repeatedly justice for the gaol delivery at Warwick in the same king's reign. He was s. by
2 CONC  his son, Ralph Boteler. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, England, 1883, p. 63, Boteler, Barons Boteler, of Oversley and Wemme]
