1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Ralph le Botiler of Pulverbatch and Norbury was the 3rd son of Sir Ralph le Botiler of Codynton, Pulverbatch and Norbury,  and Maud de Marmion.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph le Botiler of Pulverbatch and Norbury married Hawise Gobion, daughter of Richard Gobion, before 1300.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT He petitions the King and states that the king's father granted to his father that he would pay 5 marks per annum for all his debts from the debt of Philip Marmion. He asks the king to pay he pay 100s. from that debt per annum, fo
2 CONC r himself and his heirs, to Ralph and his heirs, as he has suffered greatly in the king's service in Scotland, and holds nothing but 100s. of land which is charged with the debt, and his parceners hold £300 of land charged with th
2 CONC e debt; and he has granted to pay them 100s per annum for all their debts. Endorsement: [None].
2 CONT
2 CONT The petition is dated to 1307-1327 as it clearly dates to the reign of Edward II, though there appears to be no evidence to more closely date it.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph le Botiler of Pulverbatch and Norbury died in March 1342.1,4
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Ralph le Botiler of Pulverbatch and Norbury and Hawise Gobion
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir John Botiler1 d. 1339
2 CONT # Sir William le Botiler1 d. b 28 Oct 1349
2 CONT # Sir Ralf le Botiler of Watton Woodhall+4
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph Boteler of Norbury, b. 1277  married 1300  Hawise Gobion, b. 1282, dau. and heir of Richard, son of Hugh Gobion of Higham Gobion. Ralph moved to Woodhall 1302, and when he died held the manor of Badminton and 1/2 manor of Mi
2 CONC ddleton,Warwickshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Ralph Boteler, Married Matilda/Maud de Marmion, dau. of Sir Philip de Marmion of Tamworth castle and Joan de Kilpeck, dau. of Hugh
2 CONT
