2 CONT
2 CONT RALPH BASSET, son and heir, under age in 1330. In July 1369, being then aged over 40, he became, by the death of his cousin, Robert, Lord Colvill one of the two coheirs of the estates and Barony of that family, inheriting the Cast
2 CONC le and Honour of Bytham, co. Lincoln, Thornton Steward, co. York, &C. In consequence, doubtless, of these acquisitions, he was summoned to Parliament 8 January 1370/1 and 6 October 1372, by writs directed Radulfo Basset de Sapcote
2 CONC , whereby he is held to have become LORD BASSET. He fought in the French wars and was one of the heroes of Crecy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 1stly, about 1346, Sibyl, sister of Thomas ASTLEY [3rd LORD ASTLEY], and daughter of Sir Giles Astley, by Alice, 2nd daughter and coheir of Sir Thomas DE WOLVEY. He married, 2ndly, Alice, daughter of John DERBY. He died
2 CONC  s.p.m., 17 July 1378, when the Barony fell (according to modern doctrine) into abeyance between his two daughters and coheirs. Will, as Ralph Basset, knight, Lord of Sapcote, directing his burial to be at Castle Bytham, dated the
2 CONC re the Monday after the Ascension I I May 1377, proved at Lincoln. His widow, who married Sir Robert TUCHET, and afterwards Sir Anketine MALLORY, died a widow, 12 October 1412, and was buried at Stamford, near her last husband. [C
2 CONC omplete Peerage II:7-8, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters
2 CONT * (1) Alice, da. by the 1st wife, then aged 30, and wife of Sir Laurence Dutton, afterwards wife of Sir Robert Moton, of Peckleton.  
2 CONT * (2) Elizabeth, da. by the 2nd wife, b. at Castle Bytham, 1 Aug. 1372, then aged 7 (_sic_) and wife of Richard Grey, afterwards (1393) Lord Grey of Codnor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT
2 CONT From Jim Weber 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: I disagree with CP in this situation. Due to the fact that Sibyl was born before 1317 (and probably earlier), I think that Sibyl and Ralph were the mother and father of this Ralph, and were born well before 1346.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/112735818/ralph-basset
2 CONT
2 CONT Of Sapcote, Leicestershire, of Cheadle, Staffordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son and heir to Simon Basset and Isabel le Boteler. Grandson of Ralph Basset and Elizabeth Coleville, William le Boteler and Angharad, daughter of Gruffydd ap Madoc of Wales. Ralph was born between 1320 and 1325.
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Sybil de Astley, daughter of Sir Giles de Astley and Alice Wolvey, daughter of Sir Thomas. They had two daughters, Alice, wife of Sir Robert Moton, and Eleanor, wife of John FitzWilliam.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, he was the husband of Alice Driby, the daughter of John de Driby of Breedon, Leicestershire and Amie, daughter of Peter de Gaveston, the 1st Earl of Cornwall and King Edward II's professed lover, widow of Robert Tuchet. 
2 CONC They had one daughter, Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph died testate, and was buried at Bytham. After his death, Alice remarried a third time to Sir Anketil Mallory of Kirkby Mallory, Leicestershire.
2 CONT
