1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes for Nicholas de Longford and Alice le Boteler c 1324 Nicholas de Longford was representative for Derbyshire in parliament, 17 Edward 2. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1333 Nicholas de Longford was appointed commissioner of Array for Derbyshire to call out and have in readiness for the field all men between sixteen and sixty years of age. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1341 On 19 November, Nicholas de Langeford was on a list of sheriffs of Derbyshire and Nottingham. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1347 Nicholas de Longford and Anker de Frecheville were among the Derbyshire men of England who fought at Crecy (Battle of Cressy), France. [4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice, daughter of Nicholas Longford, of Longford, Derbyshire; reportedly married William FitzHerbert, and was the mother of his son Henry. [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT In her discussion of Nicholas Longford, who died 8 February 1355/56, Rosie Bevan states, [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Apart from his son Nicholas, said to be aged 23 and more, it is believed he left a daughter Alice - according to Fitzherbert pedigrees, wife of William Fitzherbert of Norbury (Mosley, 1999) - although chronology might suggest that
2 CONC  Alice was of the next generation of the Longford family [24].
2 CONT
2 CONT [24] Her grandson, Nicholas Fitzherbert, was born c.1410.
2 CONT
2 CONT The reference to Mosley, 1999, is to Mosley, Charles (1999), Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th ed. Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd., p.2683.
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnotes: [1] Thomas Noble, ed., The history, Gazeteer, and Directory of the county of Derby: drawn up from actual observation, and from the best authorities; containing a variety of geological, mineralogical, commercial and stat
2 CONC istical information, Vol. 1 (Stephen Glover, 1829), Appendix, 23, [HathiTrust], [HathiTrust].
2 CONT
2 CONT [2] J. Charles Cox, Memorials of Old Derbyshire (London: Bemrose & Sons, 1907), 13, [HathiTrust].
2 CONT
2 CONT [3] A. Hughes, Lists and Indexes, Volume 9, List of Sheriffs for England and Wales (London: HMSO, 1898), 103, [GoogleBooks].
2 CONT
2 CONT [4] J. Charles Cox, Memorials of Old Derbyshire (London: Bemrose & Sons, 1907), 13, [HathiTrust].
2 CONT
2 CONT [5] Wikipedia article about Battle_of_Crecy, content subject to change, [Wikipedia].
2 CONT
2 CONT [6] Charles Mosley, ed., Burke's Peerage, Baronetage, & Knightage, 107th edition, Vol. 3 (Willington, Delaware: Burke's Peerage & Gentry, LLC, 2003), 3710.
2 CONT
2 CONT [7] Rosie Bevan, "A Study of a Medieval Knightly Family: The Longfords of Derbyshire – Part 1," Foundations Volume 1, Part 4 (2004), 211-231 at 216, [FoundationMedievalGenealogy].
2 CONT
2 CONT Citation: Robert and Janet Chevalley Wolfe, Janet and Robert Wolfe Genealogy, "Notes for Nicholas de Longford and Alice le Boteler" Webpage: www.umich.edu/~bobwolfe/gen/mn/m26869x26966.htm Email address: JanetRobertWolfeGenealogy@
2 CONC gmail.com
