1 NAME Fulke /le Strange/ 3rd Baron of Blackmere
2 GIVN Fulke
2 NSFX 3rd Baron of Blackmere
2 _MARNM le Strange
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 2 FEB 1330
2 PLAC Of, Longnor, Shropshire, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 30 AUG 1349
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On Fulke's death as above the Barony of Strange (of Blackmere) according to modern doctrine, fell into abeyance between his 2 infant daughters, (1) Joan, who married John Careless or Carless, (2) Eleanor, who marri
2 CONC ed Edward De Acton; although a Hampshire jury found that Fulke died without heir of his body and that his brother John was his heir. Undoubtedly John did succeed to his barony in the territorial sense; but according to modern doct
2 CONC rine he did not succeed to the alleged Parliamentary Barony and the writ by which he was subsequently summoned created a new Barony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leo v.d. Pas says that Fulke’s father was somebody else, however CP  Vol XII/1, p. 344 says what is shown is correct: Father John, 2nd Lord  Strange d. 21 July 1349. He (Fulk) was contracted, at about age 16, on 12 Mar 1346/47 to 
2 CONC Elizabeth de Stafford, and d.s.p.m. 30 Aug 1349.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. His brother John was summoned to parliament from 3 April 1360 as  'Johanni Lestraunge', and is held to have become Lord Strange [although CP  observes this technically was the creation of a new Barony, for the reason  noted bel
2 CONC ow].
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Fulk was survived by two daughters: as CP observes, at his death  [p. 344]
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ Hamon Le Strange, 1916; Pedigree No VIII - LE STRANGE OF BLACKMERE
2 CONT
2 CONT For some odd reason Hamon omits to show on the Pedigree chart the descent of this Fulk and his siblings; indeed he shows John Le Strange, 2nd Lord Strange of Blackmere, as o.b.s.p. July 20, 1349. Hamon goes on to discuss his proge
2 CONC ny on pages 316 and 317. No children are shown on the chart or mentioned in text for Fulk, 3rd Lord
2 CONT
2 CONT However, the ladies, Joan (m John Careless - a quibus Corbett of Longmor) and Eleanore (m Edward de Acton of Longmor) are shown as having a third sister Margaret - a nun. They are shown as being of Fulk Le Strange who had Longmor,
2 CONC  brother of John, 2nd Lord.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clearly there are two errors on the Pedigree Chart if the text is correct; but is there a third error in both related to the descent of Joan, Eleanor and Margaret if the other references quoted here are correct.
