1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John de Mohun, 1st Baron Mohun (died 1330), Lord of Dunster was an English noble. He fought in the wars in Flanders and Scotland. He was a signatory of the Baron's Letter to Pope Boniface VIII in 1301.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT John was the eldest son of John de Mohun and Eleanor filias Reynold. He served in Flanders in 1297 and in Scotland. He was a signatory of the Baron's Letter to Pope Boniface VIII in 1301.
2 CONT He died in 1330 and was succeeded by his grandson John, his eldest son John predeceased him in 1322.
2 CONT Marriages and issue
2 CONT He married firstly Ada de Tiptoft, they had the following issue:
2 CONT *John de Mohun, Master of Dunster (died 1322).
2 CONT *'''William de Mohun'''
2 CONT *Thomas de Mohun
2 CONT *Reginald de Mohun
2 CONT *Lawrence de Mohun
2 CONT *Robert de Mohun
2 CONT *Payn de Mohun
2 CONT *Joan de Mohun, married John Luttrell, had issue.
2 CONT He married secondly Sybilla.
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_de_Mohun,_1st_Baron_Mohun
2 CONT __________
