2 CONT (THIS JOHN DE MOHUN IS LISTED AS FATHER OF JOHN DE MOHUN, 2ND LORD MOHUN & MARGARET WHO MARRIED SIR JOHN CAREW SAME AS IN https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p801.htm#i24051)
2 CONT '''John de Mohun, 1st Lord Mohun'''1 
2 CONT M, #203521, b. 1249, d. 11 June 1279
2 CONT Last Edited=3 Dec 2020
2 CONT John de Mohun, 1st Lord Mohun was born in 1249 at Dunster, Somerset, England.2 He was the son of John de Mohun and Joan de Ferrers.2 He married Eleanor fitz Piers, daughter of Sir Reynold fitz Piers and Alice de Stanford.3 He died
2 CONC  on 11 June 1279 at Dunster, Somerset, England.2
2 CONT He lived at Dunster, Somerset, EnglandG.1 He gained the title of 1st Lord Mohun.1
2 CONT '''Child of John de Mohun, 1st Lord Mohun''' and Eleanor fitz Piers
2 CONT 1. John de Mohun, 2nd Lord Mohun+
2 CONT '''Child of John de Mohun, 1st Lord Mohun'''
2 CONT 1. Margaret Mohun+4 b. b 1326
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S37] BP2003 volume 1, page 682. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT [S7732] Geni, online https://www.geni.com. Hereinafter cited as Geni.
2 CONT 2.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinc
2 CONC t or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 339. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT [S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT From: https://www.thepeerage.com/p20353.htm#i203521
2 CONT ______
2 CONT John (V) de Mohun, 2nd Baron Mohun, 9th feudal baron of Dunster, KG (1320–1376) was a founder member and the 11th Knight of the Most Noble Order of the Garter in 1348.
2 CONT Life
2 CONT John was the last in the senior male line of Mohun of Dunster. He was the '''son of John de Mohun''' (eldest son of John Mohun, 1st Baron Mohun), '''who predeceased his father, having fought at the Battle of Boroughbridge in 1322 
2 CONC and died some time after in Scotland.'''[1] He was grandson of John de Mohun, 1st Baron Mohun and Sibyll Segrave; daughter of John Segrave, 2nd Baron Segrave – son of Nicholas de Segrave, 1st Baron Segrave. His grandfather was Sir
2 CONC e John de Mohun of Dunster, banneret, became the first Baron Mohun in 1299, and sealed the Barons' Letter to the Pope in 1301; he bore at the Battle of Falkirk (1298), and at the Siege of Carlaverock (1300).
2 CONT In 1328 and 1331, he served in the Kings service in Brittany, with Sir Bartholemew de Burghersh. In 1332, he attended Edward Prince of Wales KG, when Edward III KG entered France by Normandy, and continued in service at the Siege 
2 CONC of Calais, and again in 1333. [2] His last recorded military service was in attendance to the Prince of Wales into Gascony in 1341.[3]
2 CONT He died on 14 September 1376, leaving no sons, and was buried in Bruton priory. [2]
2 CONT Heraldry
2 CONT His Arms were Or, a cross engrailed sable. His son bore the same with a label of three points gules.[4]
2 CONT Family
2 CONT After the death of his grandfather (Sire John), John inherited the vast family estates at the age of 10, held by Henry Burghersh Bishop of Lincoln, until he came of age. He married Joan, daughter of Sir Bartholomew Burghersh the e
2 CONC lder, who was sister to Bartholomew the younger KG, one of the founders of the Garter.
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Mohun,_2nd_Baron_Mohun 
2 CONT ______
