1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/CAREW1.htm#Elizabeth CAREW1
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth CAREW
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: ABT 1372, Mallerforde, Buckinghamshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 25 Sep 1410
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John CAREW
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Agnes MARTIN
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Roger LEWKNOR (b. ABT 1369 - d. BEF 1405) ABT 1391, Mallerforde, Buckinghamshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Thomas LEWKNOR (Sir Knight) (b. ABT 1392 - d. 22 Jun 1452)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Agnes (Anne) LEWKNOR (b. ABT 1393)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. John LEWKNOR (b. ABT 1395)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books?id=yknQAAAAMAAJ&pg=RA1-PA69&lpg=RA1-PA69&dq=Roger+Lewknor&source=bl&ots=xOVQTojse-&sig=3rzJ81yqjit80inKMk2AuuTDxXQ&hl=en&ei=gCvBTMG-C4a2sAO75pijDA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CBQQ6AEw
2 CONC ATgK#v=onepage&q=Roger%20Lewknor&f=false Collections for a history of Staffordshire], Volume 2 By Staffordshire Record Society
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg.69
2 CONT
2 CONT By virtue of this entail the manor of Raunton will have devolved on Sir Roger Lewknor the son of Joane D'Oyley. This Roger Lewknor, who resided at Bradhurst, Co. Sussex, married Margaret, daughter of Sir John Carew, of Molesford, 
2 CONC Co. Bucks, Knight, and died 1401. Their eldest son, Thomas Lewknor, was then 19 years of age. They had also a younger son, John, from whom the Lewknors of Acrise, Co. Kent, were descended, and I suppose Eleanor Harcourt to have be
2 CONC en the daughter of the same Sir Roger. Sir Thomas Lewknor, the eldest son, was in 1403, found heir, through his grandmother, Joane D'Oyley, to the extensive estates of the Tregoze family, at Goring, Co. Sussex, and elsewhere in th
2 CONC at county, and removed his seat to Goring. He was thrice married, first to Elizabeth, daughter of Nicholas Carew, of Beddington, Co. Surrey, by whom he had no issue; secondly to Phelippa, relict of Sir Richard Berners, and daughte
2 CONC r and eventual heiress of Walter Dalyngrigge, son of Sir Roger Dalyngrigge, of Bodeham Castle, Co. Sussex, Knight. His last wife, Catherine, survived him, and her inquisition p.m. was held in 21 Edw. IV. Sir Thomas Lewknor left si
2 CONC x sons, between whom his large estates were divided. The eldest son, Sir Roger Lewknor, however, succeeded to Stoke D'Oyley and the principal estates, and died in 1475, leaving six sons and three daughters, of whom Thomas, the eld
2 CONC est son, succeeded to Stoke D'Oyley. .......
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p936.htm#i28101
2 CONT
2 CONT (THESE DATES FOR ELIZABETH'S PARENTS ARE AFTER SHE WAS BORN)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Carew1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, b. circa 1364, d. before 1419
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Nicholas Carew b. c 1380 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother Isabel de la Mare b. c 1375 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Elizabeth Carew was born circa 1364 at of Beddington & Warlingham, Surrey, England. She married Roger Lewkenor, Esq., son of Sir Thomas Lewknor and Joan D'Oyly, circa 1385; They had 2 sons (Thomas & John) and 1 daughter (Agne
2 CONC s/Anne). Elizabeth Carew married Sir Robert Knyvett, son of Sir John Knyvett, Lord Chancellor of England, Chief Justice of the King's Bench and Eleanor Basset, between 15 November 1400 and 1412. Elizabeth Carew died before 1419 at
2 CONC  of Ramsden-Belhouse, Essex, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 Roger Lewkenor, Esq. b. c 1365, d. b 15 Nov 1400 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children ◦Agnes (Anne) Lewknor b. c 1387
2 CONT
2 CONT ◦Sir Thomas Lewknor, Sheriff of Surrey & Sussex, Burgess of Lewes+ b. c 1392, d. 22 Jun 1452
2 CONT
2 CONT ◦John Lewknor b. c 1395
2 CONT
2 CONT  Family 2 Sir Robert Knyvett b. c 1365, d. 1419 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S8781] Unknown author, The Royal Descents of 500 Immigrants, by Gary Boyd Roberts, p. 431; Wallop Family, p. 488.
2 CONT
