1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sir Roger Lewknor
2 CONT *'''M, b. circa 1469, d. 15 January 1543
2 CONT *Father Sir Thomas Lewkenor, Sheriff of Surrey & Sussex, Constable of Bodiam Castle b. bt 1438 - 1448, d. 20 Jul 1484 
2 CONT *Mother Katherine Pelham d. 1481 
2 CONT *'''     Sir Roger Lewknor was born circa 1469 at of Trotton, Sussex, England. He married Eleanor Touchet, daughter of Sir John Touchet, 6th Lord Audley, Lord High Treasurer and Anne Echingham, circa 1491.1 Sir Roger Lewknor died 
2 CONC on 15 January 1543 at Trotton, Sussex, England.
2 CONT *'''Family Eleanor Touchet b. c 1470 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT **Jane Lewknor+ b. c 1492
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 723.
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2683.htm#i80623
2 CONT *_____________
2 CONT *'''Eleanor TOUCHET
2 CONT *Father: John TOUCHET (3º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Anne ECHINGHAM (B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *'''Married: Roger LEWKNOR of Dedisham and Bodiam (Sir Knight) (b. 1465 - d. 1543) 
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Jane LEWKNOR (m.1 Christopher Pickering - m.2 Sir Arthur Pole - m.3 Sir William Barentyn)
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#Eleanor TOUCHET1
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *'''Sir Roger Lewkenor1
2 CONT *M, #107594
2 CONT *Last Edited=15 Apr 2003
2 CONT *'''Sir Roger Lewkenor is the son of unknown Lewkenor.[2] 
2 CONT *'''He lived at Trotton, Sussex, England.[3]
2 CONT *'''Child of Sir Roger Lewkenor
2 CONT **1.Jane Lewkenor1 d. b 12 Mar 1562/63
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 136. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *2.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 657. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pe
2 CONC erage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3.[S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 16. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage,
2 CONC  106th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p10760.htm#i107594
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *Bodiam Castle is a 14th-century moated castle near Robertsbridge in East Sussex, England. It was built in 1385 by Sir Edward Dalyngrigge, a former knight of Edward III, with the permission of Richard II, ostensibly to defend the 
2 CONC area against French invasion during the Hundred Years' War.   . . . . 
2 CONT *   Edward's estates, including the castle, were inherited by his son, John Dalyngrigge. Like his father, John enjoyed the favour of the king and was described as the "King's Knight; in 1400 he was granted an annual allowance of 1
2 CONC 00 marks by the king. He died on 27 September 1408; his will ensured that his property belonged to his widow, Alice. John and Alice had no children, so on her death in 1443 the estates and castle were passed on to Richard Dalyngri
2 CONC gge, John's cousin. Richard died without issue, so in accordance with John's will the estates passed on to Richard's sister Philippa in 1470. She was married to Sir Thomas Lewknor, from a prominent Sussex family who owned land all
2 CONC  over the country.[15]   . . . . 
2 CONT *'''   Following Sir Roger Lewknor's death in 1543, his estates were divided among his descendants, and the castle and manor were split''''''.[17] John Levett of Salehurst purchased the castle in 1588.[18] . . . . 
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodiam_Castle
2 CONT *_____________ John Audley is John Touchet, Lord Audley ???
2 CONT *'''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=p_yzpuWi4sgC&pg=PA56&lpg=PA56&dq=Roger+Lewknor+1543&source=bl&ots=RRtN6Q_68a&sig=YoGbh2nBMg_mKuD-onAMJ7SpcLc&hl=en&ei=j9l3TtGjD4fhiAL3pdn4Cg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=10&ved=0CE8Q6AEwC
2 CONC Tge#v=onepage&q=Roger%20Lewknor%201543&f=false/ Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham]
2 CONT *Pg. 55
2 CONT *   15. WILLIAM BARANTYNE, Knt., of Little Haseley and Clare (in Pyrton), Oxfordshire, Sheriff of Oxfordshire, and, in right of his 3rd wife, of Camoys (in Chishelhampton), Kingsey, Chakendene, and Wheatley (in Cuddesdon), Oxfords
2 CONC hire, and Broadhurst, Horsted Keynes, and Iden, Sussex, son and heir, born 31 Dec. 1481 and baptized 1 Jan. 1481/2. He married (1st) MARY READE, daughter and co-heiress of Robert Reade, Knt., of Bore Place (in Chiddingstone), Kent
2 CONC , Chief Justice of Common Pleas, by Margaret, daughter and heiress of John Alphew. She died before 3 Dec. 1518 (date of her father's will). They had one son, Drew, and one daughter, Margaret. He married (2nd) before 1522 ANNE EATO
2 CONC N, widow of Richard Gray, of London, ironmonger. They had one son, Francis, and one
2 CONT *Pg. 56
2 CONT *daughter, Mary (wife of Anthony Huddleston, Esq.). His wife, Anne, died 27 Dec. 1522, and was buried in a church in London. He married (3rd) before 1539 JANE LEWKNOR, widow successively of Christopher Pickering, Knt. (died 7 Sept
2 CONC . 1516) and Arthur Pole, Knt. (died 1535/6), and daughter and co-heiress of '''Roger Lewknor, Knt., of Dedisham and Bodiam, Sussex, by Eleanor, daughter of John Audley, 6th Lord Audley'''. She was born about 1503 (age 40 at her fa
2 CONC ther's death in 1543). They had two sons, Drew and Charles. William and Jane's marriage was declared invalid on 15 Dec 1540, she having taken a vow of perpetual chastity following the death of her prior husband, Arthur Pole, Knt. 
2 CONC  By act of Parliament dated 34 and 35 Henry VIII (c.1543/4),  William and Jane's issue was deemed to be legitimate. SIR WILLIAM BARANTYNE died testate (P.C.C. 5 Coode) 17 Nov. 1549, and was buried at Haseley, Oxfordshire.  . . . .
2 CONC
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *William MORGAN
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1534, Langstone, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT *Died: 10 Dec 1602
2 CONT *Father: Richard MORGAN 
2 CONT *Mother: Joan WINTERSHULL
2 CONT *Married 1: Elizabeth HAGER ABT 1554
2 CONT *Married 2: Catherine LEWKNOR (dau. of '''Roger Lewknor and Elizabeth Meffant''') (w. of John Miles) ABT 1556
2 CONT *Children: ....
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/MORGAN.htm#William MORGAN1
2 CONT *_________________
2 CONT *MORGAN, William III (c.1525-1602), of Chilworth, Surr.
2 CONT *b. c.1525, o.s. of Richard Morgan of Chilworth by Joan, or Jane, da. of Robert Wintershall of Wintershall, nr. Bramley. m. (1)1 Elizabeth, da. of John Thetcher of Presthawes, Westham, Suss., 1s. 4da.; (2)2 Katherine, da. of '''Si
2 CONC r Roger Lewknor''', wid. of John Mills of Grentham. Suss., 1da.; (3) by 1585 Julian(a).3
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/morgan-william-iii-1525-1602
2 CONT *______________________
