1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT =Margaret de Briene=
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Sir Guy de Brienne, KG, Lord Bryan and Elizabeth de Montagu
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sir Guy de Brienne, KG, Lord Bryan married twice and had daughters he called Margaret by each wife.   Married (1) Joan Carew, daughter of sir John Carew/Carreu.  Children include Margaret de Bryan, married  Hugh de Courtenay.  Ma
2 CONC rried (2) Elizabeth Montacute/Montagu.  Children include  Margaret, married John Erlegh. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is copied from Christopher Earls Brennen's website on the Erlegh family, http://www.dankat.com/earls/chap1.htm:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >John(VI) married Margaret, daughter of Sir Guy de Brien K.G. (who was standard bearer to King Edward III at Crecy) and they had:
2 CONT
2 CONT four sons,
2 CONT #  John(VII), 
2 CONT # Robert, 
2 CONT # Richard and
2 CONT #  Philip, 
2 CONT and three daughters 
2 CONT # daughter l
2 CONT # daughter ll
2 CONT # daughter lll
2 CONT
2 CONT [31][11,v.2,p.199]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John(VI) died in 1372, possibly a victim of the Black Death then sweeping the country, leaving John(VII) his son and heir [7][18].  '''Alternately, he died in 1410.  
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Footnotes:
2 CONT *31.  Table displayed in the Church of St. Michael, Somerton, Somerset, England.
2 CONT * 7. “The manor of Erley or Earlstown, County Kilkenny” by G. D. Burtchaell in Journal of the Royal Society of Antiquaries of Ireland, 1906, p.154 et seq. 
2 CONT * 18.  “Dormant and extinct baronage of England” by Banks.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT Nichols, John Gough. The Herald and Genealogist (Nichols and Nichols, Printer to the Society of Antquaries, London, 1863-1874) Vol. 1, Page 523 < [https://books.google.com/books?id=Di89AQAAIAAJ&pg=PA523#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleB
2 CONC ooks] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT > Some of the families to whom these shields belong were certainly connected by alliance. The renowned Sir Guy de BRYAN, elected K.G. 1370 and summoned as a Baron to Parliament from 1350 to his death in 1390,* married for his seco
2 CONC nd wife the lady Elizabeth MONTACUTE, daughter of William first Earl of Salisbury. On his well-known monument in the abbey church of Tewkesbury the arms of Bryan and Montacute are impaled. '''By the Lady Elizabeth he had a daughte
2 CONC r, Margaret, the wife of Sir John Erlegh, who in 40 Edw. III. attended the Black Prince in his campaign in Spain''', and was present in the battle of Naziers. Sir John Erlegh, his son, married Isabel daughter of Sir John Paveley,†
2 CONC  and left one daughter, Margaret, his heiress, who was married first to Sir John de St. Maur; 2. to Sir Walter Sondes; and 3. to Sir William CHEYNEY. She died 21 Hen. VI.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT J.J. Alexander (1936). "''The Early Owners of Torbryan Manor''" < [https://devonassoc.org.uk/devoninfo/early-owners-of-torbryan-manor-1936/ link] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT Italics are for three items which “which must be regarded as doubtful or incorrect” -
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000197199571832&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.medievalgenealogy.org.uk/cp/bryan.shtml#p361 Some Corrections and Additions to the Complete Peerage: Volume 2: Bryan]
2 CONT
2 CONT > In summary, it appears that Sir Guy de Bryan was born say 1309, he being in arms in 1327 and stated to be of age in 1330. His first wife, Joan, was living 12 April 1348. …
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Richardson, Douglas. Royal Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, in 5 vols. (Salt Lake City, Utah, 2013), Vol. II, page 446.
2 CONT
2 CONT >After the death of Hugh Le Despenser, his widow, Elizabeth de Montagu, married (3rd) before 10 July 1350 (as his 2nd wife) Guy de Bryan (or Brian), K.G., son and heir of Guy de Bryan, by Gwenllian, daughter of Gruffudd ap Lloyd. 
2 CONC He was born about 1309. They had three sons, Guy Knt., William, Knt., and Philip.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/OKQMz8bMDSg/m/vGN93_pHA20J “C.P. Addition/Correction: Guy de Bryan, K.G., Lord Bryan, and his 1st wife, Joan de Carew”]  Feb 9, 2009, 4:10:18 PM. Soc.gen.medieval at GoogleGrou
2 CONC ps 
2 CONT
2 CONT > Sir Guy de Bryan and his first wife, Joan de Carew, were the parents of at least two, possibly three daughters. There are living descendants through their daughter, Elizabeth de Bryan, who married Robert Fitz Payn (formerly de G
2 CONC rey), Knt., of Stogursey, Bridghampton, Cheddon Fitzpaine, Rodway, etc., Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Church of St. Michael, Somerton, Somerset, England. < [https://www.greatenglishchurches.co.uk/html/somerton.html link] > 
2 CONT * https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00075135&tree=LEO shows as first married to Hugh Courtenay 
