1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Sir William de Bryan, Knight==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Guy de Brienne, 1st Baron of Bryan, KG and Elizabeth De Montagu
2 CONT *William de Bryan (born about 1357, died 23 September 1395, buried Seal, Kent) married Joane, who survived him - http://www.themcs.org/characters/Guy%20Bryan.htm
2 CONT * William(1357-1395) married Joan Fitzalan. The “Complete Peerage of Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom” by the Honorable Vicary Gibbs, 1912 and the other reliable resources already mentioned list William de B
2 CONC ryan’s death as September 22, 1395.After the death of William de Bryan, his wife Joan Fitzalan (Arundel) of Echynham, Sussex remarried a William de Etchngham ca. 1401.It was this second husband also named William that died on Marc
2 CONC h 20, 1413 and not William de Bryan.Many genealogists have gotten the two Williams confused obviously.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Spouse==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Joan/ Jane FitzAlan''' [John13, Eleanor12 Plantagenet [Countess of Arundel], Henry VI11, Edmund Crouch10, Eleonore Leonor9 Berenger Berengar [Queen], Raymond IV (V)8, III Berenger [Prince of Aragon]7 Alfonso, II [The
2 CONC  King of Aragon]6, V Ramon Berenguer [Prince Aragon]5 Raymond, IV Raimond Berenger Barcelona [Count]4, Matilda3 Maud, Guiscard of Apulia D' Hauteville, I Weasel Robert Guiscard[Count of Apulia]2 Roger, De Hauteville [Sir]1 Tancred
2 CONC ) was born Abt. 1360 in Echingham Sussex, England, and died September 01, 1404 in Echingham, Sussex, England. She married (1) Wiliam De Bryan Brienne Abt. 1378 in England, son of Guy Bryan Brienne and Elizabeth Montagu. He was bor
2 CONC n Abt. 1349 in Devonshire, England, and died March 20, 1412/13 in England. '''She married (2) William Echyngham Abt. 1401.'''
2 CONT
