1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT ==Baron of Chastel Walweyn  this is Welsh version of Walwyn's Castle
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT “The castle no longer remains in any form except a mound in a field, but the village Walyns Castle does exist.  It is in Pembrokeshire, South West Wales close to where I live.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy de Bryan, Knt., of Walwyn's Castle, Pembrokeshire, Batdeford (in Ipplepen), Clifton Dartmouth and Hardnegs, and Tor Bryan, Devon, etc., was born Abt. 1289 in Walwyns Castle, Pembrokeshire, Wales, and died after 27 Jan 1344 / A
2 CONC bt. 1347 in England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Guy de Brian and his wife Sybil Sully.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anne (or Alice) Holwey Bef. 1311 in England, daughter of Unknown Hogan [Lord]. She was born Bet. 1280 - 1293 in Walwyns Castle, Pembrokeshire, Wales, and died Aft. 1343 in England, daughter of Walter Holwey who was born
2 CONC  circa 1265 in Devon, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Guy Bryan and Anne Holwey are:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Guy V De14 Bryan [Baron Bryan], born 1311 in Walwyns Castle, Pembrokeshire, Wales; died August 17, 1390 in England.
2 CONT * ?Jane De Bryan, born Abt. 1325.
2 CONT
2 CONT Disputed child 
2 CONT * +	600	ii.	?Elizabeth De Bryan , born Abt. 1321 in Of, Somersetshire, England. Evidence needed to support https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-de-Erleigh/6000000029597535971 daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Guy-de-Bryan-I
2 CONC V/6000000000424759848?through=6000000029597535971
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second after 1344 to Crisli verch Gruffudd Llwyd with no issue.  She married second to Dafydd Moethe.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Richardson, Douglas. Royal Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, in 5 vols. (Salt Lake City, Utah, 2013), Vol. II, page 446.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >After the death of Hugh Le Despenser, his widow, Elizabeth de Montagu, married (3rd) before 10 July 1350 (as his 2nd wife) Guy de Bryan (or Brian), K.G., son and heir of Guy de Bryan, by [Gwenllian, daughter of Gruffudd ap Lloyd.
2 CONC ] [sic] He was born about 1309. They had three sons, Guy Knt., William, Knt., and Philip.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Comment''': more likely his mother was Ann or Alice Holwey.  Guy de Bryan’s second wife was Crisli verch Gruffudd, not her sister Gwenllian verch Gruffudd.  They were the daughters of Gruffudd ap Rhys, nicknamed Llwyd.  See P. 
2 CONC C. Bartrum: Welsh Genealogies AD 300-1400, Marchudd 17 ([https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173393022889 document attached]) 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Holwey-1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "C.P. 2 (1912): 361-362 (sub Bryan) includes a good account of the life of Guy de Bryan, K.G., Lord Bryan (died 1390). The editor states 'he appears to have m. 1stly, before 1343/4, Ann, or Alice, da. and h. of William Holway, of 
2 CONC Holway, Devon, but she was possibly his father's wife.'"
2 CONT
2 CONT "C.P. 5 (1926): 463 (sub Fitzpayn) states that Sir Guy de Bryan's first wife was named Joan. In footnote e on page 463, it is states that Joan, 1st wife of Guy, was living 12 April 1348, citing as its source Papal Letters, vol. ii
2 CONC i, pg. 450. No explanation is provided for the removal of Alice Holway given as Guy de Bryan's 1st wife in volume 2 of C.P."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://www.ancestry.com/boards/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=256&p=surnames.scudder
2 CONT # ''UK, A General and Heraldic Dictionary of the Peerages of England, Ireland, and Scotland, Extinct, Dormant, and in Abeyance, 1831''.  by the dietwn tf JCenihoorfft, for the redemption of his lands. This Guy de Brian, m. Eva^ on
2 CONC ly dau^ter and heireBS of Henry de Trad, and dying in the 3fth Edward I., was #. by his son, SIR GUYDEBRYAN, who..."- https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-90100-32193103/uk-a-general-and-heraldic-dictionary-of-the-peerages-o
2 CONC f
2 CONT # ''The complete peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom : extant, extinct, or dormant''.  by Cokayne, George E. Vol 2, page 361-2.  “BRYAN or BRIENE.”  < [https://archive.org/details/completep
2 CONC eerageo02coka/page/360/mode/1up Archive.Org] > d.  Guy de Brian, King's yeoman (valettus), and Alice his wife, were living 27 Jan. 1343/4. {Patent Roll). V.G.
2 CONT # Douglas Richardson post on SGM - https://soc.genealogy.medieval.narkive.com/tSTEBle8/cp-addition-marriage-of-joan-1st-wife-of-guy-de-bryan-lord-bryan
2 CONT # https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Holwey-1 comments : “Gwenllian [sic: ''Crisli'']  ferch Gruffudd is shown as wife of Guy Brionne and father of Sir Guy who married Joan Carew” cites 
