2 NICK Robert Grey
2 NICK Robert Fitz Payn
2 NICK Grey of Codnor
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1321
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cheddon Fitzpaine
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 MAY 1393
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Austria-Hungary
1 OCCU
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On the death of his maternal uncle [[6000000003098319247]], he acquired the FitzPayn estates, by virtue of a recent entailment.  He was not the heir-at-law, since his uncle left a daughter, age 30, who was married 
2 CONC and had issue.  Nor can misogyny be blamed, since he was not the heir male, nor did the settlement create any remainders to heirs male.
2 CONT
2 CONT He then assumed the surname FitzPayn.  But he was never summoned to Parliament, notwithstanding that his wife was also the eventual heiress of her father Lord Bryan.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT *'''Robert FitzPayn was born circa 1321.1 He was the son of Sir Richard de Grey and Joan FitzPayn.2 He married Elizabeth de Briene, daughter of Sir Guy de Briene, between 16 August 1351 and 16 October 1354.1 He died on 21 May 1393
2 CONC , an only daughter and heiress: without male issue.1
2 CONT *'''     Robert FitzPayn was baptised with the name of Robert de Grey.3 In 1354 he inherited his manors in Somerset and Dorset from his uncle, Sir Robert FitzPayn.1 In 1359 he accompanied King Edward III on the campaign in France.
2 CONC 1 He lived at Wraxall, Dorset, England.1 He lived at Staple Fitzpaine, Somerset, England.1 He lived at Cary Fitzpaine, Somerset, England.1 He lived at Charlton Mackrell, Somerset, England.1 He lived at Cheddon Fitzpaine, Somerset,
2 CONC  England.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Robert FitzPayn and Elizabeth de Briene
2 CONT **1.Isabel Grey+2 b. c 1364, d. 11 Apr 1394
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1666. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 1667.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p32798.htm#i327974
2 CONT *<nowiki>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *'''Robert De GREY (1° B. Fitzpayn)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1321
2 CONT *'''Died: 21 May 1393
2 CONT *Father: Richard De GREY (2° B. Grey of Codnor)
2 CONT *Mother: Joan FITZPAYN
2 CONT *'''Married: Elizabeth BRYAN ABT 1352
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Isabel De GREY
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/GREY1.htm#Robert De GREY (1° B. Fitzpayn)
2 CONT *<nowiki>----------------------------------------------------------------------------------</nowiki> When Robert Walerand died c. 1301 the Crown was in possession of Stogursey castle and borough, and the Crown retained control sin
2 CONC ce Robert's brother and heir John was also an idiot. (fn. 17) In 1308 the king granted custody to Robert (III) FitzPayn of Poorstock (Dors.), and in the following year, on John's death, Robert retained the estate which, by the tim
2 CONC e of his death in 1315, he held in chief. (fn. 18) Robert (IV) FitzPayn, Lord FitzPayn, son of the last, died in 1354 leaving a widow Ela (d. 1356) and a daughter Isable. The estate passed on Ela's death to Robert's nephew '''Robe
2 CONC rt Grey of Codnor (Essex), who assumed the name FitzPayn. (fn. 19) His daughter and heir Isabel (d. 1394) married Richard Poynings, Lord Poynings (d. 1387)''', and Isabel's son Robert, Lord Poynings (d. 1446), was succeeded by his
2 CONC  granddaughter Eleanor, daughter of Richard Poynings and wife of Henry Percy, later earl of Northumberland (d. 1461). Eleanor died in 1484 and was followed by her son Henry (d. 1489), Henry's son Henry Algernon (d. 1527), and Henr
2 CONC y Algernon's son Henry (d. 1537), successive earls of Northumberland. (fn. 20) By 1514 the estate was described as the manors of Stogursey, Wyndeats, and Wick.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: 'Stogursey: Castle', A History of the County of Somerset: Volume 6: Andersfield, Cannington, and North Petherton Hundreds (Bridgwater and neighbouring parishes) (1992), pp. 136-137. URL: http://www.british-history.ac.uk/repo
2 CONC rt.aspx?compid=18605  Date accessed: 04 May 2010.
2 CONT *<nowiki>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He took his mothers maiden name of Fitzpayne instead of his father's name of De Grey.  Fitzpayne was then shortened to Payne.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Fitzpayn/De Grey, Sir Robert `Grey of Codnor`
2 CONT
2 CONT     b. ABT 1321
2 CONT         Codnor/Knt., of Stogursey, Bridghampton, Cheddon Fitzpaine, Rodway, etc.
2 CONT     d. BEF May 21 1393
2 CONT     m. de Bryan, Elizabeth
2 CONT         BEF Oct 16 1354
2 CONT
2 CONT Fitzpayn/De Grey, Sir Robert `Grey of Codnor` Sir Robert FitzPAYN, 2nd Baron FitzPayn of Llanfair
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born: Before 1287, Llanfair Discoed, Chepstow, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT * Married (1):
2 CONT * Married (2): 29 Jun 1319
2 CONT * Died: 30 Nov 1354
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT BARONY OF FITZPAYN (II) 1315
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT (FITZPAYN), LORD FITZPAYN, son and heir, aged 28 and more, or 30 and more, at his father's death. He was knighted by the Prince of Wales, 22 May 1306, at Westminster. In 1310 he performed military service in place of his fa
2 CONC ther. The King took his homage and he had livery of his father's lands, 5 November 1315.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of his 1st wife is unknown. He married, 2ndly (royal licence dated 29 June 1319), Ela, widow of John LE MARESCHAL, of Hingham, Hockering, and Buxton, Norfolk, and Aslackby, co. Lincoln, hereditary Marshal of Ireland (who 
2 CONC was born 1 August 1292, and died 12 August 1316). In 1320 he conveyed the manors and advowsons of Worth and Okeford to himself and Ela his wife and the heirs male of their bodies, with remainder to his right heirs. On 30 May 1322 
2 CONC his lands, which had been taken into the King's hand because he had not come to the King in the march of Wales when ordered to do so, were restored to him, provisionally. He was with the King in his invasion of Scotland in August 
2 CONC 1322, being in the retinue of the Earl of Arundel. In 1323 he conveyed the manors of Cary, Charlton, Rodway, Stogursey, Wraxall, Wootton, Marshwood, and Stourton, the hundreds of Cannington and Whitchurch, and the advowsons of Cha
2 CONC rlton, Wraxall, Wootton, and Stourton, to himself and Ela his wife, and his heirs. On 10 May 1323 the manor of Wisley, Surrey, which had been taken into the King's hand because Robert was an adherent of Bartholomew de Badelesmere,
2 CONC  was restored to him, provisionally. In 1324 he and Ela his wife conveyed the manors of Stogursey, Rodway, Cary, Charlton, Wraxall, Staple, Okeford, Wisley, and Stourton, the hundred of Cannington, and the advowsons of Charlton, W
2 CONC raxall, Staple, Okeford, and Stourton, to themselves and the heirs male of their bodies, with remainder to Robert, son of Richard de Grey of Codnor, remainder to Gilbert, brother of the same Robert son of Richard, in successive ta
2 CONC il general, remainder to the right heirs of Robert fitz Payn. In 1327/8 they conveyed the manors and advowsons of Wootton, Frome Whitfield, and Marshwood, and the reversion of those of Worth (expectant on the death of Maud, late t
2 CONC he wife of Robert fitz Payn le fitz, who held the same in dower), to themselves and the heirs of their bodies, with remainder to John Mautravers the younger, in fee: and the like reversion of the manor and advowson of Poole Keynes
2 CONC , to the same John Mautravers, in fee. He was summoned for Military Service from 20 February 1315/6 to 27 March 1335, to Councils, from May 1324 to 18 February 1346/7, and to Parliament from 3 December 1326 to 15 November 1351, by
2 CONC  writs directed Roberto filio Pagani, fuitz Payn, or fitz Payn. In 1331 his wife, Ela, was convicted of adultery.[f] In March 1339/40 there appears to have been a false rumour of his death. On 20 May 1341 he was excused for not ha
2 CONC ving attended the last Parliament, since he had been too infirm to come. In 1354 he made a final disposition of his property, and he and his wife Ela conveyed the manors and advowsons of Staple, Cheddon, and Charlton Mackrell, and
2 CONC  the manors of Cary and Wraxall, to him and the heirs male of his body, with remainder to Robert (son of Richard de Grey of Codnor) and Elizabeth his wife, and the heirs of the body of the same Robert son of Richard, remainder to 
2 CONC his own right heirs. He died 30 November 1354. On 20 December 1354 his widow obtained possession of the manors and advowsons of Stogursey, Rodway, Tatworth, Marshwood, Wootton, and Okeford, and the hundred of Cannington, by virtue
2 CONC  of the fines levied in 17 Edward II and 1 Edward III, the escheator in cos. Somerset and Dorset being ordered to take her fealty. She died 16 February 1355/6. [Complete Peerage V:451-3]
2 CONT
2 CONT [f] On 5 Jan. 1331/2 the Bishop of Bath and Wells informed his metropolitan that he had carried out, as far as possible, the mandate he had received to punish Ela la Payne, wife of Sir Robert fitz Payn, who had been convicted of a
2 CONC dultery. To a second mandate from the Archbishop, dated xv kal. Feb. following, stating that his former mandate had not been properly executed, the Bishop replied, 8 Mar., that, as far as he could learn, Ela had not lived in his d
2 CONC iocese since he had received the first mandate, and that she could not be found. (Wells Reg., Shrewsbury, vol. i, pp. 83, 87]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Unnamed first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert also married Ela de BRIENE, daughter of Sir Guy II de BRIENE of Laugharne and Sibyl de SULLY, on 29 Jun 1319. (Ela de BRIENE was born in Walwyn's Castle, Haverfordwest, Pembrokeshire, Wales and died on 16 Feb 1355/6.) John 
2 CONC of Penna (Penne), d. 1271 (5 Oct.);//married (before 16 Oct 1354) Robert Fitzpayne/Fitz Payn, Grey of Codnor, (born about 1321, died 21 May 1393) Sir Robert FITZPAYN Master of Llanvair 2062,6093,9628
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born: Abt 1303, Marshwood, Beaminster, Dorset, England
2 CONT * Died: Before 10 Dec 1322, (dsp & vp) 9628
2 CONT * Buried: Grey Friars Church, York, Yorkshire, England Another name for Robert was Robert FITZPAINE.
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT FITZPAYN, son and heir apparent, by 1st wife. He married (contract dated at London, 2 May 1316, to marry at the Feast of St. James [25 July] following, Maud, sister and (afterwards) coheir of Sir Giles DE BADELESMERE, of Ba
2 CONC dlesmere and Chilham, Kent, Castle Combe, Wilts, &c. [LORD BADELFSMERE], and 2nd daughter of Sir Bartholomew DE BADELESMERE, of the same [LORD BADELESMERE], by Margaret, aunt and coheir of Thomas DE CLARE, and elder daughter of Si
2 CONC r Thomas DE CLARE, Lord of Inchiquin and Youghal. In March 13I9/20 he was about to go over seas with Edmund of Woodstock. He died s.p. and v.p. before 10 December 1322, and was buried in the Church of the Grey Friars at York (d). 
2 CONC His widow, who held the manors of Poole Keynes and Worth in dower, married, before 27 March 1336, John (DE VEER), EARL OF OXFORD, who was born 12 March 1311/2, and died in France, 23 or 24 January 1359/60. She died 24 May 1366, ho
2 CONC ra vesperarum. [Complete Peerage V:454-5, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT (d) He was probably killed in the Scottish wars, perhaps in the rout at Byland Abbey, 14 Oct 1322. Father: Robert 1st Baron FITZPAYN , of Llanvair, Sir b: ABT 1254 in Llanvair Discoed, Chepstow, Monmouthshire, Wales Mother: Isabel
2 CONC  (Isabella) de CLIFFORD b: ABT 1254 in Frampton-on-Severn, Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Unknown First WIFE b: ABT 1290
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: in 1st wife
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Has No Children Robert FITZPAYN , Master of Llanvair, Sir b: ABT 1303 in Marshwood, Beaminster, Dorset, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 2 Ela de BRIENE b: ABT 1295 in Walwyn's Castle, Haverfordwest, Pembrokeshire, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: 29 JUN 1319 in 2nd husband 2nd wife 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Has Children Isabel "3rd Baroness" FITZPAYN b: BEF 1324 in Llanvair Discoed, Chepstow, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
