2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #33170, d. 18 October 1382
2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde was the son of James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde and Eleanor de Bohun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Darcy, daughter of Sir John Darcy, 1st Lord Darcy de Knayth and Lady Joan de Burgh.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 18 October 1382.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde also went by the nick-name of 'The Noble Earl' on account of being the great-grandson of King Edward I.
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the title of 2nd Earl of Ormonde. He has an extensive biographical entry in the Dictionary of National Biography.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde and Elizabeth Darcy
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.James Butler, 3rd Earl of Ormonde+ d. 6 Sep 1405
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Alianore le Botiller+3 d. 1392
2 CONT
