2 CONT Older titles of Earl of Ormond (created 1328) and Chief Butler of Ireland (created c.1171)
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded 1338; the Noble Earl designation referred to the fact that he was the great grandson of King Edward I.
2 CONT
2 CONT "James the Chaste" was used by the Irish and he resided chiefly in Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will dated 31 Aug 1379; proved 28 Apr 1386
