1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Margaret Grey1,2,3
2 CONT *'''F, b. circa 1381, d. 1 June 1454
2 CONT *Father Sir Henry de Grey, 5th Lord Grey of Wilton2,3 b. bt 1338 - 1342, d. 22 Apr 1396 
2 CONT *Mother Elizabeth Talbot3 d. 10 Jan 1402 
2 CONT *     '''Margaret Grey was born circa 1381 at of Wilton on the Wye, Herefordshire, England.2,3 A contract for the marriage of Margaret Grey and Sir John Darcy, 5th Baron Darcy, 4th Lord Meinell was signed on 9 July 1397; They had 
2 CONC 2 sons (Philip & John) and 4 daughters (including Elizabeth, Maud, & Margery).2,3 Margaret Grey married Sir Thomas Swinford, son of Sir Hugh Swynford and Katherine Roet, before 12 July 1421; They had one son, William.2 Margaret Gr
2 CONC ey died on 1 June 1454.2
2 CONT *'''Family 1 Sir John Darcy, 5th Baron Darcy, 4th Lord Meinell b. c 1377, d. 9 Dec 1411 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **Joan Darcy+4 d. b 18 May 1436
2 CONT **Sir Philip Darcy, 6th Baron Darcy+ b. c 1398, d. 2 Aug 1418
2 CONT **John Darcy, 7th Baron Darcy of Nocton+4 b. c 1404, d. 1458
2 CONT *'''Family 2 Sir Thomas Swinford b. c 1368, d. 2 Apr 1432 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT **William Swinford+2 b. a 1421
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S3688] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. IV, p. 64/5; Magna Charta Sureties, 1215, by F. L. Weis, 4th Ed., p. 29; Burke's Peerage, 1938, p. 737.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 256.
2 CONT *3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 766.
2 CONT *4.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 441.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p432.htm#i12970
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret Grey1
2 CONT *'''F, #107322, b. circa 1370, d. 1 June 1454
2 CONT *Last Edited=1 May 2011
2 CONT *'''Margaret Grey was born circa 1370. She was the daughter of Henry Grey, 5th Lord Grey (of Wilton) and Elizabeth Talbot.1,2 She married, firstly, John Darcy, 5th Lord Darcy de Knayth, son of Philip Darcy, 4th Lord Darcy de Knayt
2 CONC h and Elizabeth Gray.3 She married, secondly, Sir Thomas Swynford, son of Sir Hugh Swynford and Katherine Roët, before 12 July 1421.3 She died on 1 June 1454.1 She died intestate and her estate was administered to to William Swinf
2 CONC ord of Kettlethorpe on 29 August 1454 at Lincoln, Lincolnshire, England.4
2 CONT *'''     Her married name became Darcy.3 From before 12 July 1421, her married name became Swynford.
2 CONT *'''Children of Margaret Grey and John Darcy, 5th Lord Darcy de Knayth
2 CONT ** 1.John Darcy+5 d. 1458
2 CONT ** 2.unknown daughter Darcy5
2 CONT ** 3.unknown daughter Darcy5
2 CONT ** 4.unknown daughter Darcy5
2 CONT ** 5.unknown daughter Darcy5
2 CONT ** 6.Philip Darcy, 6th Lord Darcy de Knayth+5 b. c 1398, d. 16 Jan 1417/18
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 102. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT * 2.[S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family."
2 CONT * 3.[S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 1665. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 4.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume IV, page 65. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 5.[S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p10733.htm#i107322
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret GREY (B. Darcy of Knaith) 
2 CONT *'''Died: 1 Jun 1454 
2 CONT *Father: Henry GREY (5º B. Grey of Wilton)
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth TALBOT (B. Grey of Wilton)
2 CONT *'''Married: John DARCY (5° B. Darcy of Knaith) BEF 1398
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Phillip DARCY (6° B. Darcy of Knaith)
2 CONT **2. John DARCY (7° B. Darcy of Knaith) 
2 CONT **3. Elizabeth DARCY (b. 1399 - d. AFT 18 Feb 1412)
2 CONT **4. Matilda (Maud) DARCY (b. 1401 - d. AFT 18 Feb 1412)
2 CONT **5. Margery DARCY (b. 1402 - d. AFT 18 Feb 1412) 
2 CONT *'''Married: Thomas SWINFORD (Sir Knight) (d. 2 Apr 1432) BEF 12 Jul 1421
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/GREY2.htm#Margaret GREY (B. Darcy of Nayth)
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *'''The complete peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom : extant, extinct, or dormant (1910) Vol. IV.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/completepeerageo04byucoka
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/completepeerageo04byucoka#page/63/mode/1up
2 CONT *IV. 1399.     5. '''John (Darcy), Lord Darcy, s. and h., aged 22 and more, or 23 and more, at his father's death'''. The King took his fealty, and he had livery of his inheritance, 12 June 1399, his homage being respited. (e) He 
2 CONC was sum. to Parl. from 19 Aug.(1399) 23 Ric. II to 21 Sep. (1411) 12 Hen. IV, by writs directed Johanni Darcy.(f) He was one of the Lords who sealed the exemplifications of the Acts settling the succession to the Crown, 7 June and
2 CONC  22 Dec. 1406.(g) '''He m. Margaret, da. of Sir Henry Grey, of Wilton-on-the-Wye [Lord Grey], by Elizabeth, da. of Sir Gilbert Talbot, of Eccleswall, co. Hereford [Lord
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/completepeerageo04byucoka#page/64/mode/1up
2 CONT * Talbot]. He d. 9 Dec. 1411.(a) Will dat. at his manor of Temple Hurst, 2 Aug. 1411, pr. at Cawood, 18 Feb. 1411/2.(b) '''His widow's dower was ordered to be assigned, [E.] 11 Nov. and [I.] 14 Nov. 1412.(c') She m., as 2nd wife, 
2 CONC before 12 July 1421,(d) Sir Thomas Swinford, of Kettlethorpe, co. Lincoln. He, who was b. 24 Feb. 1372/3 [sic] at Lincoln, and bap. there the next day,(e) d. 2 Apr. 1432.(f) She d.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/completepeerageo04byucoka#page/65/mode/1up
2 CONT *''' 1 June 1454.(a) Admon. at Lincoln, 29 Aug. 1454, to William Swinford of Kettlethorpe {Lincoln Reg., vol. xx, f. 18).
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Grey was born circa 1370. She was the daughter of Henry Grey, 5th Lord Grey (of Wilton) and Elizabeth Talbot. She married, firstly, John Darcy, 5th Lord Darcy de Knayth, son of Philip Darcy, 4th Lord Darcy de Knayth and E
2 CONC lizabeth Gray. She married, secondly, Sir Thomas Swynford, son of Sir Hugh Swynford and Katherine Roët, before 12 July 1421. She died on 1 June 1454. She died intestate and her estate was administered by William Swinford of Kettle
2 CONC thorpe on 29 August 1454 at Lincoln, Lincolnshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Darcy. From before 12 July 1421, her married name became Swynford.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=REG&db=updike&id=I56889
2 CONT *___________________________
2 CONT *Links
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Grey_de_Wilton
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Darcy_de_Knayth
2 CONT
