1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Faris (1999, pp. 375-376): "RICHARD GREY, 6th Lord Grey, of Wilton, son and heir, was born about 1393 (aged three years and more at his father's death). He accompanied the King to France in August 1415, being in th
2 CONC e retinue of the Earl of Dorset. He was married for the first time, it is said, to BLANCHE ______. They had two sons. He was married for the second time in 1427 to MARGARET FERRERS, daughter of William de Ferrers, Lord Ferrers, of
2 CONC  Groby, by his wife Philippe Clifford. They had two sons. RICHARD GREY, 6th Lord Grey, died testate on 13 or 20 Aug. 1442, and was buried at Bletchley. His widow was married for the second time before 14 Feb. 1445/6 to Thomas Grey
2 CONC , Knt., of Richemount, co. Bedford, afterwards Lord Richemount Grey (a Lancastrian, captured and executed in 1461, some time after the battle of Towton). She died on 16 Jan. 1451/2.
2 CONT
2 CONT C.P. 6:178-179 (1926). Paget (1957) 260:5 (never summoned to Parliament)."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT RICHARD GREY, Knt., 6th Lord Grey, married (1st), while still a minor, MAUD LE SCROPE. She presumably died in childhood without issue. . He married (2nd?) BLANCHE _____. They had two sons. He married (3rd?) before 17 June 1426 MAR
2 CONC GARET FERRERS, daughter of William Ferrers, 5th Lord Ferrers, by his wife, Philippe, daughter of Roger de Clifford, Knt. They had two sons, William and Edward.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
