2 CONT *note          Knight of the Bath 1426; suc. his mother c.1433 as 7th Baron Furnivall;  served in France 1434 and 1442; Chancellor of Ireland 1446;  Lord High Treasurer of England 1456-58; Knight of the Garter 1457; Joint Keeper o
2 CONC f the King's Mews and Falcons 1457; Chief Butler of England 1458; Chief Justice of Chester 1458/9; Steward of Wakefield 1459; Steward of Ludlow 1460; killed at the Battle of Northampton fighting for the Lancastrian side
