1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Charleton,_4th_Baron_Cherleton
2 CONT
2 CONT John Charleton (or Cherleton or Charlton), 4th Baron Cherleton, 4th Lord Charlton of Powys (25 April 1362 – 19 October 1401).
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the titles of 4th Baron Cherleton and 4th Lord of Powys (Feudal baron) on 13 July 1374, on the death of his father, John Charleton, 3rd Baron Cherleton, and held the office of Justice of North Wales from 20 March 1
2 CONC 387.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Alice FitzAlan, daughter of Richard FitzAlan, 11th Earl of Arundel and Elizabeth de Bohun, before March 1392, without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 19 October 1401, aged 39, at the Castle of Pool, Poole, Dorset. His last will was dated 1395. As he had no children, he was succeeded in the barony and lordship by his younger brother, Edward.
