3 TEXT  They had one daughter:
4 CONT Margaret de Audley, born between January 1318 and November 1322.
4 CONT Conflict
4 CONT Hugh and Margaret were among the victims of their brother-in-law, Hugh the younger Despenser. In his rashness and greed for the Clare lands, he robbed Margaret of much of her rightful inheritance. In 1321, Hugh de Audley joined th
4 CONC e other Marcher Barons in looting, burning, and causing general devastation to Despenser's lands.
4 CONT Hugh was captured at the Battle of Boroughbridge in 1322, and was saved from a hanging thanks to the pleas of his wife. He was imprisoned, and two months later Margaret was sent to Sempringham priory. She remained there until 1326
4 CONC , when Hugh escaped prison and she was released from Sempringham.
