1 OCCU 1st Earl of Stafford, Steward of the King, Earl of Stafford
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sir Ralph de Stafford=
2 CONT * BIRTH 1299 Staffordshire, England
2 CONT * DEATH 31 Aug 1372 (aged 72–73) Tonbridge, Tonbridge and Malling Borough, Kent, England
2 CONT * BURIAL Tonbridge Priory, Tonbridge, Tonbridge and Malling Borough, Kent, England
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 48355991 photos added by Bob the Greenacre Cat, Bio by Anne Shurtleff Stevens)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Earl de Stafford, Knight of the Garter. Diplomat to many European Countries.
2 CONT Ralph was born, married and died at Stafford. He was the son of Edmund de Staffard (Baron of Stafford) and Margaret Bassett. He married first Katherine de Hastang, by date 09 Feb 1327. She was the daughter of Sir John Hastang. The
2 CONC y were the parents of: Joan de Stafford (m. Sir Nicholas Beke), Margaret de Stafford (m. Sir John de Stafford.
2 CONT Secondly he married Margaret de Audley, whom he abducted against her parents' wishes. Her parents protested to King Edward, who approved the marriage, and soothed the Audleys by making her father the 1st Earl of Gloucester. Ralph 
2 CONC and Margaret were married by 06 Jul 1336. They were the parents of: Ralph (m. Maud of Lancaster), Hugh (m. Phillipa de Beauchamp), Thomas (a clerk), Elizabeth (M. Fulk le Strange, John de Ferres, Reginald Cobham), Beatrice (m. Mau
2 CONC rice FitzGerald, Thomas de Ros, Sir Knt Richard Burley), John (m. ?) and Katherine (m. Sir John de Sutton)
2 CONT Ralph was knighted in 1327, fought in the Battle of Sluys, the Battle of Crecy, the Seige of Vannes, and the navel Battle of Winchelsea. He inherited lands and became wealthy at the death of his first wife Katherine's parents with
2 CONC out paying homage taxes, indicating his relationship with Edward, the King of England. As the co-heir to the Corbet family, he inherited the lordship and the Castle Caus in 1347. He was given the title of the 1st Earl of Stafford 
2 CONC 01 Mar 1351. He died at Tonbridge Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Edmund de Stafford 1273–1308
2 CONT Margaret Basset Pype 1280–1337
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouses'''
2 CONT Margaret Audley Stafford 1318–1349 (m. 1336)
2 CONT Catherine Hastings Stafford 1300–1335
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Richard de Stafford 1305–1380
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Margaret de Stafford de Stafford 1326–1396
2 CONT Joan De Stafford De Beke 1328–1379
2 CONT Katherine Stafford Sutton 1338–1361
2 CONT Beatrice de Stafford Burley 1341–1415
2 CONT Sir Hugh de Stafford 1342–1386
2 CONT Elizabeth Stafford Cobham unknown–1376
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ralph de Stafford, 2nd Baron Stafford, 1st Earl of Stafford, KG (24 September 1301 – 31 August 1372) was an English nobleman and notable soldier during the Hundred Years War against France."
2 CONT
