1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000049409888955& Inquisitions Post Mortem] for John Tiptoft, knight, Lord Tiptoft and Powis, Writs 1 Feb. and 6 Feb. 1443. His IPMs give four different death dates: 30 Jan., 31 Jan.,
2 CONC  1 Feb. and 20 Feb. 1443. The last date is incorrect as it is after both dates of writ. John Tiptoft was his son and next heir, aged 16. Mentions Joyce his wife, who was still living.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family and Education==
2 CONT s. and h. of Sir Payn Tiptoft*. m. (1) bef. May 1407, Philippa (c.1367-2 May 1417),1 da. of Sir John Talbot, sis. and coh. of John Talbot (d.1388) of Richards Castle, Herefs., wid. of Sir Robert Assheton (d.1384), warden of the Ci
2 CONC nque Ports, and of Sir Matthew Gournay (d.1406) of Farrington Gurney, Som., s.p.; (2) by contract bef. 8 July 1421 and licence 28 Feb. 1422, Joyce (c.1403-22 Sept. 1446), yr. da. and coh. of Edward, Lord Charlton of Powis (d.1421)
2 CONC , by his 1st w. Eleanor, da. of Thomas Holand, earl of Kent, coh. of her uncle Edmund Holand, earl of Kent (d.1408), 1s. 3da. Kntd. 11 Oct. 1399; cr. Lord Tiptoft 7 Jan. 1426.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biographies==
