2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of John
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Tiptoft 1st Baron Tiptoft was born in Great Eversden, Cambridgeshire, England, United Kingdom as the son of Pain Tiptoft and Agnes Wroth. He married Philippa Talbot on 24 February 1408. In 1425, his occupation is listed a
2 CONC s chief steward of the castles and lordships of Wales. He died on 27 January 1443, in Edmonton, Middlesex, England, United Kingdom, and was buried in Enfield, Middlesex, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LTLK-XPQ/sir-john-tiptoft-1st-baron-tiptoft-1443
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Tiptoft, knight
2 CONT
2 CONT Also Known As: "Sir John /Tiploft/tiptopf/tiptot/tybobot/tibetot/", "Tybetot"
2 CONT
2 CONT Birthdate: circa 1383
2 CONT
2 CONT Birthplace: Great Eversden, Caxton, Cambridgeshire, England (United Kingdom)
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: circa January 30, 1443 (51-68)
2 CONT
2 CONT Enfield, Edmonton, Middlesex, England (United Kingdom) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Place of Burial: Enfield, Greater London, England, United Kingdom
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Immediate Family:
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Sir Payn Tiptoft, Kt., MP and Agnes Tiptoft
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Philippa Talbot and Lady Joyce Tiptoft (de Cherleton)
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Lady Joan Ingoldisthorpe; Philippa Ros / Wingfield; John Tiptoft, 1st Earl of Worcester; Lady Joyce Sutton, Baroness Dudley; Pain Tiptoft; and Edward Tiptoft « less
2 CONT
2 CONT Half-brother of William Tiptoft and Elizabeth Daneys
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation:1st Baron Tiptoft, Knight of the Shire, Speaker of the House of Commons.
2 CONT
