2 CONT
2 CONT Joyce la Zouche [1]
2 CONT *F, #118855, 
2 CONT *d. after 4 May 1372
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 Apr 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT Joyce la Zouche was the daughter of William la Zouche, 1st Lord Zouche of Mortimer and Alice de Toni.[1],[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married John de Botetourt, 2nd Lord Botetourt, son of Thomas de Botetourt and Joan de Somery, before 31 May 1347.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after 4 May 1372.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 31 May 1347, her married name became de Botetourt.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joyce la Zouche and John de Botetourt, 2nd Lord Botetourt
2 CONT *1. John de Botetourt+[1] d. 21 Sep 1369
2 CONT *2. Alice de Botetourt [1]
2 CONT *3. Joyce de Botetourt+[3] d. 1420
2 CONT *4. Catherine de Botetourt+[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 235. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 3, page 4289. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
