2 CONT *William La ZOUCHE of Mortimer
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1269, Ashby, Leicestershire, England 
2 CONT *Died: 28 Feb 1335/36
2 CONT *Buried: Tewkesbury Abbey, Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT *Notes: acquired the estates of Alan, Lord la Zouche on his death in 1314, and subsequently took the name "la Zouche" and was eventually summoned to Parliament as Lord Zouche.
2 CONT *Father: Robert De MORTIMER of Richard's Castle
2 CONT *Mother: Joyce La ZOUCHE
2 CONT *Married: Alice De TOENI BEF 25 Feb 1316/17
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Alan La ZOUCHE
2 CONT **2. Robert La ZOUCHE (b. ABT 1318)
2 CONT **'''3. Joyce La ZOUCHE (b. ABT 1320)
2 CONT *Married 2: Eleanor De CLARE (b. Oct 1292) (dau. of Gilbert De Clare, 3º E. Gloucester and Joan Plantagenet) (w. of Hugh Despencer) ABT 1329 
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Hugh La ZOUCHE (b. 1330, Caerphilly Castle, Caerphilly, Glamorganshire, Wales)
2 CONT **2. Edward La ZOUCHE
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/ZOUCHE.htm#William La ZOUCHE of Mortimer1
2 CONT *---
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes: No burial location noted, and there is no record of a Hales Abbey in or near Market Drayton. There is, however, a Halesowen Abbey at the village of Halesowen in Shropshire where some of the later generations of
2 CONC  her family were buried. Likewise uncertain about the logic surrounding her death location as being at the royally-held Weobley Castle in Herefordshire, but since asserted, will retain until further and better documented informati
2 CONC on can be ascertained. She was wife of the 2nd Baron Botetourt, but that did not confer the title of Baroness upon her. That honor would be conferred upon her granddaughter, also named Joyce, as female title owner and heiress of t
2 CONC he barony (there were no legitimate male heirs at the time of her husband's death).
