2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruthin Ruthin (/ˈrɪθɪn/ ⓘ RITH-in; Welsh: Rhuthun) is a market town and community in Denbighshire, Wales, in the south of the Vale of Clwyd
2 CONT
2 CONT >The Lord de Grey established a Collegiate Church in 1310. Now the Collegiate and Parish Church of St Peter, it dominates the Ruthin skyline. It has a double nave and boasts two medieval carved roofs. These days it is known for it
2 CONC s musical tradition. It has a large choir of children and adults and a four-manual Wadsworth-Willis organ. Behind the church can be seen the old college buildings, school and Christ's Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000204970942838&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: Jim Linwood from London - St Peter's Church, Ruthin - North Wales. < [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruthin#/media/File:St_Peter's_Church,_Ruthin_-_North_Wales._(14510486530).jpg Wikipedia] > CC BY 2.0
