2 CONC s, son of Sir Reginald de Grey, 1st Lord Grey of Wilton and Maud de Longchamp, before 1275; They had 2 sons (Sir Henry, 3rd Lord Grey of Wilton; & Sir Roger, 1st Lord Grey of Ruthin) and 3 daughters (Iseult, wife of Urian de St. P
2 CONC ierre, & of Sir William Inge; Maud, wife of John, 1st Lord Moels; & Joan, wife of Sir Ralph, 2nd Lord Basset of Drayton).9,3,4,5 Maud de Verdun died after 1293.3,5”
2 CONT * https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3T-Z.htm#_Toc21506731 JOHN de Verdun, son of THEOBALD Butler [Le Botiller] & his second wife Rohese de Verdun of Alton, Staffordshire ([1226]-before 17 Oct 1274).  He adopt
2 CONC ed his mother’s family name Verdun. ... m secondly (before 1267) ELEANOR, daughter of --- (-after 10 Jun 1278).  The Complete Peerage indicates that “a seal, said to be hers, bears the Bohun and Verdun arms”, suggesting that she “
2 CONC may have been a Bohun” and adding that “the name of her son Humphrey may be significant”[270]. CP XII/2 248, footnote (f) citing “Staffs. Hist. Coll., William Salt Arch. Soc., 1913, p. 298” [not yet consulted]. 
2 CONT * https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3D-K.htm#_Toc64628876 JOHN de Grey of Wilton, son of REYNOLD de Grey Lord Grey (of Wilton) & his wife Matilda de Longchamp ([1267/68]-28 Oct 1323).  Lord Grey (of Wilton). 
2 CONC  m firstly [ANNE de Ferrers, ... m secondly MAUD, daughter of [RALPH Basset of Drayton, Staffordshire & his wife Margaret de Somery].  The Complete Peerage states that John Lord Grey of Wilton married secondly “Maud, who is said t
2 CONC o have been da. of Ralph Basset of Drayton by Margaret...de Somery” but does not provide the basis for this speculation[510]. CP VI 174
