2 CONT John de Moels, 1st Baron Moels (1269–20 May 1310), feudal baron of North Cadbury in Somerset, was an English peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_de_Moels,_1st_Baron_Moels
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second son of Roger de Moels (c.1233-1295) the eldest surviving[1] son and heir of Nicholas de Moels (died 1269), feudal baron of a moiety of North Cadbury, Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married a certain Maud of unknown parentage[2] by whom he had children including: ....
2 CONT
2 CONT # Nicholas de Moels, 2nd Baron Moels (10 August 1289 – before 29 January 1315/6[5]), who married Margaret Courtenay (died 1349) daughter of Sir Hugh Courtenay (died 1292), feudal baron of Okehampton by his wife Eleanor le Despence
2 CONC r,[2] and father of Hugh Courtenay, 1st/9th Earl of Devon (died 1340). The marriage was childless.
2 CONT # Roger de Moels, 3rd Baron Moels, who died before 13 July 1316,[6] without male issue.
2 CONT # John de Moels, 4th Baron Moels (died before 21 August 1337[6]), who married Joan Lovel, daughter of Richard Lovel of Castle Cary, Somerset. He died leaving two daughters, each a co-heiresses to a moiety of the feudal barony of N
2 CONC orth Cadbury, the de Moels barony by writ and other lands:
2 CONT # Muriel de Moels (died before 1362), eldest daughter, who married Thomas Courtenay (died 1356/1362), 5th son of Hugh Courtenay, 1st/9th Earl of Devon (1275–1340).
2 CONT # Isabel de Moels, younger daughter, who married William de Botreaux (died 1349), of Boscastle, Cornwall, Sheriff of Cornwall, whose son was William de Botreaux, 1st Baron Botreaux (1337–1391)[7]
2 CONT # Johanna de Moels, wife of Sir Henry VII de la Pomeray (1291–1327), feudal baron of Berry Pomeroy in Devon.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/OEdGdK1nwmY/m/xPZiaaKtCgAJ
2 CONT
2 CONT On Sunday, October 6, 2019 at 3:37:53 PM UTC-4, celticp...@gmail.com wrote: 
2 CONT > Dear Newsgroup ~ 
2 CONT
2 CONT > Do you descend from Maud de Verdun and Sir John de Grey? If so, I'd very much appreciate seeing your line of descent posted here on the newsgroup. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sir John de Grey + Maud de Vernon  
2 CONT * -Maud de Grey m. John de Moels (c.1269-1310)  
2 CONT * -John de Moels (c.1304-1337) m. Joan Lovel  
2 CONT * -Muriel de Moels (c.1322-1369) m. Thomas de Courtenay (bef.1315-1356)  
2 CONT * -Margaret Courtenay (?-1422) m. Thomas Peverell (?-1402 or 1403)  
2 CONT * -Katherine Peverell (c.1394-between 1432-1438) m. Walter Hungerford (1378-1449)  
2 CONT * -Elizabeth Hungerford (?-1476) m. Philip Coutenay (1403/4-1463)  
2 CONT * -Elizabeth Courtenay (?-1493) m. James Luttrell (c.1427-1460/1)  
2 CONT * -Hugh Luttrell (?-1520/1) m. Margaret Hill  
2 CONT * -Eleanor Luttrell (?-aft 1547) m. Roger Yorke (?-1534/5)  
2 CONT * -Elizabeth Yorke (?-1601) m. Edmund Percival (c.1506-1551)  
2 CONT * -Christian Percival (?-Aft 1590) m. Richard Lowle (?-1577)  
2 CONT * -Percival Lowle (1571-1664/5) m. Rebecca ? (1575-1644/5)  
2 CONT * -Richard Lowle (1601/2-1682) m. Margaret ? (c.1604-1682)  
2 CONT * -Rebeckah Lowle (1641/2-1662) m. John Hale (1635-1707)  
2 CONT * -John Hale (1661-1725/6) m. Sarah Jacques (1663/4-1725/6)  
2 CONT * -Rebecca Hale (1683/4-1760) m. Jonathan Poore (1677/8-1742)  
2 CONT * -Mary Poore (1706-aft 1733) m. Benjamin Pierce (1700-1765) 
2 CONT
2 CONT The line from Benjamin Pierce down to me has been proven with DNA 
2 CONT
2 CONT --JoeCook 
2 CONT
