2 CONT *'''F, #116975, d. before 5 April 1353
2 CONT *Last Edited=1 May 2011
2 CONT *'''     Joan de Grey was the daughter of John de Grey, 2nd Lord Grey (of Wilton) and Matilda de Verdun.1,2 She and Sir Ralph Basset, 2nd Lord Basset of Drayton obtained a marriage license on 27 March 1304.1 She died before 5 Apri
2 CONC l 1353.1
2 CONT *'''      From 27 March 1304, her married name became Basset.1 On 13 January 1343/44 she had dower.3
2 CONT *'''Children of Joan de Grey and Sir Ralph Basset, 2nd Lord Basset of Drayton
2 CONT ** 1.Margaret Basset4 d. a 1347
2 CONT ** 2.Ralph Basset+3 d. c 1335
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 2. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VI, page 174.
2 CONT * 3.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 3.
2 CONT * 4.[S62] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry (Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.A.: Genealogical Publishing Co, 2005), page 889. Hereinafter cited as Magna Carta Ancestry.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p11698.htm#i116975 _______________________
