2 CONT
2 CONT Reginald Grey, 3rd Baron Grey de Ruthyn (c. 1362 – 30 September 1440), a powerful Welsh marcher lord succeeded to the title on his father Reginald's death in July 1388.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginald was the eldest son of Reginald Grey, 2nd Baron Grey de Ruthyn and Eleanor Le Strange of Blackmere. His paternal grandparents were Roger Grey, 1st Baron Grey de Ruthyn and Elizabeth de Hastings. His maternal grandparents w
2 CONC ere John Le Strange, 2nd Baron Strange of Blackmere and Ankaret Le Botiller. His youngest sister Ida de Grey, who married Sir John Cockayne, was an ancestress of Anne Boleyn and Mary Boleyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grey married firstly in 1378, Margaret de Ros, daughter of Thomas de Ros, 5th Baron de Ros and Beatrice Stafford. By her he had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Grey (c. 1387 – 1439), who predeceased his father. He married Constance Holland, the daughter of Elizabeth Plantagenet and John Holland, 1st Duke of Exeter by whom he had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Grey (d. aft. May 1426), married William Bonville, 1st Baron Bonville. These were the great-grandparents of Cecily Bonville who married Thomas Grey, 1st Marquess of Dorset, a descendant of Reginald Grey by his second marr
2 CONC iage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund Grey (born 1389)
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Grey (born 1391)
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Grey (born 1392), married George Lucy, Baron Lucy
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Grey (born 1393), married firstly Robert Poynings, 5th Baron Poynings, by whom she had two sons, and secondly Sir George Browne, by whom she had five children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grey married secondly on 7 February 1415, Joan de Astley, daughter of Sir William de Astley, 5th Baron Astley and Catherine de Willoughby. By her he had another six children, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Edward Grey, Baron Ferrers of Groby (c.1415/1416- 18 December 1457), married Elizabeth Ferrers of Groby and had five children including John Grey, 1st Baron Grey of Groby, the first husband of Elizabeth Woodville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice Grey, married Sir John Knyvett
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Grey, married Sir William Calthorpe, by whom she had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginald Grey (died after 24 January 1485).
2 CONT
2 CONT John Grey [given manor of Kempston]
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Grey (born 1419), married Eleanor Lowe, by whom he had issue[1]
2 CONT
