1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/GREY3.htm#Edith GREY1
2 CONT *''''''Edith GREY
2 CONT *''''''Born: ABT 1368, Ruthin, Denbighshire, Wales
2 CONT *''''''Died: 1 Jun 1426
2 CONT *Father: Reginald De GREY (2° B. Grey of Ruthin)
2 CONT *Mother: Alianor Le STRANGE (B. Grey of Ruthin)
2 CONT *''''''Married: John COKAYNE (B. Cokayne) ABT 1400, Cockayne Hatley, Bedfordshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Elizabeth COKAYNE (b. ABT 1404, Bury, Hatley, Bedfordshire, England) (m.1 Sir Phillip Butler - m.2 Sir Lawrence Cheney)
2 CONT **2. Reginald COKAYNE
2 CONT **3. Henry COKAYNE
2 CONT **4. John COKAYNE
2 CONT **4. Thomas COKAYNE
2 CONT **4. Margaret COKAYNE
2 CONT *<nowiki>----------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *''''''The Life of Saint Brychan: King of Brycheiniog and Family By Brian Starr
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=-zGOQAIlSnUC&pg=PA47&lpg=PA47&dq=Philip+Boteler+Butler+1414&source=bl&ots=YrMxJjCWY-&sig=Wob8qcqPLEtw5haBw7yy1TKx-kI&hl=en&ei=yTfSTNmhGYaksQPKwsHGCg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CCw
2 CONC Q6AEwBg#v=onepage&q=Philip%20Boteler%20Butler%201414&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.47
2 CONT *31 Ankaret Le Boteler b: Abt 1306 in Wemme, Shropshire, England d: 08 Oct 1361
2 CONT *+ John 2nd Baron Le Strange b: 25 Jan 1305/06 in Blackmere, Cornwall, England d: 21 Jul 1349 m: Abt 1329 1st Husband, 1st Wife
2 CONT **32 Alianore (Eleanore) Le Strange b: Abt 1345 in Of Knockin, Shropshire, England d: 20 Apr 1396
2 CONT **+ Reynold 2nd Baron De Grey b: Abt 1319 in Ruthin, Denbighshire, Wales d: 04 Aug 1388 m: Bef 21 Nov 1360
2 CONT ***''''''33 Ida De Grey b: Abt 1368 in Ruthin, Denbighshire, Wales
2 CONT ***''''''+ John Cokayne b: Abt 1365 in Ashbourne Hall, Derbyshire, England d: 22 May 1427 in Hatley Cokayne, Bedfordshire, Tngland m: Abt 1405
2 CONT ****34 Elizabeth Cokayne b: Abt 1395 in Bury Hatley, Bedfordshire, England
2 CONT ****+ Philip Boteler b: Abt 1388 in Woodhall, Hereford, Eng
2 CONT ****35 Philip Boteler b: 15 Aug 1414
2 CONT ****+ Isabel (Nmn-Philip) Boteler
2 CONT *<nowiki>-------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *''''''Ida de Grey (1368- 1 June 1426), also known as Edith de Grey was a Cambro-Norman noblewoman, and the daughter of Reginald Grey, 2nd Baron Grey de Ruthyn, a powerful Welsh Marcher lord. The Greys of Ruthyn were the chief Mar
2 CONC cher barons in the northern region of the Welsh Marches.
2 CONT *''''''Ida married Sir John Cockayne, Chief Baron of the Exchequer by whom she had six children. Through her eldest daughter Elizabeth, she was an ancestress of Anne Boleyn, Jane Seymour, and Catherine Howard, queens consort of Ki
2 CONC ng Henry VIII of England.
2 CONT *Family
2 CONT *''''''Ida was born at Ruthin Castle in Ruthin, Denbighshire, Wales in 1368, the youngest daughter of Reginald Grey, 2nd Baron Grey of Ruthyn and Eleanor Le Strange of Blackmere (1337- 20 April 1396). She had four siblings includi
2 CONC ng Reginald Grey, 3rd Baron Grey de Ruthyn, the implacable enemy of Owen Glendower. It was her brother's land dispute with Glendower which caused the latter to launch his rebellion against King Henry IV of England and take Reginal
2 CONC d prisoner, keeping him in confinement until he was ransomed by the king for the sum of 10,000 marks.
2 CONT *''''''Her paternal grandparents were Sir Roger Grey, 1st Baron Grey de Ruthyn and Elizabeth de Hastings. Her maternal grandparents were John Le Strange, 2nd Baron Strange of Blackmere, and Ankaret Le Botiller, daughter of Sir Wil
2 CONC liam Le Botiller and Ela de Herdeburgh. Ankaret was a direct descendant of Welsh Prince Gruffydd II ap Madog, Lord of Dinas Bran and his wife, Emma de Audley.
2 CONT *Marriage and children
2 CONT *''''''In 1387 at Bearwardcote, Derbyshire, Ida married Sir John Cockayne, Chief Baron of the Exchequer, the son of Sir John Cockayne and Cecilia de Vernon. In 1417, Sir John bought 1500 acres of land in Bedfordshire which include
2 CONC d the village of Hatley Bury. He renamed the village Cockayne Hatley and established his manor there. Henceforth, the manor of Cockayne Hatley in Bedfordshire became the principal residence of the Cockayne family.
2 CONT *''''''Together Sir John and Ida had six children:
2 CONT **    * Sir Reginald Cockayne (1390- after 10 February 1428), married Beatrice Walleys, by whom he had issue.
2 CONT **    * Henry Cockayne (1392- ater 10 February 1428)
2 CONT **    * Elizabeth Cockayne (1394- after 1422), married firstly in 1411, Sir Philip Butler by whom she had two sons; she married secondly on 13 December 1421, Sir Laurence Cheney of Fen Ditton, Sheriff of Cambridge, by whom she had
2 CONC  five children, including Elizabeth Cheney, the great-grandmother of Queens consort Anne Boleyn, Jane Seymour, and Catherine Howard.
2 CONT **    * John Cockayne (1396- after 10 February 1428)
2 CONT **    * Margaret Cockayne (1398- after 10 February 1428)
2 CONT **    * Thomas Cockayne (1400- after 10 February 1428)
2 CONT *''''''Ida's husband Sir John died in 1427 and was succeeded by their eldest son Sir Reginald. Ida died on 1 June 1426 and was buried in St. John's Church, Cockayne Hatley. There are many fine effigies of the Cockayne family which
2 CONC  can be seen in the church at Cockayne Hatley.
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''Ida Grey1,2,3
2 CONT *''''''F, d. 1 June 1426
2 CONT *Father Sir Reginald de Grey, 2nd Baron Grey of Ruthyn2,3 b. c 1323, d. 28 Jul 1388 
2 CONT *Mother Alianore le Strange2,3 d. 20 Apr 1396 
2 CONT *''''''     Ida Grey married John Cokayne, Chief Baron of the Exchequer, son of Sir John Cokayne and Cecilia Vernon, before 1394; They had 5 sons (including Reginald, Henry, John, & Thomas) and 5 daughters (Elizabeth & Margaret).2
2 CONC ,3 Ida Grey died on 1 June 1426.2
2 CONT *''''''Family John Cokayne, Chief Baron of the Exchequer d. 22 May 1429 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT **◦Elizabeth Cokayne+2 b. c 1388, d. a 1427
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S4787] Unknown author, The Ancestry of Dorothea Poyntz, by Ronny O. Bodine, p. 64; Wallop Family, Vol. 4, line 254.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 206.
2 CONT *3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 620.
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p551.htm#i16558
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT *''''''Ida Grey1
2 CONT *F, #326119
2 CONT *Last Edited=29 Dec 2008
2 CONT *''''''     Ida Grey is the daughter of Reynold de Grey, 2nd Lord Grey (of Ruthin) and Alianore Lestrange.2,3 She married Sir John Cokayne, son of Sir John Cokayne and Cecilia (?).1
2 CONT *''''''     Her married name became Cokayne.
2 CONT *''''''Child of Ida Grey and Sir John Cokayne
2 CONT **1.Sir Reginald Cokayne+2
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 988. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pe
2 CONC erage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 1666.
2 CONT *http://thepeerage.com/p32612.htm#i326119
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''Genealogical memoirs of the extinct family of Chester of Chicheley By Robert Edmond Chester- Waters
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=oGMBAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA156&lpg=PA156&dq=John+Cokayne+1438&source=bl&ots=B_V2p3sJ-S&sig=RYB_cbx_fOGQAxKtYMy0Qowz_vY&hl=en&ei=5vKbTbasG4K4sAOBnJyIBA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CBMQ6AEwAD
2 CONC gK#v=onepage&q=John%20Cokayne%201438&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 156
2 CONT *SIR PHILIP BOTELER, KT. of Watton Woodhall succeeded his cousin Sir Edward in 1413 in the estates entailed in 1312 by their common ancestors Ralph Boteler and Hawise Gobion.(3) He died 6th Nov. 1421,(32) and his widow Elizabeth m
2 CONC arried secondly Laurence Cheney Esq. of Fen Ditton, by whom she was the ancestor of the Dukes of Norfolk, the Peytons of Iselham, and other noble families.(33) She was the daughter of ''''''John Cokayne, who puchased from Sir Edwa
2 CONC rd Boteler the manor of Bury Hatley in Beds, and was one of the executors of John of Gaunt, who calls him in his will 'chief steward of my lands.'(34) He was raised on the accession of Henry IV. to the office of Chief Baron of the
2 CONC  Exchequer, which he held during the whole of this reign; but he was also a Judge of Common Pleas from 1406 until his death in 1429.(35) He was the second son of John Cokayne of Ashbourne in Derbyshire by Cecilia Irton his wife, a
2 CONC nd is confused by Foss with his nephew of the same name who died in 1438. (35) He married Ida, daughter of Reginald Lord Grey of Ruthyn by Eleanor le Strange, who died in 1424, leaving four sons and two daughters.(29) Their surviv
2 CONC ing children were:
2 CONT **	1. REGINALD, son and heir, ancestor of the Cokaynes of Cokayne Hatley.
2 CONT **	2. HENRY occurs with his wife Grace in his father's Will.
2 CONT **	3. JOHN. 4. THOMAS, a priest, who was presented to the rectory of Pulverbatch by his brother-in-law Philip Boteler on 19th July 1413.(36)
2 CONT **	1. ELIZABETH, married Sir Philip Boteler, Kt., and secondly Laurence Cheney Esq., and had issue by both marriages.
2 CONT **	2. MARGARET, married Sir Edmond d'Odingsells Kt. of Warwickshire.
2 CONT *   John Cokayne died in 1429, and desired by his Will to be buried at Bury Hatley, but his monument stands in Ashbourne Church, and is accurately figured by Dugdale as a specimen of the judicial robes worn at that period.(37)
2 CONT *	JOHN COKAYN.  Will dated 10th Feb. 6 Henry VI. (1427-8).
2 CONT *	To be buried in the parish church of Bury Hattele. To my nephew John Cokayn of Ashbourne Kt., to his wife, and to his daughter Alice, wife of Ralph Sherley Kt., one gold ring each.
2 CONT *   I desire that 3 marks a year be paid by my son Reginald Cokayn and his heirs to pray for the souls' health of Henry vj., of myself, of the said Reginald and Beatrix his wife, and of all my sons living, also for the souls of Jo
2 CONC hn late Duke of Lancaster, Richard ij., Henry iv. and Henry v., of John Cokayn by father, and Cecilia Irton* my mother, of Edmond Cokayn my brother, ''''''Ida my late wife'''''', and my dead children. To Sir William Babington Kt. 
2 CONC a book of statutes and L10 from the heritage of the heirs of Sir Philip Boteler Kt. To Reginald Cokayn, my son and heir apparent, all my armoury and my ornaments in my chapel at Bury Hatley. To Henry Cokayn, my 2'd son, and Grace 
2 CONC his wife two silver cups; to John Cokayn my 3'd son one cup; and to Thomas Cokayn my 4th son my missal, psalter, and all books of canon and civil law. To Laurence Cheyne and Elizabeth his wife my daughter a cup. To Margaret D'odyn
2 CONC gsells my daughter a cup, and I forgive her husband Sir Edmond D'Odyngsells Kt. his bond debt to me.
2 CONT *   Sir William Babyngton Kt., Reginald Cokayn, Laurence Cheyne, John Chichele Parson of Hattele, and Thomas Cokayne to be my executors.
2 CONT *   Will proved in 1429 (no month or day) in C.P.C. [12 Luffnam.] 
2 CONT **	*  Not Cecilia Vernon, as stated in the Peerages. (38)
2 CONT *_______________
