1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''This John is the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-de-Burgh-Kt-of-Burgh-Green/6000000224342501833.  Merge must be performed by a curator per https://www.geni.com/discussions/183181.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Surname also has been reported to be '''[https://www.geni.com/surnames/borough Borough]'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * https://stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/burgh10.php#lnk1 (membership required in order to view without interruption)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/BOROUGH.htm#John De BOROUGH3
2 CONT *''''''John De BOROUGH
2 CONT *Born: 5 Feb 1328, Somerton, Suffolk, England
2 CONT *Died: 1393
2 CONT *Buried: Burgh Church, Burgh, Cambridgeshire, England
2 CONT *Father: Thomas De BOROUGH
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret WALDEGRAVE
2 CONT *''''''Married 1: Mary De GREY ABT 1354, Ruthin, Denbighshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. John De BOROUGH
2 CONT **2. Thomas De BOROUGH
2 CONT *''''''Married 2: Catherine ENGAINE (d. 1409) (dau. of John Engaine and Joan)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **2. Elizabeth De BOROUGH
2 CONT **3. Margaret De BOROUGH
2 CONT **4. Joan De BOROUGH
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''Full text of "Dunham genealogy"
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/dunhamgenealogy00dunh/dunhamgenealogy00dunh_djvu.txt
2 CONT *H. — The second son of King Edward (John and the two Williams having d. in infancy), was Lionel, who was b. at Antwerp Nov. 29, 1338. He was a man of great strength and beauty of person. He was m. in 1352 to Elizabeth DeBergh, da
2 CONC u. of Lord of Connaught, and third Earl of LHster and head of one of the greatest of the Anglo-Norman houses in Ireland. Her mother was Maud, dau. of Lancaster, who after the death of her husband, who was murdered in 1332, was m. 
2 CONC to Ralph Ufford. On Nov. 13, 1362, Lionel was created Duke of Clarence. 
2 CONT *This latter title was derived from the town of Clare in Suffolk, the lordship of which with other shares in the divided Gloucester estates had been inherited by Elizabeth from her grandmother, Elizabeth of Clare, the sister of Gi
2 CONC lbert, the last Earl of Gloucester, of the house of Clare. Elizabeth d. in 1368 and left a dau. who m. Edmund Mortimer, Earl of Northumberland and Earl of March. He was sent by his father as Viceroy into Ireland and there proved h
2 CONC imself inefficient as a ruler. 
2 CONT *After the death of his wife in 1336 a second marriage was proposed, and Humprey Bohun, Earl of Hereford, was sent to negotiate a match with Violanti Galeazzo, dau. of the Lord of Paria and with elaborate arrangements the marriage
2 CONC  was consummated in 1368. Soon after the ceremonies he was taken ill and died. Personally, Lionel does not appear to have had any lofty aspirations. ''''''Thomas de Bergh, brother of Elizabeth, the wife of Lionel, who m. Lucy de B
2 CONC ellaque. dau. of John de Bellaque, was grandfather of Margaret de Bergh, who m. Sir John Zouche. Margaret de Bergh was grandmother of Elizabeth Bowett, wife of Sir John Dunham, who was dau. of Nicholas Bowett who m. Elizabeth Zouc
2 CONC he, dau. of John Zouch and Margaret de Bergh''''''. 
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1241.htm#i37265
2 CONT *''''''John de Burgh1
2 CONT *M
2 CONT *Father Thomas de Burgh 
2 CONT *Mother Lucy Bellaqua 
2 CONT *Family  
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT *◦Margaret Burgh+
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S74] Brent Ruesch's Research Notes.
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Walker, J.W.  "The Burghs of Cambs and Yorks and the Watertons of Lincs and Yorks".  Long article in ''Yorkshire Archaeological Journal'' Volume 30 (1931), page 311: <br/>
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/YAJ0301931#page/385/
2 CONT
2 CONT His date of birth comes from a proof of age, so maybe not too reliable.  His father's IPM made him younger.
2 CONT
2 CONT
