1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT 2nd but eldest surviving son, and heir, of his father, who was living in 1387, but not heard of again.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married a daughter of Sir George Felbrigg, a younger brother of Sir Simon Felbrigg of Felbrigg.  They had no issue, and on his death in 1411 his co-heirs were his 3 half-sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walker, J.W.  "The Burghs of Cambs and Yorks and the Watertons of Lincs and Yorks".  Long article in ''Yorkshire Archaeological Journal'' Volume 30 (1931), page 311: <br/>
