1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There is some conflict in these sources with the parents of Margaret Howard, John Howard who married Margaret Plaiz  is the son of Robert & Margaret (Scales) Howard, either one Generation is missing or has been add
2 CONC ed.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the complication may be due to Sir John Howard having two wives (Margaret Plaiz was his first), children by both of them, and a complex web of land trusteeships. http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/me
2 CONC mber/howard-sir-john-1366-1437
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources that do not attempt to track "our Glorious Royal Ancestors" are generally to be preferred, as they have no reason to create or perpetuate misinformation. History of Parliament Online, for instance, is only interested in tr
2 CONC acking the relationships among Members of Parliament, their constituencies, and their times, and has no other dog in the hunt (but they are not infallible either).
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: the Cliftons were not, strictly speaking, Barons at this point in time (the official title came - and soon passed on - in Tudor times), but were generic "lords" of the lands that they held.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Surtees Society vol. 144, p. 11, footnote 1b:  Constantine second lord Clifton of Buckenham, Norfolk, d. 1395, his son sir John Clifton being then one year old . Sir John died without children 1447 . His only sister Elizabeth, wif
2 CONC e of sir John Knyvet, was his heir and inherited the castle of Buckenham, Norfolk . (CP III, 308. )
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Sir Constantine Clifton, 2nd Baron Clifton1,2,3,4,5
2 CONT *''''''M, b. circa 1372, d. 19 February 1396
2 CONT *Father Sir John de Clifton, 1st Lord Clifton2,6 b. c 1353, d. 10 Aug 1388 
2 CONT *Mother Elizabeth de Cromwell2,6 b. c 1355, d. 24 Sep 1391 
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Constantine Clifton, 2nd Baron Clifton was born circa 1372 at of Buckenham, Babingley, Denton, Hilborough, & West Bradenham, Norfolk, England; Age 16 in 1388 and 19 1/2 in 1391.2,7 He married Margaret Howard, daugh
2 CONC ter of Sir Robert Howard and Margaret Scales, after February 1390; They had 1 son (Sir John, 3rd Lord Clifton) and 1 daughter (Elizabeth, wife of Sir John Knyvet).2,7,4,5 Sir Constantine Clifton, 2nd Baron Clifton died on 19 Febru
2 CONC ary 1396 at of Buckenham, Babingley, &Hilborough, Norfolk, England.2,7
2 CONT *''''''Family Margaret Howard d. 25 Mar 1434 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **◦Elizabeth Clifton+8,2,3,7,4 b. c 1392, d. b 8 Dec 1461
2 CONT **◦Sir John Clifton, 3rd Lord Clifton b. 1394, d. b 1 Dec 1447
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S4327] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. III, p. 308; The Ancestry of Dorothea Poyntz, by Ronny O. Bodine, p. 50; Wallop Family, p. 446.
