2 CONC 0CDgQ6AEwAzge#v=onepage&q=Constantine%20De%20Clifton%201372&f=false/ Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham]
2 CONT *Pg. 495
2 CONT *   10. ELIZABETH DE CROMWELL, married JOHN DE CLIFTON, Knt., of Buckenham, Babingley, Denton, Hilborough, West Bradenham, etc., Norfolk, son and heir of Constantine de Clifton, of Buckenham, Norfolk, by Katherine, daughter of Wil
2 CONC liam de la Pole, Knt. He was born about 1353 (aged 15 in 1368). They had one son, ''''''Constantine, Esq. [2nd Lord Clifton]'''''', and one daughter, Katherine (wife of Ralph Greene and Simon Felbrigg, Knt.). He was summoned to Pa
2 CONC rliament from 1 Dec. 1376 to 28 July 1388, by writs directed to Johanni de Clyfton, whereby his is held to have become Lord Clifton. SIR JOHN DE CLIFTON, 1st Lord Clifton, died at Rhodes 10 August 1388. His widow, Elizabeth, marri
2 CONC ed (2nd) EDWARD BENSTED, Knt. She died 24 Sep 1391. . . . 
2 CONT **''''''   11. CONSTANTINE DE CLIFTON, Esq., 2nd Lord Clifton, of Buckenham, Babingley, Hilborough, etc., Norfolk, Little Waltham, Essex, etc., son and heir, born about 1372 (aged 16 in 1388, aged 19 1/2 in 1391). He married after
2 CONC  Feb. 1389/90 MARGARET HOWARD, daughter of Robert Howard, Knt., of East Winch, Fersfield, and Wiggenhall, Norfolk (descendant of King John), by Margaret (or Margery), daughter of Robert de Scales, 3rd Lord Scales [see CORNWALL 8 f
2 CONC or her ancestry]. They had one son, John, Knt. [3rd Lord Clifton], and one daughter, Elizabeth. He was summoned to Parliament from 13 Nov. 1393 to 20 Nov. 1394. CONSTANTINE DE CLIFTON, Esq., 2nd Lord Clifton, died 19 Feb. 1395/6. 
2 CONC His widow, Margaret, married (2nd) (as his 3rd wife) GILBERT TALBOT, Knt., of Richard's Castle, Herefordshire and Wadley, Berkshire (died 6 Feb 1398/9), They had one son, Richard. She died 25 March 1434, and was buried at Black Fr
2 CONC iars, Norwich. . . . 
2 CONT **''''''Child of Constantine de Clifton, Esq., by Margaret Howard:
2 CONT ***	i. ELIZABETH CLIFTON, married JOHN KNYVET, Knt., of Southwick, Northamptonshire [ see GURDON 10].
