1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT High Sheriff of Northamptonshire (1347-1348, 1352-1354)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently from an unidentified source:
2 CONT
2 CONT >In the 12th century Eustace de Arden was settled as subtenant of the Ardens of Hampton at the manor of Bickenhill, Warwickshire. His family were called at various times de Arden or de Bickenhill. In Northamptonshire where they he
2 CONC ld Watford. They were also called de Watford. In 1326, Bickenhill was held by Walter Parles as great-grandson and heir of Eustace de Arden.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >In the 20th of Edward III. (1347), Nicholas de Burneby and '''Walter Parles''' accounted for three parts of one knight's fee in Watford, Syvesworth, and Murcote, which they held of the king in capite. (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * ''Magna Carta Ancestry: A study in Colonial and Medieval Families'', Richardson, Douglas, (Kimball G. Everingham, editor. 2nd edition, 2011), vol. 3 p. 434.
