2 CONT *Saleby is a village in the civil parish of Beesby with Saleby, in the East Lindsey district of Lincolnshire, England. It is on the Alford road to Louth, about 2 miles (3 km) north-east of Alford and 11 miles (18 km) south-east of
2 CONC  Louth. The hamlet of Thoresthorpe is about 1 mile (1.6 km) south of the village.
2 CONT *The Domesday book records "Saleby", with Lord of the Manor as Guy de Craon.[1]
2 CONT *The Church of England parish church of St Margaret was rebuilt in 1850 buff brick to the designs of Stephen Lewin, and was further restored in 1958. St Margaret's is a Grade II listed building.[2] '''In the chancel is a recess co
2 CONC ntaining a full length effigy of a knight in chain mail and surcoat, a memorial to Sir William de Hardreshull who died in 1303'''.[3]
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saleby ____________
2 CONT
2 CONT Descended from Hugh de Hardreshull (now Hartshill), grantee of Ansley, co. Warwick during the time of Henry 1 (1125). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Born circa 1269 in Hartshill Castle Warwickshire Died in 1303 in Saleby Louth Lincolnshire Buried in a fine tomb in St. Margaret's church Saleby Louth Lincolnshire "Fought with King Edward 1st in his campaigns to Subjugate the Sco
2 CONC ts & the Welsh"
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=118860412 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 28 2017, 12:43:50 UTC''
