2 CONT Touching the manor of Wyggesell and lands in Hernden in Sandhurst andNewynden because Wyggesell was settled on me and my wife Joyce and ourheirs on our marriage "p chartr endente," notwithstanding I have madeanother feoffment, I w
2 CONC ish the originalgift to stand good. "Moy ThomasColpeper le dymenge prochein le Purification nre dame l'an de nre syr. leRoy Henry vj-vije." Nicholas my son to make pilgrimages with variousspecified offerings to Norwich and the shr
2 CONC ine of St Thomas of Canterbury.To the Church of Pountose in Normandy where the body of Richard my sonlies a chalice etc. To Maryon Chamberer mon hopland de scarlet and fur.To Alison another hopland. To Nicholas my son a suitable b
2 CONC ed and apparelsuch as my son Waltor had at his marriage. Other bequests--ThomasFestynden to have 10 to pay
