2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000075317259836& Inquisitions Post Mortem] for Thomas Berkeley of Coberley, Writ 20 April 1405. <br>
2 CONT He died on 12 April [1405]. Margaret wife of Nicholas Mattesdon, aged 30 years and more, and Alice wife of Thomas de Brugge, 26 years and more, were his daughters and heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family and Education
2 CONT b. Coberley, 10 Oct. 1351, s. and h. of Sir Thomas Berkeley† (d.1365), by Joan, da. and h. of Geoffrey Archer of Stoke Orchard. m. (1) by 1364, Juliana; (2) by 1375, Margaret (d. 4 Apr. 1406), da. of Sir Thomas Chandos† of Snodhil
2 CONC l, Herefs., 2 da.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography
2 CONT [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/member/berkeley-thomas-1351-1405 History of Parliament Online]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000075320072940& Inquisitions Post Mortem] for John Chaundos, knight, Writ. 20 December 1428. He died on 16 December [1428] without heir of his body. Giles Brugge, esquire, was kin a
2 CONC nd one of his next heirs as the son of Alice one of the daughters of Elizabeth sister of John Chaundos, and aged 30 and more. Margaret wife of Nicholas Mattesdon was kin and his other next heir as the other daughter of Elizabeth s
2 CONC ister of John Chaundos, and aged 40 and more. Mentions '''Philippa his wife who had died before him.'''
