1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Primary Sources
2 CONT May 25. 1406 Westminster. <br>
2 CONT To the treasurer and the barons of the exchequer. Order not to trouble '''Nicholas Mattesden''' for his homage; as for a fine paid in the hanaper the king respited to a day now past the homage of the said '''Nicholas, who took to 
2 CONC wife Margaret one of the daughters and heirs of Thomas Berkeley of Coberley,''' and of Thomas Brugge who took to wife Alice the other daughter and heir, both being of full age, due by reason of issue between them and their wives b
2 CONC egotten, and commanded livery to be given them of their respective purparties; and he has taken the homage of the said Nicholas. By p.s. [4871.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 'Close Rolls, Henry IV: June 1406', in Calendar of Close Rolls, Henry IV: Volume 3, 1405-1409, ed. A E Stamp (London, 1931), pp. 43-50. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/cal-close-rolls/hen4/vol3/pp43
2 CONC -50 [accessed 3 February 2018].
