2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Edward (3) Stradling the third. He was a personage of considerable
2 CONT pretensions: he quartered the arms of St Burt in the right of his wife; then
2 CONT those of the Berkerolles (whose heir he became in 1411) and with them the arms of
2 CONT Turberville and Iestyn ab Gurgan. He married Jane daughter of Henry Beaufort,
2 CONT who became a cardinal. This lady was descended on the mother's side from the
2 CONT Arundel family*. Sir Edward like his father and Grandfather made a journey to
2 CONT Jerusalem to receive knighthood. (Was this a cheap and easy way of being dubbed?
2 CONT It is singular that we hear nothing of any of these valiant knights using
2 CONT their prowess in the tented field) Sir John Stradling a brother of this Sir
2 CONT Edward married the daughter and heiress of one Dauncey, in Somersetshire
2 CONT (?Wiltshire) and had two sons from whom are numerous descendants. Sir Edward's son was,
2 CONT
2 CONT * No proof for the Arundel mother. 
2 CONT
