2 CONT *''''''The genealogical history of the Croke family, originally named Le Blount (Volume 2). (page 4 of 47)
2 CONT *[http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/alexander-croke/the-genealogical-history-of-the-croke-family-originally-named-le-blount-volume-kor/page-4-the-genealogical-history-of-the-croke-family-originally-named-le-blount-volume-kor.s
2 CONC html/ The genealogical history of the Croke family, originally named Le Blount (Volume 2). (page 4 of 47)]
2 CONT *   John Blount, Esquire, of Kinlet and Dodington in the same county, married Alice, the daughter of ''''''Kynard de la Bere of Herefordshire, whose arms were azure, a bend, argent, cottised, or, between six martlets of the third'
2 CONC '''''*. In the seventh year of Henry the Sixth, 142S, John Blount, son and heir of Sir John Blount, Knight, and of Isabella his wife, was found to have held lands in Balterderley, Culvard, Romesore, and Bidulf, in the county of St
2 CONC afford 6 . He died in the twenty-first year of Henry the Sixth, 1442, and upon the inquisition held, he was found to have possessed Balterderley, Kilvart, Lentin, Romesore, and Bidulf, and that Humphrey was his son and heir, and o
2 CONC f the age of twenty years f . 
2 CONT *   John Blount, and Alicia de la Bere, had five sons, and five daughters. 
2 CONT *[http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/alexander-croke/the-genealogical-history-of-the-croke-family-originally-named-le-blount-volume-kor/page-5-the-genealogical-history-of-the-croke-family-originally-named-le-blount-volume-kor.s
2 CONC html/ The genealogical history of the Croke family, originally named Le Blount (Volume 2). (page 5 of 47)]
2 CONT *Humphrey, John, Edward, William, and Charles. Isabella married to John Kyene, Anne to William Gay ton, Maria to John Pigott, Eleanor to John Cheyney of Chesham, and Margaret to John Oteley.  . . . . 
2 CONT *¦ Harl. MSS. No. 1052. f. 28. b. No. 1196. f. 97. 75. Kennet, Par. Antiq. p. 3+1. from Dugdale's MSS. Sandford's Genealogical History. 
