2 CONT Knight of Sutton Bonnington, Nottinghamshire, of Braunston, Hennington in Lockington and Newbold Verdun, Leicestershire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son and heir to Thomas de Crophill. Second husband of Margery de Verdun, daughter to Sir Thebaud de Verdun and Maud de Mortimer, widow of Sir William le Blount, murdered in Liverpool, and widow of Sir Mark Husse. They were married
2 CONC  before 10 Sept 1355, and had one son, Thomas, and possibly one daughter, Maud.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margery died before Oct 1363 and he married a Joan, with whom he had two sons and two daughters; Reginald, Roger, Joan and Maud.
2 CONT
2 CONT John died at Bosworth and left a will dated 03 July 1383, proved 14 July 1383.
