2 CONT *''''''Agnes de la Bere1
2 CONT *''''''F, b. circa 1418
2 CONT *Father Sir Richard Delabere1 b. c 1389, d. 1488
2 CONT *Mother may be (Miss) Blount b. c 1387 
2 CONT *''''''     Agnes de la Bere was born circa 1418 probably at Herefordshire, England, where her father lived. She married firstly to William ap Thomas [1401- 25 August 1437], with who she had a son John ap William, who was also kno
2 CONC wn as John Herle.  In 1432 William ap Thomas inherited the Manor of Stoke Bliss from his father Thomas ap Philip Vaughan. William settled it on his wife Agnes in 1434. When William died in 1437, he left a son and heir John, 2 year
2 CONC s of age. Source - https://www.british-history.ac.uk/vch/worcs/vol4/pp349-354 Source http://www.inquisitionspostmortem.ac.uk/view/inquisition/25-042/42 1437 IPM of William ap Thomas 
2 CONT  Before 1441 she married Sir Robert Danvers, Chief Justice of the Common Pleas, son of Sir John Danvers and Joane Bruley, circa 1444.2,1
2 CONT *''''''Family Sir Robert Danvers, Chief Justice of the Common Pleas b. c 1424 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT **◦Agnes Danvers+1 b. c 1445
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 58.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 263-264.
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2335.htm#i70163
2 CONT *__________
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Danvers (de la Bere) Gender: Female  Birth: 1416  Herefordshire, England  Death: 1451 (35)  West Smithfield, London, Middlesex, England  Place of Burial: Church of the Holy Cross, London, Greater London, England, United King
2 CONC dom 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Immediate Family: Daughter of Sir Richard de la Bere, of Kinnersley Castle, Herefordshire and Joan de la Bere   ''' Wife of William ap Thomas Wife of Sir Robert Danvers, Kt., Chief Justice of the Common Pleas 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Alice Burnaby (Danvers); Henry Danvers & Agnes Dennis (Danvers)  Sister of Sir Kynard de la Bere
2 CONT
