1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Agnes St John died between 5 Oct 1420 will dated & Feb 1421 will proved, daughter of Sir John St John & sister of Oliver St John of Penmark [& later Bletsoe after his marriage to Margaret Beauchamp]. She was the gr
2 CONC anddaughter of Oliver St John & Elizabeth de la Bere. She married to John Rodeney of Rodney Stoke, Somerset. His will dated 1417, but proved 1421. His IMP mentions son & heir Walter aged 5. His will mentions wife Agnes, son Walter
2 CONC  & unborn child who is to get the 250 marks owed to him by John St John. Agnes’s will describes her of Wybley [Weobly] Castle & she wants to be buried at Lanredian (Llanrhidian) near her ancestor [presumably Elizabeth de la Bere].
2 CONC  Her will also refers to her father Lord Sir John St John, Knight, her brother Oliver St John, Knight & her sons Walter, John & Robert. 
