1 OCCU Knight, Lord of Penmark. He was coheir of Coyty Castle lands of the extinct Turbervilles in 1421.
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Oliver St. JOHN (Sir Knight)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: ABT 1400/14, Bletsoe, Bedfordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 1437, Penmark, Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John St. JOHN
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Elizabeth PAULET
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Margaret BEAUCHAMP (D. Somerset) (b. 1410 - d. 8 Aug 1482) (dau. of Sir John Beauchamp and Elizabeth Stourton) (m.2 of John Beaufort, 1º D. Somerset - m.3 of Lionel Welles, B. Welles)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Beaufort, mother of Henry VII, was the stepdaughter of Oliver St John of Lydiard Tregoze. His marriage to her mother, Margaret Beauchamp of Bletso produced six children to whom she remained close throughout her life, and 
2 CONC this gave the St Johns considerable influence at Court in the early decades of the Tudor dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. John St. JOHN (Sir Knight)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Oliver St. JOHN (Sir Knight)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Edith St. JOHN
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Elizabeth St. JOHN (B. Scrope of Bolton)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Mary St. JOHN
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Margaret St. JOHN (Abbes of Shaftesbury) (b. ABT 1436 - d. 1492)
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Agnes St. JOHN
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: ABT 1400/14, Bletsoe, Bedfordshire, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 1437, Rouen, Normandy, France 
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Peter Bartrum: St. John 1; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173427359964 [Bartrum charts https://www.geni.com/people/Philippa-ferch-Edmund-Mortimer-Earl-of-March/6000000212801313824 as the mother of Sir
2 CONC  Oliver] (Steven Ferry, December 24, 2024.)
