1 NAME Alexander /St. John/
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN St. John
2 _MARNM St. John
2 NICK Lord of Uchelolau
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1415
2 ADDR
3 STAE Wales
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1480
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Darrell Wolcott: Three Conflated Brecknock Families; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id324.html [Fam2: # 23] (Steven Ferry, October 11, 2024.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Peter Bartrum: St. John 2; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173433659836 & Einion ap Gollwyn 12; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173390904827 (Steven Ferry, December 24, 2024.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT LIVING: 1449. (Bartrum, Welsh Genealogies 1400-1500, vol. 9 p. 1568)
2 CONT  RESIDENCE: the manor Weobley (Weble). (Bartrum, Welsh Genealogies 1400-1500, vol. 9 p. 1568)
2 CONT  RESIDENCE: Wibly. (Thomas, Golden Grove MS, book 4 p. C521)
2 CONT
2 CONT Uncertainty about who the father is:
2 CONT
2 CONT ''(Research) KINSHIP: Thomas' 'Golden Grove MS' book 5 page C635 makes him the son of Sir Oliver {John} St. John, knight, and Elizabeth Delabere, his grandparents, thus omitting the generation of John from the name string.
2 CONT
2 CONT '' (Research) KINSHIP: MS. no. 8, Genealogies of Glamorgan Families, page 166 states he was the second son of Sir Oliver {John} St. John, and brother to Sir John St. John who married Mary or Margaret, heiress "of Bentham of Bledso
2 CONC l in Bedfordshire".'' ''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nevertheless, from Alexander and onwards we see a cadet branch of the de Port-St. John family emerging. His mother was a '''de Port-St. John'''''''. The de Port-St. John family have the Y-DNA haplogroup I1 (Germanic/Scandinavian),
2 CONC  whereas Alexander's Y-DNA haplogroup is R1b-L21 (Celtic). He is most probably son of Margary St. John, father unknown, and likely of French (Brittany/Normandy) origin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wales. Welsh Medieval Database Primarily of Nobility and Gentry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Welsh Genealogies, AD 300-1400 (1980), Bartrum, Peter C. (Peter Clement), (25 volumes, with supplements containing additions and corrections. [Wales]: University of Wales Press, 1980), FHL book 942.9 D2bp; FHL microfiche 6025561.,
2 CONC  vol. 5 p. 312.
2 CONT
2 CONT Welsh Genealogies AD 1400-1500 (1983), Bartrum, Peter C. (Peter Clement), (18 volumes, with supplements containing additions and corrections. Aberystwyth: National Library of Wales, 1983), FHL book 942.9 D2bw., vol. 9 p. 1567, 156
2 CONC 8*.
2 CONT
2 CONT WG 300-1400 - 5th List, Bartrum, Peter C., (Aberystwyth. Llyfrgell Genedlaethol Cymru / The National Library of Wales. 1996.), FHL 942.9 Dwbp supp. 5., p. 18.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Golden Grove books of pedigrees (filmed 1970), (Manuscript, National Library of Wales manuscript number Castell Gorfod 7. Filmed by the Genealogical Society of Utah, 1950), FHL microfilms 104,349-104,351., book 4 p. C521; book
2 CONC  5 p. C635c, 639*.
2 CONT
2 CONT MS. 8 - Glamorgan Pedigrees (MFU #12434), (Microfilm of mss. in the National Library of Wales, Aberystwyth. NLW MSS. 11964, 6611, 6544, 8, 6548, 3757, 6549, 3753. Salt Lake City, Utah: Filmed by the Genealogical Society of Utah, 1
2 CONC 950.), FHL microfilm 104312., p. 166*.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT May not be the father of Alexander. 
