1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Only son; 12th Earl of Mar; elected Regent of Scotland 2 Aug 1332; killed in the battle of Dupplin Moor; DNB. The victor in the battle of Dupplin Moor was John Baliol.
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Domhnall II, Earl of Mar'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_II,_Earl_of_Mar
2 CONT
2 CONT Domhnall (or Donald) II of Mar (c. 1302 in Saline, Fife – 11 August 1332) was Regent of Scotland for just over a week during the minority of David II.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was '''Gartnait, Earl of Mar''', and his mother was''' Christina Bruce''', sister of Robert I of Scotland. In 1332 the regent, Thomas Randolph, 1st Earl of Moray, died. On August 2 Domhnall was elected as the new regent
2 CONC  at a meeting of the Scottish nobles at Perth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the invasion of Edward Balliol, with the support of Edward III of England, Mar led the Scots loyalists to confront them. He was defeated and killed at the Battle of Dupplin Moor, only nine days after his election as rege
2 CONC nt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through his '''marriage to Isabella Stewart''' they had a son Thomas, and a single daughter, Margaret, who succeeded her brother and became in her turn Countess of Mar.
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Donald Mar 
2 CONT
2 CONT Suffix: 8th Earl of Mar 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: On 2 August 1332, Earl Donald Mar was Regent of Scotland, but was killed 10 days later at the Battle of Dupplin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: BEF 1305 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 12 AUG 1332 in Dupplin
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Gratney Mar b: BEF 1280 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Christian Bruce b: BEF 1290
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Isabel Stewart b: BEF 1315
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT  Margaret Mar b: BEF 1333
2 CONT
2 CONT  Thomas Mar b: BEF 1333
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Domhnall II, Earl of Mar (1293 – 11 August 1332) was briefly Regent of Scotland during the minority of David II, King of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Domhnall's father was Gartnait, Earl of Mar. His mother's identity is uncertain, although she seems to have been an elder daughter of Robert Bruce, Earl of Carrick.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1332 the regent of Scotland, Thomas Randolph, 1st Earl of Moray, died. On 2 August Domhnall was elected as the new regent at a meeting of the Scottish nobles at Perth. Following the invasion of Edward Balliol, with the support 
2 CONC of Edward III of England, Mar led the Scots loyalists to confront them. He was defeated and killed at the Battle of Dupplin Moor, only nine days after his election as regent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through his marriage to Isabella Stewart, daughter of Sir Alexander Stewart of Bonkyll and Jean Fitz James, they had a son,
2 CONT
2 CONT * Thomas of Mar, and a single daughter,
2 CONT * Margaret of Mar, who succeeded her brother and became, in her turn, Countess of Mar
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domhnall_II,_Earl_of_Mar Domhnall II, Earl of Mar]
