2 CONT     (3) Humprhey de Bohun VI:  (d.August/October 27, 1265).  He married
2 CONT     Alianor/Eleanor de Braose, daughter of William de Braose of Brecknock, Lordof
2 CONT     Abergavenny and his wife Eva Marshal, daughter of William Marshal and Isabelde
2 CONT     Clare.  In 1257 he helped his father keep the marches/borders and in 1263 he
2 CONT     joined his father to fortify the castles on the marches against Llewellyn.He
2 CONT     joined the barons against the king and in 1264 had custody of Winchester
2 CONT     Castle.  He fought at the battle of Evesham un 1265 where he was taken prisoner
2 CONT     and predeceased his father by ten years.  Eleanor was buried at Llanthony in
2 CONT     Gloucestershire.  They had a daughter, Agnes/Alianore who married Robert de
2 CONT     Ferrers of Chartley, a descendant of Sayer de Quincy, and they had a son,
2 CONT     Humphrey.--Adec,FHL 929.273,C769w
