1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#JohnBriouseMMargaretB
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir WILLIAM de Breuse''' (-Findon 1290, bur Sele, Sussex).  "William de Breous son and heir of John de Breus" was granted "a yearly fair at his manor of Horsham", dated 3 Aug 1233[1287].  "Domino Willilemo de Brawoso…" (presuma
2 CONC bly the donor´s stepson) witnessed the undated charter under which "Walterus de Clifford filius Walteri de Clifford et Agnetis de Cundy" donated land in Cofham to Acornbury priory, Herefordshire, for the souls of “Margaretæ uxoris
2 CONC  meæ et dominæ Mathildis filiæ meæ”[1288].  "Willielmus de Breuse miles" confirmed a donation to Acornbury priory, Herefordshire made by “dominus Johannes de Breus pater meus"  by charter dated 22 Jan [1290][1289].  '''He sat in t
2 CONC he Parliament of 1290, whereby he is held to have become Lord Brewose'''.  Leland quotes a manuscript which records the death in 1290 "apud Findon" of "Gul de Breosa senior" and his burial "in monaster de Sele"[1290].  
2 CONT
2 CONT * m firstly '''ALINE, daughter of THOMAS de Multon''' of Burgh-on-Sans, Cumberland & his wife Maud de Vaux.   
2 CONT * m secondly '''AGNES, daughter of NICHOLAS de Moeles [Mules]''' of Cadbury, Somerset & his wife ---.   
2 CONT * m thirdly (1271 or before) '''MARY, daughter of WILLIAM de Ros''' of Helmsley, Lord Ros & his wife Isabel d´Aubigny of Belvoir (-before 23 May 1326).  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Moels-20
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes de Brewes formerly Moels aka de Moels
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1233 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Nicholas (Moels) de Moels and Hawise (Newmarch) de Moels
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Hawise (Botterell) Clifford [half], James De Moels, Roger (Moels) de Moels and Maud De Moels	
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of William (Braose) de Braose — married 1268 in Cadbury, Somersetshire, Englandmap
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Giles (Braose) de Braose	
2 CONT
2 CONT Died before 1271 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT     Agnes de Moels, daughter of Nicholas de Moels by Hawise Newmarch, [1] was born about 1233. [2] She married as his 2nd wife, William de Brewes, after 1268, and they one son, Giles, Knight. [3] William de Brewes married his 3rd 
2 CONC wife in 1271, [4] by which time Agnes is presumed to have died. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT     Magna Carta Ancestry 2011 2nd ed. Vol. I p. 318 
2 CONT
2 CONT     ↑ Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, vol I, page 318
2 CONT     ↑ Our Royal, Titled, Noble and Commoner Ancestors & Cousins
2 CONT     ↑ Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, vol I, page 318
2 CONT     ↑ Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, vol I, page 318
2 CONT
2 CONT     Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, (2011), Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, Royal Ancestry series, 2nd edition, 4 vols., ed. Kimball G. Everingham, (Salt Lake City, Utah: the 
2 CONC author, 2011), volume I, page 318 #4 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Our Royal, Titled, Noble and Commoner Ancestors & Cousins database online, compiled by Mr. Marlyn Lewis, follows Douglas Richardson's Magna Carta Ancestry. It includes Magna Carta Surety Barons and many of their descendants. A
2 CONC gnes de Moels 
2 CONT
