1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#JohnBriouseMMargaretB
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir WILLIAM de Breuse''' (-Findon 1290, bur Sele, Sussex).  "William de Breous son and heir of John de Breus" was granted "a yearly fair at his manor of Horsham", dated 3 Aug 1233[1287].  "Domino Willilemo de Brawoso…" (presuma
2 CONC bly the donor´s stepson) witnessed the undated charter under which "Walterus de Clifford filius Walteri de Clifford et Agnetis de Cundy" donated land in Cofham to Acornbury priory, Herefordshire, for the souls of “Margaretæ uxoris
2 CONC  meæ et dominæ Mathildis filiæ meæ”[1288].  "Willielmus de Breuse miles" confirmed a donation to Acornbury priory, Herefordshire made by “dominus Johannes de Breus pater meus"  by charter dated 22 Jan [1290][1289].  '''He sat in t
2 CONC he Parliament of 1290, whereby he is held to have become Lord Brewose'''.  Leland quotes a manuscript which records the death in 1290 "apud Findon" of "Gul de Breosa senior" and his burial "in monaster de Sele"[1290].  
2 CONT
2 CONT * m firstly '''ALINE, daughter of THOMAS de Multon''' of Burgh-on-Sans, Cumberland & his wife Maud de Vaux.   
2 CONT * m secondly '''AGNES, daughter of NICHOLAS de Moeles [Mules]''' of Cadbury, Somerset & his wife ---.   
2 CONT * m thirdly (1271 or before) '''MARY, daughter of WILLIAM de Ros''' of Helmsley, Lord Ros & his wife Isabel d´Aubigny of Belvoir (-before 23 May 1326).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ====ThePeerage.com: [https://thepeerage.com/p14957.htm#i149564 Aline de Multon]
2 CONT * "Aline de Multon was the daughter of Thomas de Multon.1 She married William de Braose, 1st Lord Brewes, son of John de Braose and Margaret ferch Llywelyn.1 '''Child'''...: William de Breuse, 2nd Lord Brewes+1 d. c 1 May 1326"
2 CONT ** 1. G.E. Cokayne; et al editors, ''The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant'', New edition. Vol. 2, p. 302.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p402.htm#i12054 Our Royal, Noble, Titled and Commoner Ancestors and Cousins]
2 CONT * '''Father:''' Thomas de Multon2,3 d. b 14 Jan 1271
2 CONT * '''Mother:''' Maud de Vaux2,3 d. c 28 May 1293
2 CONT * '''Alina de Multon''' was born at of Burgh-on-Sands, Cumberland, England. She married Sir William de Brewes, 1st Lord Brewes, Lord Buckingham, son of John de Brewes, Lord of Gower, Bramber, Findon, & Washington and Margaret of W
2 CONC ales, circa 1245; They had 1 son (Sir William, 2nd Lord Brewes).2,3 Alina de Multon died before 1268.2,3
2 CONT * '''Family:''' Sir William de Brewes, 1st Lord Brewes, Lord Buckingham b. c 1224, d. 6 Jan 1291
2 CONT * '''Child:''' Sir William de Brewes, 2nd Lord Brewes, Lord Bramber & Gower+2,3 b. c 1261, d. c 1 May 1326
2 CONT * '''Citations'''
2 CONT ** 1. The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. II, p. 302.
2 CONT ** 2. Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 318-319.
2 CONT ** 3. Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 531-532.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===<nowiki>——————————————————————————————————————————</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline was the daughter of Thomas de MULTON , Lord of Gisland. Agnes was the daughter of Nicholas de MOELES who was custodian of the royal castles of Cardigan and Carmarthen.
2 CONT
2 CONT This marriage brought the manor of Woodlands in Dorset to William. Mary was the daughter of Robert de ROS who was on the baronial side in the war of 1264/5. Prince Edward escaped from his custody at Hereford and Robert later surre
2 CONC ndered Gloucester castle to the prince. Robert was pardoned soon after the battle of Evensham at the request of Prince Edward. Mary held Weaverthorpe in Yorkshire
