1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Margaret de Brewes
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born: Abt 1265, Stinton, Norfolk, England
2 CONT * Married (2): After 1288 9523
2 CONT * Died: Before 12 May 1335 9445,9524
2 CONT * Father	Sir Richard de Brewes,   b. Bef 1232, of, Stinton, Sall, Norfolk, England ,   d. Bef 18 Jun 1292  (Age ~ 60 years) 
2 CONT * Mother	Alice le Rus,   b. 1245-1247, of, Stinton, Sall, Norfolk, England ,   d. Bef 28 Jan 1300-1301  (Age 54 years) 
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT He [Roger de Coleville] married Margaret, daughter of Sir Richard DE BREWES, of Stinton, Norfolk, by Alice, daughter and heir of William Le Rus, of Stinton. He died 1287/8, before 6 March, date of writ for Inq. p. m. His widow die
2 CONC d 1335, before 12 May, when the writ for her Inq. p. m. is dated. [Complete Peerage III:374, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (or Margery) de Braose, died shortly before 12 May 1335; married Sir Roger de Coleville, Knight, born c1251, aged 26 in 1277, died shortly before 6 Mar 1287/8, Lord of Bytham, co Lincoln, son of Walter de Coleville, Lord 
2 CONC of Bytham, co Lincoln, died 1277, by Isabel or Elizabeth. [Magna Charta Sureties]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Neither Ancestral Roots, CP, or MCS mention a second marriage for Margaret, but Roger's death in 1288 would certainly allow for a 2nd marriage. 9110
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret married Sir Roger COLVILL of Bytham, son of Sir Walter COLVILL of Bytham and Isabel (Elizabeth) DE ALBINIACO. (Sir Roger COLVILL of Bytham was born about 1251 in Bytham Castle, Bourne, Lincolnshire, England and died on 6 
2 CONC Mar 1287-1288.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret also married Sir Walter DEVEREUX of Lenhales, son of Sir William DEVEROIS 1st Baron Deverois of Lyonshall and Alice DE GRANDISON, after 1288 9523. (Sir Walter DEVEREUX of Lenhales was born about 1261 in Lenhales, Hereford
2 CONC shire, England and died in 1320 in Lenhales, Herefordshire, England.)
2 CONT
