1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sire Johan GIFFARD, de goules, a iij lyouns passauns d'argent
2 CONT https://drawshield.net/reference/parker/l/lion.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ===John, Lord Giffard of Brimsfield===
2 CONT * b. 19 January 1241, d. 29 May 1299
2 CONT * Father	Sir Elias Giffard Knt.1 b. circa 1211?, d. 1248
2 CONT * Mother	Alice Maltravers b. after 1202
2 CONT
2 CONT John Giffard, Baron Giffard of Brimsfield (1232 1299), was an English nobleman prominent in the Second Barons' War and in Wales. His initial gift of land in Oxford led to the foundation of Gloucester College, Oxford.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT * was affianced, at the age of 4 years, to Aubrey de Camville (who was about the same age), but he did not marry her (b). [Complete Peerage V:639-44, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]. She became Abbess of Polesworth
2 CONT * (1) m. Maud de Clifford b. circa 1234, d. after December 1282. widow of Sir William LUNGESPEE
2 CONT * (2) m. Margaret, widow of Sir John de Neville, of Hallingbury [m. in 1286]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	by first wife
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1)Katherine m Sir Nicholas Daudeleye who seems to be son of James d'Audley/Alditheley by Ela dau of William Longespee 
2 CONT * 2)Alianore m Sir Fulk Lestraunge of Whitchurch (Lord Lestrange)  
2 CONT * 3)Maud m William son of Geoffrey de Joinville/Geneville, dsp  
2 CONT * 4)Elizabeth dvp 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by 2nd wife 
2 CONT * John (1287 1322) Married Aveline de Courtenay.  executed by Edward II as a rebel, and Brimpsfield Castle was destroyed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3D-K.htm#_Toc389046296
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         JOHN Giffard .  Lord Giffard of Brimpsfield.  m firstly MATILDA de Clifford, daughter of ---.  John & his wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         CATHERINE Giffard (1272-after 1322).  The Book of Lacock names Catharinam filiam Johannis Giffard as wife of Nichum de Audele, son of Jacobus de Audele 1248].  She became a nun at Ledbury[1249].  m (1299 or before) NICH
2 CONC OLAS de Audley, son of JAMES de Audley of Heleigh, Staffordshire & his wife Ela Longespee (before 1258-28 Aug 1299). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT Also called Sir John Giffard of Brimsfield.2 Arms: Gules, three lions passant, in pale, argent, and langued, azure.1 John, Lord Giffard of Brimsfield was born on 19 January 1241 at Brimsfield, Gloucestershire, England.3 He was the
2 CONC  son of Sir Elias Giffard Knt. and Alice Maltravers.1 John, Lord Giffard of Brimsfield married Maud de Clifford, daughter of Walter, 3rd Lord Clifford and Margred verch Llewelyn; Her 2nd.2,4 Summons writs - recorded "- merely -" o
2 CONC n the Welsh Rolls and ignored by Dugdale. Includes 11 Earls and 99 others "who must, if the writs be good, be accounted as Barons." In 1283.5 John, Lord Giffard of Brimsfield was summoned by writ directed "Johanni Giffard de Brimm
2 CONC esfeld" in 1283.6 John was summoned to parliament by Edward I "Longshanks", King of England on 23 June 1295 as Lord Giffard of Brimsfield.7 1st Lord Giffard of Brimsfield at Gloucestershire, England, on 23 June 1295.7 John, Lord G
2 CONC iffard of Brimsfield was a witness where Edward I "Longshanks", King of England called a Parliament and summoned his Barons on 23 June 1295.7 John, Lord Giffard of Brimsfield died on 29 May 1299 at Boynton, Wiltshire, England, at 
2 CONC age 58 years, 4 months and 10 days.3
2 CONT
