2 CONT
2 CONT 7b.   Sir John Giffard le Boeuf Knt. c.1235-c.1300 was of Twyford, Bucks., Knight of the Shire in a Parliment at Westminster 3 May 1296, one of the earliest in English history.  In the roll of arms printed with the Parliamentary w
2 CONC rits, his arms were set down thus: "Sire Johann Gyffarde le boef de Boules a III lions passant de argent e un label de azur."  The same arms are on the effigy of a relative, Sir Andrew Giffard, Crusader, in the Church of the Bless
2 CONC ed Mary, Boyton, where the  Brimpsfield Giffards had a manor.  From this line came Walter Giffard, Archbishop of York and Godfrey Giffard, Bishop of Worcester, each in turn Lord Chancellor of England.  The Hotel Giffard in Worcest
2 CONC er is named after Bishop Godfrey.
