1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Maud de Mortimer1,2,3,4,5
2 CONT *''''''F, #11063, b. circa 1286, d. 17 September 1312
2 CONT *Father      Sir Edmund Mortimer, 1st Lord Mortimer2,3,4,5 b. c 1252, d. 17 Jul 1304
2 CONT *Mother     Margaret de Fiennes2,3,4,5 b. c 1268, d. 7 Feb 1334
2 CONT *''''''     Maud de Mortimer was born circa 1286 at of Wigmore, Herefordshire, England. She married Sir Theobald de Verdun, Lord Weoberley, Baron Alton, 2nd Lord Verdun, Constable & Justiciar of Ireland, son of Sir Theobald de Ver
2 CONC dun, 1st Lord Verdun, Constable of Ireland, Baron/Lord of Duleek and Margery de Bohun, on 29 July 1302 at Wigmore, Herefordshire, England; They had 4 daughters (Joan, wife of John de Montagu, & of Sir Thomas, 2nd Lord Furnival; El
2 CONC izabeth, wife of Sir Bartholomew, 3rd Lord Burghersh; Margery, wife of Sir William le Blount, of Sir Mark Husee, & of Sir John de Crophull; & possibly Katherine).2,3,4,5 Maud de Mortimer died on 17 September 1312 at Alton, Staffor
2 CONC dshire, England; Buried at Croxden Abbey, Staffordshire. Died after childbirth.2,4,5
2 CONT *''''''Family      Sir Theobald de Verdun, Lord Weoberley, Baron Alton, 2nd Lord Verdun, Constable & Justiciar of Ireland b. 8 Sep 1278, d. 27 Jul 1316
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Joane de Verdun+6,5 b. 9 Aug 1303, d. 2 Oct 1334
2 CONT **Elizabeth de Verdun+7,8,5 b. c 1306, d. 1 May 1360
2 CONT **(Miss) Verdun+ b. c 1307
2 CONT **Margery de Verdun+9,5 b. 10 Aug 1310, d. b 12 Oct 1363
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S2862] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. II, p. 425; Magna Charta Sureties, 1215, by F. L. Weis, 4th Ed., p. 15; The Royal Descents of 500 Immigrants, by Gary Boyd Roberts, p. 303; OFHS Newsletter, Decemb
2 CONC er 1995, p. 95.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 166.
2 CONT * 3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 522.
2 CONT * 4.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 735.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 252-253.
2 CONT * 6.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 735-736.
2 CONT * 7.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 169-170.
2 CONT * 8.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 365.
2 CONT * 9.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 1.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p369.htm#i11063
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT *''''''Maud Mortimer1
2 CONT *F, #405460
2 CONT *Last Edited=28 Feb 2010
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT *''''''     Maud Mortimer is the daughter of Sir Edmund de Mortimer, 1st Lord Mortimer and Margaret de Fiennes.1 She married Theobald de Verdon.1
2 CONT *''''''      Her married name became Verdon.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family."
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p40546.htm#i405460
2 CONT *__________________________
2 CONT *Edmund Mortimer, 2nd Lord Mortimer (1251 – July 17, 1304)[1] was the second son and eventual heir of Roger Mortimer, 1st Baron Wigmore. His mother was Maud de Braose. As a younger son, Edmund had been intended for clerical or mon
2 CONC astic life, and had been sent to study at Oxford University.  ......
2 CONT *In return for his services Edmund was knighted by King Edward at Winchester in 1283. In September 1285, he married Margaret de Fiennes, the daughter of William II de Fiennes and Blanche de Brienne (herself the granddaughter of Jo
2 CONC hn of Brienne by his third wife Berenguela of Leon), the family entering the blood royal. Their surviving children were:
2 CONT ** Roger Mortimer, 1st Earl of March (25 April 1287 – 29 November 1330) married Joan de Geneville,[5] by whom he had twelve children.
2 CONT **'''''' Maud Mortimer, married Sir Theobald II de Verdun, by whom she had four daughters, Joan, Elizabeth, Margaret, and Katherine de Verdun.[5][6]
2 CONT ** John Mortimer, accidentally slain in a joust by John de Leyburne.[5]
2 CONT ** Walter Mortimer, a priest, Rector of Kingston.[5]
2 CONT ** Edmund, a priest, Rector of Hodnet and Treasurer of the cathedral at York.[5]
2 CONT ** Hugh Mortimer, a priest, Rector of church at Old Radnor.[5]
2 CONT *They also had two daughters who became nuns; Elizabeth and Joan.[5] ....
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Mortimer,_2nd_Baron_Mortimer
2 CONT *_________
2 CONT *''''''Margaret De FIENNES 
2 CONT *''''''Died: 7 Feb 1333/1334 
2 CONT *Father: William De FIENNES (2° B. Fiennes)
2 CONT *Mother: Blanche BRIENNE
2 CONT *''''''Married: Edmund De MORTIMER of Wigmore
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Roger De MORTIMER
2 CONT **2. Maud De MORTIMER
2 CONT **3. Hugh De MORTIMER (Sir) (m. Margaret De Ros)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/FIENNES.htm#Margaret De FIENNES1
2 CONT *_____________________
