3 FORM jpg
3 TITL Tyburn Tree plaque
3 NOTE From http://www.bbc.co.uk/dna/place-london/A988833
4 CONT
4 CONT
4 CONT The first execution at Tyburn took place in 1196, the last in 1783. The first hangings were carried out from tree branches on the bank of the Tyburn River (see below), but in 1220 a pair of gallows were built on the site. The Trip
4 CONC le Tree (the name given to the gallows) was built in 1571, and removed in 1759 because it was obstructing the highway. A mobile gallows was used until public executions ceased there.
