2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT *Edmund Mortimer, 2nd Lord Mortimer (1251 ÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂ July 17, 1304)[1] was the second son and eventual heir of Roger Mortimer, 1st Baron Mortimer. His mother was Maud de Braose. As a younger s
2 CONC on, Edmund had been intended for clerical or monastic life, and had been sent to study at Oxford University.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *In return for his services Edmund was knighted by King Edward at Winchester in 1283. In September 1285, he married Margaret de Fiennes, the daughter of William II de Fiennes and Blanche de Brienne (herself the granddaughter of Jo
2 CONC hn of Brienne by his third wife Berenguela of Leon), the family entering the blood royal. Their surviving children were:
2 CONT **Roger Mortimer, 1st Earl of March (25 April 1287 ÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂ 29 November 1330) married Joan de Geneville,[6] by whom he had twelve children.
2 CONT **Maud Mortimer, married Sir Theobald II de Verdun, by whom she had four daughters, Joan de Verdun, who married John de Montagu (d. August 1317), eldest son and heir apparent of William Montagu, 2nd Baron Montagu; Elizabeth de Ver
2 CONC dun, who married Bartholomew de Burghersh, 1st Baron Burghersh; Margaret de Verdun, who married firstly Sir William le Blount of Sodington, Worcestershire, secondly Sir Mark Husee, and thirdly Sir John de Crophill; and (allegedly)
2 CONC  Katherine de Verdun.[6][7]
2 CONT **John Mortimer, accidentally slain in a joust by John de Leyburne.[6]
2 CONT **Walter Mortimer, a priest, Rector of Kingston.[6]
2 CONT **Edmund, a priest, Rector of Hodnet and Treasurer of the cathedral at York.[6]
2 CONT **'''Hugh Mortimer, a priest, Rector of church at Old Radnor.[6]
2 CONT *They also had two daughters who became nuns; Elizabeth and Joan.[6]
2 CONT *Mortimer served in the king's Scottish campaign, and returned to fight in Wales in 1283. He was mortally wounded in a skirmish near Builth, and died at Wigmore Castle.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Mortimer,_2nd_Baron_Mortimer ______________________
