1 NOTE  Robert de Vere, 6th Earl of Oxford and 7th Great Chamberlain, another warrior, took part in the wars against Scotland by King Edward I. [One can see the Scots' side of these wars in the movie "Braveheart," where Edward I is portr
2 CONC ayed as a complete villain.] Robert, EO6, also fought with Longshanks in Wales. Robert additionally battled alongside Kings Edward II and Edward III in both Scotland and France in skirmishes of the Hundred Years War.
2 CONT
2 CONT He officiated at the Coronation of Queen Isabella, wife of Edward II, in 1308 and was known as:
2 CONT
2 CONT     "The Good earl of Oxford, his government, both in peace and war being so prudent, his hospitality and works of Charity so wisely abundant, and his temperance, with religious zeal, so admirably conjoined, that the common people
2 CONC  esteemed him as a Saint "
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Mortimer, daughter of Roger Mortimer, Earl of March. Robert's only son Thomas pre-deceased him, and thus he died without an heir in 1331 and his honors and titles devolved upon his nephew, John, EO7.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, EO6, is buried in the family chapel at Bures, 20 miles from Hedingham, where many of the Earls of Oxford are interred.
