2 CONC io de Ysland” and records that he conquered Man in 1076, reigned 16 years and died “in insula…Yle”[1275].  King of Man. The date of his death is indicated by the reference to his son Lagman which is dated to 1098 (see below).  [Fr
2 CONC om a chronological point of view, it is possible that he was the same person as GODFRID King of Dublin, whose death is recorded in the Annals of Ulster in 1095 "Gofraidh Meranach king of the foreigners"[1276].  If this is correct,
2 CONC  he was the son of Imar King of Dublin.]  '''m ---.  The name of Godred’s wife is not known. Godred & his wife had three children''':....
