2 CONT >>i)   [https://www.geni.com/people/L%C3%A5gmand-Gudr%C3%B8dsson/6000000008177305955?through=1341991 LAGMAN] (-Jerusalem 1111 or after).  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum names “Lagmannum, Haraldum et Olavum” as the three sons of
2 CONC  “Godredus Crovan”, recording that Lagman succeeded his father and reigned seven years, before abdicating and leaving for Jerusalem where he died[1277].  King of Man.  Morkinskinna records that Magnus III King of Norway captured “
2 CONC Logmadr, the son of King Gudrødr [who] ruled over the northern islands”, dated to 1098 from the context[1278]. 
2 CONT
