2 CONT Chapter 12.  GALLOWAY 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         FERGUS, son of --- (-[1136]).  Lord of Galloway.  "…Fergus de Galweia…Uchtred filio Fergus" witnessed a charter dated to [1136] by which "David Rex Scotiæ" granted Perdeyc to the church of Glasqow[500].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ELIZABETH, daughter of ---.  Fergus & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         UHTRED of Galloway (-1174).  "…Fergus de Galweia…Uchtred filio Fergus" witnessed a charter dated to [1136] by which "David Rex Scotiæ" granted Perdeyc to the church of Glasqow[501].  William of Newburgh names "duo fratr
2 CONC es Gilbertus et Uctredus Galwadensis provinciæ dofuini…Fergusi olim principis eiusdem provincie filii" when recording their quarrels [in 1174] and that Uhtred was killed[502].  Lord of Galloway.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of John of Fordun (Continuator - Annals) records that "Ochtred…son of Fergus…was taken prisoner by his brother Gilbert 22 Sep" and later blinded and murdered[503].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m GUNHILD, daughter of WALTHEOF & his wife Sigrid ---.  The Cronicon Cumbriæ records that “Alanus filius et hæres eiusdem Waldevi” enfeoffed “Ugthredo filio Fergus domino Galwediæ” with property and “Guynolda sorore sua”[504].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Uhtred & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          ROLAND of Galloway (-1200).  William of Newburgh names "fratri nefarie interempto filius Rollandus"[505].  Lord of Galloway.   The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1200 of "Roland son of Uchtrach king of the Foreig
2 CONC n-Irish”[506]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         --- of Galloway (-killed in battle 1185).  The Chronicle of Melrose records that he fought with his brother Roland against "Gillecolm" but was killed in the battle together with their opponent[507].  The Chronicle of J
2 CONC ohn of Fordun (Continuator - Annals) records the death of "Rotholand´s brother" in 1185 when "Ochtred´s son Rotholand" fought against "Gilpatrick and Henry Kennedy"[508]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         AUFRICA of Galloway .  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum records that “Olavus filius Godredi Crovan” married “Affricam…filiam Fergus de Galwedia”[509].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m OLAV “Morsel” King of Man, son of GODFRED “Crovan” King of Man & his wife --- ([1080]-killed 1153). 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         GILBERT of Galloway (-1 Jan 1185).  William of Newburgh names "duo fratres Gilbertus et Uctredus Galwadensis provinciæ dofuini…Fergusi olim principis eiusdem provincie filii" when recording their quarrels [in 1174], com
2 CONC menting that "Gilbertus natu major"[510].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun (Continuator - Annals) records the death of "Gilbert son of Fergus lord of Galloway" in 1185[511].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Gilbert´s wife is not known.  Gilbert & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          DUNCAN (-13 Jun 1250).  The Chronicle of Melrose records that "Duncan the son of Gilebert of Galwey" gave to the monks of Melrose a certain portion of his lands in Karec in 1193[512].  He obtained Carrick from William 
2 CONC "the Lion" King of Scotland before 1196, becoming 1st Earl of Carrick. 
