2 CONT
2 CONT Bethoc MacFergus of Galloway, married Moray.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''NOTE: The dates don't work for her to have been the mother of the Thomas Randolph, Chamberlain, who died in 1262.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.electricscotland.com/History/nation/moray.htm The Scottish Nation - Moray]
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Randolph, as superior of the whole of Nithsdale, transmitted the designation of lord of Stranith to his posterity. He married Bethoc, heiress of the lands of Bedrule, a contraction of Bethoc-rule, and Buecastle in Teviotdale, an
2 CONC d from him his descendants assumed the surname of Randolph. Thomas, his son, was one of the anti-Anglican party removed from the administration of affairs during the minority of Alexander III., 21st September, 1255, and died in 12
2 CONC 62. "
2 CONT
