1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Adam de Audley (or de Aldithley)= 
2 CONT son of '''Liulf de Audley'''.  married '''Emma daughter of Robert FitzOrm'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT EARLS of GLOUCESTER 1337-1347 (AUDLEY) from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#LiulfAudleyMStanley
2 CONT
2 CONT The primary sources which confirm the parentage and marriages of the following family have not yet been identified, unless otherwise indicated below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         LIULF .  He was granted the manors of Audley and Talke, Staffordshire.  The 1130 Pipe Roll records "Liulf de Aldredeslega" in Staffordshire[1652].  m --- de Stanley, daughter of ---.  
2 CONT * Adam, son of Liulf de Audley, granted Stanley, Staffordshire to William de Stanley, son of Adam de Stanley the grantor´s avunculus, in exchange for Talk o´ the Hill, undated but during the reign of King Stephen[1653].  If avuncu
2 CONC lus is interpreted strictly in this source, Adam de Audley´s mother was the sister of Adam de Stanley.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Liulf & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)        ''' ADAM de Audley''' (-[1203/11).  Adam, son of Liulf de Audley, granted Stanley, Staffordshire to William de Stanley, son of Adam de Stanley the grantor´s avunculus, in exchange for Talk o´ the Hill, undated but during
2 CONC  the reign of King Stephen[1654].  Ancestor of the Lords Audley[1655].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m '''EMMA, daughter of ROBERT FitzOrm''' & his wife ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)         ''' ADAM de Audley''' (-1212 or before).  He was constable to Hugh de Lacy Earl of Ulster[1656].
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         '''HENRY de Audley''' ([1175]-1246 before Nov).  He bought the manors of Egmond and Newport in Shropshire and built the castles of Heleigh, Staffordshire and Red Castle, Shropshire[1657].  m (1217) BERTRED, daughter of
2 CONC  RALPH Mainwaring [Mesnil-Warin], seneschal of Chester & his wife --- (-after 1249).  Henry & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT >(a)       RALPH (-before 1240).  According to the Complete Peerage[1658], Ralph was "very possibly" James's older brother. 
2 CONT >(b)       JAMES Audley of Heleigh, Staffordshire ([1220]-[11 Jun] 1272). 
2 CONT >(c)       ALICE .  m PIERS de Montfort of Preston, co. Rutland (-killed in battle 1265). 
2 CONT >(d)       EMMA .  m firstly HENRY Touchet .  m secondly GRUFFYDD Maelor [II] Lord of North Powys, son of MADOG Prince of Northern Powys & his wife Isota --- (-1269). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==============================
2 CONT
2 CONT  4. ADAM3 DE ALDITHLEY (LYDULPH FITZ LIULF2, LYDULPH (LIULF)1) was born 1135 in Staffordshire, England, and died 1211 in Staffordshire, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married EMMA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for ADAM DE ALDITHLEY
2 CONT He appears to have been the first member of his family to have used the surname 'de Aldithley' in official documents, when in 1155 and again in 1160 he witnessed Charters of his Overlord, Bertram de Verdun. His two brothers, Liulf
2 CONC  and Roger, still continued to sign themselves as 'Liulf fitz Liulf' and 'Roger fitz Liulf' respectively, when they witnessed Charters in 1160-1202. In 1184 and 1185, Adam de Aldithley succeeded Bertram de Verdun as Sheriff of War
2 CONC wickshire and Leiscestershire. When Bertram de Verdun departed for the Crusades in 1190 with Richard I, as special evidence of his favor, granted the Manor of Stanleigh to Adam de Aldithley. During the latter part of his life, Ada
2 CONC m decided to rearrange his estates by granting to his cousin, William (the son of his uncle, Adam de Stanleigh), all the Manor of Stanleigh and half of the Manor of Balterley in exchange for his cousin's tenancy of the Manor on Ta
2 CONC lk of the Hill. Thus it was that the two separate lines began, with the Audleys at Aldithley and the Stanleys at Stanleigh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of ADAM DE ALDITHLEY and EMMA are:
2 CONT * i. ADAM4 DE ALDITHLEY.
2 CONT * ii. HENRY DE ALDITHLEY.
2 CONT * iii. WILLIAM DE ALDITHLEY.
2 CONT * iv. LUCAS DE ALDITHLEY.
2 CONT * v. ISABEL DE ALDITHLEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~ourpage/pdf/stanleighGen.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================
2 CONT
2 CONT Audley of Staffordshire, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam de Aldithley [a] b abt 1145, d 1203-1211. He md Emma abt 1166, daughter of Ralph Fitz Orm. She was b abt 1150.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Adam de Aldithley and Emma was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Aldithley [b], Sheriff of Shropshire and Staffordshire, b abt 1172, of Heleigh, Staffordshire, England, d sh bef Nov 1246. He md Bertrade de Mainwaring 1217, daughter of Sir Ralph de Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester, and 
2 CONC Amicia le Meschin. She was b abt 1198, d aft 1249.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Henry de Aldithley and Bertrade de Mainwaring were:
2 CONT •James de Audley, Justiciar of Ireland, b abt 1220. •Alice de Aldithley b abt 1224, of Heleigh, Staffordshire, England, d aft Aug 1265. She md Sir Piers de Montfort abt 1238, son of Thurstan de Montfort and Daughter de Cantelou. •
2 CONC Emma de Aldithley b abt 1226, of Heleigh, Staffordshire, England. She md Sir Gruffydd ap Madog, Lord of Bromfield, abt 1244, son of Madog ap Gruffydd-Maelor and Gwladys verch Ithel.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geneajourney.com/audley.htmlwww.celtic-casimir.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam DE ALDITHLEY
2 CONT 	Born: 1149, Heleigh, Stafford, England 
2 CONT 	Married: 1173, Heleigh, Stafford, England 
2 CONT 	Died: 1203, Heleigh, Stafford, England 
2 CONT 	Buried: 1203, Heleigh, Stafford, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Another name for Adam was Adam DE AUDLEY. 
2 CONT Ancestral File Number: GLCB-HS. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT Adam married Emma FITZ ORM, daughter of Ralph FITZ ORM of Darlaston & Okeover and Lettice DE MONTGOMERY Heiress of Snelston, in 1173 in Heleigh, Stafford, England. (Emma FITZ ORM was born in 1153 in Darlaston, Walsall, Staffordshi
2 CONC re, England.)
