1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Hugh de Kevelioc had one [illegitimate] child by [an unknown mistress]: [Therefore, his wife Bertrade was not her mother]
2 CONT
2 CONT g)         AMICIA .  Her alleged legitimacy, the subject of a bitter dispute in the late 17th century, was championed by one of her supposed descendants Thomas Mainwaring of Baddeley, Cheshire[170].  It is difficult at this distan
2 CONC ce in time to judge the merits of the arguments, although it is interesting to note that her daughter was named Bertrade, the name of Earl Hugh’s wife who herself witnessed the charter which recorded Amicia’s marriage contract (se
2 CONC e below), which may suggest that Bertrade de Montfort was her mother.  On the other hand, Amicia is not named among the earl’s legitimate daughters who are referred to in several contemporary primary sources, as quoted above.  “H.
2 CONC  comes Cestrie” granted “servicium Giliberti filii Rogeri, scilicet servicium trium militum” to “Radulfo de Meinilwarin cum Amicia filia mea in libero maritagio” by charter dated to [1178/80], witnessed by “Bertraya comitisse Cest
2 CONC rie...Willelmo de Meinilwarin...Roberto de Meinilwarin...”[171].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m RALPH de Mesnilwarin [Mainwaring], Justice of Chester, son of ---.  Ralph & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          ROGER Mainwaring .  “Rogerus de Menilwarin” donated “grangie de Biveleg” to Deulacresse, for the soul of “domini Ranulphi quondam comitis Cestriæ et Lincolniæ avunculi mei” by undated charter, witnessed by “Willielmo d
2 CONC e Menilwarin...”[172]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         BERTRADE Mainwaring (-after 1249).  “Radulfus de Meidnilwar” granted “Smelewde...et Snellest...et dimid Pichemere...” to “Henrico de Alditelegh in liberum maritagium cum Bertrea filia mea” by undated charter, witnessed
2 CONC  by “Ran com Cestr, Hug com Ultoniæ...”[173].  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by inquisitions after a writ dated 22 Apr "4 Edw I", following the death of [her grandson] "Henry de Audidelegh..." which record the manor of 
2 CONC “Smalewode...given to Henry de Audithele grandfather of the said Henry” by “Thomas [error for Ralph?] de Meynwaryn as free marriage”[174].  m HENRY de Audley, son of ADAM de Audley & his wife Emma --- ([1175]-1246 before Nov). 
2 CONT
2 CONT =-------------------------=
2 CONT Amicia de Meschines
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 1171?
2 CONT
2 CONT Amicia de Meschines|b. c 1171?|p57.htm#i6893|Hugh de Kevelioc, 6th Earl of Chester|b. 1147\nd. 1181|p376.htm#i6940|N. N. (?)|b. c 1147|p168.htm#i18789|Ranulph de Gernon, 5th Earl of Chester|b. b 1100\nd. 16 Dec 1153|p369.htm#i6795
2 CONC |Maud of Gloucester|b. c 1124\nd. 29 Jul 1189|p378.htm#i6796|||||||
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Hugh de Kevelioc, 6th Earl of Chester b. 1147, d. 1181
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	N. N. (?)1 b. circa 1147
2 CONT
2 CONT      Amicia de Meschines was born circa 1171? At Kevelioc, Merionethshire, Wales. She was the daughter of Hugh de Kevelioc, 6th Earl of Chester and N. N. (?).1 Amicia de Meschines married Ralph Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester, so
2 CONC n of Roger Mainwaring and Ellen (?), circa 1188 at Warmingham, Cheshire, England.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Ralph Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester b. 1155
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Bertred Mainwaring+ b. c 1196
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Roger Mainwaring of Warmincham+ b. c 1196?2
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. [S215] Revised by others later George Edward Cokayne CP, III:167, footnote (b).
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. [S1191] Esq. John Burke B:C of GB&I, pg. 590.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Amicia Kyveliock is the daughter of Hugh Kyveliock. She married Sir Raufe Mainwaring, Knt. in 1179 in Warmingham, Cheshire County, England. She 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i. 	Roger Mainwaring See #7. below. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  302. Hugh de Kiviliok de Meschines, born 1147 in Kevilioc, Merionethshire (Monmouth), Wales; died 30 June 1181 in Leeke, co. Stafford, England. He was the son of 604. Ranulph de Kivilioc de Meschines II and 605. Matilda FitzRober
2 CONC t of Gloucester. He married 303. Bertrade Montfort 1169 in Montfort, Normandy, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT  303. Bertrade Montfort, born 1155 in Montfort, Eure, France; died 12 July 1189 in Evereux, Eure, France. She was the daughter of 606. Simon de Montfort II and 607. Maud d'Evereux.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hugh de Meschines and Bertrade Montfort are:
2 CONT
2 CONT   i. Agnes de Kivilioc de Meschines, born 1174 in Tutbury, co. Stafford, England; died 2 November 1247; married William de Ferrers II 2 November 1192; died 22 September 1247.
2 CONT
2 CONT   ii. Hawise de Kivilioc de Meschines, born Abt. 1180 in Chester, Cheshire, England; died 1243; married Robert de Quincy 1207; born 1172 in Buckley, Winchester, Hampshire, England; died Abt. 1219 in Palestine, Asia Minor.
2 CONT
2 CONT   iii. Matilda de Kivilioc de Meschines, born 1171 in Chester, Cheshire, England; died 1233; married (1) David of Huntingdon and Scotland 19 August 1190; born Abt. 1144; died 17 June 1219 in Scotland; married (2) William d'Albini 
2 CONC IV Aft. 1207; born 1165 in Belvoir Castle, Leicestershire, England; died Bef. 30 March 1221 in Cainell, near Rome, Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT   iv. Tanglust de Kivilioc de Meschines
2 CONT
2 CONT   v. Ranulph de Blundeville de Kivilioc de Meschines, born Abt. 1172; died October 1232; married (1) Constance of Brittany 3 February 1185/86; born Aft. 1162; died 5 September 1201 in Nantes, Brittany; married (2) Clemence de Foug
2 CONC eres Aft. 1199.
2 CONT
2 CONT  151 vi. Amicia de Kivilioc de Meschines, born Bet. 1175 and 1178 in Kivilioc, Monmouthshire, Wales; married Ralph de Mainwaring 1179 in Warmingham, Cheshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT   vii. Maud de Kivilioc de Meschines, born Abt. 1168 in Chester, Cheshire, England; married David Dunkeld 26 August 1190 in Scotland.
2 CONT www.celtic-casimir.com
