1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ralph Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester1 b. 1155
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father	Roger Mainwaring b. circa 1130
2 CONT * Mother	Ellen (?) b. circa 1133
2 CONT
2 CONT Also called Ralph de Mesnilwarin, Justice of Chester.2 Ralph Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester was the great-grandson of Richard de Mesnilwaren, son of Ranulphus who is said to have come to England with the Conqueror.3 He was born 
2 CONC in 1155 at Warmingham, Cheshire, England. He was the son of Roger Mainwaring and Ellen (?). Ralph Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester married Amicia de Meschines, daughter of Hugh de Kevelioc, 6th Earl of Chester and N. N. (?), circa
2 CONC  1188 at Warmingham, Cheshire, England.4 Ralph Mainwaring, Seneschal of Chester was living "temp. Richard I."3 Justice of Chester at England.5
2 CONT
