1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Roger Mesnilwarin, son of Randulfus, gave Plumley to Chester Abbey, England before 1119
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wikitree: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mainwaring-57 Sir Roger Mainwaring]'''
2 CONT * Sir Roger Mainwaring, son and heir of Ralph Mainwaring, was a knight, Lord of Warmincham, Cheshire, England. He flourished during the reign of King Henry III, from 1216 to 1272. (Summarized from the book "Medieval English Ancest
2 CONC ors of Robert Abell" by Carl Boyer, 3rd as found at todmar.net)  
2 CONT * He was a generous benefactor to the Cistercian abbey of Dieulacres, a religious house on the banks of the Churnet, near Leek, which had been founded by Ranulph de Blundeville, Earl of Chester, whom, in his gift, he expressly cal
2 CONC ls uncle.  
2 CONT * He had three sons: Sir Thomas, his heir; Randle, an ecclesiastic; Sir William, who had the lordship of Over Peover by gift of his father.  
2 CONT * SOURCES
2 CONT ** County families of Lancashire and Cheshire, by James Croston 
2 CONT ** Genealogy of Shropshire [by Joseph Morris] vol. 3 p. 1116 
2 CONT ** The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester (1882), Ormerod, George, ( vol. 1 p. 478; vol. 3 p. 226, 229 
2 CONT ** A short history of the Mainwaring family (1890), Finley, Reginald Mainwaring, (1890. Facsimile reprint, London: The Research Publishing Co., 1976), p. 29 
2 CONT ** The Wallop Family and Their Ancestry (1928), Watney, Vernon James, (4 volumes. Oxford: John Johnson, 1928), vol 2 p. 525.  
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mainwaring-57
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/9HPP-QJD/roger-de-mainwaring-1182-1250
