2 CONT '''''C.P.''''' 25/1/81/20, number 99
2 CONT '''Link:''' [http://aalt.law.uh.edu/AALT7/CP25(1)/CP25_1_81_17-27/IMG_0179.htm Image of document at AALT]
2 CONT '''County:''' Herefordshire
2 CONT '''Place:''' Westminster.
2 CONT '''Date:''' The day after the Purification of the Blessed Mary, 17 Edward I [3 February 1289]
2 CONT '''Parties:''' John Giffard' of Brymesfeld', querent, and Richard de Emneberwe, deforciant
2 CONT '''Property:''' The manors of Monynton' and Dylewe
2 CONT '''Action:''' Plea of covenant
2 CONT '''Agreement:''' John has acknowledged the manors to be the right of Richard.<br>
2 CONT '''For this:''' Richard has granted to John the manors and the advowson of the church of Monynton', to hold to John, of the chief lords for the life of John. And after the decease of John the manors and advowson shall remain to ''
2 CONC 'Nicholas de Audeleye and Katherine, his wife''', and the heirs begotten by Nicholas on the body of Katherine, to hold of the chief lords for ever. In default of such heirs, remainder to the right heirs of John.<br>
2 CONT Source: [http://www.medievalgenealogy.org.uk/fines/abstracts/CP_25_1_81_20.shtml#99 Abstracts of Feet of Fines]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Medlands ''(6 Jun 2024)'': [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#NicholasAudleydied1299 English Lords A–C]
2 CONT * 5. '''NICHOLAS''' de Audley (before 1258-28 Aug 1299). The Book of Lacock names “''Guillelmum de Audele…Nich’um de Audele''” as the children of “''Jacobus de Audele''” and his wife Ela, adding that William was drowned “''apud Sn
2 CONC owdoun in guerra Walliæ''”[33]. Inquisitions after a writ dated 25 Dec "11 Edw I" following the death of "''William de Auditheleye.''..” name “Nicholas his brother is his next heir and of full age...Ela his mother...Lucy late the 
2 CONC wife of Henry de Audethele”[34].  
2 CONT * '''m''' (1299 or before) '''CATHERINE Giffard''', daughter of JOHN Giffard Lord Giffard of Brimpsfield & his [first/second] wife Matilda de Clifford (1272-after 1322). The Book of Lacock names “''Catharinam filiam Johannis Giffa
2 CONC rd''” as wife of “''Nich’um de Audele''”, son of “''Jacobus de Audele''”[35]. Inquisitions following a writ dated 12 Feb "1 Edw III", after the death of "''John Giffard…of Brimmesfeld''…", record that John "married Maud de Longesp
2 CONC eye, of whom he begat Katherine de Audele, afterwards espoused to Nicholas de Audele…"[36]. She became a nun at Ledbury[37].  \
2 CONT * '''Nicholas & his wife had four children:'''
2 CONT ** a) '''THOMAS''' Audley (1288-[8 Jul/14 Dec] 1307, bur Langley Abbey, Norfolk). ... &c.
2 CONT ** b) '''NICHOLAS''' Audley (11 Nov 1289-1316 before 6 Dec). ... &c.
2 CONT ** c) '''ALICE''' (-after 1343). ... &c.
2 CONT ** d) ELA de Audley. ... &c.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Nicholas de Aldithley1
2 CONT * b. before 1258, d. 28 August 1299
2 CONT * Father	James de Aldithley, Justiciar of Ireland2,3 b. circa 1220, d. circa 11 June 1272
2 CONT * Mother	Ela Longespee 3 b. 1228, d. before 22 November 1299
2 CONT * Wife Catherine Giffard
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas de Aldithley was a witness where Nicholas, 1st Lord Audley second son and eventual representative of Nicholas de Aldithely, who was son of James de Aldithley, one of the Lords-Marcher, and an active adherent of Henry III 
2 CONC in his contests with the Barons, whose father, Henry de Aldithley, built the castle of Heleigh, and founded Hulton Abbey in 1223.4 Nicholas de Aldithley was born before 1258. 4th son.3 He was the son of James de Aldithley, Justici
2 CONC ar of Ireland and Ela Longespee.2,3 Nicholas de Aldithley married Catherine Giffard, daughter of John, Lord Giffard of Brimsfield and Maud de Clifford, before 1287.3 Nicholas de Aldithley was summoned to attend the King at Salisbu
2 CONC ry, but such summons cannot be considered as a regular writ of summons to Parliament, on 26 January 1296/97 at 25 Edward I.3 The forces of Edward I defeat a Scottish army under William Wallace. On 22 July 1298 at the Battle of Fal
2 CONC kirk, Scotland.5 Arms: Gules fretty or.6 He fought for King Edward I in the victory over the Scots led by William Wallace on 22 July 1298 at the Battle of Falkirk, Scotland. 1st Lord Audley of Heleigh before 1299.7 He died on 28 A
2 CONC ugust 1299.2,3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse:''' Catherine Giffard b. circa 1267, d. after 1322
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children
2 CONT 1. Thomas de Aldithley b. c 1288, d. 13078
2 CONT 2. Nicholas, 1st Lord Audley+ b. 11 Nov 1289, d. 13192
2 CONT 3. Ela, married 1) Owen de la Pole 2) James de Perers 3) Peter Corbet
2 CONT
