2 CONT >4. '''JOAN''' (-after 13 May 1264). King Henry III granted “the wardship of the lands and heirs of John son of Robert de Bello Campo, a minor deceased, who married Joan daughter of the said James, who is near her time or has alre
2 CONC ady given birth to an heir” 13 May 1264[31].
2 CONT >'''m''' JOHN de Beauchamp, son of ROBERT de Beauchamp & his wife Alice --- ([after 1244?]-before 13 May 1264). King Henry III granted “the wardship of the lands and heirs of Robert de Bello Campo tenant in chief, saving to Alice 
2 CONC late his wife her dower” 25 Oct 1263[32].
2 CONT
