1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Alice de Mohun
2 CONT * Birth: Abt 1228, Dunster, Williton, Somerset, England
2 CONT * Death: before 1284, Hatch Beauchamp, Taunton Deane Borough, Somerset, England
2 CONT * Burial: St Mary The Virgin Churchyard, Stoke-sub-Hamdon, South Somerset District, Somerset, England
2 CONT * Memorial ID 244220027
2 CONT * Daughter of Reginald de Mohun II, Baron De Mohun and Hawise Fitz Geoffrey 
2 CONT * Wife of  William de Clinton
2 CONT * Wife of Robert V de Beauchamp, Lord of Hache - adult by 1244, alive in 1262/3, yet dead by 1265/6
2 CONT * Mistress of James Audley 
2 CONT * Mother of Sir John de Beauchamp, I; Mary de Beauchamp; Alice de Beauchamp, Sir Humphrey de Beauchamp, and James Audley 
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: Robert IV de Beauchamp
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (1) as a young child, William de Clinton, the younger, who d. by 1237; married (2) by 1246 Robert de Beauchamp, IV, an adult in 1244, who was living in 1262-3, dead 1265-6, Lord of Hatch, Somerset, Justice in Eyre for the 
2 CONC Western Counties. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Beauchamp married Alice de Mohun, daughter of Sir Reynold de Mohun Knight and Hawise Fitz Geoffrey. (Alice de Mohun was born about 1228 in Dunster, Williton, Somerset, England and died before 1284 in Hatch Beachamp, Some
2 CONC rset, England.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Alice de Beauchamp+
2 CONT # Mary de Beauchamp
2 CONT # John de Beauchamp of Hatch Beauchamp, Somerset+
2 CONT # Sir Humphrey de Beauchamp of Ryme
2 CONT # Robert de Beauchamp
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice de Mohun, daughter of Sir Reynold de Mohun and his wife Hawise Fitz Geoffrey, married as a young child, her first husband, William de Clinton, the younger. Alice married, as her second husband, Robert (V) de Beauchamp, who w
2 CONC as an adult by 1244, alive in 1262/3, yet dead by 1265/6. Robert de Beauchamp was the Lord of Hatch, Somerset, Justice in Eyre for the Western Counties and son of Robert (IV) de Beauchamp, styled Robert fitz Simon, Lord of Hatch, 
2 CONC somerset, by his wife named Juliana, daughter of the widow, Alice Coleville.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America before 1700, 8th Edition, 246B:29
2 CONT
