4 CONT I am familiar with the database. But it utilizes information, from various genealogists and genealogy literature, some of which is accurate and accurately documented as well as, otherwise (secondarily) sourced, but also, some of w
4 CONC hich has, over the years, been exposed as here- say and "Colored genealogy, favoring a tie to promote a Family to the high society.". etc.
4 CONT
4 CONT One example, I have 2 (10th and 11th Great Grandfathers): The first is John Grosvenor, Sr. Gateway ancestor. The second is Thomas Whitney, "Sir". Well, The Millennium File does have a listing for them, the various research groups 
4 CONC dedicated to locating information, each for decades, now, for  for each respective Names, has refuted either the source, (with sources, confessions and/or for the grounds of the refutation) or presented their grounds and backround
4 CONC , for the dismissal of said "given source", through logical and deductive thought.
4 CONT Therefore, it is still not known, with any form of certainty, that the parents listed for both, are truly and 100%, they are theories and speculation, also, with multiple sourced Lineage Sites or Liturature... etc. 
4 CONT
4 CONT Here is, just for an example on what I am trying to imply, a Commentary on what is included in the millennium file and how one should approach, the information, therin.
4 CONT
4 CONT "NEXT STEP: Follow up on each and every name, date & place.  Find your own sources and confirm that what is given here is true.  Just because another researcher has made this entry, does not make it a fact.  Because there are no s
4 CONC pecific sources from the researchers for these entries, we have to find our own.  But...what a great place to start!
4 CONT I'm off to follow some leads.
4 CONT Until next time,
4 CONT Michigan Girl﻿"
4 CONT
