4 CONT  https://www.geni.com/people/John-Grosvenor/6000000011802490495
3 NOTE https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Whitney/6000000002630207001
3 NOTE Awesome, thank you!! 🤗
4 CONT If you locate anything on Thomas Whitney, Lambeth am Marsh, London or John Grosvenor, Sr. i's appreciate it. My email addy is Walker2021 at Yahoo dot com
3 NOTE If you need any primary sources on a profile, I can look them up on my data base and send it over to you (if time permits) - just let me know.
3 NOTE Thank you, Jacqueline, for your rapid response! 
4 CONT
4 CONT I am familiar with the database. But it utilizes information, from various genealogists and genealogy literature, some of which is accurate and accurately documented as well as, otherwise (secondarily) sourced, but also, some of w
4 CONC hich has, over the years, been exposed as here- say and "Colored genealogy, favoring a tie to promote a Family to the high society.". etc.
4 CONT
4 CONT One example, I have 2 (10th and 11th Great Grandfathers): The first is John Grosvenor, Sr. Gateway ancestor. The second is Thomas Whitney, "Sir". Well, The Millennium File does have a listing for them, the various research groups 
4 CONC dedicated to locating information, each for decades, now, for  for each respective Names, has refuted either the source, (with sources, confessions and/or for the grounds of the refutation) or presented their grounds and backround
4 CONC , for the dismissal of said "given source", through logical and deductive thought.
4 CONT Therefore, it is still not known, with any form of certainty, that the parents listed for both, are truly and 100%, they are theories and speculation, also, with multiple sourced Lineage Sites or Liturature... etc. 
4 CONT
4 CONT Here is, just for an example on what I am trying to imply, a Commentary on what is included in the millennium file and how one should approach, the information, therin.
4 CONT
4 CONT "NEXT STEP: Follow up on each and every name, date & place.  Find your own sources and confirm that what is given here is true.  Just because another researcher has made this entry, does not make it a fact.  Because there are no s
4 CONC pecific sources from the researchers for these entries, we have to find our own.  But...what a great place to start!
4 CONT I'm off to follow some leads.
4 CONT Until next time,
4 CONT Michigan Girl﻿"
4 CONT
4 CONT xoxoxoxoTheresa Renée
4 CONT http://www.michiganfamilytrails.com/2013/02/millenium-file-on-ancestry.html
4 CONT ﻿
3 NOTE This is Geni (not a GEDCOM) - and these profiles are historically sourced.
3 NOTE The Millenium file is completely sourced, it is a collection data based historical records attached to "family files" in an effort of the LDS to protect these historic records.  If an individual is found in the "Millenium" file - 
4 CONC this means that is it a historic profile that has attached historic documentation.  It can be used as a verification - ususally the GEDCOMS have the attached records, ie, census, court, birth, marriage, etc.  You may have to go to
4 CONC  the LDS data base and search the file.  
4 CONT "The Millennium File is a database created by the Institute of Family Research to track the records of its clients and the results of its professional research. It contains more than 880,000 linked family records, with lineages fr
4 CONC om throughout the world, including colonial America, the British Isles, Switzerland, and Germany. Many of these lineages extend back to nobility and renowned historical figures. In fact, one of the things the Millennium File focus
4 CONC es on is linking to European nobility and royalty. "
3 NOTE Unfortunately, the Millenium File, is not a reliable source, as it is nothing more than, a compilation of listings of the many private family trees on Ancestry (dot) com. Though, I do understand, why it was added... as a "lead" or
4 CONC  "indicator", it cannot be in any way considered as verification, for anyone. 
