1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The eldest son,John Legh, of Booths, wedded Elizabeth, daughter and co-heir of Sir Richard de Sanbach. by whom he had an only daughter, Maud Legh, who m. Richard Radcljffe, of Ordeshall, and conveyed to him, as her
2 CONC  inheritance, a moiety of the manor of Mobberley. John Legh dying thus without male issue, the estate of Booths devolved upon his nephew John Legh, who thus became "of Booths."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Legh of Boothes is described as one of seven loyal Chesire men who Thomas Cholmondeley, Ralph Davenport, Adam Bostock, John Done of Utkinson, Thomas Holford, Thomas Beeston and seventy retainers (Chesire Bowman)  each, be
2 CONC came the bodyguard for King Richard  "guarding over him day and night with their battle axes, upon his return from a punitive expedition in Ireland in 1399, and before the Battle of Shrewesbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books?id=yOIHAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA232&lpg=PA232&dq=White+Heart+of+the+Cheshire+Guard&source=bl&ots=c7cDDkHgvj&sig=CAdKA3RCgZPfq9SpBD62-NdGnJs&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NFdgU5f1JoT88AGlmYC4CA&ved=0CGAQ6AEwBg#v=onepage&q=White
2 CONC %20Heart%20of%20the%20Cheshire%20Guard&f=false Nooks and corners of Lancashire and Cheshire] James Croston
2 CONT
