2 CONT *''''''     Matilda de Arderne married Robert de Legh, son of Robert de Legh and Sybil de Honford. Matilda de Arderne was born at of Aldford & Alvanley, Cheshire, England.
2 CONT *''''''Family Robert de Legh d. 9 Nov 1382 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **◦Sir Piers Legh+ d. 1 Aug 1400
2 CONT **◦Sir Robert Legh, Sheriff of Cheshire+ b. bt 1361 - 1362, d. Aug 1408
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S3297] Unknown author, Magna Charta Sureties, 1215 by F. L. Weis, p. 94.
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p391.htm#i11744
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *''''''Nooks and corners of Lancashire and Cheshire: A wayfarer's notes in the ... By James Croston Pg.295-358
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=KgsNAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA297&lpg=PA297&dq=Matilda+de+Arderne+Legh&source=bl&ots=pwMh6fdCn0&sig=pX7bZGFCtY563O3X2fzJ_DhuQrU&hl=en&ei=K1v9S5SkJ4qmM_C00N4H&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=9&ved=0CCoQ6A
2 CONC EwCDhQ#v=onepage&q=Matilda%20de%20Arderne%20Legh&f=false
2 CONT *''''''Robert Legh died on the 9th November, 1382, leaving by his wife MATILDA, DAUGHTER OF SIR JOHN ARDERNE, OF ALDFORD, KNIGHT, a son ROBERT, born at Roter-le-Hay, and baptised at Audlem on the 2nd March, 1361-2, and then aged 2
2 CONC 0; and two daughters-- MARGERY, who became the wife of THOMAS de DAVENPORT, of Henbury, and KATHERINE, who married REGINALD DOWNES.
2 CONT *<nowiki>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *''''''Full text of "History of the family of Wrottesley of Wrottesley, co. Stafford"
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00wrot/historyoffamilyo00wrot_djvu.txt
2 CONT *''''''History of the family of Wrottesley of Wrottesley, co. Stafford
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/historyoffamilyo00wrot
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00wrot#page/91/mode/1up
2 CONT *	Sir Hugh de Wrottesley, K.G., A.D. 1333 to A.D. 1381. 
2 CONT *   Sir Hugh de Wrottesley, who now succeeded to his inheritance, is shewn to be son of the last Sir William by the deeds above printed, a suit in Banco of Easter term 13 Ed. II, and another suit on the Staffordshire Assize Roll o
2 CONC f 13 Ed. III. He was born in the early part of the year 1314, but is found to be a Knight and in full possession of his estates in January 1334.  
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00wrot#page/142/mode/1up
2 CONT *   Shortly after the death of Mabel ap Rees, Sir Hugh had married for a third time. His choice on this occasion was Isabella, the daughter of Sir John Arderne of Aldford, co. Chester. Sir John was lord of Elford in Staffordshire,
2 CONC  but his principal estates lay in Cheshire, where he represented Bigod one of the great Chester feudatories of A.D. 1086, and held his lands by Barony.1  The father and mother of Isabella had both died in 1349, the year of the Gre
2 CONC at Pestilence, leaving two sons, Thomas and Walcheline, under age, and three daughters, ''''''Matilda'''''', Katherine and Isabella. Sir John also left a son, Peter, by a former wife, but under a special settlement made with the l
2 CONC icense of the King as Prince of Wales, the whole of the Aldford fee passed to Thomas, the son of his third wife, Ellen de Bulkeley. This Thomas was born during the lifetime of the second wife, and was clearly illegitimate. He firs
2 CONC t appears on the Cheshire Plea Kolls under the name of Thomas Ellensone, but he subsequently assumed the name of Arderne, and will appear in these pages as Sir Thomas de Arderne at a later date. The daughters of Sir John Arderne w
2 CONC ere born in wedlock, and the Arderne estates had been settled by a Fine on the two sons in succession and their issue in tail male, and failing such with remainder to the daughters and their issue.2  Walcheline, the younger brothe
2 CONC r of Thomas, died leaving no issue, and the male line of Sir Thomas failed after two generations. The attempts of the descendants of the daughters to make good their claim to the Arderne inheritance under this entail will be descr
2 CONC ibed later on. 
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00wrot#page/153/mode/1up
2 CONT *   On the 6 December 1380, license was granted to John Burdele (Boydell), Kt., and to Katherine, his wife, to alienate to Hugh de Wrottesleye, Kt., and to Isabella, his wife, and to their issue, a messuage and thirty acres of lan
2 CONC d in Budworth, in Le Frith, and on the following 14 December a writ to the Eschaetor of co. Chester directs him to deliver to Hugh de Wrottesleye that part of the land of Alina, formerly the wife of Thomas de Alvandelegh, which be
2 CONC longed to Isabella, wife of the said Hugh, and likewise the other part which belonged to Katherine, wife of John Burdele, Kt., and which had been sold by her and the said John, to Hugh and Isabella, and which lands had fallen to t
2 CONC he said Isabella and Katherine, as kinswomen and heirs of the said Alina.1  This is the latest appearance of Sir Hugh on any public document. 
2 CONT *	1 Calendar of Welsh and Cheshire Recoi'ds, printed. (Holls series). Kalherine had been previously married to Thomas de Mascy, and seems to have been the eldest sister, for in 1368 Thomas de Mascy and Katherine, his wife, ''''''R
2 CONC obert de Legh, the younger, and Matilda, his wife'''''', and Isabella, sister of ''''''Matilda'''''', sued Thomas de Venables, of Alvandelegh, for waste in Teverton, near Tarporley, which was of their inheritance. 
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''Ancestry of John Barber White and his descendants By Almira Larkin White *http://books.google.com/books?id=hY9bAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA202&lpg=PA202&dq=John+Arderne+1266&source=bl&ots=oHIxzpn7Da&sig=sBYsPz6sxPaz2vB8QofdrcIci3Y&hl=en&
2 CONC ei=TL6uTLa5IoWcsQPGhPmDDA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0CCIQ6AEwBTgU#v=onepage&q=John%20Arderne%201266&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 201
2 CONT *   1. Agnes de Arden qy. descended from Turketill de Eardene, Co., Warwick
2 CONT **   2. Alexander de Arden
2 CONT ***   3. Eustace de Arden granter of Watford church to Abbey of St. James, Northampton; b. about 1140.
2 CONT ****   4. Eustace de Arden als. do Watford, d. 1213.
2 CONT ****Pg. 202
2 CONT *****   5. Sir John de Arden als. Arderne, knight grants lands to his brother Eustace in Watford, after 1209, named as his knight by Ranulph 3, earl of Chester and grantee from him of Aldford fee before 1229; m. Margaret dau. and 
2 CONC heir of Richard de Aldford.
2 CONT ******   6. Sir Walkelyn de Arderne, knight, Justice of Chester, d. about 1265; m. his second cousin Agnes, dau. and heir of Philip de Orreby.
2 CONT *******   7. Sir Peter de Arderne, knight, lord of Alvanley and Aldford 1265; m. Margaret ___.
2 CONT ********   8. Sir John de Arderne, knight, b. 1266; m. Margaret, dau. of Griffith ap Madog, lord of Bromfield, and Prince of Powis Valdog, contracted between 1267 and 1270. He died about 1308; qy. living 8 Edward II, a widow.
2 CONT *********   9.Sir John de Arderne of Aldford and Alvanley, knight, m. (1) Alice, dau. of Sir Hugh Venables; m. (2) Joan or Jane, dau. and co-heir of Richard de Stokeport, baron of Stokeport, and widow of Sir Nicholas de Eaton. He 
2 CONC m. (2) Ellen de Wasrneys previously concubine 1436. She d. between July 13, and Dec. 23, 1349.
2 CONT **********''''''   10. Matilda de Arderne, m. Robert de Legh, (4) 9 Lineage Lord of Adlyngton.
2 CONT *	16th LINEAGE.
