1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/De_Arderne-65
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of John Arderne and Ellena Wastneys.[1] His parents were married before 3 January, 1342, when John de Arden and Ellen his wife were granted a pardon,[2] so he was born before then as we was born prior to their marri
2 CONC age.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Prince of Wales Vs Margaret, Widow of John son of Thomas de Ardene
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/De_Arderne-65
2 CONT
2 CONT In 10 Henry IV [30 September, 1408-29 September, 1409] at Chester, the prince of Wales, as earl of Chester, versus Margaret formerly wife of John, son of Thomas de Ardene, in a suit for the right to the manors of Aldford, Alderdel
2 CONC egh and Echeles, the advowsons of the churches of Aldford and Alderdelegh, and a rent of ten marks from the manor of Upton in Wyrehale. The pleadings show the following descent:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT John de Ardene, seised of the manors, advowsons and rent, in the reign of Edward III [1327-1377], married Elena, and had two sons and two daughters:
2 CONT #Thomas, who had:
2 CONT ##John de Ardene, living 8 Henry IV [30 September, 1406-29 September, 1407], but dead by 10 Henry IV, married Margaret, the plaintiff;
2 CONT #'''Walkeline, who died with no surviving children;'''
2 CONT #Matilda, who was married to Robert, son of Robert de Legh, and had:
2 CONT ##Robert de Legh, Kt, living 10 Henry IV;
2 CONT #Isabella, who was married to Hugh de Wrotteslegh, and they had:
2 CONT ##John de Wrotteslegh, who had:
2 CONT ##Hugh de Wrotteslegh, living in 10 Henry IV.
2 CONT The pleadings also state that Thomas and Walkeline were illegitimate, being styled sons of Elena only— and that John de Ardene, the husband of Elena, had left no male heir of his body. Margaret claimed under a settlement made by h
2 CONC er husband in 8 Henry IV [30 September 1406-29 September 1407], a licence of alienation having been obtained from the prince of Wales, as earl of Chester, and a verdict was given in her favour. Under a previous settlement of 21 Ed
2 CONC ward III [25 January, 1347-24 January, 1348], also made with the licence of the prince of Wales, as earl of Chester, the same properties had been settled on John de Ardene and Elena, his wife, for their lives, with remainder to Th
2 CONC omas, son of Elena, and their heirs male of his body, with remainder to Walcheline, brother of Thomas, and the heirs male of his body, and failing such, to the heirs of the bodies of John and Elena. Under the first settlement, the
2 CONC  Arderne estates would have been divided between Robert de Legh and Hugh de Wrottesley.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: Major-General The Hon G Wrottesley, ed, Pedigrees from the Plea Rolls Collected from the Pleadings in the Various Courts of Law AD 1200 to 1500 from the Original Rolls (1905), 256. e-book Internet Archive (https://archive
2 CONC .org/details/pedigreesfromple00wrotrich/page/256/mode/1up : accessed 11 June, 2022. [Chester Pleas: 10. Hen. 4. m. 9].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Collins's peerage of England;: genealogical, biographical, and ..., Volume 9 By Arthur Collins Pg.143 < [http://books.google.com/books?id=PfwUAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA143&lpg=PA143&dq=Walkelin+Arderne&source=bl&ots=ZzhRBw76oB&sig=-Lft-da1msy
2 CONC 1P6aiZtfXvhnzcR8&hl=en&ei=wCGtTO7SCpCosAOz56GmDA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CCEQ6AEwBDgK#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Johannes de Arderne, Lord of Watheford, 12 Henry III. was father of
2 CONT **Walkeline de Arderne, Chief Justice of Chester, Lord of Aldford, Alderley, and Wever, Jure Uxoris, who married the heiress of Oreby, and had issue,
2 CONT ***  Sir Peter de Arderne, Knt. who, by Margaret his wife, had
2 CONT **** Sir John de Arderne, Lord of Aldford, from 3 to 33 Edward I. who, by Margaret, was father of
2 CONT *****  A younger son, Peter, of Audley, who died 1346, and
2 CONT ******Sir John Arderne, Knt. son and heir, 8 Edward III. who, by Elen Daughter of William de Wasteneys, had three sons,
2 CONT *******  First, '''Walkeline''' '''de Arderne'''
2 CONT *******Second, Sir John, of whom presently. [no - son of 1st wife] 
2 CONT *******  Third, Sir Thomas de Arderne, of Aldford, 35 Edward III. whose great grand-daughter and heiress married Thomas Stanley, second son to Stanley, of Lathom.
2 CONT
