1 OCCU Lord Boteler, 2nd Chief Butler of Ireland, Lord Justice of Ireland, 4th Chief Butler of Ireland, Chief Butler of Ireland, Baron, Gentleman, 2nd Chief of Ireland, Lord Justice
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://wappenwiki.org/index.php/House_Boteler_of_Wem
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theobald_le_Botiller,_2nd_Chief_Butler_of_Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald le Botiller, also known as Theobald Boteler, Theobald Butler, 2nd Baron Butler (January, 1200 – July 19, 1230) was the son of Theobald Walter, 1st Baron Butler and Maud le Vavasour. He was born in Norfolk, England. He had
2 CONC  livery of his lands on 2 July 1221.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Firstly, Theobald married Joan de Mareis (or Marisco) sometime between 1220 and 1224. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Theobald Butler, 3rd Chief Butler of Ireland (c.1224-1248). This son later married Margery de Burgh, daughter of Richard Mor de Burgh and Egidia de Lacy, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Maud Butler, who married John FitzAlan, 6th Earl of Arundel. She was the mother of John FitzAlan, 7th Earl of Arundel.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his first wife, Theobald remained a widower. Henry III of England requested the marriage of Theobald to Rohese de Verdon, daughter of Nicholas de Verdon of Alton, Staffordshire and Joan de Lacy. The agreement to
2 CONC  marry occurred on 4 September 1225. The marriage is presumed to have shortly followed. This was the second marriage for both Theobald and Rohese.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * John de Verdon, Lord of Westmeath (b.1226)
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Career
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald was summoned cum equis et armis (Latin: "with horse and arms") to attend the King into Brittany, as "Theobaldus Pincerna" on 26 October 1229. He died on 19 July 1230 in Poitou, France, at the age of 30 and was buried in t
2 CONC he Abbey of Arklow, County Wicklow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. George Edward Cokayne. The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct, or Dormant, I-XIII (Thrupp, Stroud, Gloucestershire, GL5 2BU: Sutton Publishing Limited, 2000
2 CONC ), II:448.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Ibid., II:447.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Some corrections and additions to The Complete Peerage, http://www.medievalgenealogy.org.uk/, II:448.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis, Lines: 70A-29, 149-29
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. FMG on the Botiller/Butler descendants of Hervey Walter or FitzWalter
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald le Botiller, also known as Theobald Boteler, Theobald Butler, was 2nd Baron Butler. He had livery of his lands on 2 July 1221.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald first married Joan de Mareis (or Marais) sometime between 1220 and 1224 After her death, Theobald remained a widower. King Henry III of England requested the marriage of Theobald to Rohese de Verdon, daughter of Nicholas 
2 CONC de Verdon of Alton, Staffordshire and Joan de Lacy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald was summoned cum equis et armis (Latin: "with horse and arms") to attend the King into Brittany, as "Theobaldus Pincerna" on 26 October 1229. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at the age of 30.
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theobald_le_Botiller for more information.
2 CONT
