1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Fulk FitzWarin (d. 1250)  married secondly to '''Clarice de Auberville''', daughter and heiress of Robert de Auberville of Iden and Iham, Sussex (a great-grandson of Ranulf de Glanvill) by his wife Clarice de Gestling.[32][33][34]
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT The progeny from this second marriage appears to have been a single surviving daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mabel FitzWarin (−1297), who married 1stly William de Crevequer (no issue), and 2ndly John de Tregoz, Lord Tregoz (d. before 6 Sept 1300), by whom she had two daughters and coheirs, Clarice and Sybil[28][31]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Auberville-3
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarice d'Auberville [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fulk married secondly to Clarice de Auberville, daughter and heiress of Robert de Auberville of Iden and Iham, Sussex (a great-grandson of Ranulf de Glanvill) by his wife Clarice de Gestling.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Fouke" married "dame Clarice de Auberville" after the death of his first wife.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fulk FitzWarin and Clarice his wife (“Fulco fil Warini et Claric ux eius”), are recorded in a lawsuit c. Oct 1250, in Kent, England.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT "dame Clarice" died and was buried ("a la Novele Abbeye"), one year before the death of her husband.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT # Entered by Travis Wagner, Oct 24, 2011
2 CONT # Douglas Richardson, C.P. Addition
2 CONT # The Legend of Fulk Fitz Warin, p. 410
2 CONT # Fine Rolls, Vol. II (1836), 34 Hen III, p. 89
2 CONT # The Legend of Fulk Fitz Warin, p. 414
2 CONT # Medieval Lands - Fulk III http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3D-K.htm#FulkFitzWarinIIIdied1250
2 CONT # Douglas Richardson, "C.P. Addition: Clarice de Auberville, wife of Sir Fulk Fitz Warin"
