1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Mabel FitzWarin
2 CONT * Last Edited	4 Apr 2020
2 CONT * F, #15398
2 CONT * b. Say  1232 / 1245
2 CONT *  d. Before  24 May 1297
2 CONT * Father	Sir Fulk II FitzWarin2,3 b. c 1185
2 CONT * Mother	Clarice d' Auberville3 b. c 1205
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel FitzWarin was born circa 1232 at of Whittington, Shropshire, England.3 She married William de Crevequer, son of Hamo de Crevecoeur and Maud d' Avranches, circa 1254.3 Mabel FitzWarin married Sir John de Tregoz, Lord of Trego
2 CONC z & Ewyas Harold, son of Sir Robert II de Tregoz and Juliane de Cantelowe, before 6 April 1263; They had 1 son (John) & 2 daughters (Clarice, wife of Sir Roger la Warre; & Sibyl, wife of Sir William de Grandison, 1st Lord Grandiso
2 CONC n).2,3 Mabel FitzWarin died circa 24 May 1297.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT Sir John de Tregoz, Lord of Tregoz & Ewyas Harold b. c 1242, d. 21 Aug 1300
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT # Clarissa de Tregoz+3 b. c 1260, d. b 28 Aug 1300.  Married  in or before Sep. 1276 Roger la Warr.  
2 CONT # Sibella de Tregoz+2,3 b. c 1272, d. 21 Oct 1334.  Married as ''his first wife'', William de Grandison, 1st Lord Grandison, sometime before 1285. Sibyl died 21 Oct 1334, and was buried in Dore Abbey.  (TCP)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel married Sir John Baron de Tregoz Knight, son of Robert Tregoz and Juliane de Cantelou 141.,160 (Sir John Baron de Tregoz Knight was born about 1232 in Ewyas Harold, Herefordshire, England, died before 6 Sep 1300 in Bristol, 
2 CONC Gloucestershire, England 141,160 and was buried in St. Augustine's, Bristol, Gloucestershire, England.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/FitzWarin-9
2 CONT
2 CONT See discussion on soc.gen.medieval < [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/LQOOvM9g1G0/m/AdHWW8w_UToJJ%7C here] >  (the 18 December, 2005 post at 7:29 PM by John P Ravilious) and this short post < [https://groups.g
2 CONC oogle.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/Olmr3L7M13s/m/FpEvUICc0DAJ here] >.
2 CONT
2 CONT They quote Richardson citing documents as:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Robert [de Auberville], with Hugh his brother, he witnessed a charter of John de Eu to the Monks of Robertsbridge. (Mon. Ang. II.921a n 10).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord of Iden and Isham, Sussex, jure uxoris, of which he had livery, 21st July 1205 (Cl. 7 Joh. m 20). Fought in Ireland, 1210 (Rot. de Prestito 12 John). He attended the king at the siege of Bytham Castle
2 CONT
2 CONT 1221 (Cl. 5 Hen. 3. m 15d). Constable of Hastings Castle, 8th Aug.
2 CONT 1225 (Cl. 9 Hen. 3. m 9). Warden of the Sea ports from Portsmouth to Sandwich, 17th March 1228 (Pat. 12 Hen. 3. m 5). He died before 18th March 1230, when John de Gatesden was appointed Constable of Hastings in his place (Pat. 14 
2 CONC Hen. 3. m 5). He married Clarice. They had issue, Clarice de Auberville, daughter and heir, of Iden and Isham. She married Fulk Fitz Warine (III) as his 2nd wife. They were both living 1250 (Rot. Fin. 34 Hen. 3. m 2). They had iss
2 CONC ue, Mabel Fitz Warin, daughter and heiress to her mother. She married as his 1st wife, John Lord Tregoz, of Ewyas, etc." [Douglas Richardson, extract from Gerald Paget, Baronage of England (1957), 11: 1-2].
2 CONT
2 CONT and concerning proof of her parentage, Douglas Richardson wrote: 'For evidence that Mabel Fitz Warin was heiress of her mother, Clarice de Auberville, I find that Mabel and her husband, Sir John Tregoz, were granted free warren of
2 CONC  Iden and I[s]ham, Sussex 11 June 1271. ' [Douglas Richardson, cites Moor, Knights of Edward I 5 (H.S.P. 84) (1932)]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p513.htm#i15398 cites 
2 CONT ## [S2699] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. IV, p. 141, Vol. VI, p. 62, Vol. XII/2, p. 21; Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 113.
2 CONT ## [S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. III, p. 97.
2 CONT ## [S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. V, p. 185-186.
2 CONT # https://cybergata.com/roots/7612.htm cites
2 CONT ##Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists, 8th Edition, Frederick Lewis Weis, additions, Walter Lee Shippard Jr., 2004, 255A:29-30, Sir John de Tregoz, an adult by 1261, died shortly before 6 Sep 1300, was the son of Robert 
2 CONC II de Tregoz and Juliane de Dammartin. Sir John married as his first wife, Mabel Fitz Warin, who was the widow of William de Crevequer, and the daughter of Sir Fulk Fitz Warin of Whittington, county of Salop. 160
2 CONT # William de Crevequer  is listed as the 1st spouse of Mabel FitzWarin.
2 CONT # https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/engunttz.htm#JohnTresgozdied1300
