2 CONT Death date-After 1321 Living- 1293-1321-(Bartrum-Welsh Genealogies 300-1400-Vol.2-Page 53) Living.-He is mentioned and assessed in a tax roll 1293/4 as Madoc ab Davydd Hendwr, Edemion. Living- The bailiwick of commote of Penllyn c
2 CONC ommitted to him, 15 Edward 11,(Lloyd, History of the Princes, the Lords Marcher and the Ancient Nobility of Powys Fadog,, Vol 6,page 17.) Residence- Hen'dwr (Bartrum-Welsh Genealogies, 300-1400, vol. 2, page 57) Property-Baron of 
2 CONC Hendwr. (Griffith, Pedigrees of Anglesey and Canarvonshire Families, page 26.) Property- Lord of Hendwr.(Lloyd, History of the Princes, the Lords Marcher and the Ancient Nobility of Powys Fadog,  vol 6, page 17.)
2 CONT
2 CONT REMARKS- Baron has the same signification here as a landed proprietor,and equivalent to Lord in other Welsh pedigrees. (Dynn - Heraldic Visitations of Wales, vol 2,page 340.)
2 CONT
2 CONT KINSHIP CONFLICT-Dynns Heraldic Visitations of Wales, vol 2, page 112, inserts an extra generation between Madog and Iowerth called Dafydd.
2 CONT
2 CONT KINSHIP CONFLICT-Griffiths Pedigrees of Anglesey and Carnarvonshire Families , gives him the wrong father.
2 CONT
2 CONT KINSHIP CONFLICT-Lloyds, History of the Princes etc., vol 6, page 17,makes him a son of Dafydd ap Gruffudd ab Owain "Brogyntyn"
2 CONT
2 CONT KINSHIP CONFLICT-Griffith's Pedigrees of Anglesey etc, page 223, makes him the father of his 2nd. great-granddaughters, Anharad, Margred and Lleucu. Source: Welsh Medievel Database primarily of Nobility and Gentry.
