2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Archaeologia cambrensis    By John Skinner, Cambrian Archaeological Association
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=0gtPAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA269&lpg=PA269&dq=Gruffydd+Nannau&source=bl&ots=B-9B-R5d5m&sig=AWXnRV_-GEG1SZLC5t35t0J0Jbw&hl=en&ei=MgmfToqNH_LPiALS-8GDCg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=9&ved=0CE0Q6AEwCA#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Gruffydd%20Nannau&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 269
2 CONT **CHART
2 CONT *Gruffydd Nannau, lord of Nannau, ab Howel ab Davydd ab '''Meurig Vychan ab Howel Sele''', descended from Cadwgan ab Bleddyn ab Cynvyn, Prince of Powys = Jane, da of Humphrey ab Howel ab Ieuan ab Einion of Ynys Maengwyn, descended
2 CONC  from Osbwrn Wyddel
2 CONT **      Hugh Nannau of Nannau, Esq. = Annest, d. of Rhys Vaughan of Cors y Gedol, Esq.
2 CONT ***	Jane, second of five daughters of Hugh Nannau, Esq. = 1st Elisua Lloyd of Rhiwaedog, ab William, Esq., o.s.p. = 2ndly, Lewis Gwyn of Dolau Gwyn, Esq. (His first wife) ch: 1. Jane Gwyn; 2. Ann, prima ux. of Lewis Lloyde of Rhiw
2 CONC aedog, Esq., s.p..
2 CONT ****	      1. Jane Gwyn, h. of Dolau Gwyn = 2nd son Gruffydd Nannau (son of Gruffydd Nannau & Ellen, d. of John ab Cadwaladr)
2 CONT ***	1. Gruffydd Nannau of Nannau, Esq., n. 1568, M.P. for Meirionydd, 1593 = Ellen, d. of John ab Cadwaladr of Rhiwlas in Penllyn, Esq. ch: eldest son Hugh Nannau of Nan.; 2nd son Gruffydd Nannau
2 CONT ****	      eldest son Hugh Nannau of Nannau, Esq., n. 22 Oct. 1588; Sheriff, 1627; ob. 1647-8 = Ann, d. of Gruffydd Vaughan of Cors Gedol, Esq.
2 CONT ****	      2nd son Gruffydd Nannau = 1. Jane Gwyn, of Dolau Gwyn (d. of Lewis Gwyn & Jane Nannau)
2 CONT ***	2. Richard Nannau, parson of Llangelynin
2 CONT ***	3. Edward Nannau, ancestor of the Nanneys of Maes y Pandy, co. Mer. = Elizabeth, d. of Lewis Gwyn of Dolau Gwyn, Esq.
2 CONT ***	4. Robert, a merchant in London, = Joyce, d of Pyrs ___ ____________________
2 CONT *'''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA297&lpg=PA297&dq=Gruffydd+Nannau&source=bl&ots=2Exfur4D9Q&sig=O5SkEltmxxkM8ikct6XSQ58BohQ&hl=en&ei=SRGfTtnKOunfiALBrqVl&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0CDgQ6AEwBTgo#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Nannau&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 296
2 CONT *15. JANE FERCH HUMPHREY AP HYWEL, married (as his 2nd wife) GRUFFUDD AP HYWEL, of Nannau, son of Hywell ap Dafydd ap '''Meurig''' Fychan, of Nannau, by his 1st wife, Elen daughter of Robert Salesbury, of Llanrwst. They had two so
2 CONC ns, Hugh and John, and three daughters, Margaret (wife of William ap Tudor), Elizabeth, and Anne. He married (1st) ELEN FERCH TUDUT FYCHAN. He was living 1541-2.
2 CONT **Pg. 297
2 CONT **16. JOHN NANNAU alias JOHN AP GRUFFUDD, of Dyffydan (in Dolgelly), Merionethshire. He married ELSBETH FERCH DAFYDD LLWYD, of Trawvynydd. They had one son, Lewis, and two daughters, Ellen and Jane. He held land in the township of
2 CONC  Dyffrydan in Dolgelly, Merionethshire.
2 CONT ***17. LEWIS AP JOHN AP GRUFFUDD, Gent., of Dyffrydan (in Dolgelly), Merionethshire. He married ELLEN FERCH HYWELL AP GRUFFUDD They had two sons, Rees and Owen. LEWIS AP JOHN AP GRUFFUDD was living 28 August 1654. _______________
2 CONT *'''Merion in the Welsh tract: With sketches of the townships of Haverford and ... By Thomas Allen Glenn
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=fmiqHA3Fe2oC&pg=PA217&lpg=PA217&dq=Gruffydd+Nannau&source=bl&ots=NSDHm-5cTv&sig=4ML8ep7ENOxupogJsVO6bR0lFjU&hl=en&ei=SRGfTtnKOunfiALBrqVl&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=8&ved=0CEEQ6AEwBzgo#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Gruffydd%20Nannau&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 218
2 CONT *XI. DAVID AP '''MEURIC''' VAUGHAN, of Nannau, who married Ellen, dau. Howell ap Rhys ap David ap Howell ap Gruffydd ap Owen ap Bleddyn, Lord of Dinmael ap Owain Brogyntyn, descended from the Princes of Powysland, and had:
2 CONT **XII. HOWELL AP DAVID, of Nannau. He appears in a roll of accounts for Merionethshire, ending Michaelmas, 2nd Henry VIII. (1510), as surety for one William ap Jenkin ap Ierworth, "farmer," of the mills of Llanvachreth and Llanegr
2 CONC yn. He married Ellen, dau. of Robert Salsbury, of Llan-Rwst, ap Thomas Salsbury hen (liv. 1451), ap Sir Henry Salsbury, Knight of the Holy Sepulchre (died about 1399), ap Rawling Salsbury ap William Salsbury, M.P. 1322, and had:
2 CONT ***XIII. GRIFFITH AP HOWELL, of Nannau, and Lord there-of; living 33d Henry VIII. (1541-2). Hugh Nannau, the eldest son, signed the pedigree as head of the family, 24 July 1588. (Dwnn II, p. 266.) He married Jane, dau. Humphrey ap
2 CONC  Howell ap Ievan, of Yns y Maen Gwyn. Her mother was Anne, dau. of Sir Richard Herbert, Knight of Coldbrook. [Jane was a lineal descendant of Henry IV., King of England,] and had:
2 CONT ****continues with CHART
2 CONT ****HUGH, Lord of Nannau, m. Annest, dau. Rhys Vaughan, of Cors y Gedol, living 1588.
2 CONT ****JOHN Nannau, alias John ap Griffith, of Nannau. He held certain lands in township of Dyffreydan in Dolgelly Parish, and else-where. = ELIZABETH, dau. David Lloyd, of Trawsfynedd.
2 CONT *****LEWIS AP JOHN GRIFFITH, of Dyffrydan, etc. He was living 28 Augt., 1654, being then described as holding the lands of Dewisbren and Debafeder. = ELLEN, dau. Howell ap Griffith. (cont. with ch:)
2 CONT *****ELLEN born prior 1588.
2 CONT *****JANE born prior 1588.
2 CONT ****MARGARET m. William ap Tudor, ap Gruffyd ap Ednyfed of Egryn Abbey.
2 CONT ****ELIZABETH Anne. _____________________
2 CONT *'''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=p_yzpuWi4sgC&pg=PA286&lpg=PA286&dq=Gruffydd+Nannau&source=bl&ots=RRtQ2OT89c&sig=cPBatDAsKMNZ-1XbgUe7pDRmVJA&hl=en&ei=Kx2fTvnHCorTiAK16MFL&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=8&ved=0CEkQ6AEwBzg8#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Gruffydd%20Nannau&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 286
2 CONT *16. JANE FERCH HUMPHREY AP HYWEL, married (as his 2nd wife) GRUFFUDD AP HYWEL, of Nannau, son of Hywel ap Dafydd ap '''Meurig''' Fychan, of Nannau, by his 1st wife, Elen daughter of Robert Salesbury, of Llanrwst. They had two son
2 CONC s, Hugh and John, and three daughters, Margaret (wife of William ap Tudor), Elizabeth, and Anne. He married (1st) ELEN FERCH TUDUT FYCHAN. He was living 1541-2.
2 CONT **Pg. 297
2 CONT **17. JOHN NANNAU alias JOHN AP GRUFFUDD, of Dyffydan (in Dolgelly), Merionethshire. He married ELSBETH FERCH DAFYDD LLWYD, of Trawvynydd. They had one son, Lewis, and two daughters, Ellen and Jane. He held land in the township of
2 CONC  Dyffrydan in Dolgelly, Merionethshire.
2 CONT ***18. LEWIS AP JOHN AP GRUFFUDD, Gent., of Dyffrydan (in Dolgelly), Merionethshire. He married ELLIN FERCH HYWEL AP GRUFFUDD They had two sons, Rees and Owen. LEWIS AP JOHN AP GRUFFUDD was living 28 August 1654. _________________
