2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *''''''Merion in the Welsh tract: With sketches of the townships of Haverford and ...    By Thomas Allen Glenn
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=fmiqHA3Fe2oC&pg=PA217&lpg=PA217&dq=Gruffydd+Nannau&source=bl&ots=NSDHm-5cTv&sig=4ML8ep7ENOxupogJsVO6bR0lFjU&hl=en&ei=SRGfTtnKOunfiALBrqVl&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=8&ved=0CEEQ6AEwBzgo#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Gruffydd%20Nannau&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 218
2 CONT *   XI. DAVID AP MEURIC VAUGHAN, of Nannau, who married Ellen, dau. ''''''Howell ap Rhys'''''' ap David ap Howell ap Gruffydd ap Owen ap Bleddyn, Lord of Dinmael ap Owain Brogyntyn, descended from the Princes of Powysland, and had
2 CONC :
2 CONT **   XII. HOWELL AP DAVID, of Nannau. He appears in a roll of accounts for Merionethshire, ending Michaelmas, 2nd Henry VIII. (1510), as surety for one William ap Jenkin ap Ierworth, "farmer," of the mills of Llanvachreth and Llan
2 CONC egryn. He married Ellen, dau. of Robert Salsbury, of Llan-Rwst, ap Thomas Salsbury hen (liv. 1451), ap Sir Henry Salsbury, Knight of the Holy Sepulchre (died about 1399), ap Rawling Salsbury ap William Salsbury, M.P. 1322, and had
2 CONC :
2 CONT ***   XIII. GRIFFITH AP HOWELL, of Nannau, and Lord there-of; living 33d Henry VIII. (1541-2). Hugh Nannau, the eldest son, signed the pedigree as head of the family, 24 July 1588. (Dwnn II, p. 266.) He married Jane, dau. Humphrey
2 CONC  ap Howell ap Ievan, of Yns y Maen Gwyn. Her mother was Anne, dau. of Sir Richard Herbert, Knight of Coldbrook. [Jane was a lineal descendant of Henry IV., King of England,] and had:
2 CONT ****continues with CHART
2 CONT ****	HUGH, Lord of Nannau, m. Annest, dau. Rhys Vaughan, of Cors y Gedol, living 1588.
2 CONT ****	JOHN Nannau, alias John ap Griffith, of Nannau. He held certain lands in township of Dyffreydan in Dolgelly Parish, and else-where. = ELIZABETH, dau. David Lloyd, of Trawsfynedd.
2 CONT *****	      LEWIS AP JOHN GRIFFITH, of Dyffrydan, etc. He was living 28 Augt., 1654, being then described as holding the lands of Dewisbren and Debafeder. = ELLEN, dau. Howell ap Griffith. (cont. with ch:)
2 CONT *****	      ELLEN born prior 1588.
2 CONT *****	      JANE born prior 1588.
2 CONT ****	MARGARET m. William ap Tudor, ap Gruffyd ap Ednyfed of Egryn Abbey.
2 CONT ****	ELIZABETH
2 CONT ****	Anne.
2 CONT *_____________________
