1 NAME Robert /le Strange/ Lord of Wrockwardine
2 GIVN Robert
2 SURN le Strange
2 NSFX Lord of Wrockwardine
2 _MARNM le Strange
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1232
2 PLAC Hunstanton, Norfolk, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1276
2 PLAC Litcham, Norfolk, England
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE AUG 1276
1 OCCU Crusader in 1270
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Le Strange of Wrockwarden was younger son of John Le Strange III of Knockyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was younger brother of Roger, Baron Strange, of Ellesmere. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was about to go to the Holy Land in 1270/71.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was pardoned for cutting and selling a part of a wood, which had been given to him by his brother Hamon, at Chawton in 1272 in Hampshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He did homage for the manor, which his brother Hamon had given him by charter, of Wrockwardine in 1275 in Telford & Wrekin, England [George Edward Cokayne The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the 
2 CONC United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct, or Dormant, I-XIII (in 6) (Thrupp, Stroud, Gloucestershire, GL5 2BU: Sutton Publishing Limited, 2000), XII/1:341].
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in August 1276 in (probably) Litcham, Norfolk, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms: Gules crusily and two lions passant argent [Gerard J. Brault, editor, Aspilogia III: The Rolls of Arms, Edward I (1272-1307) (Woodbridge, Suffolk: The Boydell Press, 1997), E:194].
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT SHROPSHIRE DESCENT
2 CONT
2 CONT LE STRANGE
2 CONT
2 CONT LORDS AND BARONS OF BLAKEMERE  Robert le Strange
2 CONT  4th son of John III of Knokyn/Knockin
2 CONT   (d.c. Aug. 1276)
2 CONT  4th son John [III], inherited Wrockwardine, fought in the Crusades. ~1240, Robert born in Wales, s/o 121697006. Sir John le Strange III & 121697007. Lucia de Tregoz. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ~1245, Eleanor born in England, 2nd d/o §William de Albo de Monasterio, Lord of Whitchurch. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bef. 6/11/1260, Alianore coheir to her father. (S) CPRs. [The eldest sister Bertreya, of full age, kept herself in the castle. 4 sisters were coheirs.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1260-1, Robert’s father gave him half of the manor of Litcham, Norfolk; witnessed by his brothers Hamon and Roger, and his brother-in-law, Gruffud ap Gwenwynwyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1262-67, Robert’s brother John enfeoffed him with the manors of Rowton and Ellardine.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5/14/1264, Robert and his brothers at the battle of Lewes in support of the king. After the battle, Simon de Montfort ordered them exiled to Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8/4/1265, Robert fought at Evesham, serving in the barons revolt under Gilbert de Clare, Earl of Goucester, against Simon de Montfort, Earl of Leicester.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10/19/1265, Robert granted a capital messuage in London formerly belonging to John de Turri, enemy of the king. [His brothers also receiving similar properties.] (S) CPRs.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6/28/1266, The king granted Robert’s request for a pardon for Hugh Corbet for the death of Adam le Ventrer. (S) CPRs.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8/1/1267, Robert exchanged the manors of Rowton and Ellardine with Giles de Erdington acquiring the manors of Marbury, Cheshire; and Halehurst, Salop.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1269, Robert’s father died; his older brother John succeeding in Knokyn [who was married to Joan de Somery; d/o Rogery de Somery & Nicola de Albini.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Older brother Hamon enfeoffed Robert and his wife with Wrockwardine and Chawton in Hampshire. [The grant of Wrockwardine was not recognized by the king until after Hamon’s death.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert enfeoffed his son Fulk in the manor of Sutton Madock.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1/25/1271, Letters of protection issued to Hamon and Robert, going beyond seas in aid of the Holy Land. (S) CPRs.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8/19/1270 from Dover, Lord Edward and his army left on the 8th crusade. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and his older brother Hamon went on crusade with Prince Edward; leaving after the Prince. [Hamon, who brought 11 knights with him, died on crusade. While on crusade Hamon married Isabelle d’Ybelin, Queen of Cyprus.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 11/10/1270, Lord Edward arrived in Tunis to find that King Louis had died, the crusader forces had been decimated by disease, and King Charles of Sicliy, his uncle by marriage, had already arranged a peace treaty with the emir of 
2 CONC Tunis. The French fleet returned the next day.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1/1271, The English army retreated to Sicily.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 5/1271, Lord Edward moved his forces to Acre; waiting for support to arrive [which never came.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 11/16/1272, Lord Edward ascended to the throne while returning from crusade. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By 8/2/1274, The crusaders had returned to England. [Various groups left at different times and returned by different routes.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 5/23/1275 at Le Knokyn, Robert’s brother John quitclaimed to him his share of Wrockwardine. (S) CCRs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bef. 6/10/1275, Robert did homage to the king for Wrockwardine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aft. 7/18/1275, Robert received seisin of Chawton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12/1275, Robert had lost his seal and appeared at the Curia Regis to petition for a different seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert’s brother John drowned.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5/16/1276, Robert le Strange, keeper of the lands that belonged to John le Strange, to cause John, son and heir of the said John, to have seisin of his father's lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bef. 9/10/1276, Robert died; when Eleanor assigned her dower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alianore married 2nd Bogo de Novill, then Sheriff of Shropshire. [No children.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1/19/1278, The manor of Merbury was committed to Eleanor, late wife of Robert le Strange. [Probably on the death of their youngest son Robert.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 6/10/1280, Grant to Guncelin de Badelesmere of the marriage of John son and heir of Robert Lestrange. (S) CPRs.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1281, Eleanor heir to her sister Berta who died unmarried. 1301-1306, Eleanor died, buried at High Ercall: “DAME ALIANORE LESTRANGE DE BLANCMINSTER GIST ICI. DIEU DE SA ALME EIT MERCI”; [from her brass which still existed in 1860.
2 CONC ]
2 CONT
2 CONT (S) Baronia Anglica Concentrata, Banks, 1844, P421. (S) The Battle Abbey Roll, Abbey, 1889, P3. (S) A Chronicle of the Early Le Stranges, Le Strange, 1916.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert and Alianore: i. John le Straung, born 1266 in England ii. Fulk le Straung (5910052), born 1268 in England. 
