2 CONT CP 25/1/288/46, number 578.<br>
2 CONT Link:	[http://aalt.law.uh.edu/AALT4/CP25%281%29/CP25_1_288/IMG_0095.htm Image of document at AALT]<br>
2 CONT County:	Devon. Somerset.<br>
2 CONT Place:	Westminster.<br>
2 CONT Date:	Three weeks from Easter, 34 Edward III [26 April 1360].<br>
2 CONT Parties:	'''James de Audelegh' of Heleye and Isabel, his wife''', querents, and Hugh de Newehalle, the parson of the church of Southmolton', and Philip War[..e?]wyk, chaplain, deforciants.<br>
2 CONT Property:	The manors of Warkelegh', Merwode, Ilfridecombe, Upexe, Seintemaryechurche, Bearecharterey and Wolryngton' by Fremyngton' and 2 messuages, 1 carucate and 1 ferling of land, 20 acres [of meadow], 10 acres of wood and 18 p
2 CONC ounds of rent in Cridye Peyteuyn, Hassok', Cridynton', Shillyngford' and Tottenesse and the advowsons of the churches of Saterlegh' and of the manors of Warkelegh' and Merwode in the county of Devon and the manor of Pulle and the 
2 CONC advowson of the church of the same manor in the county of Somerset.<br>
2 CONT Action:	Plea of covenant.<br>
2 CONT Agreement:	Hugh and Philip have granted to James and Isabel the manors, 1 messuage, 1 ferling of land, 2 acres of meadow, 1 acre of wood and the rent and the advowsons and have rendered them to them in the court, to hold to James 
2 CONC and Isabel, of the chief lords for the lives of James and Isabel. And besides Hugh and Philip granted for themselves and the heirs of Hugh that 1 messuage, 1 carucate of land, 18 acres of meadow and 9 acres of wood in the vill of 
2 CONC Cridye Peyteuyn - which Christian, who was the wife of Thomas Wyger, held for life of the inheritance of Hugh on the day the agreement was made, and which after the decease of Christian ought to revert to Hugh and Philip and the h
2 CONC eirs of Hugh - after the decease of Christian shall remain to James and Isabel, to hold together with the aforesaid manors, tenements and advowsons of the chief lords for the lives of James and Isabel. And after the decease of Jam
2 CONC es and Isabel 14 pounds of rent in the vill of Tottenesse shall remain to '''James, son of the same James and Isabel''', and the male heirs of his body, to hold of the chief lords for ever. In default of such heirs, successive rem
2 CONC ainders (1) to the heirs of the bodies of James de Audelegh' and Isabel and (2) to the right heirs of James de Audelegh'. And the manors of Warkelegh', Merwode, Ilfridecombe, Bearecharterey and Wolryngton' and the advowsons of the
2 CONC  churches of Saterlegh' and of the manors of Warkelegh' and Merwode shall remain to '''Thomas, brother of the aforesaid James, son of James and Isabel''', and the male heirs of his body, to hold of the chief lords for ever. In def
2 CONC ault of such heirs, successive remainders (1) to the heirs of the bodies of James de Audelegh' and Isabel and (2) to the right heirs of James de Audelegh'. And the manors of Upexe and Pulle and 1 messuage, 1 carucate of land, 18 a
2 CONC cres of meadow, 9 acres of wood and 4 pounds of rent in the vills of Cridye Peyteuyn, Hassok' and Cridynton' and the advowson of the church of the manor of Pulle shall remain to '''Roland, brother of the aforesaid James, son of Ja
2 CONC mes and Isabel''', and the male heirs of his body, to hold of the chief lords for ever. In default of such heirs, successive remainders (1) to '''Oliver, brother of the same Roland''', and the male heirs of his body, (2) to the he
2 CONC irs of the body of James de Audelegh' and Isabel and (3) to the right heirs of James de Audelegh'. And the manor of Seintemaryechurche, 1 messuage, 1 ferling of land, 2 acres of meadow and 1 acre of wood in the vill of Shillyngfor
2 CONC d' shall remain to the aforesaid Oliver and his aforesaid heirs, to hold of the chief lords for ever. In default of such heirs, successive remainders (1) to the aforesaid Roland and his aforesaid heirs, (2) to the heirs of the bod
2 CONC ies of James de Audelegh' and Isabel and (3) to the right heirs of James de Audelegh'. For this:	James de Audelegh' and Isabel have given them 300 pounds sterling.<br>
2 CONT Source: [http://www.medievalgenealogy.org.uk/fines/abstracts/CP_25_1_288_46.shtml#578 Abstracts of Feet of Fines]
