2 CONT v. BLANCHE DE AUDLEY, married FULK FITZ WARIN, Knt., 4th Lord Fitz Warin, of Whittington, Shropshire, Wantage, Berkshire, Bentham (in Badgeworth), Gloucestershire, Edlington, Yorkshire, etc., son and heir of Fulk Fitz Warin, Knt.,
2 CONC  3rd Lord Fitz Warin, of Whittington, Shropshire, Wantage, Berkshire, etc., by Joan, said to be a daughter of Henry de Beaumont, Knt., 1st Lord Beaumont, Earl of Buchan and Moray., He was born at Whittington, Shropshire 2 March 13
2 CONC 40/1, and baptized in the church there. They had one son, Fulk, Knt. In 1369 he granted Roger le Strange, lord of Knockin, all his lands and tenements in the town of New Marton, which formerly belonged to Ivo Fitz Warin his kinsma
2 CONC n. He accompanied John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster in his expedition to France in 1373, being in the retinue of the Earl of Warwick. SIR FULK FITZ WARIN, 4th Lord Fitz Warin died 12 Feb. 1373/4. His widow, Blanche was living in 13
2 CONC 74-5 (date of settlement). She died before 1 April 1386. etc.
