2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/FitzAlan-619
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline was the daughter of Edmund FitzAlan, 2nd Earl of Arundel, and Alice de Warenne.[1][2][3][4] Her birth date is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline married Roger le Strange[3][4][5] before July 1351.[1][2] They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John[1][2][4][5]
2 CONT # Roger[1][2][5]
2 CONT # Ebles, who became rector of Wistanstow, Shropshire and Gresforrd, Denbighshire[1][2]
2 CONT # Edward[1][2][5]
2 CONT # Edmund[1][2]
2 CONT # Joan, who married Thomas Poynings[1][2]
2 CONT # Lucy, who married William Willoughby[1][2][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1369 John de Rochford and his wife Isabel sued Aline and her husband for Isabel's downright to a third of the manor of Shenstone, Staffordshire.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline received 1500 marks under the 1375 will of her brother Richard, in addition to 1000 marks which he had already given her and her husband.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Following her husband's death in 1382, Aline asked Richard de Ellesmere, who held the living of Llanymynech, Shropshire, to secure her dower rights.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline died on 20 January 1385/6.[1][2]
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Aline's brother Richard names "my nephews and nieces sons and daughters of Roger le Strange and to my sister Dame Alaine le Strange wife to the said Roger." (Cited in Medlands - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH
2 CONC %20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#AlineFitzAlanMRogerLestrange.) That gives proof that Aline, daughter of Edmund FitzAlan, married Roger le Strange.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Marlyn Lewis gives a confused account of this family and should not be trusted - in particular confusing Aline's son Ebles, a priest who died before 12 December 1401, with Ebles le Strange, Lord of Knockin, who died in 1335 and MA
2 CONC Y have been the father of an illegitimate daughter Isabel.[8]
2 CONT
