1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Gerard de Lisle, 1st Baron Lisle==
2 CONT '''Gerard II de Lisle, 1st Baron Lisle (1304 – 9 June 1360) of Kingston Lisle, (Latinised to de Insula ("from the Island"), French de L'Isle) was an English nobleman and soldier during King Edward III's campaigns in Scotland and F
2 CONC rance.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was born circa 1304,[1] the son and heir''' of Sir Warin de Lisle, of Kingston Lisle in the parish of Sparsholt, Berkshire, Keeper of Windsor Castle, by his wife Alice le Tyeys, daughter of Henry le Tyeys, 1st Lord Tyeys. ''
2 CONC 'His grandfather''' was Gerard I de Lisle of Kingston Lisle, the younger son of Robert de Lisle of Rougemont by his wife Alice FitzGerold (granddaughter of Henry I FitzGerold (d.1173/4)), the heiress of Kingston. The arms of Baron
2 CONC s Lisle of Rougemont were: Or, a fess between two chevrons sable. In 1269 Alice '''granted the manor of Kingston to her younger son Gerard I de Lisle, whose family adopted the arms of FitzGerold: Gules, a lion statant guardant arg
2 CONC ent crowned or.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He resided chiefly at Stowe Nine Churches in Northamptonshire and Kingston Lisle (in Sparsholt), Berkshire (now Oxfordshire).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was knighted in 1327. In 1329 he proved his right to free warren in his demesne lands at Stowe and Kislingbury, Northamptonshire by grant of King Henry III to Geoffrey de Armenters. In 1332 Richard Herman was attached to ans
2 CONC wer Gerard de Lisle concerning a plea why with force and arms he broke the close of the said Gerard at Alverston, Hampshire and dug in his separate soil there, and took and carried away twenty cartloads of earth extracted therefro
2 CONC m to the value of 40 shillings, and depastured, trampled on, and consumed his grass once growing there to the value of 60 shillings. In 1339 Gerard had a dispute with his mother, Alice, regarding the presentation of the church of 
2 CONC Stowe, Northamptonshire, but admitted it was not his turn to present; he also complained of trespass on his park at Stowe.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He served on the English side in the Second War of Scottish Independence in 1333 and 1335, under Richard FitzAlan, 10th Earl of Arundel. He served with him again during the Hundred Years' War in France and fought at the Battle 
2 CONC of Crecy, 1346.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was summoned to Parliament on 15 December 1357, by writs directed to Gerardo de Insula or de L'Isle, whereby he is held to have become Baron Lisle. He was summoned to a Council 20 June 1358.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He married twice:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Firstly (after 3 December 1329) to Eleanor de Arundel''' (d. before 1347), daughter of Edmund de Arundel (or Fitz Alan), Knight, 9th Earl of Arundel, by Alice, daughter of William de Warenne, Knight. She was the widow of Willia
2 CONC m de Saint John. '''In 1338 he settled the manors of Stowe and Church Brampton, Northamptonshire on himself and his wife Eleanor'''. She was living in '''1342, in which year Gerard sued his receiver''', John son of Robert de Hulle
2 CONC , '''regarding various monies received from various manors, among them Abbotstone, Hampshire and Walberton, Sussex, which Eleanor held in dower of her first marriage. He presented to the churches of Abbotstone, Hampshire, 1349, an
2 CONC d Mundford, Norfolk, 1349 and 1352'''. She was dead by 1347 when '''he contracted to marry Margery, widow''' of Nicholas de la Beche, late Constable of the Tower of London, '''but who was abducted''' and married by Sir John Dalton
2 CONC . '''By Eleanor, Gerard had one son:
2 CONT *Sir Warin Lisle, 2nd Baron Lisle.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He married secondly (before 1 July 1351 (date of settlement) and possibly as early as 29 July 1349 (date of his presentation to Abbotstone church)) to Elizabeth le Strange''' (d.1362), daughter of Sir John le Strange, 2nd Baron
2 CONC  Strange of Blackmere, by Ankaret le Boteler, daughter of William le Boteler, 1st Baron Boteler of Wem. '''Elizabeth was the widow''' of Edmund de Saint John, 3rd Baron Saint John of Basing (died at Calais 18 Aug. 1347). '''After 
2 CONC his death his widow Elizabeth, married''' as her third husband Richard de Pembridge (or Pembrugge), KG, of Orwell, Cambridgeshire, Burgate and Lyndhurst, Hampshire, etc., Warden of the New Forest, Governor of Bamborough Castle, Go
2 CONC vernor of Dover Castle and Warden of the Cinque Ports, Chamberlain of the Household. She died 14–16 Sept. 1362. Warin (??? '''Surely should be Gerard de Lisle) had by his second wife Elizabeth le Strange two sons and one daughter:
2 CONT *Richard de Lisle
2 CONT *Henry de Lisle
2 CONT *Elizabeth de Lisle, who married Edmund de Stonor, Knight, of Stonor, in Pyrton, Oxfordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1351 Philip Warde, formerly bailiff of Gerard de Lisle in the manor of Walberton, Sussex, owed him a debt of £10 7s.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerard_de_Lisle,_1st_Baron_Lisle
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________
2 CONT *'''Sir Gerard de L'Isle, 1st Lord Lisle1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8
2 CONT *'''M, #15958, b. circa 1304, d. 9 June 1360
2 CONT *Father	Sir Warin de Lisle, Keeper of Windsor Castle4,7,8 b. c 1277, d. c 16 Mar 1322
2 CONT *Mother	Alice Tyeys4,7,8 b. c 1287, d. 2 Aug 1347
2 CONT *'''     Sir Gerard de L'Isle, 1st Lord Lisle was born circa 1304 at of Kingston Lisle in Sparsholt, Berkshire, England; Age 23 in Feb 1327, age 40+ in 1350.3,4,7,8 He married Eleanor FitzAlan''', daughter of Sir Edmund FitzAlan, 
2 CONC 9th Earl Arundel, Chief Justice of North & South Wales and Alice de Warren, '''after 3 December 1329; They had 4 sons''' (Sir Warin, 2nd Lord Lisle; Richard; Gerard; & Edmund).3,6,9 '''Sir Gerard de L'Isle, 1st Lord Lisle married 
2 CONC Elizabeth le Strange''', daughter of Sir John le Strange, 2nd Lord Strange of Blackmere and Ankaret le Boteler, '''before 29 July 1349.9,8 A settlement for the marriage Sir Gerard de L'Isle, 1st Lord Lisle and Elizabeth le Strange
2 CONC  was made on 1 July 1351; They had 2 sons''' (Richard; & Henry) & '''1 daughter''' (Elizabeth, wife of Sir Edmund Stonor).2,3,4,5,9,8 '''Sir Gerard de L'Isle, 1st Lord Lisle died on 9 June 1360 at of Stowe, Northampshire, England.
2 CONC 3,4,9,8
2 CONT *'''Family 1     Eleanor FitzAlan'' b. c 1308, d. b 30 Mar 1347
2 CONT *'''Child	
2 CONT **Sir Warin de Lisle, 2nd Lord Lisle, 5th Lord Tyeys+3,9 b. c 4 Apr 1333, d. 28 Jun 1382
2 CONT *'''Family 2     Elizabeth le Strange''' d. bt 14 Sep 1362 - 16 Sep 1362
2 CONT *Child	
2 CONT **Elizabeth de L'Isle+9 b. c 1349
2 CONT *Citations
