1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joan was the daughter and coheiress of Oliver de Ingham in Norfolk, and widow of Roger Le Strange of Nockin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan married Sir Roger Le Strange 4th Baron Strange of Knockyn, son of Sir John Le Strange 2nd Baron le Strange of Knockyn and Iseult (Isolda), before March 25, 1344.He was her 1st husband and his 2nd wife. (Sir Roger Le Strange 4
2 CONC th Baron Strange of Knockyn was born on 15 Aug 1301 in Knockin, Oswestry, Shropshire, England and died on 29 Jul 1349 in Sedgebrook, Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan also married Sir Miles II Staplton K.G., of Bedale, son of Sir Gilbert de Stapleton of Bedale and Agnes FitzAlan Heiress of Bedale, on 30 Nov 1350. her 2nd husband and his 2nd wife. (Sir Miles II Staplton K.G., of Bedale was 
2 CONC born in 1320 in Bedale, North Riding Yorkshire, England, died on 4 Oct 1364 in Battle of Auray, France and was buried in Ingham, Smallburgh, Norfolk, England.) Henceforward Stapleton is often described as 'of Ingham' as of 'Bedale
2 CONC ', and became a considerable proprietor in Norfolk. Swww.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan de Ingham BIRTH	1320 Ingham, North Norfolk District, Norfolk, England DEATH	12 Dec 1365 (aged 44–45) Bedale, Hambleton District, North Yorkshire, England BURIAL	 Ingham Priory Ingham, North Norfolk District, Norfolk, England 
2 CONC  MEMORIAL ID	85623024 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan was the daughter and coheiress of Oliver de Ingham in Norfolk, and widow of Roger Le Strange of Nockin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents	 Oliver II de Ingham 1278–1344
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse	 Miles II Stapleton 1320–1364
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Joan Stapleton Plaiz unknown–1385
2 CONT
2 CONT Miles III Stapleton 1357–1419
2 CONT
2 CONT Stapleton's eldest son John died before him, and he was succeeded at Ingham as well as Bedale by Miles, his son by the heiress of Ingham. 
