1 NAME Angharad /Hanmer/
2 GIVN Angharad
2 SURN Hanmer
2 _MARNM Hanmer
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1380
2 PLAC Hanmer,Clywd,Flintshire,Wales
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1473
2 PLAC Emral,Worthenbury
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Wales
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, http://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/4731/Hanmer%201.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (March 2, 2017; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT See Peter Batrtum, http://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5559/puleston.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (March 2, 2017; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Puleston was the eldest son of Robert Puleston of Emral and Lowri, daughter of Griffith Vychan and sister of Owain Glyndwr, Prince of Wales. He was born at Emral.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married '''Angharad''', daughter of neighbouring landowner Griffith Hanmer of Hanmer, Flintshire and his wife Gwerfyl (daughter of Tudor ap Grono, a great great grandfather of King Henry VII of England, and Tudor's wife Mallt, 
2 CONC daughter of Madoc of Hendwr). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1471, Angharad was one of the "honourable ladies of the court of Margaret of Anjou", wife of King Henry VI. The only surviving letters from Margaret of Anjou were found in the roof of Emral Hall.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 3 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Katrin (or Katherine), who died without issue
2 CONT # Margaret, who married Dafydd ap Ieuan ap Einion, Constable of Harlech Castle, Merionethshire, and 
2 CONT # Sir Roger Puleston
2 CONT
2 CONT Links 
2 CONT *http://www.puleston-jones.com/page21.htm
