2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Croft held the office of Captain of Merk Castle, near Calais. He lived at Croft Castle, Herefordshire, England. Between 1402 and 1404 he was frequently employed in negotiations in Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Croft is the son of John de Croft.1 He married Janet Glendower, daughter of Owen Glendower.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir John de Croft and Janet Glendower
2 CONT #William de Croft+1 married Margaret Walwyn, daughter of Thomas Walwyn.1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1419/1420, holding the manors of Dalton, Leighton Conyers, part of Over Kellet, the Advowson of Claughton and various lands in Warton and Farleton in Westmorland.  Sir John’s seal, showing the lozengy coat of arms, is a
2 CONC ppended to several of the Legh of Lyme deeds.  He had sons (by Mabel/Maud his first wife) John, Peter and Richard as well as a daughter Ellen who married Thomas de Dacre around 1386 and another daughter, Margaret, who married Sir 
2 CONC William Curwen in 1395.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2573.htm#i77327
2 CONT *''''''Sir John Croft1
2 CONT *''''''M, b. circa 1368
2 CONT *Father Sir John Croft1 b. c 1336 
2 CONT *Mother (Miss) Harrock1 b. c 1346 
2 CONT *''''''     Sir John Croft was born circa 1368 at of Croft Castle, Herefordshire, England.1 He married Janet ferch Owain Glendower, daughter of Owen Glendower, Lord Glyndyvrdwy & Sycharth and Margaret Hanmer, circa 1390.1
2 CONT *''''''Family Janet ferch Owain Glendower b. c 1376 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT **◦William Croft+1 b. c 1393, d. a 1433
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 53.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p32487.htm#i324866
2 CONT *''''''Sir John de Croft1
2 CONT *M, #324866
2 CONT *Last Edited=11 Dec 2008
2 CONT *''''''     Sir John de Croft is the son of John de Croft.1 He married Janet Glendower, daughter of Owen Glendower.1
2 CONT *''''''     Sir John de Croft held the office of Captain of Merk Castle, near Calais.1 He lived at Croft Castle, Herefordshire, England.1 Between 1402 and 1404 he was frequently employed in negotiations in Flanders.1
2 CONT *''''''Child of Sir John de Croft and Janet Glendower
