2 DATE 7 AUG 1390
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Wales
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5128/bleddyn%20ap%20cynfyn%2026.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (May 4, 2017; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH:---Pleas and inquisitions relative to the lands held in capite of the Crown, by David de Hendwr, which prove that he died at Hendwr, 7th August, 1390., seized of a moeity of the Manor  of "Hendwr) and a great extent of other
2 CONC  property in Edmeimion, that a feeoffment before his marriage with Isabel or Elizabeth Deueros (Devereus), was dated about the feast of St. James the Apostle, 7th of Richard, 11. (25th, July, that by her he had a son and heir, nam
2 CONC ed Thomas, who in the 12th year of the said King, was of the age of three rears. ,Source:- Dwnn, Heraldic Visitations of Wales. (Vol 2age 110-fn.  1)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT David de Hendour, Baron of Edernion. He marries Margaret de Cornwall and who's family relocates to Cornwall becoming the ancestor of the Henders of Cornwall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by; HRH Prince Kieren de Muire von Drakenberg
