1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Easily confused with his son, who was Chamberlain.  Please see the Dictionary of Welsh Biography -- https://www.geni.com/people/Gwilym-ap-Gwilym/6000000003048287785   (August 25, 2016; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT ************************
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''William Fychan ap Gwilym, Deputy Chamberlain of North Wales1,2,3
2 CONT *'''M, #90657, b. circa 1420
2 CONT *Father	Sir Gwilym Griffeth4 b. c 1390
2 CONT *Mother	Janet Stanley4 d. 1466
2 CONT *OTHER REFERENCES HAVE DIFFERENT MOTHER FOR ALICE DALTON
2 CONT *'''     William Fychan ap Gwilym, Deputy Chamberlain of North Wales was born circa 1420 at of Penryhn, Caernarvonshire, Wales.1 He married Alice Dalton''', daughter of Sir Richard Dalton and Isabel Stanley, '''circa 1444.1,2,3
2 CONT *'''Family     Alice Dalton''' b. c 1424
2 CONT *'''Child	
2 CONT **Sir William Griffith, Chamberlain of North Wales+1,2,3 b. c 1447, d. 1505 or 1506
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 243.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 559.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 345.
2 CONT *[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p3018.htm#i90657 ________________________
2 CONT *Joan (Jane) TROUTBECK
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1459, Mobberley, Cheshire, England
2 CONT *Notes: The Griffiths of Penrhyn were one of the most powerful families in North Wales at the time and were a branch of the Tudor family descended from Ednyfed Fychan (d. 1246) and the Welsh royal and princely houses. The half-sis
2 CONC ter of Sir William (according to some pedigrees, but possibly his daughter), Agnes Griffith (d. 1542), married Sir Roland de Velville.
2 CONT *Father: William TROUTBECK of Dunham (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret STANLEY (B. Grey of Codnor)
2 CONT *Married: William GRIFFITH of Penhryn (Sir Knight) ('''son of William Griffith and Alice Dalton''') ABT 1475, Penrhyn, Carnaervonshire, Wales
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. William GRIFFITH of Penrhyn (b. ABT 1476) (m.1 Jane Stradling - m.2 Jane Pulleston)
2 CONT **2. Edmund GRIFFITH
2 CONT **3. Alice GRIFFITH
2 CONT **4. Jane GRIFFITH (b. ABT 1505)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TROUTBECK.htm#Joan (Jane) TROUTBECK1 ____________
2 CONT *Bangor University
2 CONT *Penrhyn Castle Papers
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Between 1431 and 1531, the son, grandson and great-grandson of Gwilym ap Griffith held the Penrhyn estate and added to it. They succeeded in allying themselves with prominent English houses, especially the Stanleys, which began w
2 CONC ith the marriage of Gwilym ap Griffith with Joan Stanley of Hooton. '''Gwilym Fychan, the son of that marriage, married before 1447, Ales daughter and heiress''' of Sir Richard Dalton of Althorp, Northants. '''The marriage reflect
2 CONC s the Stanley connection, as Ales Dalton was the granddaughter''' of Isabel de Pilkington by her second marriage, whose daughter by Thomas de Lathom, her first husband, brought Lathom and Knowsley to the Stanleys. '''Gwilym Fychan
2 CONC  married secondly, Gwenllian, daughter''' of Iorwerth ap David. Robert, '''his eldest son by this marriage''', was the ancestor of the family of Griffith of Plas Newydd, Anglesey, and Llanfair-is-gaer, Caernarvonshire. Edmund '''t
2 CONC he second son''' founded the estate of Carreg-lwyd, Anglesey. '''His son and heir from his first marriage was''' William Griffith (ca.1445-1505/6). He is not always easy to distinguish in the documents from his father. He married 
2 CONC firstly Joan Troutbeck, widow of Sir William Butler of Bewsey, Cheshire, whose mother was Margaret, daughter of Sir Thomas Stanley, first Baron Stanley.
2 CONT *From: http://www.archiveswales.org.uk/anw/get_collection.php?inst_id=39&coll_id=10875&expand=
2 CONT ________________
2 CONT *'''The Visitations of Yorkshire in the Years 1563 and 1564: Made by William ...     By William Flower
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=pjMEAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA394&lpg=PA394&dq=dorothy+hilton+1563&source=bl&ots=V957x6rW7I&sig=QTLYEYcfE7e4_bC5Kio5BoVTfyY&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwju9suQ1vfJAhVJ2GMKHbOBBcs4FBDoAQgeMAE#v=onepage&q=dalton&f=fa
2 CONC lse
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/visitationsyork00britgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/visitationsyork00britgoog#page/n97/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.85
2 CONT **	Dalton.
2 CONT *Sir Rychard Dalton  of Byspam in Lancashyre, Knight. = ; ch: Sir Robert (m. . . .  Latham), Sir John (2 son.) Dalton
2 CONT **Sir John Dalton Knight 2 son. ; ch: B (Pg.86 Sir Pyter Dalton Knight. = . . . .  doughter of . . . .  ; ch: John Dalton.)
2 CONT **Sir Robert Dalton son & heyre of Sir Rychard Dalton Knight. = . . . .  doughter of Sir Thomas Latham. ; ch: A (Pg.86 Sir John (m. . . . .  Hussey) Dalton)
2 CONT ***https://archive.org/stream/visitationsyork00britgoog#page/n98/mode/1up
2 CONT ***Sir John Dalton Knight. = . . . .  doughter of Sir Henry Hussey Knight. ; ch: Sir John (m. . . . .  Pylkyngton.) Dalton
2 CONT ****Sir John Dalton Knight son & heyre to Sir John. = . . . .  doughter of Sir Rychard Pylkngton. ; ch: Sir Rychard (m. Kateren Venables), Robert (m. Margaret . . . .  ) Dalton.
2 CONT *****Sir Rychard Dalton Knight son & heyr to Sir John. = Kateren doughter of Sir Thomas Venables, Knight. ; ch: '''Ales (m. William Gryffyth)''', other doters Dalton
2 CONT ******'''Ales doter''' of Sir Rychard Dalton. '''= William Gryffyth of Penryn in Carmarthenshyre. ; ch:''' Sir William, Jennet Gryffyth.
2 CONT *****Robert Dalton of Bispayne, 2nd son. = Margaret doughter of . . . . ; ch: William (m. Elsabeth Beaconsall), John (3rd son.), Rychard (m. doughter of Fleming) Dalton
2 CONT ****** .... etc. _________________
2 CONT *'''Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&pg=RA1-PA448&lpg=RA1-PA448&dq=dorothy+hilton+1563&source=bl&ots=kvmDGXPP73&sig=_tEATIE3oPQx2W9Gas-zL6t5j8c&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwju9suQ1vfJAhVJ2GMKHbOBBcs4FBDoAQgzMAY#v=onepage&q=DAL
2 CONC TON&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.559
2 CONT *12. JOAN TROUTBECK, born in 1459. She married (1st) WILLIAM BOTELER, Knt., 2nd but eldest son and heir of John Boteler, Knt., of Bewsey (in Warrington), Burtonwood, Great Sankey, etc., Lancashire, by his 1st wife, Margaret, daugh
2 CONC ter of Peter Gerard. He was born 25 Nov. 1450. They had no issue. SIR WILLIAM BOTELER died 8 June 1471. His widow, Joan, married (2nd) (as his 1st wife) WILLIAM GRIFFITH, K.B., of Penrhyn,Caernarvonshire, Marshal of the King's Hal
2 CONC l, Chamberlain of North Wales, '''son of Gwilyn Fychan ap Gwilym (otherwise know as William Griffith), Marshal of the King's Hall, deputy to various Chamberlains of North Wales, by his 1st wife, Alice, daughter''' of Richard Dalto
2 CONC n, Knt. He was born about 1447. They had one son, William, Knt., and three daughters, Jane (wife of William Herbert, Knt.), Margaret (wife of Nicholas Dutton, Knt., and Simon Thelwall), and Ann (wife of ——Winnington). He married (
2 CONC 2nd) ELIZABETH GREY, daughter of Robert Grey, Esq., Constable of Ruthin Castle. They had one son, William Grey, and one daughter, Alice .... etc. _________________
2 CONT *'''Plantagenet Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...     By Douglas Richardson
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=kjme027UeagC&printsec=frontcover&dq=Plantagenet+ancestry&hl=en&sa=X&ei=U8VLUYTME-boiALhroHwBw&ved=0CEcQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=Dalton&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 595
2 CONT *15. JOAN TROUTBECK, born in 1459. She married (1st) WILLIAM BOTELER, Knt., 2nd but eldest son and heir of John Boteler, Knt., of Bewsey (in Warrington), Burtonwood, Great Sankey, etc., Lancashire, by his 1st wife, Margaret, daugh
2 CONC ter of Peter Gerard. he was born 25 Nov. 1450. They had no issue. SIR WILLIAM BOTELER died 8 Jun 1471. His widow, Joan, married (2nd) (as his 1st wife) WILLIAM GRIFFITH, K.G., of Penrhyn, Caernarvonshire, Marshal of the King's Hal
2 CONC l, Chamberlain of North Wales, '''son of Gwilym Fychan ap Gwilym (otherwise know as William Griffith), Marshal of the King's Hall, deputy of various Chamberlains of North Wales, by his 1st wife, Alice, daughter''' of Richard Dalto
2 CONC n, Knt. He was born about 1447. They had one son, William, Knt., and three daughters, Jane (wife of William Herbert, Knt.), Margaret (wife of Nicholas Dutton, Knt., and Simon Thelwall), and Ann (wife of __ Winnington). He married 
2 CONC (2nd) ELIZABETH GREY, daughter of Robert Grey, Esq., Constable of Ruthin Castle. They had one son, William Grey, and one daughter, Alice (wife of Pierce Vychan, of Coetmor). SIR WILLIAM GRIFFITH died in 1505 or 1506. _____________
2 CONC ________
