1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOAN OF SOMERVILLE===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the English Close Rolls===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 May 1355: Rhys ap Griffith as the husband of Joan, the eldest daughter of Philip de Somervill and Margaret, his wife. The younger daughter and co-heiress was Elizabeth, who had married John de Stafford, but was now dead. Eli
2 CONC zabeth's share of the Somervill property, therefore, fell to her daughter and heir Maud, now under age, and for whom her father, John de Stafford, was guardian. On the 28th March, 1356, Maud was of age and was the wife of Edmund V
2 CONC ernoun. [https://archive.org/details/collectionsforhi12staf/page/281/mode/1up Collections for a History of Staffordshire. Edited by Sir William Salt. Volume XII. New Series (Harrison and Sons, London 1909), page 281]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan SOMERVILLE , Heiress of Wychnor (Philip SOMERVILLE , of Wychnor & Cossington, Sir8, Robert SOMERVILLE , of Wychnor & Great Benton,Sir7, John SOMERVILLE , of Wychnor & Cossington, Sir6, Roger de SOMERVILLE , of Wychnor, Sir5, 
2 CONC Roger de SOMERVILLE , of Wychnor, Sir4, Roger de SOMERVILLE , of Wychnor, Sir3, Gaulter de SOMERVILLE , of Wychnor, Sir2, Gaulter de SOMERVILLE , Sir1) was born ABT 1310 in Wychnor, Burton-upon-Trent, Staffordshire, England, and d
2 CONC ied 1376. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=REG&db=jweber&id=I26669
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Rhys "Hen" ap GRIFFITH , of Llansadwrn, Sir BEF 1339 in Settlement date, son of Gruffudd ap HEILIN , of Penrhyn and Efa verch GRUFFUDD. He was born BEF 1288 in Llansadwrn, Llandovery, Carmarthenshire, Wales, and died 1
2 CONC 0 MAY 1356 in Wychnor, Burton-upon-Trent, Staffordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joan SOMERVILLE , Heiress of Wychnor and Rhys "Hen" ap GRIFFITH , of Llansadwrn, Sir are:
2 CONT * i.	Rhys II "Jevan" ap GRIFFITH , of Abermarlais, Sir was born ABT 25 DEC 1325 in Abermarlais, Llangadog, Carmarthenshire, Wales, and died 27 MAY 1380 in Wychnor, Burton-upon-Trent, Staffordshire, England.
2 CONT *ii.	Henry GRIFFITH , of Wychnor & Long Benton, Sir was born ABT 1332 in Wychnor, Burton-upon-Trent, Staffordshire, England, and died 25 MAY 1372 in Longbenton, Tynemouth, Northumberland, England. He married Joan CLINTON , Heiress
2 CONC  of Coleshill BEF 1371 in 3rd husband 2nd wife, daughter of John III CLINTON , of Coleshill, Sir and Joan HILLARY. She was born BET 1341 AND 1342 in Coleshill Manor, Arden, Warwickshire, England, and died BEF 1386.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children listed at http://thesignsofthetimes.com.au/37/694668.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT *Thomas AP RHYS HÊN de Somervill
2 CONT *Rhys Ieuanc AP RHYS HÊN
2 CONT *Henry AP RHYS HÊN
2 CONT *Margred FERCH RHYS HÊN
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://thesignsofthetimes.com.au/37/694668.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT eldest daughter and co-heiress
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 Feb 1325, Westminster
2 CONT Licence for Philip de Somervill to enfeoff Richard de Byllyngton of the manors of Alrewas and Wychenoure, co. Stafford, held in chief, and for him to re-grant them in tail male to the said Philip and Margaret his wife, with remain
2 CONC ders to Res ap Griffit and Joan his wife, and the heirs of their bodies, and to the right heirs of the said Philip.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. II, vol. 5, p. 87
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 Mar 1337, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Licence for Philip de Somervill to enfeoff John de Warrewik and John Prince, chaplain, of the homages and other services due to him by certain tenants of the manors of Allerwas, held in chief, to wit, Richard de Vernoun, John de A
2 CONC rderne, James de Stafford and Isabella, his wife, William de Leycestre, John de Horsebrok, Nicholas Allerwas, William de Horsebrok, John Hugyn of Strethay and Richard de Strethay, and for them to re-grant these to him and Margaret
2 CONC , his wife, in tail male with remainders to Rees ap Griffyth, knight, and Joan, his wife, in tail, and to the right heirs of the said Philip.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. III, vol. 3, p. 393
2 CONT
