1 NAME William /Martin/ 1st Baron Martin
2 GIVN William
2 SURN Martin
2 NSFX 1st Baron Martin
2 _MARNM Martin
2 NICK William de Canville
2 NICK 2nd Lord Canville
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1257
2 ADDR
3 CITY Combmartin
3 STAE England
1 BURI
2 DATE OCT 1324
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 8 OCT 1324
2 PLAC Combe Martin
2 ADDR
3 CITY Barnstaple
3 STAE England
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Martin, grandson and heir, being son and heir of Nicholas son of Nicholas, by Maud de Brian. He was aged 25 in 1282, and received livery of his inheritance 1 April 1282, having done homage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Jan 1282, Rhuddlan
2 CONT
2 CONT Inspeximus and confirmation of a charter of William Martin granting to the lady Eleanor de Mohun, for life, the manors of Kingeston, Combe Martin, Langacre, Moleton, co. Devon, and Ludeford, co. Somerset, at a rent of 200l. a year
2 CONC , and if the said William die first the said Eleanor to pay 1d. a year only for the same to his heirs. Witnesses:—John de Bello Campo, Gilbert de Knovill, Thomas de Pyn, Malger de Sancto Albino, Walter de Dunheved, Walter de Heliu
2 CONC n, Guy Ferre and William de Bluntesdon, knights, Robert de Maleston, Henry de Brok', John de Lameslever, and many others.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. I, vol. 2, p. 53
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 Feb 1287, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT [Protection with clause volumus for] William Martyn, going beyond seas with Gilbert de Clare, until the Ascension.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. I, vol. 2, p. 263
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Oct 1295, Canterbury
2 CONT
2 CONT Appointment of William Martyn, who is going to Gascony on the king's service, to the custody, during pleasure, of the lands late of Hugh Luvel, deceased, tenant in chief, which custody the king had granted to John de Soules, but t
2 CONC aken into his hands again for divers causes; and he is to have the issues arising therefrom and the goods' of the said custody if they belong to the king.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Oct 1295, Canterbury
2 CONT
2 CONT William Martyn, going to Gascony in the company of Edmund the king's brother, for as long as he is on that service.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. I, vol. 3, pp. 148, 150
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 May 1296, Roxburgh
2 CONT
2 CONT Grant to William Martyn, staying in Gascony on the king's service, of the custody, during the minority of the heir, of the manor of Baggetrip, late of Adam de Baggetrip, who held by knight service of the heir of Hugh Lovel, tenant
2 CONC  in chief. This is in addition to a former grant to him of the custody, during pleasure, of the lands late of the said Hugh Lovel, a custody which had been formerly granted to John de Soiiles, but afterwards taken into the king's 
2 CONC hands again.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Aug 1296, Dundee
2 CONT
2 CONT Grant to William Martyn, staying in Gascony on the king's service, of the marriage of the heir of Adam de Baggetripe, a minor in the king's custody.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. I, vol. 3, pp. 187, 194
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Apr 1297, Plympton
2 CONT
2 CONT Order to release the demand made upon William Martyn, grandson (nepoti) and heir of Nicholas son of Martyn, tenant in chief, for the scutage of three knights' fees for the king's army of Wales in the fifth year of his reign, as Ni
2 CONC cholas was with the king by his order for the service of three fees, which he then acknowledged to the king, as appears by the rolls of the marshalsea.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Close Rolls, 25 Edw. I, p. 27
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Nov 1297, Eltham
2 CONT
2 CONT Inspeximus and confirmation of an agreement between John de Hastingges, lord of Bergeveny and William Martyn, lord of Kammoys, who are staying with the king beyond seas on his service, dated Gaunt in Flanders, September 30, 1297, 
2 CONC whereby William son and heir of the former is to marry Eleanor the eldest daughter of the latter, and Edmund son and heir of the latter is to marry Jonetta the eldest daughter of the former, each of the girls to be dowered by thei
2 CONC r fathers-in-law with land to the value of 100l. a year in case their husbands die before their fathers, and in case their husbands die after their fathers but leaving their wives surviving, they are to have the usual dowers. Witn
2 CONC esses: the noble baron (ber), Anthony du Bek bishop of Durham, Sir William de Brewuse, Sir Walter de Beauchamp, then steward of the household, Sir Guy de Warwyk, Sir Peter Corbet, and others.
2 CONT
2 CONT Licence for the said William Martin to demise for six years to whomsoever he will of the king's allegiance land to the value of 100l. a year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. I, vol. 3, p. 314
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Apr 1298, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Grant to William Martyn, who when lately coming with the king from Flanders on the king's service lost his horses, armour and other goods to the value of 510l., through a storm at, sea near the port of Sandwich, of custodies and m
2 CONC arriages to that value this side Trent, when they fall in.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. I, vol. 3, p. 340
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT He was summoned to Parliament from 24 June 1295 to 24 September 1324, by writs directed Willelmo Martyn, whereby he is held to have become Lord Martin, and was present in Parliament as a Trier of Petitions in 1320.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Jan 1303, Odiham
2 CONT
2 CONT Licence after inquisition ad quod damnum made by the sheriff of Devon, for. the prior and convent of Berdestaple, to appropriate to their own uses the advowson of the church of St, Peter, Berdestaple, which they acquired from the 
2 CONC ancestors of William Martyn, before the publication of the statute of mortmain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. I, vol. 4, p. 104
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 Aug 1305, Rayleigh
2 CONT
2 CONT Grant to William Martyn of the custody, during the minority of the heirs, of the lands late of Henry de la Pomeroy, tenant in chief, with the marriage of the heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Oct 1305, Sheen
2 CONT
2 CONT Grant to William Martyn, in extension of a grant to him of the custody during the minority of the heirs, of the lands late of Henry de la Pomeraye, tenant in chief, with the marriage of the heirs, of the said custody with knights'
2 CONC  fees, advowsons of churches, dowers when they fall in, and all other things belonging thereto.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. I, vol. 4, pp. 376, 381
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT He was summoned to attend the Coronation of Edward II on 25 February 1307/8, and was present on 9 February when the great seal was delivered to the Chancellor.
2 CONT
2 CONT In September 1308, after the death of Geoffrey Canville [Lord Canville], he succeeded to the inheritance of his mother, Maud de Brian.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 Mar 1309, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Licence, upon fine, after inquisition ad quod damnum, for the alienation in mortmain by William de Tracy, parson of the church of Morteho, of a rent of 66s. 8d. and half an acre of land in Morteho and Westdune, which he holds by k
2 CONC night service from William Martyn, tenant in chief, for the endowment of a chaplain to celebrate divine service daily in the church of St. Mary, Morteho, for the soul of the grantor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. II, vol. 1, p. 108
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 Jun 1310, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Licence for William Martyn, the elder, to grant to Henry de Lacy, earl of Lincoln, and Joan his wife, and their issue, with remainder failing issue to himself and his heirs, the manors of Blakedon, co. Somerset, and Langare, Upexe
2 CONC , and Holun, co. Devon, held in chief, the knights' fees of the manors with 3,000 acres of wood in the manor of Holun, and the advowsons of the churches of Holun and Blakedon excepted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. II, vol. 1, p. 230
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Oct 1313, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Licence, upon fine made by William Martyn, for him and Eleanor his wife to grant 2 messuages, 2 mills, 2 carucates of land, and 12 marks of rent in Beare and Welrington, held in chief, to John Chartray, for his life, with remainde
2 CONC r after his death to their son Henry and the heirs of his body, with remainder failing such issue to the said William Martyn and Eleanor and to the heirs of the said William Martyn. By fine of 5 marks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. II, vol. 2, p. 31
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 Oct 1313, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Order to discharge William Martin of the scutage that they demand from him for three knights' fees for the late king's army of Wales in the fifth year of his reign, as Nicholas son of Martin, his father, had his service in the sai
2 CONC d army for the above fees, which service he acknowledged to the late king, as appears by the rolls of his marshalsea.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Close Rolls, 7 Edw. II, p. 17
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT On 19 February 1314/5 he was appointed justice of West and South Wales and keeper of the castle of Carmarthen and other of the King's castles there, which office he held till 24 June 1316.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 May 1316, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Protection, with clause, until Michaelmas, for William Martyn, justice of South Wales, staying in Wales on the king's service.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. II, vol. 2, p. 452
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1317 was one of those appointed to check any illegal confederacies in Devon, and in 1318 he was made a member of the standing royal council. In November 1318 the sheriff of Devon was ordered to hire two ships [at Martin's expen
2 CONC se) to convey victuals and other necessaries to him and his men, who were going to serve the King in the marches of Scotland. Hugh de Courtenay and William Martin were in November 1321 ordered to attack any who might rise against 
2 CONC the King in Cornwall and Devon, assembling all horse and foot there; at the same time he was one of the conservators of the peace in Gower, and was ordered to abstain from the meeting of the "Good Peers" at Doncaster, which had be
2 CONC en convened by Thomas, Earl of Lancaster. In the following February he was ordered to lead his forces to Coventry to resist the Earl of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Dec 1322, Haddlesley
2 CONT
2 CONT Commitment during pleasure to William Martyn of the keeping of the castle of Heleie with the park and other appurtenances, the town of Betteleye, the manor of Tunstall and two parts of the manors of Endon and Horton, co. Stafford,
2 CONC  late of Nicholas Daudele, tenant in chief, and in the king's hand by reason of the minority of James, his son and heir ; so that he answer for the issues thereof at the Exchequer. By bill of the treasurer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Fine Rolls, 16 Edw. II, p. 190
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 Jul 1323, Burstwick
2 CONT
2 CONT Commitment to William Martyn of the keeping of the castle and manors of Helegh, Tunstall, Horton and Endon, late of Nicholas Daudeleye, tenant in chief, and in the king's hand by reason of the minority of the heir, the keeping whe
2 CONC reof William had before of the king's commitment, so that he answered at the Exchequer for the issues thereof ; to hold from Michaelmas next until the full age of the heir, rendering 100l. a year at the Exchequer, to wit, 75l. 6s.
2 CONC  1½d. at which the premises are extended yearly, and 241. 13s. l0½d. of increment, in moieties at Easter and Michaelmas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Fine Rolls, 17 Edw. II, p. 223
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Inquisition Post Mortem
2 CONT
2 CONT 563. William Martyn
2 CONT
2 CONT Writ, 18 Oct 18 Edward II. [1324]
2 CONT
2 CONT South Wales. Inq. 23 Oct., 18 Edw. II.
2 CONT
2 CONT The country (Patriam) of Kemmys, including the castle and town of Neuport, held of the king in chief by service of 1¼ knight's fee.
2 CONT
2 CONT William his son, aged 30, is his next heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT C. Edw. II. File 88. (18.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Nov 1324, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Order to John de Hampton, escheator in the counties of Gloucester, Worcester, Hereford, Salop and Stafford, and the march of Wales adjacent, to deliver to William Martyn, son and heir of William Martyn, tenant in chief, the lands 
2 CONC late of his said father, he having done homage and fealty.
2 CONT
2 CONT The like to John Everard, escheator in the counties of Cornwall, Devon, Somerset and Dorset.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 Nov 1324, Westminster
2 CONT
2 CONT Order to [John de Hampton, escheator...] not to meddle with the castle of Helegh and the manors of Tunstall, Horton and Endon, late of Nicholas Daudele, tenant in chief, and in the king's hand by reason of the minority of his heir
2 CONC , which the escheator has taken into the king's hand on account of the death of William Martyn, to whom the king before committed the keeping thereof ; delivering any issues thereof received by him from 5 November last to Ralph de
2 CONC  Camoys or his attorney, pursuant to letters patent of that date wherein the king committed to the said Ralph the keeping of the said castle and manors until the full age of the heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Fine Rolls, 18 Edw. II, pp. 313, 319
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 17 Apr 1326, Kenilworth
2 CONT
2 CONT Presentation of Robert de Tauton to the church of Taustok, in the diocese of Exeter, in the king's gift by reason of his custody of the land and heir of William Martyn, tenant in chief.
2 CONT
2 CONT Calendar of Patent Rolls, Edw. II, vol. 5, p. 256
2 CONT
2 CONT    Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT William married Eleanor Fitz PIERS, daughter of Reynold (Reginald) Fitz PIERS and Alice de STANFORD, by Jan 1281/2 in Somerset, England. (Eleanor Fitz PIERS was born in Blaen Llyfni, Brecknockshire, Wales.)
2 CONT
2 CONT    Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Complete Peerage VIII:535-7; Calendar of Patent Rolls; Calendar of Close Rolls; Calendar of Fine Rolls; Calendar of Inquisitions Post Mortem, and other analogous documents, preserved in the Public Record Office, Vol. VI, Edward II
2 CONC , p. 358
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.celtic-casimir.com/webtree/14/36160.htm
