1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1295
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Peter Bartrum: Cydifor Fawr 16; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173378030042 & Cydrych 6; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173377996932 [based on his marriage to Nest f
2 CONC erch Gwilym Sais this Philip should date at c.1290, and Bartrum has assigned him to the wrong https://www.geni.com/people/Llewelyn-ab-Ifor-Lord-of-St-Clear-manor/6000000006444566084?through=6000000002603760016] (Steven Ferry, June
2 CONC  3, 2025.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Philip ap Llywelyn1 
2 CONT *'''M, #146455, b. circa 1330
2 CONT *Father      Llewelyn ap Ivor, Lord St. Clear1 b. c 1280
2 CONT *Mother     Angharad fil Morgan ap Meredith1 b. c 1298
2 CONT *'''     Philip ap Llywelyn was born circa 1330 at of Sain Pyr, Matharn, Monmouthshire, Wales, England.1 He married Nest verch Gwilym circa 1355 at England.1
2 CONT *'''Family      Nest verch Gwilym b. c 1331
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Gwenllian ferch Philip+1 b. c 1363
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p4877.htm#i146455 __________________
2 CONT *'''Phillip Ap LLYWELYN
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1334, Sain Pyr, Matharn, Monmouthshire, England 
2 CONT *Father: Llywelyn Ap IFOR
2 CONT *Mother: Angharad Verch MORGAN
2 CONT *'''Married: Nest Verch GWILYM (b. ABT 1338)
2 CONT *Children: 
2 CONT **1. Gwenllian Verch PHILLIP 
2 CONT **2. Dafydd Ap PHILLIP (b. ABT 1380) 
2 CONT **3. Gwilym Ap PHILLIP (b. ABT 1382) 
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/MORGAN.htm#Phillip Ap LLYWELYN1 _______________
2 CONT *'''Philip ap Llewellyn1 
2 CONT *M, #471582
2 CONT *Last Edited=10 Jun 2011 
2 CONT *'''     Philip ap Llewellyn is the son of Llewellyn ap Ivor and Angharad Meredyth.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerage 1884-1971: Containing Extinct, Abeyant, Dormant and Suspended Peerages With Genealogies and Arms (London, U.K.: Heraldry Today, 1972), page 271. Hereinafter cited as The New Extinct Pe
2 CONC erage.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p47159.htm#i471582 _______________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry ; or, Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland enjoying territorial possessions or high official rank : but uninvested with heritable honours (1837) Vol. 1
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera01inburk
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera01inburk#page/222/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.222
2 CONT *   LEWELLEN, Lord of St. Clare and Gwynvaye, in the county of Carmarthen, who m. Angharad, daughter and co-heir of Sir Morgan Meredith, Lord of Tredegar, descended from RHYS, King of South Wales, and had two sons, viz. 
2 CONT **	MORGAN, Lord of St. Clare and Tredegar, from whom derived the Morgans of Tredegar. 
2 CONT *And 
2 CONT *'''   PHILIP LLEWELIN AP IVOR, who bore for his armorial ensigns, arg. a lion rampant gardant crowned ppr.(f)  He m. Neste, daughter and heiress of Gwilim Sayes ap Madog ap Howell Velyn, and his great-great-great-great grandson, 
2 CONT *   HENRY LEWIS, esq. of St. Pierre, living in 1547, espoused Bridget, daughter and heiress of Thomas(|) Kemeys, and was father of ....
2 CONT **	(|) The Harleian MSS. style this person GEORGE Kemeys. _____________________________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic dictionary of the peerage and baronetage of the British Empire (1869)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera00inburk
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera00inburk#page/1115/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.1115
2 CONT *   LLEWELLYN AP IVOR, lineally descended from Cadivor Vawr, Lord of Kilsaint, m. Angharad, dau. and co-heir fo Sir Morgan Meredith, Lord of Tredegar (descended from Rhys, Prince of South Wales), and thus acquired the Tredegar est
2 CONC ates. Llewellin was father of three sons, viz,
2 CONT **	MORGAN, his heir.
2 CONT **	Ivor, of Werncleppa, or Gwerney Cleppa, near Tredegar, ancestor of the MORGANS of Werncleppa, whose last male heir, Roger Morgan, Esq., d. in 1632, when his estate passed to the Tredegar family.
2 CONT **'''	Philip, whose son, DAVID AP PHILIP AP LLEWELLIN, seated at St. Pierrer, in the county of Monmouth, was ancestor of the family of LEWIS of St. Pierre. (See BURKE'S Landed Gentry.)
2 CONT *The eldest son,
2 CONT *   MORGAN AP LLEWELLIN, Lord of St. Clere, in Carmarthenshire, and of Tredegar, co. Monmouth, m. Maud, dau. of Rhys ap Gronwy, Lord of Kybor, and had two sons, .... _____________________________________________
2 CONT *'''A history of the family of Morgan, from the year 1089 to present times ([1902?])
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/historyoffamilyo00morg
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00morg#page/13/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.13
2 CONT *   VIII. LLEWELYN ap IVOR of Tredegar, Lord of St Clear, married Angharad, daughter of Sir Morgan ap Meredith, from the Welsh Lords of Caerleon, ap Griffith ap Meredith ap Rhys, who bore "Argent a lion rampant sable." Sir Morgan 
2 CONC died 1332, when Angharad was aged 32. They had : 1. Morgan. 2. Ivor Hael, whence MORGAN OF GWERN-Y-CLEPPA. 3. '''Philip, whence LEWIS OF ST. PIERRE.''' 
2 CONT *   IX. MORGAN of Tredegar and St. Clear, married Maud, daugter of Rhun ap Grono ap Llwarch, Lord of Cibwr. He died before 1384. Issue: 1. Llewelyn. 2. Philip, whence MORGAN OF LANGSTONE. 3. John, father of Gwenllian, married Davi
2 CONC d Goch ap David, 4. Christian, married Jevan ap Jenkin Kemeys. 5. Ann, married David Gwilim David of Rhiwperra. 6. Margaret, married Traherne ap Meyric of Merthyr. 7. A daughter, married Thomas ap Gwillim of Carnllwyd. 8. Elenor, 
2 CONC married Grono ap Howel Bennet.  __________________________________
2 CONT *Links
2 CONT * http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~pholling/aqwg41.htm#1110
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________
