0 @N6000000002248181444@ NOTE Heir to his grandfather, he was still under age in 1227, and obtained possession of his lands in 1234. In 1236, he confirmed his grandfather's gift of the advowson of Shipton church to Bruton and in Jul 1244 made a grant to Christ
1 CONC  church in Hampshire. In 1255 he served with Prince Edward in Wales, and was summoned for service there from 1257 to 1264. He appears to have been knighted by 1258, and in 1259, and again in 1269, he made an agreement with his unc
1 CONC le, Philip Basset, and Ela, Philip's wife, respecting Thurlbear and other manors. At his death, custody of his lands was granted to Philip Basset.
0 @N6000000003949636515@ NOTE grandson and heir of William, and son of Drew and Aline. He was still under age in 1227, and in 1232-33 was amerced for not taking knighthood. He was heir to his father and his grandfather, and obtained possession of his lands in 
1 CONC 1234. In 1236 he confirmed his grandfather's gift of the advowson of Shipton church to Bruton, and in July 1244 made a grant to Christchurch, Hants. He was pardoned a forest trespass in Somerset in 1247. In 1255 he was serving wit
1 CONC h Prince Edward in Wales, and was summoned for service there from 1257 to 1264. He seems to have been knighted by 1258. In 1259, and again in 1269, he made an agreement with his uncle Philip Basset, and Ela, Countess of Warwick, P
1 CONC hilip's wife, respecting Thurlbear and other manors. He married Berthe, whose parentage is not known (m). He died 23 September 1270. The custody of his lands was granted to Philip Basset.
