0 @N6000000003949783715@ NOTE For evidence of the parentage of Aline de Gay, wife of Alan Basset, I direct your attention to an agreement made in King Henry II's court in 1190, regarding the division of Philip de Gay's estate, which agreement was re-confirmed 
1 CONC by King Henry II's son, King Richard, in
1 CONT 1198.   A copy of the reconfirmation is provided below:
1 CONT 383 (2735R).  Aline and Cecily de Gay.  Resealing of confirmation (Vezelay, 3rd July 1190) of agreement in Henry II's court concerning division of inheritance from their father, Philip de Gay.  Cecily is to have all the land in No
1 CONC rbroch' [Northbrook], and quit claims the
1 CONT rest to Aline; if either dies without legitimate issue, the other party shall inherit.
1 CONT It appears that Cecily, sister of Aline de Gay, died without issue soon after 1198.  As best I can determine, Aline and her husband, Alan Basset, later held all of the Gay family holdings, including Northbrook which was assigned t
1 CONC o Cecily.  These lands passed by
1 CONT descent from the Basset family onto the Despenser family.
