0 @N6000000002188011430@ NOTE William de Beauchamp, 9th Earl of Warwick
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT William de Beauchamp, 9th Earl of Warwick (1237-1298) was an English nobleman and soldier, described as a “vigorous and innovative military commander”[1]. He was active in the field against the Welsh for many years, and at the end
1 CONC  of his life campaigned against the Scots.
1 CONT Contents
1 CONT [hide]
1 CONT
1 CONT     * 1 Soldier
1 CONT     * 2 Family
1 CONT     * 3 Notes
1 CONT     * 4 External links
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Soldier
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a close friend of Edward I of England, and was an important leader in Edward's invasion of Wales in 1277.[2][3] In 1294 he raised the siege of Conwy Castle, where the King had been penned in[4], crossing the estuary[5]. He 
1 CONC was victorious on March 5, 1295 at the battle of Maes Madog, against Madog ap Llywelyn[6]. In a night attack on the Welsh infantry, he used cavalry to drive them into compact formations, which were then shot up by his archers, and
1 CONC  charged[7].
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT His father was William de Beauchamp of Elmley, his mother Isabel Mauduit, sister and heiress of William Mauduit, 8th Earl of Warwick.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Maud FitzGeoffrey. His children included:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Isabella[8], married Hugh le Despenser, Earl of Winchester
1 CONT     * Guy, who married Alice de Toeni, widow of Thomas de Leyburne
1 CONT     * Sarah[9]
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Notes
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. ^ CHAP1
1 CONT    2. ^ F. M. Powicke, The Thirteenth Century (1962 edition), p. 409.
1 CONT    3. ^ Osprey Publishing - The Castles of Edward I in Wales 1277–1307
1 CONT    4. ^ Welsh Castles - Conwy Castle
1 CONT    5. ^ T. F. Tout, The History of England From the Accession of Henry III. to the Death of Edward III (1216-1377) , online.
1 CONT    6. ^ R. R. Davies, The Age of Conquest: Wales 1063-1415 (1991), p. 383.
1 CONT    7. ^ Powicke, p. 442-3.
1 CONT    8. ^ thePeerage.com - Person Page 10687
1 CONT    9. ^ thePeerage.com - Person Page 21562
