0 @N6000000003216133544@ NOTE Attempted to take certain estates in Scotland by right of his wife and took part in the invasion of Scotland by William Balliol in 1332. He helped defeat the Scots at the Battle of Dupplin Moor (1332) but was captured by the Scots
1 CONC  in 1334 though ransomed the following year. Appoined Keeper of Berwick-on-Tweed 1337-55, Chief Keeper of Southampton 1340, Chief Justice of Gloucestershire and Worcestershire 1341, Captain in the army that defeated the French at 
1 CONC the Battle of Morlaix (1342) and was present at the Battle of Crecy and the following siege of Calais 1346-7. Granted the post of Steward of the King's Household in 1345 and made Keeper of Pembroke and Tenby Castles 1349-51.
1 CONT 2nd Baron Talbot, K.B.
