0 @N6000000000337421207@ NOTE Weis, p. 151; 203:  Prince of North Wales;  he married, secondly, outside the church, his cousin, Christina verch Gronw ap Owen ap Edwin. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #2:  Ellis Peters, "Dead Man's Ransom" (New York:  Mysterious Press, 1984), pp. 55-56.
1 CONT
1 CONT This fine historical novelist paints this picture:  "Cadfael had seen him once before, a few years past, [NOTE: this story is set in 1141] and he was not a man to be easily forgotten, for all he made very little ado about state an
1 CONC d ceremony, barring the obvious royalty he bore about his own person.  He was barely thirty-seven years old, in his vigorous prime; very tall for a Welshman, and fair, after his grandmother Ragnhild of the Danish kingdom of Dublin
1 CONC , and his mother Angharad, known for her flaxen hair the dark women of the south."  
0 @N6000000000437138873@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> Prince Of The Welsh, Prince Of Gwynedd From:  Gendex, http://www.gendex.com/users/jast/D0043/G0000077.html#I2586
