1 CONC nd Volume IV; Ashmole's Berkshire Vol. III, ps. 7 and 16; Visitations of London, Vol. 15, p. 40; Harlean Society Publications; The Fowler Family by Robert Fowler, p. 44, note 13; The Fowler Arms, which can be found on p. 44 of The
1 CONC  Fowler Family, by Lucy Charlotte Fowler, published in 1899, by her sister, Jean E. Fowler of Gastard House, Corsham, co. Wilt, England; English Baronetage by Thomas Wotton, printed in 1741, Vol. LV, ps. 102-03, number 2101 b as t
1 CONC he libraries were arranged in the British Museum in London; Burke's Commoners Vol. II, p. 385, edition of 1834; The House of Fowler, pub. 1940, p. 19; NEHGR, Vol. XI--Descendants of Ambrose Fowler of Windsor, Conn. I don't know to
1 CONC  what these refs. refer.
