1 CONT Ralph de Mortimer
1 CONT
1 CONT Ranulph or Ralph de Mortimer (c. 1190 – August 6, 1246) was lord of Wigmore and a member of the Mortimer family, one of the main powers in the Welsh Marches. He was the son of Roger de Mortimer and Isabel de Ferrieres.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1230, Ralph married Gwladus Ddu, daughter of Llywelyn the Great. On Ralph's death in 1246 he was succeeded by their eldest son, Roger de Mortimer.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT Roger de Mortimer, 1st Baron Wigmore 
1 CONT Hugh de Mortimer 
1 CONT John de Mortimer 
1 CONT Peter de Mortimer 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT John Edward Lloyd (1911) A history of Wales from the earliest times to the Edwardian conquest (Longmans, Green & Co.) 
