1 CONT Died of Food Poisoning
1 CONT
1 CONT  The only legitimate son of England's King, Henry I, drowns off Harfleur in the White Ship disaster of 1120.
1 CONT
1 CONT  Having just returned from the First Crusade, Robert Curthose invades England in 1101, attempting to take the throne from his brother, Henry I.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ref: 1100-35
1 CONT Ref: Henry Duke Councilor His Descendants and Connections, WFT. Genealogy Library.
1 CONT Approx-- 7 other Concubine's found.--
1 CONT Ref: Fourth and Youngest Son of William , riegned for 35 years.
1 CONT King Henry died while on a visit to Normandy and in his will named his favorite daughter, Matilda , as heir to all of his dominions.
1 CONT No sooner had Henry breathed his last than Stephen (Son of Adela,daughterof King William) hastened to England and with the influence of some Barons induced William, Archbishop of Canterbury, to crown
1 CONT  Stephen Kingof England.
1 CONT Ref; "Medieval GEDCOM Files", By, Marilyn R. Lewis
