0 @N6000000002188011289@ NOTE Maud Chaworth
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Matilda de Chaworth, Countess of Lancaster and Countess of Leicester (1282–1322) was the daughter of Sir Patrick de Chaworth and Lady Isabella de Beauchamp, daughter of William de Beauchamp, 9th Earl of Warwick. Her half-brother w
1 CONC as the notorious Hugh the younger Despenser. In 1297, she married Henry Plantagenet, 3rd Earl of Leicester, one of the principals behind the deposition of King Edward II. He was the younger son of Blanche of Artois and Edmund Crou
1 CONC chback, 1st Earl of Lancaster, Earl of Leicester, and was thus the grandson of Henry III of England and Eleanor of Provence.
1 CONT
1 CONT Maud and Henry had seven children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry of Grosmont, 1st Duke of Lancaster, (about 1300–1360/61); 
1 CONT Blanche of Lancaster, (about 1305–1380); 
1 CONT Maud of Lancaster, (about 1310–1377); married William de Burgh, 3rd Earl of Ulster 
1 CONT Joan of Lancaster, (about 1312–1345); 
1 CONT Isabel of Lancaster, Abbess of Ambresbury, (about 1317–after 1347); 
1 CONT Eleanor of Lancaster, (1318–22 Sept. 1371/72), married (1) John De Beaumont and (2) 5 Feb. 1344/5, Richard FitzAlan, 10th Earl of Arundel; 
1 CONT Mary of Lancaster, (about 1320–1362), who married Henry, 3rd Baron Percy and was the mother of Henry Percy, 1st Earl of Northumberland. 
