1 CONT [S6 <s1.htm>] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VIII, page 402.
0 @N6000000002187738276@ NOTE Domhnall I of Mar
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Domhnall I of Mar - Domhnall mac Uilleim (Donald, William's son) - was the seventh known Mormaer of Mar, ruling from 1276 until his death somewhere between 1297 and 1302.
1 CONT
1 CONT Domhnall was a strong supporter of the Bruce cause during the crisis of the late 13th century. He was at Norham in 1292, probably in the camp of Robert de Brus, then Mormaer or Earl of Carrick.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was married to Helen, the daughter of Llywelyn ap Iorwerth, who herself had previously been married to Mormaer Maol Chaluim II of Fife. By Helen, he had three sons, including his successor Gartnait, and two daughters. His daugh
1 CONC ter Isabella of Mar was the first wife of Robert I of Scotland and mother of Marjorie Bruce.
1 CONT
1 CONT The last record of a living Domhnall comes from 1297, and the earliest record of his son Gartnait as Mormaer is from 1305, creating the range of Domhnall's possible year of death to somewhere in between these two points. However, 
1 CONC a document dating to 1302,1 containing terms of reconciliation between Edward I and Robert, stipulates that Robert should act as warden of Gartnait, implying that Domhnall had just died.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT References
1 CONT 1. Barrow, Robert Bruce, pp. 122-3 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Bibliography
1 CONT Barrow, G.W.S., Robert Bruce and the Community of the Realm of Scotland, (Edinburgh, 1988)
