0 @N6000000001220381481@ NOTE [2753682.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT !Died from a fall from a horse. [Magna Charta Sureties]
1 CONT
1 CONT WAITE, FOSTER LINES - 22nd ggrandfather
1 CONT
1 CONT !Born after 1210. [Ped. of Charlemagne]
1 CONT
1 CONT Son of William de Broase and Maud de Clare; m.c. 1219, Margaret verch Llewellyn. [Ancestral R oots, p. 31]
1 CONT
1 CONT John de Braose, lord of Bramber, Gower and Tetbury, fell from his horse at Bramber in 1232. T he Brut y Tywysogyon says he "was drawn at his own horse's tail; and so he met a cruel death. " John's heir, William was only 12 when Jo
1 CONC hn died.
1 CONT    William de Braose arranged for the safekeeping of his eldest grandson John in Gower.
1 CONT    John de Braose was known to the Welsh as "tadody" or "fatherless child". He challenged hi s uncle Reginald in persistent lawsuits, demanding the inheritance of his father who was unju stly starved to death at Windsor.
1 CONT    Llywelyn gave Gower to John as a dowry for his daughter and created a rival de Braose powe r in the Welsh marches. The lawsuits were settled after John came of age and he was able to p urchase Bramber and Tetbury from Reginald.
1 CONC  The king gave John charge of Whitecastle, Grosmon t and Skenfrith castles in 1228. ["Barons de Braose" <http://freespace.virgin.net/doug/thomps on/BraoseWeb/stage.htm]
1 CONT
1 CONT b.c. 1204, d. 18 Jul 1232; son of William IV de Braose and Maud or Matilda de Fay de Clare; m . Margred verch Llywelyn; father of:
1 CONT 1. John
1 CONT 2. William V who m. Aline Multon and Mary de Ros
1 CONT 3. Llywelyn
1 CONT 4. Roger
1 CONT 5. Hugh
1 CONT 6. Richard who m. Alice de Rus
1 CONT  [dfox <pifox@shentel.net, 30 Mar 2002]
