1 CONC 00.mcc.ac.uk/genuk/big/eng/History/Barons/baronsl. html]
1 CONT
1 CONT m. Margaret of Wales; father of Maud who m. John Gifford. [WFT vol 11 Ped 3809]
1 CONT
1 CONT It was probably Richard FitzPons's great-grandson, William (Walter???) Clifford III (1221-63 ) who was responsible for building the stone round keep at Bronllys Castle on the original mo tte or mound. [The Castles of Wales, p. 43]
1 CONT
1 CONT The spirit of this family was exemplified by a second Walter de Clifford who, during a quarre ll with his sovereign in 1250, caused the King's messenger to 'eate the King's Writ, Waxe an d All'! [Skipton Castle]
1 CONT
1 CONT Eldest son; m. Margaret, dau of Llewelyn, Prince of Wales, and left an only daughter, Maud. [ The Diaries of Lady Anne Clifford, p. 5]
1 CONT
