1 CONT James de Alditheley was a great favorite of Richard, Earl ofCornwall, at whose coronation as King of Almaine (Germany) he assisted. He hadlivery of his lands in the 31st year of King Henry III., and was constituted in two years af
1 CONC terwards constable of Newcastle-under-Lyne. Being one the lords-marchers he was actively employed for some years against the Welsh, and was appointed governor of the castles of Salop and Bridgenorth, and sheriff of the counties of
1 CONC  Salop and Stafford. He was the Justice of Chester, sealed 1259. In the47th year of Henry III., he was made Justice of Ireland; and in the same year,upon the misunderstanding between the king and the barons, regarding the provisio
1 CONC ns of Oxford, being referred to the arbitration of monarch of France, he wasone of the noblemen who undertook for the king therein. The next year we find him with Roger de Mortimer and the other barons-marchers, giving battle to L
1 CONC lewellyn, Prince of Wales, and afterwards joining the Earl of Gloucester at Eveshamin rescuing the king, who had become captive to the Earl of Leicester at the battle of Lewes. In the 52nd year of Henry III., he performed a pilgri
1 CONC mage to the shrine of St. James in Galicia, in Spain, and the following year embarked inthe Crusade with the king and Prince Edward. He married Ela, daughter of William Longespee, Earl of Salisbury. She was living in 1282. [HBJ] H
1 CONC e died of a broken neck. .. +Ela Longespee b: Abt. 1228 in of Stratton Audley & Wretchwick, OXF, ENG m: 1244 d: Abt. 22 November 1299 3 Alice de Aldithley b: 1225 in of Staffordshire, ENG .. +Piers de Montfort b: Abt. 1215 in of B
1 CONC eaudesert Castle, WAR,ENG d: 04 August 1265 in Worcestershire, ENG@S193@
