0 @N6000000003949866191@ NOTE  In May 1320 Elizabeth, his widow renounced her dower in certain lands. She married, 8 June 1322, Sir Thomas DE FURNIVALLE, of Sheffield, Worksop, &c. (LORD FURNIVALLE], who died shortly before 18 April 1332. She died in August 13
1 CONC 54, and was buried in the Prior of St. Frideswide (now Christ Church), Oxford, where her tomb is still to be seen in the Latin Chapel. See FURNIVALLE. [Complete Peerage IX:80-2, XIV:482, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
