0 @N6000000002188011999@ NOTE Henry de Beaumont, 5th Earl of Warwick
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry de Beaumont, 5th Earl of Warwick (1192 – 10 October 1229), Earl of Warwick, Baron of Hocknorton and Hedenton, was the son of Waleran de Beaumont, 4th Earl of Warwick and Margaret, daughter of Henry de Bohun, 1st Earl of Here
1 CONC ford and Maud of Essex. He was also known as Henry de Newburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT When Henry was 12 his father died and he was committed to the care of Thomas Basset of Headington, Oxon. It was during this time that the King had seized his estates at Gower in South Wales and gave them to William de Braose. This
1 CONC  led to constant disputes between succeeding Earls and the Braose family. When he matured, he joined the court of King John's side and commanded the Royal Army. He fought for Henry III at the sieges of Montsorel and Biham and at t
1 CONC he storming of Lincoln. In 1213 he paid two hundred and four marks eight shillings scutage towards the cost of the war in Wales, and the following year contributed forty two marks to that in Poictou.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family and children
1 CONT He married firstly Margaret, daughter and co-heiress of Henry D'Oili, Baron Hocknorton and Lord of the Manor of Lidney; the latter was a great-nephew of Robert D'Oili, the builder of Oxford Castle. Henry married secondly Philippa,
1 CONC  daughter and co-heiress of Thomas Basset, Lord of Hedenton. She married secondly Richard Siward, but divorced him in 1242. He had children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas de Beaumont, 6th Earl of Warwick, his heir. 
1 CONT Margaret de Newburg, Countess of Warwick, married twice: 
1 CONT John Marshal, Earl of Pembroke; 
1 CONT John du Plessis, 7th Earl of Warwick. 
1 CONT Alice de Newburg, married Hugo de Bastenbrege, Lord of Montfort. 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT Edward T. Beaumont, J.P. The Beaumonts in History. A.D. 850-1850. Oxfor
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Waleran de Beaumont Earl of Warwick
1 CONT 1204 – 1229 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Thomas de Beaumont 
0 @N6000000000337437268@ NOTE Source #1:  George Edward Cokayne, "The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant or Dormant," New Edition, Revised and Much Enlarged, Edited by The Hon. Vicary Gibbs and H. A. Do
1 CONC ubleday (London:  The St. Catherine Press, 1926), Vol V, pp. 305-310 and the genealogical diagram of Ferrers of Chartley and allied familes between pp. 320-321.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #2:  Frederick Lewis Weis, "Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700" - Seventh Edition, with additions and corrections by Walter Lee Sheppard, Jr., assisted by Davis Faris (Baltimore, M
1 CONC D:  Genealogical Publishing Co, 1995), p. 161; 198
1 CONT
