1 CONC er, fitzHamon is also described as the alleged grandson of Hamo Dentatus (â€˜The Toothy', i.e., probably buck-toothed).[1]. The second explanation might make sense if his father were also named Hamon and thus confused with the gra
1 CONC ndfather and namesake Hamon, Count of Corbeil.
