1 CONC , Duke of Normandy, later styled "The Conqueror". Robert and his father were thus kin to the Conqueror although this connection does not appear to have profited Robert significantly until 1087 when his cousin William Rufus ascende
1 CONC d the throne.
1 CONT Robert's mother is said to have been Halwisa (or Hawisa) alias Elisabeth d'Avoye, widow of Hugh Magnus, Prince of France and later co-king of France (elder brother of Henry I of France) and daughter of one Henri l'Oiseteur.
1 CONT He was a cousin of William the Conqueror, although the details of his descent from the Norman dukes is uncertain. His family held the lordships of Torigny, Creully, Mazy, and Evrecy in Normandy.
