1 CONT Peter Fitz-Herbert, who, being very obsequious to King John, was reputed one of that prince's evil counsellors. In 1214, he was constitutedgovernor of Pykering Castle, co. York, and sheriff of the shire; but afterwards falling off
1 CONC  in his allegiance, his lands at Alcester were seized by the crown, and given to William de Camvill. Returning, however, to his duty upon the accession of Henry III, those lands were restored to him. He m. 1st, Alice, dau. of Roge
