1 CONT Isabella Despenser's marriage to FitzAlan was later annulled on the petiti
1 CONT on of her husband, who claimed that he had been coerced intothe union f
1 CONT or political reasons (i.e., her father's ambition). The son and two daught
1 CONT ers that had been born to them were specifically bastardized by the annulm
1 CONT ent decree. I can't remember offhand if either of the daughters ever marri
1 CONT ed, but the son did, and his descendants used the surname Arundell (S
