1 CONC  Lord Lancaster. He took part in the siege of Carlaverock in July 1300.
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas was convicted of treason, executed and his lands and titles forfeited in 1322. But Henry, who had not participated in his brother's rebellion, petitioned for his brother's lands and titles, and on March 29, 1324 he was inve
1 CONC sted as Earl of Leicester, and a few years later the earldom of Lancaster was also restored to him.
1 CONT
1 CONT On the Queen’s return to England with Roger Mortimer, 1st Earl of March in September 1326, Henry joined her party against Edward II, which led to a general desertion of the king’s cause and overturned the power of Hugh le Despense
1 CONC r, 1st Earl of Winchester and his namesake son Hugh the younger Despenser. He was sent in pursuit and captured the king at Neath. He was appointed to take charge of the King, and was responsible for his custody at Kenilworth Castl
1 CONC e.
1 CONT
1 CONT After Edward II's death Henry was appointed guardian of the new king Edward III of England, and was also appointed captain-general of all the King's forces in the Scottish marches.
1 CONT
1 CONT In about the year 1330, he became blind.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was succeeded as Earl of Lancaster and Leicester by his eldest son, Henry of Grosmont, who subsequently became Duke of Lancaster.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married once, to Maud Chaworth, before 2 March 1296/1297. (Some references claim he married Alix de Joinville, but she in fact married Henry's brother John.) With Maud he had seven children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry of Grosmont, 1st Duke of Lancaster, (about 1300-1360/61) 
1 CONT Blanche of Lancaster, (about 1305 - 1380) 
1 CONT Maud of Lancaster, (about 1310-1377) 
1 CONT Joan of Lancaster, (about 1312-1345) 
1 CONT Isabel of Lancaster, Abbess of Ambresbury, (about 1317-after 1347) 
1 CONT Eleanor of Lancaster, (about 1318-1371/72) 
1 CONT Mary of Lancaster, (about 1320-1362), who married Henry, 3rd Baron Percy and was the mother of Henry Percy, 1st Earl of Northumberland. 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT The Earl of Leicester and Lancaster Lord High Steward
1 CONT 1324–1345 Succeeded by:
1 CONT The Duke of Lancaster 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Thomas Earl of Leicester and Lancaster Succeeded by:
1 CONT Henry of Grosmont 
