0 @N6000000005076571829@ NOTE 1st Duke of Lancaster
1 CONT
1 CONT from thePeerage.com:
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry Grosmont of Derby Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Lancaster was born between 1299 and 1314 at Grosmont Castle, Monmouthshire, Wales.1 He was the son of Henry Plantagenet, 3rd Earl of Lancaster and Matilda de Chaworth. He married Is
1 CONC abella de Beaumont, daughter of Henry Beaumont, 1st Earl of Buchan and Alice Comyn, circa 1337.2 He died on 24 March 1360/61 at Leicester Castle, Leicester, Leicestershire, England, from the bubonic plague.1,2 He was buried at New
1 CONC ark Abbey, Leicester, Leicestershire, England.1
1 CONT      Henry Grosmont of Derby Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Lancaster gained the title of Earl of Derby on 16 March 1337.1 He gained the title of Earl of Leicester on 22 September 1345.1 He gained the title of Lord of Beaufort and Nogen
1 CONC t on 22 September 1345.1 He succeeded to the title of Earl of Lancaster on 22 September 1345.1 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) in 1348.1 He gained the title of Earl of Lincoln on 20 August 1349.1 He gained 
1 CONC the title of 1st Duke of Lancaster on 6 March 1351.1 He gained the title of Earl of Moray on 5 April 1359.1
1 CONT Children of Henry Grosmont of Derby Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Lancaster and Isabella de Beaumont
1 CONT Matilda Plantagenet, Countess of Leicester b. 4 Apr 1339, d. 10 Apr 13622
1 CONT Blanche of Lancaster, Countess of Derby+ b. 25 Mar 1345, d. 12 Sep 13692
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 76. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
1 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 228. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 1
1 CONC 06th edition.
