1 CONC 1322).
1 CONT
1 CONT First marriage and offspring
1 CONT Sometime between September 1 and November 6, 1330, she married John Beaumont, 2nd Lord Beaumont, son of Henry Beaumont, 4th Earl of Buchan (c. 1288 - 1340) and his wife Alice Comyn (c. 1291-1349). They had two children:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1. Henry Beaumont, 3rd Lord Beaumont, born late 1339
1 CONT 2. Matilda Beaumont (died July 1467), married Hugh de Courtenay
1 CONT
1 CONT Eleanor was a lady-in-waiting to Queen Philippa, and was in service to her in Ghent when her son Henry was born. John de Beaumont died in a tournament on 14 April 1342.
1 CONT
1 CONT Second marriage
1 CONT
1 CONT On 5 February 1344 at Ditton Church, Stoke Poges, Buckinghamshire, she married Richard Fitzalan, 10th Earl of Arundel, 4th Earl of Surrey, known by the soubriquet of "Copped Hat", Justiciar of North Wales, Governor of Carnarvon Ca
1 CONC stle, Admiral of the West.(2)
1 CONT
1 CONT His previous marriage, to Isabel le Despenser, had taken place when they were children. It was annulled by Papal mandate as she, since her father's attainder and execution, had ceased to be of any importance to him. Pope Clement V
1 CONC I obligingly annulled the marriage, bastardized the issue, and provided a dispensation for his second marriage to the woman with whom he had been living in adultery (the dispensation, dated 4 March 1344/1345, was required because 
1 CONC his first and second wives were first cousins).
1 CONT
