1 CONT 2. John Fitzalan(bef 1349-1379)
1 CONT 3. Thomas Arundel, Archbishop of York (c. 1350-February 19, 1413)
1 CONT 4. Joan Fitzalan (bef. 1351-April 17, 1419), married Humphrey de Bohun, 7th Earl of Hereford
1 CONT 5. Alice Fitzalan (1352-March 17, 1416), married Thomas Holland, 2nd Earl of Kent
1 CONT
1 CONT Eleanor died at Arundel and was buried at Lewes Priory in Lewes, Sussex, England. Her husband was buried beside her; in his will Richard requests to be buried "near to the tomb of Eleanor de Lancaster, my wife; and I desire that m
1 CONC y tomb be no higher than hers, that no men at arms, horses, hearse, or other pomp, be used at my funeral, but only five torches...as was about the corpse of my wife, be allowed."
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT
1 CONT * Fowler, Kenneth. The King's Lieutenant, 1969
1 CONT * Nicolas, Nicholas Harris. Testamenta Vetusta, 1826.
1 CONT
1 CONT Notes
1 CONT
1 CONT * 1The surname "Plantagenet" has been retrospectively applied to the descendants of Geoffrey V, Count of Anjou and Empress Matilda without historical justification: it is simply a convenient, if deceptive, method of referring to p
1 CONC eople who had, in fact, no surname. The first descendant of Geoffrey to use the surname was Richard Plantagenet, 3rd Duke of York (father of both Edward IV of England and Richard III of England) who apparently assumed it about 144
1 CONC 8.
1 CONT * 2also called Richard de Arundel.
0 @N6000000003484298326@ NOTE (Research):>Death note: Death Surety:2
0 @N6000000006296781837@ NOTE Eleanor of Lancaster (sometimes called Eleanor Plantagenet </wiki/Plantagenet>[1]; 11 September 1311 - 11 January 1372) was the fifth daughter of Henry Plantagenet, 3rd Earl of Lancaster </wiki/Henry_Plantagenet,_3rd_Earl_of_Lanca
1 CONC ster> and his wife.
1 CONT 6 November 1330, she married John de Beaumont, 2nd Lord Beaumont </w/index.php?title=John_de_Beaumont,_2nd_Lord_Beaumont&action=edit&redlink=1>, son of Henry Beaumont, 4th Earl of Buchan </wiki/Henry_Beaumont,_4th_Earl_of_Buchan> 
1 CONC (c. 1288 - 1340) and his wife Alice Comyn </wiki/Alice_Comyn> (1289- 3 July 1349). They had two children:
1 CONT Henry Beaumont, 3rd Lord Beaumont </w/index.php?title=Henry_Beaumont,_3rd_Lord_Beaumont&action=edit&redlink=1>, (4 April 1340 - 17 June 1369), married as her first husband, Margaret de Vere </wiki/Maud_de_Badlesmere> (died 15 June
1 CONC  1398), by whom he had issue.
1 CONT Matilda Beaumont (died July 1367), married Hugh de Courtenay
1 CONT Eleanor was a lady-in-waiting to Queen Philippa </wiki/Philippa_of_Hainault>, and was in service to her in Ghent when her son Henry was born. John de Beaumont died in a tournament on 14 April 1342.
1 CONT On 5 February 1344 at Ditton Church </w/index.php?title=Ditton_Church&action=edit&redlink=1>, Stoke Poges </wiki/Stoke_Poges>, Buckinghamshire </wiki/Buckinghamshire>, she married Richard FitzAlan, 10th Earl of Arundel </wiki/Rich
1 CONC ard_FitzAlan,_10th_Earl_of_Arundel>.[2]
1 CONT His previous marriage, to Isabel le Despenser </wiki/Isabel_le_Despenser>, had taken place when they were children. It was annulled </wiki/Annul> by Papal mandate as she, since her father's attainder </wiki/Attainder> and executio
1 CONC n, had ceased to be of any importance to him. Pope Clement VI </wiki/Pope_Clement_VI> obligingly annulled the marriage, bastardized </wiki/Illegitimacy> the issue, and provided a dispensation </wiki/Dispensation> for his second ma
1 CONC rriage to the woman with whom he had been living in adultery (the dispensation, dated 4 March 1344/1345, was required because his first and second wives were first cousins).
1 CONT The children of Eleanor's second marriage were:
1 CONT Richard </wiki/Richard_FitzAlan,_11th_Earl_of_Arundel> (1346 - 1397), who succeeded as Earl of Arundel </wiki/Earl_of_Arundel>
1 CONT John Fitzalan </wiki/John_FitzAlan,_1st_Baron_Arundel> (bef 1349 - 1379)
1 CONT Thomas Arundel </wiki/Thomas_Arundel>, Archbishop of Canterbury </wiki/Archbishop_of_Canterbury> (c. 1345 - 19 February 1413)
1 CONT Joan Fitzalan </wiki/Joan_Fitzalan> (1347/1348 - 7 April 1419), married Humphrey de Bohun, 7th Earl of Hereford </wiki/Humphrey_de_Bohun,_7th_Earl_of_Hereford>
1 CONT Alice Fitzalan </wiki/Alice_Fitzalan> (1350 - 17 March 1416), married Thomas Holland, 2nd Earl of Kent </wiki/Thomas_Holland,_2nd_Earl_of_Kent> (Thomas Holand)
1 CONT Mary Fitzalan (died 29 August 1396), married John Le Strange, 4th Lord Strange of Blackmere </w/index.php?title=John_Le_Strange,_4th_Lord_Strange_of_Blackmere&action=edit&redlink=1>, by whom she had issue
1 CONT Eleanor Fitzalan (1356 - before 1366)
1 CONT Eleanor died at Arundel </wiki/Arundel> and was buried at Lewes Priory </wiki/Lewes_Priory> in Lewes </wiki/Lewes>, Sussex </wiki/Sussex>, England. Her husband was buried beside her; in his will Richard requests to be buried "near
1 CONC  to the tomb of Eleanor de Lancaster, my wife; and I desire that my tomb be no higher than hers, that no men at arms, horses, hearse, or other pomp, be used at my funeral, but only five torches...as was about the corpse of my wife
1 CONC , be allowed."
