0 @N6000000003949736310@ NOTE Roger Beauchamp, grandson and heir [of Roger 1st Baron de Beauchamp], being son and heir of Roger Beauchamp, who dvp. 1373/4 (his wife was granted letters of admin. 15 May 1374), son and heir of the 1st Baron. He was never summone
1 CONC d to Parliament nor were any of his descendants. He was b. at Bletsoe, bap. 14 Aug 1362, and was aged 17 in 1380, and made proof of his age in 1384, when he had livery of his lands, viz. Blesoe, co. Bedford, Bloxham and Spelsbury,
1 CONC  Oxon, and Lydiard Tregoz, WIlts. He was knighted by 18 Feb 1393. In 1395 he attended the King into Ireland. In 1399, MP for Beds. He m. Joan Clopton. He d. 13 May 1406, will dated 1406, PCC 11 March. [Complete Peerage II:45, XIV:
1 CONC 75]
1 CONT Note: CP XIV:75 states that he didn't marry Joan Clopton, but an unknown "Mary", while his father m. Joan Clopton, daughter of Walter Clopton, but she was his father's 2nd wife and not mother of this Roger. @@check ancestry.
1 CONT Note: CP does not name him a Baron, even though he was grandson and heir of the 1st Baron, which is a hereditary title. Also volume XIV corrected volume II to state that he was MP in 1399.
