1 CONT
1 CONT James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde
1 CONT
1 CONT James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde was born circa 1305[citation needed] and died on 6 January 1337. He was the son of Sir Edmond Butler and Lady Joan FitzGerald. He married Eleanor de Bohun, daughter of Humphrey de Bohun, 4th Earl 
1 CONC of Hereford and Lady Elizabeth Plantagenet, in 1327. They had one daughter and one son:
1 CONT
1 CONT Petronilla Butler (d. 1387), married Gilbert Talbot, 3rd Baron Talbot, and had issue. 
1 CONT James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde (b. b 1337-1382), married Elizabeth Darey, daughter of Sir John Darey, Lord Justice of Ireland, and had issue. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Peerage of Ireland 
1 CONT Preceded by - New Creation - Earl of Ormonde, 1328–1337 
1 CONT Succeeded by James Butler 
