1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt"><b>Eleanor de Bohun</b></span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt"> (c.1360 &#150; October 3, 1399) was the elder daughter and co-heiress with her sister 
1 CONT Mary de Bohun, of their father Humphrey de Bohun, 7th Earl of Hereford. Her mother 
1 CONT was Joan Fitzalan, daughter of Richard Fitzalan, 10th Earl of Arundel and his 
1 CONT second wife Eleanor of Lancaster.</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt"><b>Marriage</b></span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">In 1376 she was married to Thomas of Woodstock, 1st Duke of Gloucester. 
1 CONT Thomas was the youngest son of Edward III of England and Philippa of Hainault.</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt"><b>Children</b></span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">They had five children:</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 1. Humphrey Plantagenet, 2nd Earl of Buckingham (c. 1381- 2 September 1399).</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 2. Anne Plantagenet (c. 1383 - 1438) married to Thomas Stafford, 3rd Earl of 
1 CONT Stafford, Edmund Stafford, 5th Earl of Stafford and William Bourchier</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 3. Joan Plantagenet (1384 - 16 August 1400) married to Gilbert Talbot, 5th Baron 
1 CONT Talbot (1383-1419). Died in childbirth.</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 4. Isabelle Plantagenet (12 March 1385/1386 - April 1402)</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 5. Philippa Plantagent (c. 1388) Died young</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">Eleanor de Bohun was invested as a Lady Companion, Order of the Garter in 
1 CONT 1384.1 She was a nun after 1397 at Barking Abbey, she is buried in</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
