0 @N6000000002188651293@ NOTE Eleanor de Bohun
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Eleanor de Bohun (c. 1360 – October 3, 1399) was the elder daughter and co-heiress with her sister Mary de Bohun, of their father Humphrey de Bohun, 7th Earl of Hereford.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Marriage
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1376 she was married to Thomas of Woodstock, 1st Duke of Gloucester. Thomas was the youngest son of Edward III of England and Philippa of Hainault.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT
1 CONT They had five children:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Humphrey Plantagenet, 2nd Earl of Buckingham (c. 1381- 2 September 1399).
1 CONT    2. Anne Plantagenet (c. 1383 - 1438) married to Thomas Stafford, 3rd Earl of Stafford, Edmund Stafford, 5th Earl of Stafford and William Bourchier
1 CONT    3. Joan Plantagenet (1384 - 16 August 1400) married to Gilbert Talbot, 5th Lord Talbot (1383-1419). Died in childbirth.
1 CONT    4. Isabelle Plantagenet (12 March 1385/1386 - April 1402)
1 CONT    5. Philippa Plantagent (c. 1388) Died young
1 CONT
1 CONT Eleanor de Bohun was invested as a Lady Companion, Order of the Garter in 1384.1 She was a nun after 1397 at Barking Abbey, she is buried in Westminster Abbey.
