0 @N6000000002188651468@ NOTE Eleanor de Bohun, Countess of Ormonde
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Eleanor de Bohun, Countess of Ormonde (17 October 1304 – 7 October 1363) was an English noble woman born to Humphrey de Bohun, 4th Earl of Hereford and Lady Elizabeth Plantagenet daughter of Edward I, King of England and Eleanor o
1 CONC f Castile. After the deaths of her parents, she was placed in the care of her aunt Mary Plantagenet and brought up at Amesbury Priory alongside various cousins including Joan Gaveston, Isabel of Lancaster and Joan de Monthermer. E
1 CONC leanor was married twice first in 1327 to James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde son of Sir Edmond Butler and Lady Joan FitzGerald. James, her first husband died in 1337 and six years later 1343 she married a second time to Sir Thomas 
1 CONC de Dagworth, Lord Dagworth. By her first marriage, Eleanor is ancestress to Anne Boleyn.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT
1 CONT by James Butler:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * John Butler (born 6 November 1330, died young)
1 CONT     * Petronilla Butler (died 1387) married Gilbert Talbot, 3rd Baron Talbot
1 CONT     * James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde (4 October 1331 – 18 October 1382) married Elizabeth Darcy
1 CONT
1 CONT by Thomas Dagworth:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Thomasine Dagworth, (born ca. 1344 – 20 July 1409) married (1) John De Dagworth (2) William, 4th Baron Furnival
1 CONT     * Nicholas Dagworth (died January, 1401)
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * thepeerage.com Accessed March 22, 2008
1 CONT     * Eleanor de Bohun Accessed March 23, 2008
