0 @N6000000002188658604@ NOTE Margaret de Audley
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret de Audley (1318 – September 7, 1347) was the daughter of Hugh de Audley, 1st Earl of Gloucester and Margaret de Clare. She was a great-granddaughter of King Edward I of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret was abducted by Ralph Stafford, 1st Earl of Stafford. A complaint was filed by her parents, but King Edward III of England supported Stafford. He appeased Hugh and Margaret by creating Hugh Earl of Gloucester.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Hugh de Stafford, 2nd Earl of Stafford, born circa 1336 in Staffordshire, England
1 CONT     * Margaret de Stafford, born circa 1338 in Staffordshire, England
1 CONT     * Katherine de Stafford, born circa 1340 in Staffordshire, England
1 CONT     * Elizabeth de Stafford, born circa 1340 in Staffordshire, England
1 CONT     * Beatrice de Stafford, born circa 1341 in Staffordshire, England
1 CONT     * Joan de Stafford, born in 1344 in Staffordshire, England
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Wikipedia user Noles1984 family genealogy
