1 CONC or 22 or 30 Aug) 1349 during the pestilence, aged 18.
1 CONT
1 CONT The manors which Sir John de Ferrers and his wife had held jointly at his death, and those - held in her own right - of which she had been jointly enfeoffed with her first husband, were liberated to her, 24 June and 20 Aug 1367.  
1 CONT
1 CONT She married, 3rdly, and his 1st wife, Sir Reynold de Cobeham, of Sterborough, Surrey (Lord Cobeham).  He was born at Sterborough 8 June 1348 and died 3 (or 6) July 1403, aged 55, and was buried in Lingfield Church (brass)
1 CONT
