0 @N6000000002188616592@ NOTE Hugh de Stafford, 2nd Earl of Stafford
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh de Stafford, 2nd Earl of Stafford KG (1336 – 16 October 1386) was the eldest son of Ralph Stafford, 1st Earl of Stafford and Margaret de Audley.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh de Stafford, 2nd Earl of Stafford succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Audley circa 1358. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Stafford on 31 August 1372.
1 CONT
1 CONT On or before 1 March 1350 Hugh de Stafford married Philippa de Beauchamp daughter of Thomas de Beauchamp, 11th Earl of Warwick and Katherine Mortimer. They had nine children.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Ralph Stafford (born about 1354 – 1385)
1 CONT    2. Margaret de Stafford, (b. abt. 1364 – 9 June 1396 married Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland
1 CONT    3. Thomas Stafford (b. abt. 1368 – 4 July 1392)
1 CONT    4. William Stafford (21 September 1375 – 6 April 1395)
1 CONT    5. Humphrey Stafford (b. abt. 1376)
1 CONT    6. Katherine de Stafford (b. abt. 1376 – 8 April 1419), married Michael de la Pole, 2nd Earl of Suffolk
1 CONT    7. Edmund Stafford (2 March 1377 – 22 July 1403)
1 CONT    8. Joan de Stafford (1378 – 1 October 1442)
1 CONT    9. Hugh Stafford (1382 – 25 October 1420
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
