0 @N6000000001563069512@ NOTE Sir John Howard; born c1357; Sheriff of Essex and Herts temp. Henrys IV and V, MP Cambs; married 1st Margaret (died 1381), daughter and heiress of Sir John Plaiz, of Tofte, Norfolk and Stansted Mountfichet, Essex; married 2nd 1383
1 CONC  Alice,
1 CONT daughter and heiress of Sir William Tendring, of Tendring Hall, Stoke by Nayland, Suffolk; died on pilgrimage at Jerusalem 17 Nov 1437. [Burke's Peerage]
0 @N6000000003615871981@ NOTE John became Sheriff of both Essex and Hertford in 1403 after moving to h 
1 CONT is wife Margaret's manor in Essex. John also server as Sheriff on sever
1 CONT al occasions in later years. After Margaret's death in 1383, John marri
1 CONT ed Alice Tendring who brought additional wealth to the Howard fold. John h
1 CONT eld the office of Admiral of The Northern Seas, and he sat during one Parl
1 CONT iament as Knight of the shire for Cambridge, through the Paiz influenc
1 CONT e. In 1436 John went on a pilgrimage to the Holy Land and died at Jerusal
1 CONT em in 1437.
