0 @N6000000002329575658@ NOTE Robert I Bruce of Scots, epic hero, was commonly known as "Robert the Bruce", King of Scotland. Although given a bad rap in the Mel Gibson movie Braveheart, after the death of William Wallace, Robert I later unified Scotland and d
1 CONC efeated the 
1 CONT English army. He then assumed the crown of Scotland, thus bringing an end to the Second Interregnum and England's reign over Scotland in defiance of King Edward I of England. Robert the Bruce reigned over Scotland 1306-1329.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT For more see Robert the Bruce
1 CONT
1 CONT Also See The Legend of the Spider.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert the Bruce is said to have been the 17th Earl of Bruce. I have reports of "eight by the same name." The movie Braveheart, in its Hollywoodism even goes so far as to say, "There were seventeen Roberts of Bruce before you." I 
1 CONC can count. I 
1 CONT have less, and some of them are not named Robert. Hey, 'but dis is what I got.' :-)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert I, Bruce of Scots, was born 11July1274 in Turnbury (Turnberry), Essex. In c1295 he married Isobel of Mar (aka Matilda; c1278-c1320). They only had one child prior to her death, after which he married Elizabeth de Burgh 
1 CONT (1280/1-26Oct1327). He also had children from (an) unknown concubine(s).
1 CONT
