0 @N6000000003051159926@ NOTE He was mortally wounded at the battle of Evesham while fighting with the baronial forces of Simon de Montfort against King Henry and Prince Edward, and died two months later as a prisoner in Beeston Castle. His father, Humphrey V,
1 CONC  was Earl of Hereford and Constable of England, but since the son died before the father, Humphrey VI never inherited the earldom.
