0 @N6000000002188017032@ NOTE John FitzAlan, 7th Earl of Arundel
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT John FitzAlan, 7th Earl of Arundel (Arundel, Sussex, 14 September 1246 – 18 March 1272) was an English nobleman. He was the son of John FitzAlan, 6th Earl of Arundel (d. 1267), and Maude le Botiller, daughter of Theobald le Botill
1 CONC er.
1 CONT
1 CONT Arundel married Isabella de Mortimer, daughter of Roger Mortimer, 1st Baron Wigmore, in 1260. They had a son Richard FitzAlan, 8th Earl of Arundel. Arundel's titles also included Baron of Clun and Oswestry.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT John FitzAlan Earl of Arundel
1 CONT 1267 - 1272 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Richard FitzAlan 
