0 @N6000000003051219567@ NOTE [Wikipedia, "John FitzAlan, 7th Earl of Arundel", retrieved 21 Jun 08]
1 CONT John FitzAlan, 7th Earl of Arundel (14 September 1246 - 18 March 1272) was an English nobleman. He was also feudal Lord of Clun and Oswestry in the Welsh Marches.
1 CONT
1 CONT Family
1 CONT He was the son of John FitzAlan, 6th Earl of Arundel (d. 1267), and Maud le Boteler, daughter of Theobald le Botiller (or Boteler) and Rohese (or Rohesia) de Verdun. Through his father, FitzAlan was also descended from Alan fitzFl
1 CONC aad, and Llywelyn the Great.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage
1 CONT Lord Arundel married Isabella de Mortimer, daughter of Roger Mortimer, 1st Baron Wigmore, in 1260. They had a son Richard FitzAlan, 8th Earl of Arundel.
