0 @N6000000002188014676@ NOTE Robert de Vere, 6th Earl of Oxford
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert de Vere, 6th Earl of Oxford (c. 24 June 1257 – 17 April 1331) was the son and heir of Robert de Vere, 5th Earl of Oxford. Robert the younger took part in several of the military campaigns of Edward I, Edward II and Edward I
1 CONC II in Wales, Scotland and France. He was married to Margaret Mortimer, daughter of Roger Mortimer, 1st Baron Wigmore. He also officiated at the Coronation of Queen Isabella, wife of Edward II, in 1308. His only son Thomas died bef
1 CONC ore him, and when Robert died in 1331, he was succeeded by his nephew John de Vere, 7th Earl of Oxford.
1 CONT Peerage of England
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Robert de Vere Earl of Oxford
1 CONT 1296–1331 Succeeded by
1 CONT John de Vere
