0 @N6000000003615380746@ NOTE Elizabeth Princess of England * was born about 1095 in Talby, Yorkshire, England. (88) Parents: Henry I Beauclerc King Of England * and Matilda (originally Edith) Dunkeld Queen Of England *.
1 CONT She was married to Fergus Lord of Galloway * about 1124 in Carrick, Argyllshire, Scotland. (88) Children were: Uchtred * Lord of Galloway, Gilbert of Galloway (Carrick), Affrica de Galloway, Margaret de Galloway.
0 @N6000000003615765480@ NOTE Turton (with a ?) has Elizabeth as daughter of William Rufus (William II King of England).
1 CONT
1 CONT Curt Hofemann, curt_hofemann@yahoo.com, has one source indicating that Elizabeth is the same as Sybilla, wife of Alexander of Scotland. Possible (she probably would have married Fergus after 1124), though I think unlikley.  Curt's
1 CONC  other source has them as two different people.
1 CONT
1 CONT Possily your ID I04761 Sybilla FitzHenry & this Elizabeth are one & the same.  There are conflicting sources:
1 CONT
1 CONT Same:
1 CONT Sibyl, but called Elizabeth by Sandford [Ref: Sheppard Apr65 p96] unfortunately I did not note the identity of "Sanford" in my notes... Curt
1 CONT
1 CONT Not same:
1 CONT He married Elizabeth, natural daughter of Henry I, and sister of Sibilla, who married Alexander I, brother of David." [Ref: Sir Herbert Maxwell, "A History of Dumfries and Galloway" by Sir Herbert Maxwell, Edinburgh, 1896, pp. 47-
1 CONC 48]
1 CONT
1 CONT Regards,
1 CONT Curt
