0 @N6000000002188017059@ NOTE Theobald le Botiller
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Theobald le Botiller, also known as Theobald Butler, 2nd Baron Butler (January, 1200 – July 19, 1230) was the son of Theobald Walter, 1st Baron Butler and Maud le Vavasour. He was born in Norfolk, East Anglia, England. He had live
1 CONC ry of his lands on 2 July 1221.
1 CONT
1 CONT After the death of his first wife Joan de Mareis, Theobald remained a widower. Henry III of England requested the marriage of Theobald to Rohese de Verdon, daughter of Nicholas de Verdon of Alton, Staffordshire and Clemence. The a
1 CONC greement to marry occurred on 4 September 1225. The marriage is presumed to have shortly followed. This was the second marriage for both Theobald and Rohese.
1 CONT
1 CONT Theobald was summoned cum equis et armis (Latin: "with horse and arms") to attend the King into Brittany, as "Theobaldus Pincerna" on 26 October 1229. He died on 19 July 1230 in Poitou, France, at the age of 30. Theobald, 2nd Baro
1 CONC n Butler, was buried in the Abbey of Arklow, County Wicklow, Leinster, Ireland.
1 CONT
1 CONT His daughter, Maude le Botiller, was married to John FitzAlan, 6th Earl of Arundel and was mother of John FitzAlan, 7th Earl of Arundel.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT George Edward Cokayne. The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct, or Dormant, I-XIII (Thrupp, Stroud, Gloucestershire, GL5 2BU: Sutton Publishing Limited, 2000), II:
1 CONC 448. 
1 CONT Ibid., II:447. 
1 CONT Some corrections and additions to The Complete Peerage, http://www.medievalgenealogy.org, II:448. 
