0 @N6000000001783279296@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT 1st Lord of LITCHAM; Constable of Scarborough Castle
1 CONT <http://fabpedigree.com/s048/f752878.htm>
1 CONT
1 CONT Brother of Sir William de Felton,1st of Edlingham (d 21.09.1358, Constable of Roxburgh Castle was the fSir Robert "whose parentage is unknown" was Sir Robert de Felton of Litcham, 1st Lord (d Bannockburn 24.06.1314, Constable of S
1 CONC carborough Castle)
1 CONT <http://www.stirnet.com/main/index.php?option=com_wrapper&Itemid=79&startUrl=http://www.stirnet.com/HTML/genie/british/ff/felton1.htm>
1 CONT
1 CONT In the 25 [year of the reign of] Edward I, he obtained a charter from the crown for a weekly market at his manor of Litcham in Norfolk and likewise a free warren there.  In the 34th of the same reign he was in the expedition then 
1 CONC made into Scotland, in the 4th [year of the reign of] Edward II he had a military summons for a similar service.  The next year he was constituted governor of Scarborough Castle, and was summoned to Parliament as a Baron  8 Januar
1 CONC y, 22 May, 26 July and 26 November, 1212.  His lordship d. 1314 and was s. by his son…(A Genealogical History of the Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct . Pg 196, Bernard Burke)
1 CONT <http://books.google.com/books?id=1ysWkXKSrpIC&pg=PA196&lpg=PA196&dq=robert+de+felton+1314&source=web&ots=K7iPNxFqdO&sig=TP5vJ2Lk07uPUquv4pssni_7k3U&hl=en&sa=X&oi=book_result&resnum=3&ct=result>
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT Robert married Hawise Lestraunge (daughter of Sir John Lestraunge of Knockin by Joan de Somery)
1 CONT Sir John de Felton of Litcham, 2nd Lord (1334, Constable of Newcastle, Admiral)
1 CONT Sir Hamon de Felton of Litcham, 3rd Lord (d 1379)
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Margaret (d 25.03.1368, widow of Sir William de Kerdestone of Kerdiston)
1 CONT
1 CONT Not sure which wife was mother of
1 CONT Mary de Felton
1 CONT Alianore de Felton
1 CONT <http://www.stirnet.com/main/index.php?option=com_wrapper&Itemid=79&startUrl=http://www.stirnet.com/HTML/genie/british/ff/felton1.htm>
1 CONT
1 CONT Death
1 CONT He fought in the Battle of Bannockburn for Edward I on 24 June 1314 and was killed in action.
0 @N6000000003949900045@ NOTE Copied from the Stradling family website "www.stradling.org.uk/docs/Oth_recs.htm":
1 CONT "Victoria County History of Warwickshire."
1 CONT Certain lands in Losley were sold with the manor of Walton Mauduit by the Earl of Warwick to Simon de Wauton, Bishop of Norwich (1258-66). The bishop conveycd them to John de Wauton, who was probably his great-nephew.
1 CONT In January 1246 Mr. Simon de Wauton (or Walton) received a grant of a weekly market on Wednesday and a fair on the eve and day of SS. Peter and Paul at his manor of LITTLE WELLESBOURNE. This Mr. Simon, who bought property in Walto
1 CONC n Deyville, became Bishop of Norwich in 1258 and died in 1265. His successor Sir John de Wauton died in or shortly before 1277,
1 CONT His successor, Roger Deyville, became heavily indebted to the Jews and sold the manor to Simon de Wauton, who granted it to his son John. This Simon may have been identical with the Mr. Simon who held the manor of Welles-bourne Ha
1 CONC stings (see above) and who in 1240 bought from William Mauduit and Alice his wife 6 acres in Walton called Litlemede lying beside the Portwey. Mr. Simon was elderly when he became bishop and may well have been married when young.
0 @N6000000001353926636@ NOTE Roger le Strange, 5th baron, summoned to parliament from 20 September, 1355, to 9 August, 1382, b. 1327. This nobleman was constantly engaged in the wars of Gascony and Brittany, temp. Edward III and Richard II. His lordship m. La
1 CONC dy Aliva FitzAlan, dau. of Edmund, Earl of Arundel, and dying in 1382, was s. by his son, John le Strange, 6th baron. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages,Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 51
1 CONC 6, Strange, Barons Strange of Knokyn]
